TURATH_CHUNK(49,[{"num":9800,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَتَبَ إِلَى بَكْرِ بْنِ وَائِلٍ: مِنْ مُحَمَّدٍ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ إِلَى بَكْرِ بْنِ وَائِلٍ، أَسْلِمُوا تَسْلَمُوا، فَمَا وَجَدْنَا مَنْ يَقْرَؤُهُ إِلَّا رَجُلٌ مِنْ بَنِي ضُبَيْعَةَ فَهُمْ يُسَمَّوْنَ بَنِي الْكَاتِبِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار – كشف الأستار (1670)، وأبو يعلى (2947) وصححه ابن حبان (6558) كلهم من طريق نصر بن علي، حدثنا نوح بن قيس، عن أخيه خالد بن قيس، عن قتادة، عن أنس، فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب كتاب النبي ﷺ إلى بكر بن وائل","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب سيرة النبي ﷺ","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (1670) and Abū Yaʿlā (2947), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6558).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Letter to Bakr ibn Wā’il","part_en":"Book of the Biography of the Prophet ﷺ","group_ar":"جموع ما جاء في كتب النبي ﷺ إلى الملوك والأمراء يدعوهم إلى الإسلام","group_en":"A Collection of Reports Concerning the Prophet’s ﷺ Letters to Kings and Rulers Inviting Them to Islam","part_no":48,"group_no":41,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported that the Prophet ﷺ wrote to Bakr ibn Wā’il: “From Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Bakr ibn Wā’il: Embrace Islam and you will be safe.” We could find no one able to read it except a man from Banū Ḍubayʿah; consequently, they came to be known as Banū al-Kātib—the descendants of the scribe."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["seerah",661],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار -«كشف الأستار» (1670)- وأبو يعلى (2947)، وصححه ابن حبان (6558)."},{"num":9801,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمْ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: يَأْتِي زَمَانٌ يَغْزُو فِئَامٌ مِنَ النَّاسِ، فَيُقَالُ: فِيكُمْ مَنْ صَحِبَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ فَيُقَالُ: نَعَمْ. فَيُفْتَحُ عَلَيْهِ، ثُمَّ يَأْتِي زَمَانٌ فَيُقَالُ: فِيكُمْ مَنْ صَحِبَ أَصْحَابَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ فَيُقَالُ: نَعَمْ. فَيُفْتَحُ، ثُمَّ يَأْتِي زَمَانٌ فَيُقَالُ: فِيكُمْ مَنْ صَحِبَ صَاحِبَ أَصْحَابِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ فَيُقَالُ: نَعَمْ. فَيُفْتَحُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الجهاد والسير (2897)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2532-208) كلاهما من طرق عن سفيان بن عيينة قال: سمع عمرو جابرا، يخبر عن أبي سعيد الخدري، فذكره، واللفظ للبخاري، وساقه مسلم نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2897) and Muslim (208–2532).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A time will come when groups of people will go out to fight. It will be asked, ‘Is there among you anyone who accompanied the Prophet ﷺ?’ They will reply, ‘Yes,’ and victory will be granted to them. Then another time will come, and it will be asked, ‘Is there among you anyone who accompanied the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ?’ They will reply, ‘Yes,’ and victory will be granted. Then another time will come, and it will be asked, ‘Is there among you anyone who accompanied one who accompanied the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ?’ They will reply, ‘Yes,’ and victory will be granted.”"]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿مُحَمَّدٌ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ وَالَّذِينَ مَعَهُ أَشِدَّاءُ عَلَى الْكُفَّارِ رُحَمَاءُ بَيْنَهُمْ تَرَاهُمْ رُكَّعًا سُجَّدًا يَبْتَغُونَ فَضْلًا مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرِضْوَانًا سِيمَاهُمْ فِي وُجُوهِهِمْ مِنْ أَثَرِ السُّجُودِ ذَلِكَ مَثَلُهُمْ فِي التَّوْرَاةِ وَمَثَلُهُمْ فِي الْإِنْجِيلِ كَزَرْعٍ أَخْرَجَ شَطْأَهُ فَآزَرَهُ فَاسْتَغْلَظَ فَاسْتَوَى عَلَى سُوقِهِ يُعْجِبُ الزُّرَّاعَ لِيَغِيظَ بِهِمُ الْكُفَّارَ وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ مِنْهُمْ مَغْفِرَةً وَأَجْرًا عَظِيمًا﴾ [الفتح: ٢٩].","وقال تعالى:","﴿لَقَدْ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إِذْ يُبَايِعُونَكَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ فَعَلِمَ مَا فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ فَأَنْزَلَ السَّكِينَةَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَأَثَابَهُمْ فَتْحًا قَرِيبًا﴾ [الفتح: ١٨].","وقال تعالى:","﴿لَا يَسْتَوِي مِنْكُمْ مَنْ أَنْفَقَ مِنْ قَبْلِ الْفَتْحِ وَقَاتَلَ أُولَئِكَ أَعْظَمُ دَرَجَةً مِنَ الَّذِينَ أَنْفَقُوا مِنْ بَعْدُ وَقَاتَلُوا وَكُلًّا وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الْحُسْنَى وَاللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ﴾ [الحديد: ١٠]."],"en":["Allah Most High said:","“Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah, and those with him are firm against the disbelievers and merciful among themselves. You see them bowing and prostrating, seeking bounty from Allah and His pleasure. Their mark is upon their faces from the trace of prostration. That is their description in the Torah. Their description in the Gospel is like a crop that sends forth its shoots, strengthens them, grows thick, and stands firmly upon its stalks, delighting the sowers, so that through them He may enrage the disbelievers. Allah has promised those among them who believe and perform righteous deeds forgiveness and a magnificent reward.”","[Al-Fatḥ: 29]","And He Most High said:","“Allah was certainly pleased with the believers when they pledged allegiance to you beneath the tree. He knew what was in their hearts, so He sent tranquillity down upon them and rewarded them with an imminent victory.”","[Al-Fatḥ: 18]","And He Most High said:","“Those among you who spent and fought before the Conquest are not equal to those who did so afterward. They are greater in rank than those who spent and fought afterward, though Allah has promised the finest reward to all. Allah is fully aware of what you do.”","[Al-Ḥadīd: 10]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",1],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2897)، ومسلم (208-2532)."},{"num":9802,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَأْتِي عَلَى النَّاسِ زَمَانٌ يُبْعَثُ مِنْهُمُ الْبَعْثُ فَيَقُولُونَ: انْظُرُوا هَلْ تَجِدُونَ فِيكُمْ أَحَدًا مِنْ أَصْحَابِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ ؟ فَيُوجَدُ الرَّجُلُ فيُفْتَح لَهُمْ بِهِ، ثُمَّ يُبْعَثُ الْبَعْثُ الثانى فَيَقُولُونَ: هَلْ فِيهِمْ مَنْ رَأَى أَصْحَابَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ ؟ فيُفْتَح لَهُمْ بِهِ، ثُمَّ يُبْعَثُ الْبَعْثُ الثَّالِثُ فَيُقَالُ: انْظُرُوا هَلْ تَرَوْنَ فِيهِمْ مَنْ رَأَى مَنْ رَأَى أَصْحَابَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ ؟ ثُمَّ يَكُونُ الْبَعْثُ الرَّابِعُ فَيُقَالُ: انْظُرُوا هَلْ تَرَوْنَ فِيهِمْ أَحَدًا رَأَى مَنْ رَأَى أَحَدًا رَأَى أَصْحَابَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ ؟ فَيُوجَدُ الرَّجُلُ فَيُفْتَحُ لَهُمْ بِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2532-209) عن سعيد بن يحيى بن سعيد الأموي، ثنا أبي، ثنا ابن جريج، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر قال: زعم أبو سعيد الخدري قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (209–2532).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A time will come upon the people when a military expedition will be dispatched from among them. They will say, ‘Look and see whether you can find among yourselves anyone who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ.’ Such a man will be found, and victory will be granted to them because of him. Then a second expedition will be dispatched, and they will say, ‘Is there among them anyone who saw the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ?’ Victory will be granted to them because of him. Then a third expedition will be dispatched, and it will be said, ‘Look and see whether there is among them anyone who saw someone who had seen the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ.’ Then there will be a fourth expedition, and it will be said, ‘Look and see whether there is among them anyone who saw someone who had seen someone who had seen the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ.’ Such a man will be found, and victory will be granted to them because of him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",2],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (209-2532)."},{"num":9803,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عِمْرَانَ بْنِ حُصَيْنٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: خَيْرُكُمْ قَرْنِي، ثُمَّ الَّذِينَ يَلُونَهُمْ، ثُمَّ الَّذِينَ يَلُونَهُمْ. قَالَ عِمْرَانُ: لاَ أَدْرِي أَذَكَرَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعْدُ قَرْنَيْنِ أَوْ ثَلاَثَةً. قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ بَعْدَكُمْ قَوْمًا يَخُونُونَ وَلاَ يُؤْتَمَنُونَ، وَيَشْهَدُونَ، وَلاَ يُسْتَشْهَدُونَ، وَيَنْذِرُونَ وَلاَ يَفُونَ، وَيَظْهَرُ فِيهِمُ السِّمَنُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الشهادات (2651)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2535-214) كلاهما من طرق عن شعبة، ثنا أبو جمرة قال: سمعت زهدم بن مضرب قال: سمعت عمران بن حصين فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2651) and Muslim (214–2535).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The best of you are my generation, then those who follow them, and then those who follow them.” ʿImrān said: “I do not know whether the Prophet ﷺ mentioned two or three generations after his own.” The Prophet ﷺ then said: “After you will come people who betray and are not trusted, who bear witness without being asked to testify, who make vows but do not fulfil them, and among whom obesity will become widespread.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["This is the wording of al-Bukhārī. Muslim’s wording is similar, except that he mentioned the words, “then those who follow them,” three times. He then said:","ʿImrān said, “I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it twice or three times after mentioning his own generation. Then, after them, there will be people who bear witness…” to the end of the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",3],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[6740],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2651)، ومسلم (214-2535)."},{"num":9804,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ:  سَأَلَ رَجُلٌ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَيُّ النَّاسِ خَيْرٌ؟ قَالَ: الْقَرْنُ الَّذِي أَنَا فِيهِ، ثُمَّ الثَّانِي، ثُمَّ الثَّالِثُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2536) من طرق عن حسين بن علي الجعفي، عن زائدة، عن السدي، عن عبدالله البهيَّ، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2536).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “Which people are the best?” He replied: “The generation in which I live, then the second, and then the third.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",4],"full":1,"rep":[13335],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2536)."},{"num":9805,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ النُّعْمَانِ بْنِ بَشِيرٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: خَيْرُ النَّاسِ قَرْنِي، ثُمَّ الَّذِينَ يَلُونَهُمْ، ثُمَّ الَّذِينَ يَلُونَ الَّذِينَ يَلُونَهُمْ، ثُمَّ يَأْتِي قَوْمٌ تَسْبِقُ أَيْمَانُهُمْ شَهَادَتَهُمْ، وَشَهَادَتُهُمْ أَيْمَانَهُمْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (18348)، والحارث في مسنده كما في البغية (1036)،ـ وأبو نعيم في الحلية (912)، وابن حبان (6727) كلهم من طريق أبي النضر هاشم بن القاسم، ثنا شيبان، عن عاصم، عن خيثمة والشعبي، عن النعمان بن بشير قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (18348), al-Ḥārith in his Musnad as cited in al-Bughyah (1036), Abū Nuʿaym in Ḥilyat al-Awliyāʾ (2/78, 4/125), and Ibn Ḥibbān (6727).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of mankind are my generation, then those who follow them, and then those who follow those who follow them. Afterward, people will come whose oaths precede their testimony and whose testimony precedes their oaths.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",5],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (18348)، والحارث في مسنده كما في البغية (1036)، وأبو نعيم في الحلية (2/78، 4/125)، وابن حبان (6727)."},{"num":9806,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: خَيْرُ النَّاسِ قَرْنِي، ثُمَّ الَّذِينَ يَلُونَهُمْ، ثُمَّ الَّذِينَ يَلُونَهُمْ، ثُمَّ يَجِيءُ أَقْوَامٌ تَسْبِقُ شَهَادَةُ أَحَدِهِمْ يَمِينَهُ، وَيَمِينُهُ شَهَادَتَهُ.","قَالَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ: \"وَكَانُوا يَضْرِبُونَنَا عَلَى الشَّهَادَةِ وَالْعَهْدِ\"."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الشهادات (2652)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2533-210) كلاهما من حديث منصور، عن إبراهيم بن يزيد، عن عبيدة السلماني، عن عبدالله قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2652) and Muslim (210–2533). This is the wording of al-Bukhārī. Muslim’s wording is similar and contains:","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The best of mankind are my generation, then those who follow them, and then those who follow them. Afterward, people will come whose testimony will precede their oaths and whose oaths will precede their testimony.” Ibrāhīm said: “They used to discipline us concerning testimony and pledges.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["“The best of my nation are the generation nearest to me, then those who follow them, and then those who follow them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",6],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[6741],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2652)، ومسلم (210-2533). وهذا لفظ البخاري، ولفظ مسلم نحوه، وفيه: «خير أمتي القرن الذي يلوني، ثم الذين يلونهم، ثم الذين يلونهم»."},{"num":9807,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: بُعِثْتُ مِنْ خَيْرِ قُرُونِ بَنِي آدَمَ قَرْنًا فَقَرْنًا، حَتَّى كُنْتُ مِنَ الْقَرْنِ الَّذِي كُنْتُ فِيهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المناقب (3557) عن قتيبة بن سعيد، ثنا يعقوب بن عبد الرحمن، عن عمرو، عن سعيد المقبري، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3557).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was sent from the best generations of the children of Adam, generation after generation, until I came from the generation in which I was born.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",7],"full":1,"rep":[8545],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3557)."},{"num":9808,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  خَيْرُ أُمَّتِي الْقَرْنُ الَّذِينَ بُعِثْتُ فِيهِمْ، ثُمَّ الَّذِينَ يَلُونَهُمْ، - وَاللهُ أَعْلَمُ أَذَكَرَ الثَّالِثَ أَمْ لَا، قَالَ: ثُمَّ يَخْلُفُ قَوْمٌ يُحِبُّونَ السَّمَانَةَ، يَشْهَدُونَ قَبْلَ أَنْ يُسْتَشْهَدُوا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2534) من طرق عن أبي بشر، عن عبد الله بن شقيق، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2534). In another wording recorded by him, Abū Hurayrah said:","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of my nation are the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them.” Allah knows best whether he mentioned the third generation or not. He then said: “After them will come people who love corpulence and who bear witness before being asked to testify.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["“I do not know whether he said it two or three times.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",8],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2534). وفي لفظ له: «قال أبو هريرة: فلا أدري مرتين أو ثلاثة»."},{"num":9809,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ وَاثِلَةَ بْنِ الأسقع قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا تَزَالُونَ بِخَيْرٍ مَا دَامَ فِيكُمْ مَنْ رَآنِي وَصَاحَبَنِي، وَاللهِ لَا تَزَالُونَ بِخَيْرٍ مَا دَامَ فِيكُمْ مَنْ رَأَى مَنْ رَآنِي، وَصَاحَبَ مَنْ صَاحَبَنِي، وَاللهِ لَا تَزَالُونَ بِخَيْرٍ مَا دَامَ فِيكُمْ مَنْ رَأَى مَنْ رَأَى مَنْ رَآنِي، وَصَاحَبَ مَنْ صَاحَبَ مَنْ صَاحَبَنِي."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي شيبة في مصنفه (33084) - ومن طريقه ابن أبي عاصم في السنة (1522)، والطبراني في الكبير (22/ح 207)- عن زيد بن الحباب، ثنا عبد الله بن العلاء أبو الزبير الدمشقي، ثنا عبد الله بن عامر، عن واثلة بن الأسقع فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah in his Muṣannaf (33084; 12/178), and through him by Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (1522), and by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (22/85).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will continue to be upon goodness so long as there remains among you someone who saw me and accompanied me. By Allah, you will continue to be upon goodness so long as there remains among you someone who saw those who saw me and accompanied those who accompanied me. By Allah, you will continue to be upon goodness so long as there remains among you someone who saw those who saw those who saw me and accompanied those who accompanied those who accompanied me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",9],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي شيبة في مصنفه (32417)، ومن طريقه ابن أبي عاصم في السنة (1522)، والطبراني في الكبير (22/85)."},{"num":9810,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى الأشعري قَالَ: صَلَّيْنَا الْمَغْرِبَ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، ثُمَّ قُلْنَا: لَوْ جَلَسْنَا حَتَّى نصلى مَعَهُ الْعِشَاءَ، قَالَ: فَجَلَسْنَا، فَخَرَجَ عَلَيْنَا، فَقَالَ: مَا زِلْتُمْ هَا هُنَا؟.قُلْنَا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، صَلَّيْنَا مَعَكَ الْمَغْرِبَ، ثُمَّ قُلْنَا: نَجْلِسُ حَتَّى نصلى مَعَكَ الْعِشَاءَ.قَالَ: أَحْسَنْتُمْ أَوْ أَصَبْتُمْ.قَالَ: فَرَفَعَ رَأْسَهُ إِلَى السَّمَاءِ، وَكَانَ كَثِيرًا مِمَّا يَرْفَعُ رَأْسَهُ إِلَى السَّمَاءِ، فَقَالَ: النُّجُومُ أَمَنَةٌ لِلسَّمَاءِ، فَإِذَا ذَهَبَتِ النُّجُومُ أَتَى السَّمَاءَ مَا تُوعَدُ، وَأَنَا أَمَنَةٌ لأصحابى فَإِذَا ذَهَبْتُ أَتَى أَصْحَابِي مَا يُوعَدُونَ، وأصحابى أَمَنَةٌ لِأُمَّتِي فَإِذَا ذَهَبَ أَصْحَابِي أَتَى أُمَّتِي مَا يُوعَدُونَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2531) من طرق عن حسين بن علي الجعفي، عن مجمع بن يحيى، عن سعيد بن أبي بردة، عن أبي بردة، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن بقاء النبي ﷺ أمان لأصحابه، وبقاء أصحابه أمان للأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2531).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Presence Was a Safeguard for His Companions, and His Companions’ Presence Was a Safeguard for the Nation","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī reported: We performed the sunset prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and then said: “If only we remained seated until we could perform the night prayer with him.” So we remained seated. He came out to us and asked: “Are you still here?” We replied: “O Messenger of Allah, we performed the sunset prayer with you and then decided to remain seated until we could perform the night prayer with you.” He said: “You have done well,” or, “You have acted correctly.” He then raised his head toward the sky—and he would often raise his head toward the sky—and said: “The stars are a safeguard for the sky. When the stars disappear, that which the sky has been promised will come upon it. I am a safeguard for my Companions; when I depart, that which my Companions have been promised will come upon them. My Companions are a safeguard for my nation; when my Companions depart, that which my nation has been promised will come upon it.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His words, “When the stars disappear,” mean when they lose their light and scatter. His words, “I am a safeguard,” with fatḥahs on the letters, mean a safeguard from tribulations and wars. His words, “That which my Companions have been promised will come upon them,” refer to the tribulations and wars that occurred during the lives of the Companions."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",10],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[14714],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2531)."},{"num":9811,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُقْبَةَ بْنِ عَامِرٍ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَرَجَ يَوْمًا فَصَلَّى عَلَى أَهْلِ أُحُدٍ صَلاَتَهُ عَلَى الْمَيِّتِ، ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ إِلَى الْمِنْبَرِ، فَقَالَ: إِنِّي فَرَطٌ لَكُمْ، وَأَنَا شَهِيدٌ عَلَيْكُمْ، وَإِنِّي وَاللَّهِ لأَنْظُرُ إِلَى حَوْضِي الْآنَ، وَإِنِّي أُعْطِيتُ مَفَاتِيحَ خَزَائِنِ الأَرْضِ ـ أَوْ مَفَاتِيحَ الأَرْضِ، ـ وَإِنِّي وَاللَّهِ مَا أَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ أَنْ تُشْرِكُوا بَعْدِي، وَلَكِنْ أَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ أَنْ تَنَافَسُوا فِيهَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4042)، ومسلم في الفضائل (2296-30) كلاهما من طريق يزيد بن أبي حبيب، عن أبي الخير، عن عقبة بن عامر قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب قول النبي ﷺ: «أنا فرط لكم»","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4042) and Muslim (30–2296).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Statement, “I Shall Precede You”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day and performed a prayer for the martyrs of Uḥud like his prayer over the deceased. He then proceeded to the pulpit and said: “I shall precede you, and I shall be a witness over you. By Allah, I can see my Basin at this very moment. I have been given the keys to the treasures of the earth—or the keys of the earth. By Allah, I do not fear that you will associate partners with Allah after me; rather, I fear that you will compete with one another over the world.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His words, “I shall precede you,” mean: I shall go ahead of you. It is said, “The people went ahead,” meaning that they preceded the others to the water."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",11],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4042)، ومسلم (30-2296)."},{"num":9812,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُعَاوِيَةَ بْنِ أَبِي سُفْيَانَ، أَنَّهُ قَامَ فِينَا، فَقَالَ: أَلاَ إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَامَ فِينَا فَقَالَ: أَلاَ إِنَّ مَنْ قَبْلَكُمْ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ افْتَرَقُوا عَلَى ثِنْتَيْنِ وَسَبْعِينَ مِلَّةً، وَإِنَّ هَذِهِ الْمِلَّةَ سَتَفْتَرِقُ عَلَى ثَلاَثٍ وَسَبْعِينَ، ثِنْتَانِ وَسَبْعُونَ فِي النَّارِ، وَوَاحِدَةٌ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَهِيَ الْجَمَاعَةُ. زَادَ ابْنُ يَحْيَى وَعَمْرٌو فِي حَدِيثَيْهِمَا: وَإِنَّهُ سَيَخْرُجُ مِنْ أُمَّتِي أَقْوَامٌ تَجَارَى بِهِمْ تِلْكَ الأَهْوَاءُ كَمَا يَتَجَارَى الْكَلْبُ لِصَاحِبِهِ. وَقَالَ عَمْرٌو: الْكَلْبُ بِصَاحِبِهِ، لاَ يَبْقَى مِنْهُ عِرْقٌ وَلاَ مَفْصِلٌ إِلاَّ دَخَلَهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4597)، وأحمد (16937)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (65)، والحاكم في المستدرك (1/128) كلهم من طريق صفوان بن عمرو، ثني أزهر بن عبد الله الهوزني، عن أبي عامر عبد الله بن لُحي، عن معاوية فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل جماعة الصحابة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4597), Aḥmad (16937), Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (65), and al-Ḥākim in al-Mustadrak (443).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the United Body of the Companions","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān stood among us and said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ once stood among us and said: “Those among the People of the Scripture who came before you divided into seventy-two religious sects. This nation will divide into seventy-three sects: seventy-two will be in the Fire and one will be in Paradise, and it is the united community.” Ibn Yaḥyā and ʿAmr added in their narrations: “Indeed, there will arise among my nation people through whom those desires will course just as rabies courses through its victim.” ʿAmr said: “Rabies spreads through its victim, leaving no vein or joint without entering it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",12],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4597)، وأحمد (16937)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (65)، والحاكم في المستدرك (443)."},{"num":9813,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَوْفِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: افْتَرَقَتِ الْيَهُودُ عَلَى إِحْدَى وَسَبْعِينَ فِرْقَةً، فَوَاحِدَةٌ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَسَبْعُونَ فِي النَّارِ، وَافْتَرَقَتِ النَّصَارَى عَلَى ثِنْتَيْنِ وَسَبْعِينَ فِرْقَةً، فَإِحْدَى وَسَبْعُونَ فِي النَّارِ، وَوَاحِدَةٌ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَالَّذِي نَفْسُ مُحَمَّدٍ بِيَدِهِ! لَتَفْتَرِقَنَّ أُمَّتِي عَلَى ثَلاَثٍ وَسَبْعِينَ فِرْقَةً، فَوَاحِدَةٌ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَثِنْتَانِ وَسَبْعُونَ فِي النَّارِ. قِيلَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ مَنْ هُمْ؟ قَالَ: الْجَمَاعَةُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابنُ ماجه (3992)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (63)، واللالكائي في شرح أصول اعتقاد أهل السنة (149) كلهم من طرق عن عباد بن يوسف الكندي الحمصي، ثنا صفوان بن عمرو، عن راشد بن سعد، عن عوف بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل جماعة الصحابة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (3992), Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (63), and al-Lālakā’ī in Sharḥ Uṣūl al-Iʿtiqād (149).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the United Body of the Companions","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAwf ibn Mālik reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Jews divided into seventy-one sects: one will be in Paradise and seventy will be in the Fire. The Christians divided into seventy-two sects: seventy-one will be in the Fire and one will be in Paradise. By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, my nation will certainly divide into seventy-three sects: one will be in Paradise and seventy-two will be in the Fire.” It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, who are they?” He replied: “The united community.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",13],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[15869],"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3992)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (63)، واللالكائي في شرح أصول الاعتقاد (149)."},{"num":9814,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ افْتَرَقَتْ عَلَى إِحْدَى وَسَبْعِينَ فِرْقَةً، وَإِنَّ أُمَّتِي سَتَفْتَرِقُ عَلَى ثِنْتَيْنِ وَسَبْعِينَ فِرْقَةً، كُلُّهَا فِي النَّارِ، إِلاَّ وَاحِدَةً، وَهِيَ الْجَمَاعَةُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3993)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (64) كلاهما عن هشام بن عمار، ثنا الوليد بن مسلم، ثنا أبو عمرو، ثنا قتادة، عن أنس بن مالك قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل جماعة الصحابة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (3993) and Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (64).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the United Body of the Companions","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Children of Israel divided into seventy-one sects, and my nation will divide into seventy-two sects. All of them will be in the Fire except one, and it is the united community.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",14],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[15870],"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3993)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (64)."},{"num":9815,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ قَالَ: لَا تُوقِدُوا نَارًا بِلَيْلٍ فَلَمَّا كَانَ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ قَالَ: أَوْقِدُوا، وَاصْطَنِعُوا، فَإِنَّهُ لَا يُدْرِكُ قَوْمٌ بَعْدَكُمْ صَاعَكُمْ وَلَا مُدَّكم."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (11208)، وأبو يعلى (984)، والحاكم (4336) كلهم من طرق عن يحيى بن سعيد القطان، ثنا محمد بن أبي يحيى الأسلمي، حدثني أبي، أن أبا سعيد الخدري أخبره فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل جماعة الصحابة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (11208), Abū Yaʿlā (984), and al-Ḥākim in al-Mustadrak (4336).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the United Body of the Companions","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported that on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not light a fire at night.” Later, he said: “Light your fires and prepare your food, for no people who come after you will attain the merit of even your ṣāʿ or your mudd.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",15],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (11208)، وأبو يعلى (984)، والحاكم في المستدرك (4336)."},{"num":9816,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["اللهِ بْنَ عُمَرَ قَالَ:  صَلَّى بِنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ذَاتَ لَيْلَةٍ، صَلَاةَ الْعِشَاءِ فِي آخِرِ حَيَاتِهِ، فَلَمَّا سَلَّمَ قَامَ فَقَالَ: أَرَأَيْتَكُمْ لَيْلَتَكُمْ هَذِهِ؟ فَإِنَّ عَلَى رَأْسِ مِائَةِ سَنَةٍ مِنْهَا لَا يَبْقَى مِمَّنْ هُوَ عَلَى ظَهْرِ الْأَرْضِ أَحَدٌ.","قَالَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ: فَوَهَلَ النَّاسُ فِي مَقَالَةِ رَسُولِ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم تِلْكَ فِيمَا يَتَحَدَّثُونَ مِنْ هَذِهِ الْأَحَادِيثِ عَنْ مِائَةِ سَنَةٍ، وَإِنَّمَا قَالَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم:لا يَبْقَى مِمَّنْ هُوَ الْيَوْمَ عَلَى ظَهْرِ الْأَرْضِ أحد.يريد بِذَلِكَ أَنْ يَنْخَرِمَ ذَلِكَ الْقَرْنُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في مواقيت الصلاة (601)، ومسلم في الفضائل (2537) كلاهما من طريق الزهري، أخبرني سالم بن عبد الله وأبو بكر بن سليمان، أن عبد الله بن عمر قال: فذكر الحديث والسياق لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في انخرام قرن الصحابة بتمام مائة عام بعد النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (601) and Muslim (2537). This wording is Muslim’s.","chapter_en":"Reports That the Generation of the Companions Would Come to an End One Hundred Years After the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported: During the latter part of his life, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the night prayer one evening. After concluding the prayer, he stood and said: “Consider this night of yours: at the end of one hundred years from now, none of those presently upon the face of the earth will remain.” Ibn ʿUmar said: The people misunderstood this statement of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ because of the reports they narrated concerning one hundred years. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had only said: “None of those who are upon the face of the earth today will remain.”","By that, he meant that the generation then living would come to an end."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",16],"full":1,"rep":[8290],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (601)، ومسلم (2537)، والسياق لمسلم."},{"num":9817,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ أَنَّ عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ خَطَبَ بِالْجَابِيَةِ، فَقَالَ: قَامَ فِينَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَقَامِي فِيكُمْ، فَقَالَ: اسْتَوْصُوا بِأَصْحَابِي خَيْرًا، ثُمَّ الَّذِينَ يَلُونَهُمْ، ثُمَّ الَّذِينَ يَلُونَهُمْ، ثُمَّ يَفْشُو الْكَذِبُ حَتَّى إِنَّ الرَّجُلَ لَيَبْتَدِئُ بِالشَّهَادَةِ قَبْلَ أَنْ يُسْأَلَهَا، فَمَنْ أَرَادَ مِنْكُمْ بَحْبَحَةَ الْجَنَّةِ فَلْيَلْزَمُ الْجَمَاعَةَ، فَإِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ مَعَ الْوَاحِدِ، وَهُوَ مِنَ الِاثْنَيْنِ أَبْعَدُ، لَا يَخْلُوَنَّ أَحَدُكُمْ بِامْرَأَةٍ، فَإِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ ثَالِثُهُمَا، وَمَنْ سَرَّتْهُ حَسَنَتُهُ وَسَاءَتْهُ سَيِّئَتُهُ، فَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (114)، وابن حبان (7254)، والحاكم (387) كلهم من طريق عبد الله بن المبارك، أنا محمد بن سوقة، عن عبد الله بن دينار، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في انخرام قرن الصحابة بتمام مائة عام بعد النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (114), Ibn Ḥibbān (7254), and al-Ḥākim in al-Mustadrak (387).","chapter_en":"Reports That the Generation of the Companions Would Come to an End One Hundred Years After the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb delivered a sermon at al-Jābiyah and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once stood among us just as I now stand among you and said: “Treat my Companions well, then those who follow them, and then those who follow them. Afterward, lying will become widespread, until a man will volunteer testimony before being asked to give it. Whoever among you desires the spacious central region of Paradise must adhere to the united community, for Satan is with the solitary person and is farther away from two. None of you must be alone with a woman, for Satan will be their third. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and distressed by his evil deed is a believer.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",17],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (114)، وابن حبان (7254)، والحاكم في المستدرك (387)."},{"num":9818,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لاَ تَسُبُّوا أَصْحَابِي، فَلَوْ أَنَّ أَحَدَكُمْ أَنْفَقَ مِثْلَ أُحُدٍ ذَهَبًا مَا بَلَغَ مُدَّ أَحَدِهِمْ وَلاَ نَصِيفَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3673)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2541) كلاهما من حديث الأعمش قال: سمعت ذكوان يحدث عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب تحريم سبِّ الصحابة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3673) and Muslim (2541).","chapter_en":"The Prohibition of Reviling the Companions","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not revile my Companions. If one of you were to spend gold equal to Mount Uḥud, it would not equal even one mudd given by one of them, nor even half of it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",18],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3673)، ومسلم (2541)."},{"num":9819,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدَ اللهِ بْنَ بُسْرٍ قال: سمعت رسول الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: طُوبَى لِمَنْ رَآنِي، وَطُوبَى لِمَنْ آمَنَ بِي وَلَمْ يَرَنِي، وَطُوبَى لَهُ وَحُسْنُ مَآبٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه يعقوب بن سفيان في المعرفة والتاريخ (2/351) عن آدم بن أبي أياس-والضياء في المختارة (9/98-99) من وجه آخر عن آدم، ومن رواية داود بن رُشيد – كلاهما عن بقية، ثنا محمد بن عبد الرحمن اليحصبي، سمعت عبدالله بن بسر فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب تحريم سبِّ الصحابة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān in al-Maʿrifah wa-al-Tārīkh (2/351) and al-Ḍiyāʾ in al-Mukhtārah (9/98–99).","chapter_en":"The Prohibition of Reviling the Companions","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Busr reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Glad tidings to the one who saw me. Glad tidings to the one who believed in me without seeing me. Glad tidings are his, and an excellent final abode.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",19],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه يعقوب بن سفيان في المعرفة والتاريخ (2/351)، والضياء في المختارة (86)."},{"num":9820,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، قَالَ: ذَكَرَ أَصْحَابُ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَالِكَ بْنَ الدُّخْشُمِ عِنْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَوَقَعُوا فِيهِ، وَشَتَمُوهُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: دَعُوا لِي أَصْحَابِي فَقَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّهُ كَهْفُ الْمُنَافِقِينَ وَمَلْجَؤُهُمُ الَّذِي يَلْجَؤُونَ إِلَيْهِ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَلَيْسَ يَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، وَأَنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ؟ قَالُوا: بَلَى، وَلَا خَيْرَ فِي شَهَادَتِهِ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا يَشْهَدُ بِهَا عَبْدٌ صَادِقًا مِنْ قَلْبِهِ، ثُمَّ يَمُوتُ عَلَى ذَلِكَ، إِلَّا حَرَّمَهُ اللَّهُ عَلَى النَّارِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (10877)، والبزار في مسنده (7221) من حديث آدم بن أبي إياس، ثنا شيبان، عن قتادة، عن أنس قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تحريم سبِّ الصحابة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (10877) and al-Bazzār in his Musnad (7221). This is al-Nasāʾī’s wording. Al-Bazzār’s wording is abbreviated and contains:","chapter_en":"The Prohibition of Reviling the Companions","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik reported: The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ mentioned Mālik ibn al-Dukhshum in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and began speaking against and insulting him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Leave my Companions alone for my sake.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, he is the refuge of the hypocrites and the shelter to which they resort.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Does he not testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?” They replied: “Yes, but there is no good in his testimony.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No servant sincerely testifies to that from his heart and then dies upon it except that Allah makes the Fire forbidden for him.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["“They said, ‘He is the leader of the hypocrites.’ The Prophet ﷺ replied, ‘Leave my Companions alone for my sake. Do not revile my Companions.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",20],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (10877)، والبزار في مسنده (7221). واللفظ للنسائي، ولفظ البزار مختصر، وفيه: «فقالوا: إنه رأس المنافقين، فقال النبي ﷺ: دعوا لي أصحابي، لا تسبوا أصحابي»."},{"num":9821,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ قَالَ: إِنِّي سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ:  إِنَّ خَيْرَ التَّابِعِينَ رَجُلٌ يُقَالُ لَهُ: أُوَيْسٌ، وَلَهُ وَالِدَةٌ، وَكَانَ بِهِ بَيَاضٌ، فَمُرُوهُ فَلْيَسْتَغْفِرْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الفضائل (2542-224) من طرق عن عفان بن مسلم، ثنا حماد –هو ابن سلمة-، عن سيعد الجريري، عن أبي نضرة، عن أسير بن جابر، عن عمر بن الخطاب قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في إطلاق النبي ﷺ لفظ «التابعين» لمن جاء بعد الصحابة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (224–2542).","chapter_en":"Reports in Which the Prophet ﷺ Applied the Term “Successors” to Those Who Came After the Companions","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل الصحبة","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtue of Companionship","part_no":49,"group_no":1,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The best of the Successors is a man called Uways. He has a mother and was afflicted with a whiteness of the skin. Ask him to seek forgiveness for you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",21],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (224-2542)."},{"num":9822,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُرْوَةَ بْنِ الزُّبَيْرِ، قَالَ: سَأَلْتُ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عَمْرٍو عَنْ أَشَدِّ، مَا صَنَعَ الْمُشْرِكُونَ بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ عُقْبَةَ بْنَ أَبِي مُعَيْطٍ جَاءَ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُوَ يُصَلِّي، فَوَضَعَ رِدَاءَهُ فِي عُنُقِهِ، فَخَنَقَهُ بِهِ خَنْقًا شَدِيدًا، فَجَاءَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ حَتَّى دَفَعَهُ عَنْهُ فَقَالَ: أَتَقْتُلُونَ رَجُلاً أَنْ يَقُولَ رَبِّيَ اللَّهُ. وَقَدْ جَاءَكُمْ بِالْبَيِّنَاتِ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3678) عن محمد بن يزيد الكوفي، ثنا الوليد، عن الأوزاعي، عن يحيى بن أبي كثير، عن محمد بن إبراهيم، عن عروة بن الزبير، قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب دفاع أبي بكر عن رسول الله ﷺ وهو بمكة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3678).","chapter_en":"Abū Bakr’s Defence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ While He Was in Makkah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr reported: I asked ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr about the harshest thing the polytheists had done to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He replied: I saw ʿUqbah ibn Abī Muʿayṭ approach the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying. He placed his cloak around his neck and strangled him severely with it. Abū Bakr came and pushed him away, saying: “Would you kill a man merely because he says, ‘My Lord is Allah,’ when he has brought you clear proofs from your Lord?” [Ghāfir: 28]"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording:","“While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying in the courtyard of the Kaʿbah, ʿUqbah ibn Abī Muʿayṭ approached, seized the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by the shoulder, twisted his garment around his neck, and strangled him severely. Abū Bakr then approached, seized ʿUqbah by the shoulder, and pushed him away from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ…”","Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4815).","Another wording recorded by him (3856) states:","“While the Prophet ﷺ was praying in the Ḥijr of the Kaʿbah…”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3678). وفي لفظ: «بينا رسول الله ﷺ يصلي بفناء الكعبة، إذا أقبل عقبة بن أبي معيط، فأخذ بمنكب رسول الله ﷺ، ولوى ثوبه في عنقه، فخنقه به خنقا شديدا، فأقبل أبو بكر، فأخذ بمنكبه، ودفع عن رسول الله ﷺ…» رواه البخاري (4815). وفي لفظ bukhari(3856): «بينا النبي ﷺ يصلي في حجر الكعبة…»."},{"num":9823,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: لَمَّا أُسْرِيَ بِالنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ الْأَقْصَى أَصْبَحَ يَتَحَدَّثُ النَّاسُ بِذَلِكَ، فَارْتَدَّ نَاسٌ فَمَنْ كَانَ آمَنُوا بِهِ، وَصَدَّقُوهُ، وَسَمِعُوا بِذَلِكَ إِلَى أَبِي بَكْرٍ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ، فَقَالُوا: هَلْ لَكَ إِلَى صَاحِبِكَ يَزْعُمُ أَنَّهُ أُسْرِيَ بِهِ اللَّيْلَةَ إِلَى بَيْتِ الْمَقْدِسِ، قَالَ: أَوَ قَالَ ذَلِكَ؟ قَالُوا: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: لَئِنْ كَانَ قَالَ ذَلِكَ لَقَدْ صَدَقَ، قَالُوا: أَوَ تُصَدِّقُهُ أَنَّهُ ذَهَبَ اللَّيْلَةَ إِلَى بَيْتِ الْمَقْدِسِ، وَجَاءَ قَبْلَ أَنْ يُصْبِحَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، إِنِّي لَأَصُدِّقُهُ فِيمَا هُوَ أَبْعَدُ مِنْ ذَلِكَ، أُصَدِّقُهُ بِخَبَرِ السَّمَاءِ فِي غَدْوَةٍ أَوْ رَوْحَةٍ، فَلِذَلِكَ سُمَيَّ أَبُو بَكْرٍ الصِّدِّيقَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الحاكم (4407) ومن طريقه البيهقي في الدلائل (382) من طريق محمد بن كثير الصنعاني قال: حدثنا معمر بن راشد، عن الزهري، عن عروة، عن عائشة فذكرته. قال الحاكم: صحيح الإسناد.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب لقب أبي بكر بالصِّدِّيق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ḥākim (4407), and through him by al-Bayhaqī in Dalā’il al-Nubuwwah (2/360–361). Al-Ḥākim said: “Its chain is authentic.”","chapter_en":"Abū Bakr’s Title, al-Ṣiddīq","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: When the Prophet ﷺ was taken by night to al-Masjid al-Aqṣā, the people began speaking about it the following morning. Some who had previously believed in and affirmed him abandoned their faith. They hurried to Abū Bakr and asked: “Have you heard about your companion? He claims that he was taken by night to Bayt al-Maqdis.” He asked: “Did he actually say that?” They replied: “Yes.” He said: “If he said it, then he has certainly spoken the truth.” They asked: “Do you truly believe him when he says that he travelled to Bayt al-Maqdis last night and returned before morning?” He replied: “Yes. I believe him concerning something even more extraordinary than that: I believe him concerning news from heaven that comes to him in the morning or evening.” For that reason, Abū Bakr was called al-Ṣiddīq—the utterly truthful affirmer."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",23],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8629],"tks":"حسن: رواه الحاكم (4407)، ومن طريقه البيهقي في الدلائل (382). قال الحاكم: صحيح الإسناد."},{"num":9824,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَةَ زوج النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَتْ: لَمْ أَعْقِلْ أَبَوَىَّ قَطُّ، إِلاَّ وَهُمَا يَدِينَانِ الدِّينَ، وَلَمْ يَمُرَّ عَلَيْنَا يَوْمٌ إِلاَّ يَأْتِينَا فِيهِ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ طَرَفَىِ النَّهَارِ بُكْرَةً وَعَشِيَّةً، فَلَمَّا ابْتُلِيَ الْمُسْلِمُونَ خَرَجَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ مُهَاجِرًا قِبَلَ الْحَبَشَةِ، حَتَّى إِذَا بَلَغَ بَرْكَ الْغِمَادِ لَقِيَهُ ابْنُ الدَّغِنَةِ ـ وَهْوَ سَيِّدُ الْقَارَةِ ـ فَقَالَ: أَيْنَ تُرِيدُ يَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ؟ فَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: أَخْرَجَنِي قَوْمِي، فَأَنَا أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَسِيحَ فِي الأَرْضِ، فَأَعْبُدَ رَبِّي. قَالَ ابْنُ الدَّغِنَةِ: إِنَّ مِثْلَكَ لاَ يَخْرُجُ، وَلاَ يُخْرَجُ، فَإِنَّكَ تَكْسِبُ الْمَعْدُومَ، وَتَصِلُ الرَّحِمَ، وَتَحْمِلُ الْكَلَّ، وَتَقْرِي الضَّيْفَ، وَتُعِينُ عَلَى نَوَائِبِ الْحَقِّ، وَأَنَا لَكَ جَارٌ، فَارْجِعْ فَاعْبُدْ رَبَّكَ بِبِلاَدِكَ. فَارْتَحَلَ ابْنُ الدَّغِنَةِ، فَرَجَعَ مَعَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ، فَطَافَ فِي أَشْرَافِ كُفَّارِ قُرَيْشٍ، فَقَالَ لَهُمْ: إِنَّ أَبَا بَكْرٍ لاَ يَخْرُجُ مِثْلُهُ، وَلاَ يُخْرَجُ، أَتُخْرِجُونَ رَجُلاً يُكْسِبُ الْمَعْدُومَ، وَيَصِلُ الرَّحِمَ، وَيَحْمِلُ الْكَلَّ، وَيَقْرِي الضَّيْفَ، وَيُعِينُ عَلَى نَوَائِبِ الْحَقِّ. فَأَنْفَذَتْ قُرَيْشٌ جِوَارَ ابْنِ الدَّغِنَةِ وَآمَنُوا أَبَا بَكْرٍ وَقَالُوا لاِبْنِ الدَّغِنَةِ مُرْ أَبَا بَكْرٍ فَلْيَعْبُدْ رَبَّهُ فِي دَارِهِ، فَلْيُصَلِّ وَلْيَقْرَأْ مَا شَاءَ، وَلاَ يُؤْذِينَا بِذَلِكَ، وَلاَ يَسْتَعْلِنْ بِهِ، فَإِنَّا قَدْ خَشِينَا أَنْ يَفْتِنَ أَبْنَاءَنَا وَنِسَاءَنَا. قَالَ ذَلِكَ ابْنُ الدَّغِنَةِ لأَبِي بَكْرٍ، فَطَفِقَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ يَعْبُدُ رَبَّهُ فِي دَارِهِ، وَلاَ يَسْتَعْلِنُ بِالصَّلاَةِ وَلاَ الْقِرَاءَةِ فِي غَيْرِ دَارِهِ، ثُمَّ بَدَا لأَبِي بَكْرٍ فَابْتَنَى مَسْجِدًا بِفِنَاءِ دَارِهِ، وَبَرَزَ فَكَانَ يُصَلِّي فِيهِ، وَيَقْرَأُ الْقُرْآنَ، فَيَتَقَصَّفُ عَلَيْهِ نِسَاءُ الْمُشْرِكِينَ وَأَبْنَاؤُهُمْ، يَعْجَبُونَ وَيَنْظُرُونَ إِلَيْهِ، وَكَانَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ رَجُلاً بَكَّاءً لاَ يَمْلِكُ دَمْعَهُ حِينَ يَقْرَأُ الْقُرْآنَ، فَأَفْزَعَ ذَلِكَ أَشْرَافَ قُرَيْشٍ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ، فَأَرْسَلُوا إِلَى ابْنِ الدَّغِنَةِ فَقَدِمَ عَلَيْهِمْ، فَقَالُوا لَهُ إِنَّا كُنَّا أَجَرْنَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ عَلَى أَنْ يَعْبُدَ رَبَّهُ فِي دَارِهِ، وَإِنَّهُ جَاوَزَ ذَلِكَ، فَابْتَنَى مَسْجِدًا بِفِنَاءِ دَارِهِ، وَأَعْلَنَ الصَّلاَةَ وَالْقِرَاءَةَ، وَقَدْ خَشِينَا أَنْ يَفْتِنَ أَبْنَاءَنَا وَنِسَاءَنَا، فَأْتِهِ فَإِنْ أَحَبَّ أَنْ يَقْتَصِرَ عَلَى أَنْ يَعْبُدَ رَبَّهُ فِي دَارِهِ فَعَلَ، وَإِنْ أَبَى إِلاَّ أَنْ يُعْلِنَ ذَلِكَ فَسَلْهُ أَنْ يَرُدَّ إِلَيْكَ ذِمَّتَكَ، فَإِنَّا كَرِهْنَا أَنْ نُخْفِرَكَ، وَلَسْنَا مُقِرِّينَ لأَبِي بَكْرٍ الاِسْتِعْلاَنَ.","قالت عائشة: فأتى ابن الدغنة أبا بكر فقال: قد علمت الذي عقدت لك عليه، فإما أن تقتصر على ذلك، وإما أن ترد إلي ذمتي، فإني لا أحب أن تسمع العرب أني أخفرت في رجل عقدت له.قال أبو بكر: فإني أرد إليك جوارك، وأرضى بجوار الله،- ورسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يومئذ بمكة- فقال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: قد أريت دار هجرتكم، رأيت سبخة ذات نخل بين لابتين وهما الحرتان.فهاجر من هاجر قِبل المدينة حين ذكر ذلك رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، ورجع إلى المدينة بعض من كان هاجر إلى أرض الحبشة، وتجهز أبو بكر مهاجرا، فقال له رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: على رسلك، فإني أرجو أن يؤذن لي قال أبو بكر: هل ترجو ذلك بأبي أنت؟ قال: نعم فحبس أبو بكر نفسه على رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم ليصحبه، وعلف راحلتين كانتا عنده ورق السمر أربعة أشهر."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الكفالة (2297) عن يحيى بن بكير، حدثنا الليث، عن عُقيل، قال ابن شهاب: فأخبرني عروة بن الزبير أن عائشة زوج النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قالت.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ابن الدغنة سيد القارة يصف أبا بكر كما وصفت خديجة النبي ﷺ لما بُعث، فتواردا فيهما على نعت واحد من غير أن يتواطآ على ذلك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2297).","chapter_en":"Ibn al-Dughunnah, the Chief of al-Qārah, Describes Abū Bakr as Khadījah Had Described the Prophet ﷺ When He Was Commissioned—Both Describing Them with the Same Qualities Without Prior Agreement","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reported: For as long as I could remember, I had always known my parents to practise the religion, and not a day passed without the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visiting us at both ends of the day, morning and evening. When the Muslims were subjected to persecution, Abū Bakr set out as an emigrant toward Abyssinia. When he reached Bark al-Ghimād, he met Ibn al-Dughunnah, the chief of al-Qārah. Ibn al-Dughunnah asked: “Where are you going, Abū Bakr?” Abū Bakr replied: “My people have driven me out, so I intend to travel throughout the earth and worship my Lord.” Ibn al-Dughunnah said: “A man such as you neither leaves nor should be driven out. You provide for the destitute, maintain ties of kinship, support those burdened with responsibilities, honour guests and assist people when calamities befall them in the cause of truth. I grant you my protection. Return and worship your Lord in your own land.” Ibn al-Dughunnah then travelled back with Abū Bakr. He went around to the prominent disbelievers of Quraysh and said: “A man such as Abū Bakr neither leaves nor should be driven out. Would you expel a man who provides for the destitute, maintains ties of kinship, supports those burdened with responsibilities, honours guests and assists people when calamities befall them in the cause of truth?” Quraysh accepted Ibn al-Dughunnah’s protection and guaranteed Abū Bakr’s safety. They said to Ibn al-Dughunnah: “Tell Abū Bakr to worship his Lord inside his house. Let him pray and recite whatever he wishes, but he must not trouble us with it or practise it publicly, for we fear that he may tempt our sons and women away from their religion.” Ibn al-Dughunnah conveyed this to Abū Bakr. Abū Bakr therefore began worshipping his Lord within his house and did not perform his prayers or recite publicly outside it. Later, however, Abū Bakr decided to build a place of prayer in the courtyard of his house. He came out and began praying and reciting the Qur’an there. The women and children of the polytheists began crowding around him, marvelling at him and watching him. Abū Bakr was a man who wept profusely and could not restrain his tears whenever he recited the Qur’an. This alarmed the polytheist leaders of Quraysh, so they sent for Ibn al-Dughunnah. When he came to them, they said: “We granted Abū Bakr protection on the condition that he worship his Lord within his house, but he has gone beyond that. He has built a place of prayer in his courtyard and publicly performs his prayers and recites the Qur’an. We fear that he may tempt our sons and women away from their religion. Go to him. If he is willing to restrict himself to worshipping his Lord inside his house, he may do so. But if he insists on practising publicly, ask him to return your protection to you. We dislike violating the protection you have granted, but we will not allow Abū Bakr to worship publicly.” ʿĀ’ishah continued: Ibn al-Dughunnah went to Abū Bakr and said: “You know the terms upon which I made my agreement with you. Either restrict yourself to those terms or return my protection to me, for I do not want the Arabs to hear that the protection I granted to a man was violated.” Abū Bakr replied: “I return your protection to you and am content with the protection of Allah.” At that time, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was still in Makkah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “I have been shown the land to which you will emigrate. I saw a saline tract containing date palms between two fields of black volcanic rock.”","These were the two lava plains. After the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned this, those who emigrated went toward Madinah, and some who had emigrated to Abyssinia returned to Madinah. Abū Bakr prepared to emigrate, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told him: “Wait, for I hope that permission will be granted to me.” Abū Bakr asked: “Do you truly hope for that—may my father be sacrificed for you?” He replied: “Yes.” Abū Bakr therefore remained behind for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that he could accompany him. For four months, he fed two riding camels that he owned with the leaves of the samur tree."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",24],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (2297)."},{"num":9825,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن الْبَرَاءِ بْنِ عَازِبٍ يَقُولُ: جَاءَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ إِلَى أَبِي فِي مَنْزِلِهِ، فَاشْتَرَى مِنْهُ رَحْلاً، فَقَالَ لِعَازِبٍ: ابْعَثِ ابْنَكَ يَحْمِلْهُ مَعِي. قَالَ فَحَمَلْتُهُ مَعَهُ، وَخَرَجَ أَبِي يَنْتَقِدُ ثَمَنَهُ، فَقَالَ لَهُ أَبِي: يَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ حَدِّثْنِي كَيْفَ صَنَعْتُمَا حِينَ سَرَيْتَ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، أَسْرَيْنَا لَيْلَتَنَا، وَمِنَ الْغَدِ حَتَّى قَامَ قَائِمُ الظَّهِيرَةِ، وَخَلاَ الطَّرِيقُ لاَ يَمُرُّ فِيهِ أَحَدٌ، فَرُفِعَتْ لَنَا صَخْرَةٌ طَوِيلَةٌ، لَهَا ظِلٌّ لَمْ تَأْتِ عَلَيْهِ الشَّمْسُ، فَنَزَلْنَا عِنْدَهُ، وَسَوَّيْتُ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَكَانًا بِيَدِي يَنَامُ عَلَيْهِ، وَبَسَطْتُ فِيهِ فَرْوَةً، وَقُلْتُ: نَمْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَأَنَا أَنْفُضُ لَكَ مَا حَوْلَكَ. فَنَامَ، وَخَرَجْتُ أَنْفُضُ مَا حَوْلَهُ، فَإِذَا أَنَا بِرَاعٍ مُقْبِلٍ بِغَنَمِهِ إِلَى الصَّخْرَةِ، يُرِيدُ مِنْهَا مِثْلَ الَّذِي أَرَدْنَا، فَقُلْتُ: لِمَنْ أَنْتَ يَا غُلاَمُ؟ فَقَالَ لِرَجُلٍ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْمَدِينَةِ أَوْ مَكَّةَ. قُلْتُ أَفِي غَنَمِكَ لَبَنٌ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمُ. قُلْتُ أَفَتَحْلُبُ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. فَأَخَذَ شَاةً. فَقُلْتُ: انْفُضِ الضَّرْعَ مِنَ التُّرَابِ وَالشَّعَرِ وَالْقَذَى. قَالَ: فَرَأَيْتُ الْبَرَاءَ يَضْرِبُ إِحْدَى يَدَيْهِ عَلَى الأُخْرَى يَنْفُضُ، فَحَلَبَ فِي قَعْبٍ كُثْبَةً مِنْ لَبَنٍ، وَمَعِي إِدَاوَةٌ حَمَلْتُهَا لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَرْتَوِي مِنْهَا، يَشْرَبُ وَيَتَوَضَّأُ، فَأَتَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَكَرِهْتُ أَنْ أُوقِظَهُ، فَوَافَقْتُهُ حِينَ اسْتَيْقَظَ، فَصَبَبْتُ مِنَ الْمَاءِ عَلَى اللَّبَنِ حَتَّى بَرَدَ أَسْفَلُهُ، فَقُلْتُ: اشْرَبْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ـ قَالَ ـ فَشَرِبَ، حَتَّى رَضِيتُ ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلَمْ يَأْنِ لِلرَّحِيلِ. قُلْتُ بَلَى ـ قَالَ ـ فَارْتَحَلْنَا بَعْدَ مَا مَالَتِ الشَّمْشُ، وَاتَّبَعَنَا سُرَاقَةُ بْنُ مَالِكٍ، فَقُلْتُ: أُتِينَا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. فَقَالَ لاَ تَحْزَنْ، إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَنَا. فَدَعَا عَلَيْهِ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَارْتَطَمَتْ بِهِ فَرَسُهُ إِلَى بَطْنِهَا ـ أُرَى فِي جَلَدٍ مِنَ الأَرْضِ، شَكَّ زُهَيْرٌ ـ فَقَالَ: إِنِّي أُرَاكُمَا قَدْ دَعَوْتُمَا عَلَىَّ، فَادْعُوَا لِي، فَاللَّهُ لَكُمَا أَنْ أَرُدَّ عَنْكُمَا الطَّلَبَ. فَدَعَا لَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَنَجَا، فَجَعَلَ لاَ يَلْقَى أَحَدًا إِلاَّ قَالَ: كَفَيْتُكُمْ مَا هُنَا. فَلاَ يَلْقَى أَحَدًا إِلاَّ رَدَّهُ. قَالَ وَوَفَى لَنَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المناقب (3615)، ومسلم في الزهد والرقائق (2009-75) كلاهما من طريق زهير بن معاوية، ثنا أبو إسحاق، قال: سمعت البراء بن عازب يقول: فذكره.وهذا لفظ البخاري، ولفظ مسلم نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في هجرة أبي بكر مع النبي ﷺ إلى المدينة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3615) and Muslim (75–2009).","chapter_en":"Abū Bakr’s Emigration to Madinah with the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib reported: Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, came to my father at his home and purchased a camel saddle from him. He said to ʿĀzib: “Send your son to carry it with me.” So I carried it with him, while my father went out to receive its price. My father said to him: “Abū Bakr, tell me what you and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did when you travelled by night.” He replied: “Yes. We travelled throughout that night and the following day until the midday heat became intense and the road became deserted, with no one passing along it. A tall rock appeared before us with a shaded area untouched by the sun, so we stopped beside it. With my own hands, I levelled a place for the Prophet ﷺ to sleep and spread a hide there. I said, ‘Sleep, O Messenger of Allah, while I scout the area around you.’ “He fell asleep, and I went out to scout the surroundings. I then saw a shepherd approaching the rock with his sheep, seeking the same shade that we had sought. I asked him, ‘Young man, to whom do you belong?’ “He named a man from Madinah or Makkah. I asked, ‘Do your sheep have any milk?’ “He replied, ‘Yes.’ “I asked, ‘Will you milk one?’ “He replied, ‘Yes.’ “He took hold of a ewe, and I told him, ‘Clean the udder of dust, hair and dirt.’” Al-Barāʾ demonstrated by striking one hand against the other as though dusting it off. “He milked a quantity of milk into a wooden bowl. I had with me a leather vessel that I had carried for the Prophet ﷺ so that he could drink from it and perform ablution. I returned to the Prophet ﷺ and disliked waking him, but I arrived just as he awoke. I poured water over the milk until its lower portion became cool and said, ‘Drink, O Messenger of Allah.’” He drank until I was satisfied, and then asked: “Is it not time to depart?” I replied: “Yes.” We resumed our journey after the sun had passed its zenith. Surāqah ibn Mālik pursued us, so I said: “O Messenger of Allah, they have reached us!” He replied: “Do not grieve; indeed, Allah is with us.” The Prophet ﷺ supplicated against Surāqah, and his horse sank into the ground up to its belly—or so I believe—in a solid patch of earth. Zuhayr was uncertain about this wording. Surāqah said: “I believe that you have supplicated against me. Supplicate for me, and I swear by Allah that I will turn the pursuers away from you.” The Prophet ﷺ supplicated for him, and he was freed. Thereafter, whenever Surāqah met anyone, he would say: “I have taken care of this area for you.” He turned back everyone he encountered. Al-Barāʾ said: “He fulfilled his promise to us.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",25],"full":1,"rep":[9707],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3615)، ومسلم (75-2009)."},{"num":9826,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، عَنْ أَبِي بَكْرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قُلْتُ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَنَا فِي الْغَارِ: لَوْ أَنَّ أَحَدَهُمْ نَظَرَ تَحْتَ قَدَمَيْهِ لأَبْصَرَنَا. فَقَالَ: مَا ظَنُّكَ يَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ بِاثْنَيْنِ اللَّهُ ثَالِثُهُمَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3653)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2381) كلاهما من طريق همام، ثنا ثابت، ثنا أنس بن مالك، أن أبا بكر الصديق حدثه قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في هجرة أبي بكر مع النبي ﷺ إلى المدينة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3653) and Muslim (2381). This is al-Bukhārī’s wording. Muslim added at its beginning:","chapter_en":"Abū Bakr’s Emigration to Madinah with the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported from Abū Bakr that he said: While I was in the cave with the Prophet ﷺ, I said: “If one of them were to look beneath his feet, he would see us.” He replied: “What do you think, Abū Bakr, of two whose third is Allah?”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["“I looked at the feet of the polytheists above our heads while we were in the cave and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, if one of them…’”","He then mentioned the remainder of the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",26],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3653)، ومسلم (2381). وهذا لفظ البخاري، وزاد مسلم في أوله: نظرت إلى أقدام المشركين على رؤوسنا ونحن في الغار، فقلت: يا رسول الله، لو أن أحدهم… فذكره."},{"num":9827,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ، قَالَ: خَطَبَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ خَيَّرَ عَبْدًا بَيْنَ الدُّنْيَا وَبَيْنَ مَا عِنْدَهُ، فَاخْتَارَ مَا عِنْدَ اللَّهِ. فَبَكَى أَبُو بَكْرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ، فَقُلْتُ فِي نَفْسِي: مَا يُبْكِي هَذَا الشَّيْخَ؟ إِنْ يَكُنِ اللَّهُ خَيَّرَ عَبْدًا بَيْنَ الدُّنْيَا وَبَيْنَ مَا عِنْدَهُ، فَاخْتَارَ مَا عِنْدَ اللَّهِ، فَكَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ هُوَ الْعَبْدَ، وَكَانَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ أَعْلَمَنَا. قَالَ: يَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ، لاَ تَبْكِ، إِنَّ أَمَنَّ النَّاسِ عَلَىَّ فِي صُحْبَتِهِ وَمَالِهِ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، وَلَوْ كُنْتُ مُتَّخِذًا خَلِيلاً مِنْ أُمَّتِي لاَتَّخَذْتُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ، وَلَكِنْ أُخُوَّةُ الإِسْلاَمِ وَمَوَدَّتُهُ، لاَ يَبْقَيَنَّ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ باب إِلاَّ سُدَّ إِلاَّ باب أَبِي بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الصلاة (466)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2382-2) كلاهما من طريق أبي النضر، عن عبيد بن حنين، عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر من أمنِّ الناس على النبي ﷺ في صحبته وماله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (466) and Muslim (2–2382).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Generous of People Toward the Prophet ﷺ in His Companionship and Wealth","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported: The Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon and said: “Allah gave one of His servants the choice between this world and what is with Him, and the servant chose what is with Allah.” Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, began to weep. I thought to myself: “Why is this elderly man weeping merely because Allah offered one of His servants the choice between this world and what is with Him, and the servant chose what is with Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ himself was that servant, and Abū Bakr was the most knowledgeable among us. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Abū Bakr, do not weep. The person who has been the most generous toward me through his companionship and wealth is Abū Bakr. If I were to take an intimate friend from among my nation, I would take Abū Bakr, but the brotherhood and affection of Islam remain. Let no doorway leading into the mosque remain except that it be closed, apart from the doorway of Abū Bakr.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",27],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (466)، ومسلم (2-2382)."},{"num":9828,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي الدَّرْدَاءِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: كُنْتُ جَالِسًا عِنْدَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِذْ أَقْبَلَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ آخِذًا بِطَرَفِ ثَوْبِهِ حَتَّى أَبْدَى عَنْ رُكْبَتِهِ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَمَّا صَاحِبُكُمْ فَقَدْ غَامَرَ. فَسَلَّمَ، وَقَالَ: إِنِّي كَانَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَ ابْنِ الْخَطَّابِ شَىْءٌ، فَأَسْرَعْتُ إِلَيْهِ، ثُمَّ نَدِمْتُ، فَسَأَلْتُهُ أَنْ يَغْفِرَ لِي، فَأَبَى عَلَىَّ، فَأَقْبَلْتُ إِلَيْكَ، فَقَالَ: يَغْفِرُ اللَّهُ لَكَ يَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ. ثَلاَثًا، ثُمَّ إِنَّ عُمَرَ نَدِمَ، فَأَتَى مَنْزِلَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ، فَسَأَلَ: أَثَمَّ أَبُو بَكْرٍ؟ فَقَالُوا: لاَ. فَأَتَى إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَسَلَّمَ، فَجَعَلَ وَجْهُ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَتَمَعَّرُ حَتَّى أَشْفَقَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَجَثَا عَلَى رُكْبَتَيْهِ، فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَاللَّهِ أَنَا كُنْتُ أَظْلَمَ، مَرَّتَيْنِ. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ بَعَثَنِي إِلَيْكُمْ فَقُلْتُمْ: كَذَبْتَ. وَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: صَدَقَ. وَوَاسَانِي بِنَفْسِهِ وَمَالِهِ، فَهَلْ أَنْتُمْ تَارِكُو لِي صَاحِبِي. مَرَّتَيْنِ فَمَا أُوذِيَ بَعْدَهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3661) عن هشام بن عمار، ثنا صدقة بن خالد، ثنا زيد بن واقد، عن بسر بن عبيد الله، عن عائذ الله أبي إدريس، عن أبي الدرداء قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر من أمنِّ الناس على النبي ﷺ في صحبته وماله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3661).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Generous of People Toward the Prophet ﷺ in His Companionship and Wealth","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū al-Dardāʾ reported: I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when Abū Bakr approached, holding up the edge of his garment so that his knee was exposed. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Your companion has certainly become involved in a serious dispute.” Abū Bakr greeted him and said: “There was a disagreement between Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and me. I spoke hastily to him, but then regretted it. I asked him to forgive me, but he refused, so I have come to you.” The Prophet ﷺ said three times: “May Allah forgive you, Abū Bakr.” Then ʿUmar regretted what had happened and went to Abū Bakr’s house. He asked: “Is Abū Bakr here?” They replied: “No.” He therefore went to the Prophet ﷺ and greeted him. The Prophet’s ﷺ face began to change with anger until Abū Bakr became fearful for ʿUmar. Abū Bakr fell to his knees and said twice: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I was more at fault.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah sent me to you, but you said, ‘You have lied,’ whereas Abū Bakr said, ‘He has spoken the truth.’ He supported me with himself and his wealth. Will you then leave my companion alone for my sake?” He repeated it twice. Thereafter, Abū Bakr was never harmed."]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording:","“There was a discussion between Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, and Abū Bakr angered ʿUmar. ʿUmar left him in anger, so Abū Bakr followed him, asking him to forgive him, but he would not do so and eventually shut his door in his face. Abū Bakr then went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ…”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",28],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3661)."},{"num":9829,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَا نَفَعَنَا مَالٌ قَطُّ مَا نَفَعَنَا مَالُ أَبِي بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الحميدي (250)، وأبو يعلى (4418)، وعبد الله بن أحمد في زوائد الفضائل لأبيه (29) كلهم من طريق سفيان (هو ابن عيينة) قال: حفظت من الزهري، عن عروة، عن عائشة فذكرته.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر من أمنِّ الناس على النبي ﷺ في صحبته وماله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Ḥumaydī (250), Abū Yaʿlā (4418), and ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad in his additions to his father’s Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (29).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Generous of People Toward the Prophet ﷺ in His Companionship and Wealth","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No person’s wealth has benefited us as much as the wealth of Abū Bakr.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",29],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الحميدي (250)، وأبو يعلى (4418)، وعبد الله بن أحمد في زوائد الفضائل لأبيه (29)."},{"num":9830,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا نَفَعَنِي مَالٌ قَطُّ مَا نَفَعَنِي مَالُ أَبِي بَكْرٍ. قَالَ: فَبَكَى أَبُو بَكْرٍ، وَقَالَ: هَلْ أَنَا وَمَالِي إِلاَّ لَكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائي في الفضائل (9)، وابن ماجه (94)، وأحمد (7446)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (6858) كلهم من طريق أبي معاوية، حدثنا الأعمش، عن أبي صالح، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر من أمنِّ الناس على النبي ﷺ في صحبته وماله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī in al-Faḍāʾil (9), Ibn Mājah (94), and Aḥmad (7446), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6858).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Generous of People Toward the Prophet ﷺ in His Companionship and Wealth","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No wealth has ever benefited me as much as the wealth of Abū Bakr.” Abū Bakr wept and said: “O Messenger of Allah, are my wealth and I not entirely at your service?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",30],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي في الفضائل (9)، وابن ماجه (94)، وأحمد (7446)، وصححه ابن حبان (6858)."},{"num":9831,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ بَعْضِ أَصْحَابِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَرَجَ فاستوى عَلَى الْمِنْبَرِ، فتشهد فَلَمَّا مَضَى تَشْهَدَهُ كَانَ أَوَّلُ كَلَامٍ تَكَلَّمَ بِهِ أَنِ اسْتَغْفَرَ لِلشُّهَدَاءِ الَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا يَوْمَ أَحَدٍ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: إِنَّ عَبْدًا مِنْ عِبَادِ اللَّهِ خُيِّرَ بَيْنَ الدُّنْيَا وَبَيْنَ مَا عِنْدَ رَبِّهِ، فَاخْتَارَ مَا عِنْدَ رَبِّهِ، ففطن لَهَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ الصِّدِّيقُ أَوَّلَ النَّاسِ فعرف إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ نَفْسَهُ، فَبَكَى أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَقَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ : عَلَى رِسْلِكَ يَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ! سُدُّوا هَذِهِ الْأَبْوَابَ الشَّوَارِعَ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ إِلَّا بَابَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ، فَإِنِّي لَا أَعْلَمُ أمرا أَفْضَلُ عِنْدِي يَدًا فِي الصحابة مِنْ أَبِي بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن سعد في الطبقات (612)، والطبراني في مسند الشاميين (3219) كلاهما من طرق عن الزهري، عن أيوب بن بشير، عن بعض أصحاب النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر من أمنِّ الناس على النبي ﷺ في صحبته وماله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Saʿd in al-Ṭabaqāt (2/228) and al-Ṭabarānī in Musnad al-Shāmiyyīn (3219).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Generous of People Toward the Prophet ﷺ in His Companionship and Wealth","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["One of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and ascended the pulpit. He recited the testimony of faith, and after completing it, the first thing he did was seek forgiveness for the martyrs who had been killed on the day of Uḥud. He then said: “One of Allah’s servants was given the choice between this world and what is with his Lord, and he chose what is with his Lord.” Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq was the first person to understand the meaning of these words. He realised that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was referring to himself, so Abū Bakr began to weep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Take it easy, Abū Bakr! Close all these doors that open into the mosque except the door of Abū Bakr, for I know of no one among the Companions whose favours toward me are greater than those of Abū Bakr.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",31],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن سعد في الطبقات (612)، والطبراني في مسند الشاميين (3219)."},{"num":9832,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن الزُّبَيْرِ قَالَ: قَالَ أَبُو قُحَافَةَ لِأَبِي بَكْرٍ: يَا بُنيَّ، إِنِّي أَرَاكَ تُعْتَقُ رِقَابًا ضِعَافًا، فَلَوْ أَنَّكَ إِذْ فَعَلْتَ مَا فَعَلْتَ أَعْتَقَتْ رِجَالًا جُلْدا يَمْنَعُونَكَ وَيَقُومُونَ دُونَكَ؟ قَالَ: فَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: يَا أَبَتِ، إِنِّي إِنَّمَا أُرِيدُ مَا أُرِيدُ لله عَزَّ وَجَلَّ، قَالَ: فيُتَحَدَّثُ مَا نَزَلَ هؤلاء الْآيَاتُ إِلَّا فِيهِ، وفيما قَالَ لَهُ أَبُوهُ: ﴿فَأَمَّا مَنْ أَعْطَى وَاتَّقَى (5) وَصَدَّقَ بِالْحُسْنَى (6)﴾ [سورة الليل: 5، 6] إِلَى قَوْلِهِ: ﴿وَمَا لِأَحَدٍ عِنْدَهُ مِنْ نِعْمَةٍ تُجْزَى (19) إِلَّا ابْتِغَاءَ وَجْهِ رَبِّهِ الْأَعْلَى (20) وَلَسَوْفَ يَرْضَى (21)﴾ [سورة الليل:٥-٢١]."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه عبد الله بن أحمد في زوائده على \"فضائل الصحابة\" لأبيه (66)، وصحّحه الحاكم (3942) كلاهما من طريق محمد بن إسحاق، حدثني محمد بن عبد الله بن أبي عتيق، عن عامر بن عبد الله بن الزبير، عن أبيه قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر من أمنِّ الناس على النبي ﷺ في صحبته وماله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad in his additions to his father’s Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (66), and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (3942).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Generous of People Toward the Prophet ﷺ in His Companionship and Wealth","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr reported: Abū Quḥāfah said to Abū Bakr: “My son, I see you freeing weak slaves. If you are going to do this, why do you not free strong men who could protect you and stand in your defence?” Abū Bakr replied: “My father, I seek through what I am doing only Allah Almighty.” It is related that these verses were revealed concerning him: “As for the one who gives and fears Allah, and believes in the finest reward…” up to His words: “No one has any favour with him for which repayment is sought, but only seeking the Countenance of his Lord, the Most High. And he will surely be pleased.” [Sūrat al-Layl: 5–21]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه عبد الله بن أحمد في زوائده على «فضائل الصحابة» لأبيه (66)، وصححه الحاكم (3942)."},{"num":9833,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنَّ مِنْ أمَنِّ النَّاسِ عليَّ فِي صُحْبَتِهِ وَمَالِهِ أَبَا بَكْرٍ، وَلَوْ كُنْتُ مُتَّخِذًا خَلِيلاً مِنْ أُمَّتِي لاَتَّخَذْتُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ إِلاَّ خُلَّةَ الإِسْلاَمِ، لاَ يَبْقَيَنَّ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ خَوْخَةٌ إِلاَّ خَوْخَةُ أَبِي بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في الموطأ (944-رواية محمد بن الحسن الشيباني) عن أبي النضر مولى عمر بن عبيد الله، عن عبيد بن حنين، عن أبي سعيد الخدري فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب لو كان للنبي ﷺ خليل لكان أبا بكر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ (944, the recension of Muḥammad al-Shaybānī), al-Bukhārī (3904), and Muslim (2–2382).","chapter_en":"Had the Prophet ﷺ Taken an Intimate Friend, It Would Have Been Abū Bakr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the people, the one who has been most generous toward me through his companionship and wealth is Abū Bakr. If I were to take an intimate friend from among my nation, I would take Abū Bakr, but there remains the intimate bond of Islam. Let no small doorway leading into the mosque remain except the doorway of Abū Bakr.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",33],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (944 -رواية محمد الشيباني)، والبخاري (3904)، ومسلم (2-2382)."},{"num":9834,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: خَرَجَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي مَرَضِهِ الَّذِي مَاتَ فِيهِ عَاصِبٌ رَأْسَهُ بِخِرْقَةٍ، فَقَعَدَ عَلَى الْمِنْبَرِ، فَحَمِدَ اللَّهَ وَأَثْنَى عَلَيْهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: إِنَّهُ لَيْسَ مِنَ النَّاسِ أَحَدٌ أَمَنَّ عَلَىَّ فِي نَفْسِهِ وَمَالِهِ مِنْ أَبِي بَكْرِ بْنِ أَبِي قُحَافَةَ، وَلَوْ كُنْتُ مُتَّخِذًا مِنَ النَّاسِ خَلِيلاً لاَتَّخَذْتُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ خَلِيلاً، وَلَكِنْ خُلَّةُ الإِسْلاَمِ أَفْضَلُ، سُدُّوا عَنِّي كُلَّ خَوْخَةٍ فِي هَذَا الْمَسْجِدِ غَيْرَ خَوْخَةِ أَبِي بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الصلاة (467) عن عبد الله بن محمد الجعفي، ثنا وهب بن جرير، ثنا أبي، سمعت يعلى بن حكيم، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لو كان للنبي ﷺ خليل لكان أبا بكر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (467). He also narrated it through another chain (3656) with the wording:","chapter_en":"Had the Prophet ﷺ Taken an Intimate Friend, It Would Have Been Abū Bakr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās reported: During the illness from which he died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out with his head bound in a piece of cloth. He sat upon the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, and then said: “There is no one among the people who has been more generous toward me with himself and his wealth than Abū Bakr ibn Abī Quḥāfah. If I were to take an intimate friend from among the people, I would take Abū Bakr as an intimate friend, but the intimate bond of Islam is better. Close every small doorway leading into this mosque except the doorway of Abū Bakr.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["“If I were to take an intimate friend from among my nation, I would take Abū Bakr, but he is my brother and companion.”","He narrated it through another chain (3657), containing:","“But the brotherhood of Islam is better.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",34],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (467). ورواه bukhari(3656) من وجه آخر بلفظ: «لو كنت متخذا من أمتي خليلا لاتخذت أبا بكر، ولكن أخي وصاحبي». ورواه bukhari(3657) من وجه آخر وفيه: «ولكن أخوة الإسلام أفضل»."},{"num":9835,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ أَبِي مُلَيْكَةَ، قَالَ: كَتَبَ أَهْلُ الْكُوفَةِ إِلَى ابْنِ الزُّبَيْرِ فِي الْجَدِّ. فَقَالَ: أَمَّا الَّذِي قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَوْ كُنْتُ مُتَّخِذًا مِنْ هَذِهِ الأُمَّةِ خَلِيلاً لاَتَّخَذْتُهُ. أَنْزَلَهُ أَبًا، يَعْنِي أَبَا بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3658) عن سليمان بن حرب، أنا حماد بن زيد، عن أيوب، عن عبد الله بن أبي مليكة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لو كان للنبي ﷺ خليل لكان أبا بكر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3658).","chapter_en":"Had the Prophet ﷺ Taken an Intimate Friend, It Would Have Been Abū Bakr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Mulaykah reported: The people of Kūfah wrote to Ibn al-Zubayr regarding the grandfather’s share of inheritance. He replied: “As for the one about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘If I were to take an intimate friend from this nation, I would take him,’ he treated him as a father.” He meant Abū Bakr."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",35],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3658)."},{"num":9836,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن مَسْعُودٍ، يُحَدِّثُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ:  لَوْ كُنْتُ مُتَّخِذًا خَلِيلًا لَاتَّخَذْتُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ خَلِيلًا، وَلَكِنَّهُ أَخِي وَصَاحِبِي، وَقَدِ اتَّخَذَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ صَاحِبَكُمْ خَلِيلًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2383-3) عن محمد بن بشار العبدي، ثنا محمد بن جعفر، ثنا شعبة، عن إسماعيل بن رجاء، سمعت عبد الله بن أبي الهذيل، عن أبي الأحوص، سمعت عبد الله بن مسعود فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لو كان للنبي ﷺ خليل لكان أبا بكر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (3–2383).","chapter_en":"Had the Prophet ﷺ Taken an Intimate Friend, It Would Have Been Abū Bakr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If I were to take an intimate friend, I would take Abū Bakr as an intimate friend. Rather, he is my brother and companion, and Allah has taken your companion as an intimate friend.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording:","“If I were to take an intimate friend from among the people of the earth, I would take Ibn Abī Quḥāfah as an intimate friend, but your companion is the intimate friend of Allah.”","Narrated by Muslim (6–2383).","In another wording:","“Indeed, I renounce before every close companion the intimacy of his companionship. If I were to take an intimate friend, I would take Abū Bakr as an intimate friend. Indeed, your companion is the intimate friend of Allah.”","Narrated by Muslim (7–2383)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",36],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (3-2383)."},{"num":9837,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جندب بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَبْلَ أَنْ يَمُوتَ بِخَمْسٍ وَهُوَ يَقُولُ: إِنِّي أَبْرَأُ إِلَى اللَّهِ أَنْ يَكُونَ لِي مِنْكُمْ خَلِيلٌ، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ تَعَالَى قَدِ اتَّخَذَنِي خَلِيلًا، كَمَا اتَّخَذَ إِبْرَاهِيمَ خَلِيلًا، وَلَوْ كُنْتُ مُتَّخِذًا مِنْ أُمَّتِي خَلِيلًا لَاتَّخَذْتُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ خَلِيلًا... الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (532-23) من طريق عبد الله بن عمرو، عن زيد بن أبي أنيسة، عن عمرو بن مرة، عن عبد الله بن الحارث النجراني قال: حدثني جندب قال: سمعت النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لو كان للنبي ﷺ خليل لكان أبا بكر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (23–532).","chapter_en":"Had the Prophet ﷺ Taken an Intimate Friend, It Would Have Been Abū Bakr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jundab ibn ʿAbdullāh reported: I heard the Prophet ﷺ, five days before his death, saying: “I declare before Allah that I have no intimate friend from among you, for Allah Most High has taken me as an intimate friend just as He took Abraham as an intimate friend. If I were to take an intimate friend from among my nation, I would take Abū Bakr as an intimate friend…” to the end of the hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",37],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (23-532)."},{"num":9838,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: سُدُّوا عَنِّي كُلَّ بَابٍ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ إِلا بَابَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ، وَلَوْ كُنْتُ مُتَّخِذًا خَلِيلا لاتَّخَذْتُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ خَلِيلا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار (6557)، والطبراني في مسند الشاميين (154) كلاهما من طريق عبد الرحمن بن ثابت بن ثوبان، عن حميد الطويل، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب لو كان للنبي ﷺ خليل لكان أبا بكر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār (6557) and al-Ṭabarānī in Musnad al-Shāmiyyīn (154).","chapter_en":"Had the Prophet ﷺ Taken an Intimate Friend, It Would Have Been Abū Bakr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Close every doorway leading into the mosque except the doorway of Abū Bakr. If I were to take an intimate friend, I would take Abū Bakr as an intimate friend.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",38],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار (6557)، والطبراني في مسند الشاميين (154)."},{"num":9839,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جُبَيْرِ بْنِ مُطْعِمٍ عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: أَتَتِ امْرَأَةٌ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَمَرَهَا أَنْ تَرْجِعَ إِلَيْهِ. قَالَتْ: أَرَأَيْتَ إِنْ جِئْتُ وَلَمْ أَجِدْكَ؟، كَأَنَّهَا تَقُولُ: الْمَوْتَ. قَالَ عَلَيْهِ السَّلاَمُ إِنْ لَمْ تَجِدِينِي فَأْتِي أَبَا بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3659) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2386) كلاهما من طريق إبراهيم بن سعد، أخبرني أبي، عن محمد بن جبير بن مطعم، عن أبيه قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ وأفضلهم بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3659) and Muslim (2386).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Beloved of People to the Prophet ﷺ and the Best of Them After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim reported: A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he instructed her to return to him. She asked: “What if I return and do not find you?” It was as though she meant his death. He ﷺ replied: “If you do not find me, then go to Abū Bakr.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",39],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3659)، ومسلم (2386)."},{"num":9840,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَمَّارِ بن يَاسِرٍ رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَمَا مَعَهُ إِلاَّ خَمْسَةُ أَعْبُدٍ، وَامْرَأَتَانِ، وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3660) عن أحمد بن أبي الطيب، ثنا إسماعيل بن أبي مجالد، ثنا بيان بن بشر، عن وبرة بن عبد الرحمن، عن همام قال: سمعت عمارا يقول: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ وأفضلهم بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3660).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Beloved of People to the Prophet ﷺ and the Best of Them After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir reported: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at a time when no one was with him except five slaves, two women and Abū Bakr."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",40],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3660)."},{"num":9841,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ أن رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ فِي مَرَضِهِ: مُرُوا أَبَا بَكْرٍ يُصَلِّي بِالنَّاسِ، قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: قُلْتُ: إِنَّ أَبَا بَكْرٍ إِذَا قَامَ فِي مَقَامِكَ لَمْ يُسْمِعِ النَّاسَ مِنَ الْبُكَاءِ، فَمُرْ عُمَرَ فَلْيُصَلِّ، فَقَالَ: مُرُوا أَبَا بَكْرٍ فَلْيُصَلِّ لِلنَّاسِ، قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ لِحَفْصَةَ: قُولِي لَهُ: إِنَّ أَبَا بَكْرٍ إِذَا قَامَ فِي مَقَامِكَ لَمْ يُسْمِعِ النَّاسَ مِنَ الْبُكَاءِ، فَمُرْ عُمَرَ فَلْيُصَلِّ لِلنَّاسِ، فَفَعَلَتْ حَفْصَةُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَهْ، إِنَّكُنَّ لأَنْتُنَّ صَوَاحِبُ يُوسُفَ، مُرُوا أَبَا بَكْرٍ فَلْيُصَلِّ لِلنَّاسِ.قَالَتْ حَفْصَةُ لِعَائِشَةَ: مَا كُنْتُ لأُصِيبَ مِنْكِ خَيْرًا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في كتاب قصر الصلاة في السفر (89) عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.ومن طريقه رواه البخاري في الأذان (679).","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ وأفضلهم بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik (89), al-Bukhārī (679) and Muslim (79–418).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Beloved of People to the Prophet ﷺ and the Best of Them After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported that during his illness, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” ʿĀ’ishah said: “I said, ‘When Abū Bakr stands in your place, the people will be unable to hear him because of his weeping. Tell ʿUmar to lead the prayer instead.’” He said: “Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” ʿĀ’ishah then said to Ḥafṣah: “Tell him, ‘When Abū Bakr stands in your place, the people will be unable to hear him because of his weeping. Tell ʿUmar to lead the people in prayer instead.’” Ḥafṣah did so, whereupon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Enough! You are indeed like the women associated with Joseph. Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” Ḥafṣah later said to ʿĀ’ishah: “I have never received any good from you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",41],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (89)، والبخاري (679)، ومسلم (79-418)."},{"num":9842,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى، قَالَ: مَرِضَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَاشْتَدَّ مَرَضُهُ فَقَالَ: مُرُوا أَبَا بَكْرٍ فَلْيُصَلِّ بِالنَّاسِ. قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: إِنَّهُ رَجُلٌ رَقِيقٌ، إِذَا قَامَ مَقَامَكَ لَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ أَنْ يُصَلِّيَ بِالنَّاسِ. قَالَ: مُرُوا أَبَا بَكْرٍ فَلْيُصَلِّ بِالنَّاسِ فَعَادَتْ فَقَالَ: مُرِي أَبَا بَكْرٍ فَلْيُصَلِّ بِالنَّاسِ، فَإِنَّكُنَّ صَوَاحِبُ يُوسُفَ. فَأَتَاهُ الرَّسُولُ فَصَلَّى بِالنَّاسِ فِي حَيَاةِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الأذان (678)، ومسلم في كتاب الصلاة (101:420) كلاهما من طريق حسين بن علي، عن زائدة، عن عبد الملك بن عمير، عن أبي بردة، عن أبي موسى فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ وأفضلهم بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (678) and Muslim (101–420).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Beloved of People to the Prophet ﷺ and the Best of Them After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī reported: The Prophet ﷺ became ill, and his illness grew severe. He said: “Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” ʿĀ’ishah said: “He is a tenderhearted man. If he stands in your place, he will be unable to lead the people in prayer.” He said: “Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” She repeated her objection, so he said: “Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer, for you are like the women associated with Joseph.” The messenger went to Abū Bakr, and he led the people in prayer during the lifetime of the Prophet ﷺ."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",42],"full":1,"rep":[2236,8408],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (678)، ومسلم (101:420)."},{"num":9843,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عُمَرَ قَالَ: لَمَّا اشْتَدَّ بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَجَعُهُ قِيلَ لَهُ فِي الصَّلاَةِ فَقَالَ: مُرُوا أَبَا بَكْرٍ فَلْيُصَلِّ بِالنَّاسِ.قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: إِنَّ أَبَا بَكْرٍ رَجُلٌ رَقِيقٌ، إِذَا قَرَأَ غَلَبَهُ الْبُكَاءُ، قَالَ: مُرُوهُ فَيُصَلِّي فَعَاوَدَتْهُ، قَالَ: مُرُوهُ فَيُصَلِّي، إِنَّكُنَّ صَوَاحِبُ يُوسُفَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الأذان (682) عن يحيى بن سليمان، حدثنا ابن وهب، حدثني يونس، عن ابن شهاب، عن حمزة بن عبد الله أنه أخبره، عن أبيه قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ وأفضلهم بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (682).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Beloved of People to the Prophet ﷺ and the Best of Them After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar reported: When the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ pain became severe, he was asked about the prayer. He said: “Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.” ʿĀ’ishah said: “Abū Bakr is a tenderhearted man. When he recites, he is overcome by weeping.” He said: “Tell him to lead the prayer.” She raised the matter with him again, so he said: “Tell him to lead the prayer. You are like the women associated with Joseph.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",43],"full":1,"rep":[2238,8409,12568],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (682)."},{"num":9844,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ زَمْعَةَ بْنِ الْأَسْوَدِ بْنِ الْمُطَّلِبِ بْنِ أَسَدٍ قَالَ: لَمَّا اسْتُعِزَّ بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَنَا عِنْدَهُ فِي نَفَرٍ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ، قَالَ: دَعَا بِلَالٌ لِلصَّلَاةِ، فَقَالَ: مُرُوا مَنْ يُصَلِّي بِالنَّاسِ، قَالَ: فَخَرَجْتُ، فَإِذَا عُمَرُ فِي النَّاسِ، وَكَانَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ غَائِبًا، فَقَالَ: قُمْ يَا عُمَرُ، فَصَلِّ بِالنَّاسِ. قَالَ: فَقَامَ، فَلَمَّا كَبَّرَ عُمَرُ سَمِعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ صَوْتَهُ، وَكَانَ عُمَرُ رَجُلًا مُجْهِرًا، قَالَ: فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:: فَأَيْنَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ؟ يَأْبَى اللهُ ذَلِكَ وَالْمُسْلِمُونَ، يَأْبَى اللهُ ذَلِكَ وَالْمُسْلِمُونَ قَالَ: فَبَعَثَ إِلَى أَبِي بَكْرٍ، فَجَاءَ بَعْدَ أَنْ صَلَّى عُمَرُ تِلْكَ الصَّلَاةَ، فَصَلَّى بِالنَّاسِ.","قَالَ: وَقَالَ عَبْدُ اللهِ بْنُ زَمْعَةَ: قَالَ لِي عُمَرُ: وَيْحَكَ، مَاذَا صَنَعْتَ بِي يَا ابْنَ زَمْعَةَ، وَاللهِ مَا ظَنَنْتُ حِينَ أَمَرْتَنِي إِلَّا أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمَرَكَ بِذَلِكَ، وَلَوْلَا ذَلِكَ مَا صَلَّيْتُ بالناس.قال: قُلْتُ: وَاللهِ مَا أَمَرَنِي رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَلَكِنْ حِينَ لَمْ أَرَ أَبَا بَكْرٍ رَأَيْتُكَ أَحَقَّ مَنْ حَضَرَ بِالصَّلَاةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4660)، و أحمد (18906) كلاهما من طريق محمد بن إسحاق، حدثني الزهري، حدثني عبد الملك بن أبي بكر بن عبد الرحمن بن الحارث بن هشام، عن أبيه، عن عبد الله بن زمعة قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ وأفضلهم بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4660) and Aḥmad (18906).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Beloved of People to the Prophet ﷺ and the Best of Them After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Zamʿah ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muṭṭalib ibn Asad reported: When the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ illness became overwhelming, I was with him among a group of Muslims. Bilāl called for the prayer, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “Tell someone to lead the people in prayer.” I went out and found ʿUmar among the people, while Abū Bakr was absent. I said: “Stand, ʿUmar, and lead the people in prayer.” He stood, and when ʿUmar pronounced the opening takbīr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard his voice, for ʿUmar was a man with a loud voice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Where is Abū Bakr? Allah and the Muslims refuse this! Allah and the Muslims refuse this!” He then sent for Abū Bakr. Abū Bakr arrived after ʿUmar had completed that prayer and thereafter led the people in prayer. ʿAbdullāh ibn Zamʿah continued: ʿUmar said to me: “Woe to you! What have you done to me, Ibn Zamʿah? By Allah, when you instructed me, I assumed only that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had ordered you to do so. Had it not been for that, I would never have led the people in prayer.” I replied: “By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not order me to do so. However, when I did not see Abū Bakr, I considered you the person present who was most entitled to lead the prayer.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The expression “استُعِزَّ” is used when a sick person is overcome and loses control of himself because of the severity of his illness.","ʿUmar’s leading of the people in prayer may have occurred initially while Abū Bakr was absent from that gathering, as the hadith indicates. Thereafter, Abū Bakr continued to lead the people in prayer."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",44],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4660)، وأحمد (18906)."},{"num":9845,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَهْلِ بْنِ سَعْدٍ، قَالَ: كَانَ قِتَالٌ بَيْنَ بَنِي عَمْرِو بْنِ عَوْفٍ، فَبَلَغَ ذَلِكَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَتَاهُمْ لِيُصْلِحَ بَيْنَهُمْ بَعْدَ الظُّهْرِ، فَقَالَ لِبِلاَلٍ: إِنْ حَضَرَتْ صَلاَةُ الْعَصْرِ وَلَمْ آتِكَ فَمُرْ أَبَا بَكْرٍ فَلْيُصَلِّ بِالنَّاسِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (941)، والنسائي (793)، وأحمد (22816)، وصحّحه ابن خزيمة (853)، وابن حبان (2261) كلهم من طريق حماد بن زيد، حدثنا أبو حازم، عن سهل بن سعد فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ وأفضلهم بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (941), al-Nasā’ī (793), Aḥmad (22816), Ibn Khuzaymah (853), and Ibn Ḥibbān (2261). Its chain is authentic.","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Beloved of People to the Prophet ﷺ and the Best of Them After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd reported: There was fighting among Banū ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf. When news of it reached the Prophet ﷺ, he went to them after the noon prayer to reconcile them. He said to Bilāl: “If the time for the afternoon prayer arrives and I have not returned to you, then tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer…” The remainder of the hadith follows."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The hadith concerning Abū Bakr’s leading of the afternoon prayer during the Prophet’s ﷺ absence was narrated by al-Bukhārī (7190)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",45],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (941)، والنسائي (793)، وأحمد (22816)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (853)، وابن حبان (2261). وإسناده صحيح."},{"num":9846,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  مَنْ أَصْبَحَ مِنْكُمُ الْيَوْمَ صَائِمًا؟ قَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ: أَنَا، قَالَ: فَمَنْ تَبِعَ مِنْكُمُ الْيَوْمَ جَنَازَةً، قَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ: أَنَا. قَالَ: فَمَنْ أَطْعَمَ مِنْكُمُ الْيَوْمَ مِسْكِينًا، قَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ: أَنَا. قَالَ: فَمَنْ عَادَ مِنْكُمُ الْيَوْمَ مَرِيضًا، قَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ: أَنَا. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا اجْتَمَعْنَ فِي امْرِئٍ إِلَّا دَخَلَ الْجَنَّةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (1028) عن محمد بن أبي عمر المكي، ثنا مروان بن معاوية الفزاري، عن يزيد بن كيسان، عن أبي حازم الأشجعي، عن أبي هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ وأفضلهم بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1028).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Beloved of People to the Prophet ﷺ and the Best of Them After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Who among you began this day fasting?” Abū Bakr replied: “I did.” He asked: “Who among you followed a funeral procession today?” Abū Bakr replied: “I did.” He asked: “Who among you fed a poor person today?” Abū Bakr replied: “I did.” He asked: “Who among you visited a sick person today?” Abū Bakr replied: “I did.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “These qualities are never combined in a person except that he enters Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",46],"full":1,"rep":[3456,4103],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1028)."},{"num":9847,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: مَنْ أَنْفَقَ زَوْجَيْنِ مِنْ شَيْءٍ مِنَ الأَشْيَاءِ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ دُعِيَ مِنْ أَبْوَابِ – يَعْنِي: الْجَنَّةَ- يَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ هَذَا خَيْرٌ، فَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْ أَهْلِ الصَّلاَةِ دُعِيَ مِنْ باب الصَّلاَةِ، وَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْجِهَادِ دُعِيَ مِنْ باب الْجِهَادِ، وَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْ أَهْلِ الصَّدَقَةِ دُعِيَ مِنْ باب الصَّدَقَةِ، وَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْ أَهْلِ الصِّيَامِ دُعِيَ مِنْ باب الصِّيَامِ، وَبَابِ الرَّيَّانِ، فَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: مَا عَلَى هَذَا الَّذِي يُدْعَى مِنْ تِلْكَ الأَبْوَابِ مِنْ ضَرُورَةٍ، وَقَالَ: هَلْ يُدْعَى مِنْهَا كُلِّهَا أَحَدٌ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، وَأَرْجُو أَنْ تَكُونَ مِنْهُمْ يَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3666)، ومسلم في الزكاة (1027-85) كلاهما من طرق عن الزهري قال: أخبرني حميد بن عبد الرحمن بن عوف، أن أبا هريرة، قال: فذكره.وهذا لفظ البخاري، وسياق مسلم نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ وأفضلهم بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3666) and Muslim (85–1027).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Beloved of People to the Prophet ﷺ and the Best of Them After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever spends two of any kind of property in the path of Allah will be called from the gates—meaning the gates of Paradise—‘O servant of Allah, this is good!’ Whoever was devoted to prayer will be called from the Gate of Prayer. Whoever was devoted to jihad will be called from the Gate of Jihad. Whoever was devoted to charity will be called from the Gate of Charity. Whoever was devoted to fasting will be called from the Gate of Fasting, the Gate of al-Rayyān.” Abū Bakr said: “A person called from any of those gates will have no cause for distress. Will anyone be called from all of them, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Yes, and I hope that you will be among them, Abū Bakr.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording narrated by them:","“Whoever spends two of something in the path of Allah will be called by the gatekeepers of Paradise, each gatekeeper saying, ‘So-and-so, come here!’”","Abū Bakr said:","“O Messenger of Allah, such a person would face no ruin.”","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied:","“I truly hope that you will be among them.”","Narrated by Muslim (86–1027) and al-Bukhārī (2841). The expression “لا توى” means that there will be no destruction or loss."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",47],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13211,16264],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3666)، ومسلم (85-1027)."},{"num":9848,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ:  قَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي مَرَضِهِ: ادْعِي لِي أَبَا بَكْرٍ أَبَاكِ وَأَخَاكِ حَتَّى أَكْتُبَ كِتَابًا، فَإِنِّي أَخَافُ أَنْ يَتَمَنَّى مُتَمَنٍّ، وَيَقُولُ قَائِلٌ: أَنَا أَوْلَى، وَيَأْبَى اللهُ وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ إِلَّا أَبَا بَكْرٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2387) عن عبيد الله بن سعيد، ثنا يزيد بن هارون، أخبرنا إبراهيم بن سعد، ثنا صالح بن كيسان، عن الزهري، عن عروة، عن عائشة قالت: فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ وأفضلهم بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Muslim (2387) and al-Bukhārī (7217).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Beloved of People to the Prophet ﷺ and the Best of Them After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: During his illness, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Call Abū Bakr and your brother for me so that I may write a document, for I fear that someone may aspire to the position and another may say, ‘I am more entitled to it,’ whereas Allah and the believers will accept none but Abū Bakr.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",48],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (2387)، والبخاري (7217)."},{"num":9849,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: خَرَجْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي بَعْضِ أسفاره...وفيه قصة ضياع عقد لعائشة وبقاء الناس من أجله بدون ماء ولا وضوء، وتوبيخ أبي بكر لعائشة وطعنه إياها، فَأَنْزَلَ اللهُ آيَةَ التَّيَمُّمِ، فَتَيَمَّمُوا، فَقَالَ أُسَيْدُ بْنُ حضير: مَا هِيَ بِأَوَّلِ بَرَكَتِكُمْ يَا آلَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ، قالت: فَبَعَثْنَا الْبَعِيرَ الَّذِي كُنْتُ عَلَيْهِ فأصبنا الْعِقْدَ تَحْتَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك في كتاب الطهارة (120) عن عبد الرحمن بن القاسم، عن أبيه، عن عائشة، فذكرته.ورواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3672) ومسلم في الطهارة (367-108) كلاهما من طريق مالك به.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا بكر أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ وأفضلهم بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik (120), al-Bukhārī (3672) and Muslim (108–367).","chapter_en":"Reports That Abū Bakr Was the Most Beloved of People to the Prophet ﷺ and the Best of Them After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys… The hadith contains the account of ʿĀ’ishah’s necklace being lost, because of which the people remained without water and could not perform ablution. Abū Bakr reproached ʿĀ’ishah and prodded her. Allah then revealed the verse concerning dry ablution, and the people performed dry ablution. Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr said: “O family of Abū Bakr, this is not the first blessing that has come through you.” ʿĀ’ishah said: “We then made the camel upon which I had been riding stand up, and we found the necklace beneath it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",49],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه مالك (120)، والبخاري (3672)، ومسلم (108-367)."},{"num":9850,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ جَرَّ ثَوْبَهُ خُيَلاَءَ لَمْ يَنْظُرِ اللَّهُ إِلَيْهِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ. فَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: إِنَّ أَحَدَ شِقَّىْ ثَوْبِي يَسْتَرْخِي، إِلاَّ أَنْ أَتَعَاهَدَ ذَلِكَ مِنْهُ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّكَ لَسْتَ تَصْنَعُ ذَلِكَ خُيَلاَءَ قَالَ مُوسَى: فَقُلْتُ لِسَالِمٍ: أَذَكَرَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ: مَنْ جَرَّ إِزَارَهُ؟ قَالَ: لَمْ أَسْمَعْهُ ذَكَرَ إِلاَّ ثَوْبَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3665)، ومسلم في اللباس (2085-44) كلاهما من طريق سالم بن عبد الله، عن عبد الله بن عمرقال: فذكره.وهذا لفظ البخاري، وسياق مسلم مختصر، ليس فيه قصة أبي بكر الصديق.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن أبا بكر ليس ممن يجرُّ ثوبه خيلاء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3665) and Muslim (44–2085). This is al-Bukhārī’s wording; Muslim’s version is abbreviated and does not include the account concerning Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq.","chapter_en":"Abū Bakr Was Not Among Those Who Dragged Their Garments Out of Arrogance","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.” Abū Bakr said: “One side of my garment slips down unless I continually attend to it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “You are not doing that out of arrogance.” Mūsā said: “I asked Sālim, ‘Did ʿAbdullāh specifically mention, “Whoever drags his lower garment”?’” He replied: “I heard him mention only ‘his garment.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",50],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3665)، ومسلم (44-2085). وهذا لفظ البخاري، وسياق مسلم مختصر، ليس فيه قصة أبي بكر الصديق."},{"num":9851,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ زَيْدِ بْنِ أَسْلَمَ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ يَقُولُ: أَمَرَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمًا أَنْ نَتَصَدَّقَ فَوَافَقَ ذَلِكَ مَالاً عِنْدِي، فَقُلْتُ: الْيَوْمَ أَسْبِقُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ إِنْ سَبَقْتُهُ يَوْمًا فَجِئْتُ بِنِصْفِ مَالِي، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا أَبْقَيْتَ لأَهْلِكَ. قُلْتُ: مِثْلَهُ. قَالَ وَأَتَى أَبُو بَكْرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ بِكُلِّ مَا عِنْدَهُ، فَقَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا أَبْقَيْتَ لأَهْلِكَ. قَالَ: أَبْقَيْتُ لَهُمُ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ. قُلْتُ لاَ أُسَابِقُكَ إِلَى شَىْءٍ أَبَدًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1678)، والترمذي (3675) كلاهما من حديث الفضل بن دكين، حدثنا هشام بن سعد، عن زيد بن أسلم، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أنه تصدق بماله كله في سبيل الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1678) and al-Tirmidhī (3675).","chapter_en":"He Gave All His Wealth in Charity in the Cause of Allah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Aslam reported: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, say: One day, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed us to give charity. This coincided with a time when I had wealth, so I said, “Today I will surpass Abū Bakr, if ever I am to surpass him.” I brought half of my wealth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “What have you left for your family?” I replied, “The same amount.” Then Abū Bakr came with everything he possessed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him: “What have you left for your family?” He replied, “I have left Allah and His Messenger for them.” I said, “I will never compete with you in anything again.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",51],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1678)، والترمذي (3675)."},{"num":9852,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن الزُّبَيْرِ عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: كَانَ اسْمُ أَبِي بَكْرٍ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عُثْمَانَ، فَقَالَ لَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَنْتَ عَتِيقُ اللهِ مِنَ النَّارِ، فَسُمِّيَ عَتِيقًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار (2213)، والطبراني في الكبير (1/5)، وابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (17،8)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (6864) كلهم من طريق حامد بن يحيى البلخي، عن سفيان بن عيينة، عن زياد بن سعد (هو الخراساني)، عن عامر بن عبد الله بن الزبير، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في لقب أبي بكر عتيقًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār (2213), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (1/5), and Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Āḥād wa-al-Mathānī (1708); authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6864). They narrate it through Ḥāmid ibn Yaḥyā al-Balkhī, from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, from Ziyād ibn Saʿd al-Khurāsānī, from ʿĀmir ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr, from his father.","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Abū Bakr’s Title “ʿAtīq”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr reported: Abū Bakr’s name was ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “You are the one whom Allah has set free from the Fire.” He was therefore called ʿAtīq."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",52],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار (2213)، والطبراني في الكبير (1/5)، وابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (1708)، وصححه ابن حبان (6864)."},{"num":9853,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: إن أَبَا بكرخرج وَعُمَرُ يُكَلِّمُ النَّاسَ، فَقَالَ: اجْلِسْ، فَأَبَى، فَقَالَ: اجْلِسْ، فَأَبَى، فَتَشَهَّدَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَمَالَ إِلَيْهِ النَّاسُ وَتَرَكُوا عُمَرَ، فَقَالَ: أَمَّا بَعْدُ، فَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْكُمْ يَعْبُدُ مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَإِنَّ مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَدْ مَاتَ، وَمَنْ كَانَ يَعْبُدُ اللَّهَ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ حي لاَ يَمُوتُ، قَالَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى: وَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ إِلَّا رَسُولٌ إِلَى الشَّاكِرِينَ [آل عِمْرَانَ:١٤٤] وَاللَّهِ لَكَأَنَّ النَّاسَ لَمْ يَكُونُوا يَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّ اللَّهَ أنزلها حَتَّى تَلاَهَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ، ، فَتَلَقَّاهَا مِنْهُ النَّاسُ، فَمَا يُسْمَعُ بَشَرٌ إِلاَّ يَتْلُوهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الجنائز (1241، 1242) عن بشر بن محمد، أنا عبد الله، أخبرني معمر ويونس، عن الزهري، أخبرني أبو سلمة، قال: أخبرني ابن عباس أن أبا بكر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في موقف أبي بكر الصديق عند وفاة النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1241, 1242).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq’s Stance at the Death of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās reported: Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, came out while ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, was speaking to the people. Abū Bakr said, “Sit down,” but ʿUmar refused. He again said, “Sit down,” but he refused. Abū Bakr then recited the testimony of faith, so the people turned toward him and left ʿUmar. He said: “To proceed: Whoever among you worshipped Muḥammad ﷺ, then Muḥammad ﷺ has died. But whoever worships Allah, then Allah is Ever-Living and never dies.” Allah Most High says: “Muḥammad is no more than a messenger; other messengers have passed away before him. If he were to die or be killed, would you turn back on your heels? Whoever turns back on his heels will not harm Allah in the least, and Allah will reward the grateful.” [Āl ʿImrān 3:144] By Allah, it was as though the people had not known that Allah had revealed this verse until Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, recited it. The people received it from him, and no one could be heard except reciting it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1241، 1242)."},{"num":9854,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ زوج النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أن رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَاتَ وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ بِالسُّنْحِ...فذكرت الْحَدِيثَ، وَفِيهِ: ثُمَّ خَرَجَ فَقَالَ: أَيُّهَا الْحَالِفُ عَلَى رِسْلِكَ، فَلَمَّا تَكَلَّمَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ جَلَسَ عُمَرُ، فَحَمِدَ اللَّهَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ وَأَثْنَى عَلَيْهِ، وَقَالَ: أَلاَ مَنْ كَانَ يَعْبُدُ مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَإِنَّ مُحَمَّدًا قَدْ مَاتَ، وَمَنْ كَانَ يَعْبُدُ اللَّهَ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ حي لاَ يَمُوتُ، وَقَالَ: إِنَّكَ مَيِّتٌ وَإِنَّهُمْ مَيِّتُونَ [الزمر:٣٠] وَقَالَ: ﴿وَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ إِلَّا رَسُولٌ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُ أَفَإِنْ مَاتَ أَوْ قُتِلَ انْقَلَبْتُمْ عَلَى أَعْقَابِكُمْ وَمَنْ يَنْقَلِبْ عَلَى عَقِبَيْهِ فَلَنْ يَضُرَّ اللَّهَ شَيْئًا وَسَيَجْزِي اللَّهُ الشَّاكِرِينَ﴾ [سورة آل عمران: 144] [آل عِمْرَانَ: ١٤٤] قَالَ: فَنَشَجَ النَّاسُ يَبْكُونَ، قَالَ: وَاجْتَمَعَتِ الأَنْصَارُ إِلَى سَعْدِ بْنِ عُبَادَةَ فِي سَقِيفَةِ بَنِي سَاعِدَةَ، فَقَالُوا: مِنَّا أَمِيرٌ وَمِنْكُمْ أَمِيرٌ، فَذَهَبَ إِلَيْهِمْ أَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ وَأَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ بْنُ الْجَرَّاحِ، فَذَهَبَ عُمَرُ يَتَكَلَّمُ، فَأَسْكَتَهُ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، وَكَانَ عُمَرُ يَقُولُ: وَاللَّهِ مَا أَرَدْتُ بِذَلِكَ إِلاَّ أَنِّي قَدْ هَيَّأْتُ كَلاَمًا قَدْ أَعْجَبَنِي، خَشِيتُ أَنْ لاَ يَبْلُغَهُ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، ثُمَّ تَكَلَّمَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ فَتَكَلَّمَ أَبْلَغَ النَّاسِ، فَقَالَ فِي كَلاَمِهِ: نَحْنُ الأُمَرَاءُ وَأَنْتُمُ الْوُزَرَاءُ، فَقَالَ حُبَابُ بْنُ الْمُنْذِرِ: لاَ وَاللَّهِ لاَ نَفْعَلُ، مِنَّا أَمِيرٌ وَمِنْكُمْ أَمِيرٌ، فَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: لاَ وَلَكِنَّا الأُمَرَاءُ وَأَنْتُمُ الْوُزَرَاءُ، هُمْ أَوْسَطُ الْعَرَبِ دَارًا، وَأَعْرَبُهُمْ أَحْسَابًا، فَبَايِعُوا عُمَرَ أَوْ أَبَا عُبَيْدَةَ، فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: بَلْ نُبَايِعُكَ أَنْتَ، فَأَنْتَ سَيِّدُنَا، وَخَيْرُنَا، وَأَحَبُّنَا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَأَخَذَ عُمَرُ بِيَدِهِ، فَبَايَعَهُ وَبَايَعَهُ النَّاسُ.فَقَالَ قَائِلٌ: قَتَلْتُمْ سَعْدَ بْنَ عُبَادَةَ، فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: قَتَلَهُ اللَّهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3667، 3668) عن إسماعيل بن عبد الله، ثنا سليمان بن بلال، عن هشام بن عروة، عن عروة بن الزبير، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في موقف أبي بكر الصديق عند وفاة النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3667, 3668).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq’s Stance at the Death of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while Abū Bakr was at al-Sunḥ. She then related the hadith, in which it states: Abū Bakr then came out and said: “O you who are swearing, take it easy.” When Abū Bakr began speaking, ʿUmar sat down. Abū Bakr praised and extolled Allah and then said: “Take heed! Whoever worshipped Muḥammad ﷺ, then Muḥammad has died. But whoever worships Allah, then Allah is Ever-Living and never dies.” He then recited: “Indeed, you will die, and they too will die.” [Al-Zumar 39:30] He also recited: “Muḥammad is no more than a messenger; other messengers have passed away before him. If he were to die or be killed, would you turn back on your heels? Whoever turns back on his heels will not harm Allah in the least, and Allah will reward the grateful.” [Āl ʿImrān 3:144] The people then began sobbing and weeping. The Anṣār gathered around Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah in the portico of Banū Sāʿidah. They said: “Let there be a leader from among us and a leader from among you.” Abū Bakr, ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ went to them. ʿUmar began to speak, but Abū Bakr silenced him. ʿUmar used to say: “By Allah, I intended nothing by that except that I had prepared words which pleased me, and I feared that Abū Bakr might not express them as effectively.” Abū Bakr then spoke, and he was the most eloquent of the people. Among the things he said was: “We are the rulers, and you are the ministers.” Al-Ḥubāb ibn al-Mundhir said: “No, by Allah, we will not accept that. There must be a leader from among us and a leader from among you.” Abū Bakr replied: “No. We are the rulers, and you are the ministers. They are the Arabs’ most central tribe by territory and the noblest of them by lineage. Therefore, pledge allegiance to ʿUmar or Abū ʿUbaydah.” ʿUmar said: “Rather, we shall pledge allegiance to you. You are our leader, the best among us and the most beloved of us to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” ʿUmar took Abū Bakr’s hand and pledged allegiance to him, and the people also pledged allegiance to him. Someone said: “You have killed Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah!” ʿUmar replied: “Allah has killed him.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["He was pledged allegiance as caliph in the portico of Banū Sāʿidah on the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died. The following day, Tuesday, the general public pledged allegiance to him.","Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, a group from al-Khazraj and a group from Quraysh initially withheld their allegiance. They later pledged allegiance, except for Saʿd. It is also said that ʿAlī did not pledge allegiance to him until after Fāṭimah’s death. Thereafter, he remained obedient and compliant toward him, praised him and regarded him as superior.","According to what al-Zubayr ibn Bakkār mentioned, the inscription on his signet ring was: “How excellent is Allah, the All-Powerful.” Others said its inscription was: “A humble servant of a Majestic Lord.”","The ḥāfiẓ Ibn ʿAbd al-Barr mentioned all of this in al-Istīʿāb.","Abū Bakr died on Monday in Jumādā al-Ūlā, in the thirteenth year after the Hijrah, at the age of sixty-three."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3667، 3668)."},{"num":9855,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن طارق بن شهاب قال: جاء وفد بزاخة من أسدٍ وغطفان إلى أبي بكر يسألونه الصلح، فخيَّرهم بين الحرب المجلية والسلم المخزية، فقالوا: هذه المجلية قد عرفناها، فما المخزية؟ قال: ننزع منكم الحلقة والكراع، ونغنم ما أصبنا منكم، وتردون علينا ما أصبتم منا، وتدون لنا قتلانا، وتكون قتلاكم في النار، وتتركون أقواماً يتبعون أذناب الإبل حتى يُرِيَ الله خليفة رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم والمهاجرين أمراً يعذرونكم به، فعرض أبو بكرٍ ما قال على القوم، فقام عمر بن الخطاب فقال: قد رأيت رأياً وسنشير عليك، فأما ما ذكرت من الحرب المجلية والسلم المخزية فنعم ما ذكرت، وما ذكرت أن نغنم ما أصبنا منكم وتردون ما أصبتم منا فنعم ما ذكرت، وأما ما ذكرت: تدون قتلانا وتكون قتلاكم في النار، فإن قتلانا قاتلت فقتلت على أمر الله، أجورها على الله، ليس لها دياتٌ، فتتابع القوم على ما قال عمر."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو بكر البرقاني في كتابه \"المخرَّج على الصحيحين\" كما في كتاب الجمع بين الصحيحين للحميدي –بإسناده عن مسدد، عن يحيى القطان، عن سفيان الثوري، عن قيس بن مسلم، عن طارق بن شهاب، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من أخبار أبي بكر الصديق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Bakr al-Barqānī in al-Mukhraj ʿalā al-Ṣaḥīḥayn, as cited in al-Ḥumaydī’s al-Jamʿ bayna al-Ṣaḥīḥayn. It was also narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Book of Legal Judgments (7221).","chapter_en":"Accounts Concerning Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ṭāriq ibn Shihāb reported: A delegation from Buzākhah, consisting of members of Asad and Ghaṭafān, came to Abū Bakr seeking peace. He gave them a choice between a war that would drive them from their homes and a humiliating peace. They said: “We understand the war that drives people from their homes, but what is the humiliating peace?” He replied: “We will take your weapons and riding animals from you. We will retain as spoils whatever we seized from you, while you must return whatever you seized from us. You must pay blood money for those of us whom you killed, while your dead will be in the Fire. You must also leave some people to follow the tails of camels until Allah shows the caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Emigrants something by which they may excuse you.” Abū Bakr presented his proposal to the people. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb stood and said: “You have formed an opinion, and we shall offer you our counsel. As for what you said about a war that drives them from their homes and a humiliating peace, what you said is excellent. As for retaining whatever we seized from them while they return whatever they seized from us, what you said is excellent. But as for your statement that they must pay blood money for our dead while their dead will be in the Fire—our dead fought and were killed in obedience to Allah’s command. Their rewards are with Allah, and no blood money is due for them.” The people then successively agreed with what ʿUmar had said."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",55],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو بكر البرقاني في كتابه «المخرج على الصحيحين»، كما في كتاب «الجمع بين الصحيحين» للحميدي. ورواه البخاري (7221)."},{"num":9856,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ أَنَّهُمْ خَرَجُوا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي سَفَرٍ، فَنَزَلُوا رُفَقَاءَ، رُفْقَةٌ مَعَ فُلَانٍ، وَرُفْقَةٌ مَعَ فُلَانٍ، قَالَ: فَنَزَلْتُ فِي رُفْقَةِ أَبِي بَكْرٍ، فَكَانَ مَعَنَا أَعْرَابِيٌّ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْبَادِيَةِ، فَنَزَلْنَا بِأَهْلِ بَيْتٍ مِنَ الْأَعْرَابِ، وَفِيهِمْ امْرَأَةٌ حَامِلٌ، فَقَالَ لَهَا الْأَعْرَابِيُّ: أَيَسُرُّكِ أَنْ تَلِدِي غُلَامًا؟ إِنْ أَعْطَيْتِنِي شَاةً وَلَدْتِ غُلَامًا.فَأَعْطَتْهُ شَاةً، وَسَجَعَ لَهَا أَسَاجِيعَ، قَالَ: فَذَبَحَ الشاة، فَلَمَّا جَلَسَ الْقَوْمُ يَأْكُلُونَ، قَالَ رَجُلٌ: أَتَدْرُونَ مَا هَذِهِ الشاة؟ فَأَخْبَرَهُمْ، قَالَ: فَرَأَيْتُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ مُتَبَرِّزًا مُسْتَنْبِلًا مُتَقَيِّئًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (11482) عن يحيى بن آدم، حدثنا زهير، عن الأسود بن قيس، عن نُبيح (هو ابن عبد الله العنزي)، عن أبي سعيد الخدري فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من أخبار أبي بكر الصديق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (11482).","chapter_en":"Accounts Concerning Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported: They set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey and divided into separate groups, one group accompanying one person and another accompanying someone else. I joined Abū Bakr’s group. With us was a Bedouin, and we stopped near a Bedouin household in which there was a pregnant woman. The Bedouin said to her: “Would you like to give birth to a boy? If you give me a sheep, you will give birth to a boy.” She gave him a sheep, and he recited rhyming phrases for her. He then slaughtered the sheep. When the people sat down to eat, a man asked: “Do you know the story of this sheep?” He told them what had happened. I then saw Abū Bakr relieving himself, seeking stones for cleansing, and vomiting."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",56],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (11482)."},{"num":9857,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ خَادِمِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: قَدِمَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَلَيْسَ فِي أَصْحَابِهِ أَشْمَطُ غَيْرَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ فَغَلَفَهَا بِالْحِنَّاءِ وَالْكَتَمِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3919) عن سليمان بن عبدالرحمن، حدثنا محمد بن حمير، حدثنا إبراهيم بن أبي عبلة، أن عقبة بن وسّاج، حدثه عن أنس قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من أخبار أبي بكر الصديق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3919).","chapter_en":"Accounts Concerning Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik reported: When the Prophet ﷺ arrived, none of his Companions had graying hair except Abū Bakr, so he dyed it with henna and katam."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word “ashmaṭ” refers to whiteness in the hair of the head or beard mixed with black hair.","The phrase “he coated it” means that he dyed it.","Among the accounts concerning Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq is what al-Bukhārī (3842) narrated from ʿĀ’ishah, who said:","Abū Bakr had a slave who paid him an agreed portion of his earnings, and Abū Bakr used to eat from those earnings. One day, the slave brought him something, and Abū Bakr ate from it. The slave asked:","“Do you know what this is?”","Abū Bakr asked:","“What is it?”","He replied:","“During the pre-Islamic period, I pretended to practice divination for a man. I was not good at divination, but I deceived him. He later met me and gave me this in return. This is what you have eaten from.”","Abū Bakr placed his hand into his mouth and vomited everything in his stomach.","Among the accounts concerning him is also what al-Bukhārī (3921) narrated from ʿĀ’ishah:","Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, married a woman from the tribe of Kalb named Umm Bakr. When Abū Bakr emigrated, he divorced her, and her paternal cousin married her. He was the poet who composed the following elegy for the disbelievers of Quraysh:","What lies within the well—the well of Badr—","Of wooden platters adorned with camel humps?","What lies within the well—the well of Badr—","Of singing girls and noble drinking companions?","Umm Bakr bids me farewell in safety,","But can I have peace after my people are gone?","The Messenger tells us that we shall live again—","But how can echoes and owls ever live?","Among the accounts concerning him, may Allah be pleased with him, is his fighting against the apostates:"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",57],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3919)."},{"num":9858,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: لَمَّا تُوُفِّيَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَاسْتُخْلِفَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ بَعْدَهُ، وَكَفَرَ مَنْ كَفَرَ مِنَ الْعَرَبِ، قَالَ عُمَرُ لأَبِي بَكْرٍ: كَيْفَ تُقَاتِلُ النَّاسَ، وَقَدْ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أُمِرْتُ أَنْ أُقَاتِلَ النَّاسَ حَتَّى يَقُولُوا: لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ. فَمَنْ قَالَ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ. عَصَمَ مِنِّي مَالَهُ وَنَفْسَهُ، إِلاَّ بِحَقِّهِ، وَحِسَابُهُ عَلَى اللَّهِ. فَقَالَ وَاللَّهِ لأُقَاتِلَنَّ مَنْ فَرَّقَ بَيْنَ الصَّلاَةِ وَالزَّكَاةِ، فَإِنَّ الزَّكَاةَ حَقُّ الْمَالِ، وَاللَّهِ لَوْ مَنَعُونِي عِقَالاً كَانُوا يُؤَدُّونَهُ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَقَاتَلْتُهُمْ عَلَى مَنْعِهِ. فَقَالَ عُمَرُ فَوَاللَّهِ مَا هُوَ إِلاَّ أَنْ رَأَيْتُ اللَّهَ قَدْ شَرَحَ صَدْرَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ لِلْقِتَالِ، فَعَرَفْتُ أَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الاعتصام بالكتاب والسنة (7284)، ومسلم في الإيمان (20) كلاهما عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا ليث بن سعد، عن عقيل، عن الزهري قال: أخبرني عبيد الله بن عبد الله بن عتبة بن مسعود، عن أبي هريرة فذكر الحديث ولفظهما سواء.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب من أخبار أبي بكر الصديق","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7284) and Muslim (20).","chapter_en":"Accounts Concerning Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي بكر وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of the Virtues and Accounts of Abū Bakr","part_no":49,"group_no":2,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, Abū Bakr succeeded him as caliph and those Arabs who fell into disbelief did so, ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said to Abū Bakr: “How can you fight the people when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, “There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.” Whoever says, “There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,” has protected his property and life from me, except where it is lawfully due, and his reckoning is with Allah’?” Abū Bakr replied: “By Allah, I will certainly fight anyone who separates prayer from zakāh, for zakāh is the right due upon wealth. By Allah, if they withheld from me even a rope which they used to give to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would fight them for withholding it.” ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said: “By Allah, once I saw that Allah Almighty had opened Abū Bakr’s heart to fighting them, I knew that it was the truth.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Concerning the phrase, “those Arabs who fell into disbelief did so,” Ibn Ḥazm said in al-Milal wa-al-Niḥal that they consisted of three groups:","A group that openly declared disbelief, apostatized and followed the false claimants to prophethood: Musaylimah, Ṭulayḥah, al-Aswad and Sajāḥ bint al-Ḥārith, who was one of the Arab Christians and claimed prophethood.","A group that remained upon Islam but withheld zakāh.","A group that waited to see which side would prevail.","End of quotation.","The expression “they withheld zakāh” includes two possible meanings:","The first is that they denied zakāh’s obligatory nature. The second is that they refused to deliver it to the caliph.","Their argument was based on the statement of Allah Most High:","“Take charity from their wealth to purify and cleanse them thereby, and pray for them. Indeed, your prayer is a source of reassurance for them. And Allah is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.” [Al-Tawbah 9:103]","They said:","“The one to whom Allah commanded us to deliver zakāh has died. Delivering it to him brought us reassurance, whereas delivering it to Abū Bakr and his praying for us does not bring us reassurance. Consequently, the obligation of zakāh and of delivering it to the caliph has ceased.”","This meaning is indicated by the statement of al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him:","“By Allah, I will certainly fight anyone who separates prayer from zakāh, for zakāh is the right due upon wealth.”","That is, he meant anyone who distinguished between the obligation of prayer and the obligation of zakāh by acknowledging that prayer was obligatory while denying that zakāh was obligatory, even though Allah Most High joined them together in obligation. He made prayer the right of Allah over His servants and zakāh the right due upon wealth.","Just as Allah’s right over His servants does not lapse, the right due upon wealth likewise does not lapse. It is therefore incorrect to say that Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq fought them merely because they refused to deliver zakāh to the caliph.","Abū Ḥanīfah, Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal and others held that if they said, “We will pay it ourselves, but we will not deliver it to the ruler,” it would not be permissible to fight them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",58],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[3910,7859],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7284)، ومسلم (20)."},{"num":9859,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ أَعِزَّ الإِسْلاَمَ بِأَحَبِّ هَذَيْنِ الرَّجُلَيْنِ إِلَيْكَ بِأَبِي جَهْلٍ أَوْ بِعُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ. قَالَ وَكَانَ أَحَبَّهُمَا إِلَيْهِ عُمَرُ. قَالَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3681)، و أحمد (5696)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (6881) كلهم من طريق خارجة بن عبد الله الأنصاري، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ لإسلام عمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3681) and Aḥmad (5696), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6881), all through Khārijah ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar.","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Supplication for ʿUmar to Embrace Islam","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, strengthen Islam through whichever of these two men is more beloved to You: Abū Jahl or ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.” The more beloved of the two to Him was ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “O Allah, strengthen Islam through whichever of these two men is more beloved to You,” occurred at the beginning. This means that the Prophet ﷺ initially supplicated concerning both men, but later supplicated specifically for ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb alone because he was the more beloved of the two to Allah."]},"intro_majmu":{"ar":["هو عمر بن الخطاب بن نفيل القرشي العدوي، ولد بعد عام الفيل بثلاث عشرة سنة. وكانت إليه السفارة في الجاهلية، وكان عند البعث شديدًا على المسلمين، ثم أسلم، فكان إسلامه فتحًا على المسلمين وفرجًا لهم من الضيق. قال عبد الله بن مسعود: «وما عبدنا الله جهرًا حتى أسلم عمر»."],"en":["He was ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb ibn Nufayl, of the Qurashī clan of ʿAdī. He was born thirteen years after the Year of the Elephant. During the pre-Islamic period, he was entrusted with diplomatic representation. At the beginning of the Prophetic mission, he was severe toward the Muslims. He then embraced Islam, and his acceptance of Islam was a victory for the Muslims and a relief from their hardship.","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd said:","“We were unable to worship Allah openly until ʿUmar embraced Islam.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",59],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3681)، وأحمد (5696)، وصححه ابن حبان (6881)."},{"num":9860,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اللَّهُمَّ أَعِزَّ الإِسْلاَمَ بِعُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ خَاصَّةً."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (105) وصحّحه الحاكم (4486) ومن طريقه البيهقي في الكبرى (122) كلاهما من طرق عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ لإسلام عمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (105) and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (4485); al-Bayhaqī also narrated it through al-Ḥākim in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (6/370). Its routes are from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀ’ishah, and its chain is sound.","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Supplication for ʿUmar to Embrace Islam","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, strengthen Islam specifically through ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",60],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (105)، وصححه الحاكم (4485)، ومن طريقه البيهقي في الكبرى (122)."},{"num":9861,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عُمَرَ عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: بَيْنَمَا هُوَ فِي الدَّارِ خَائِفًا، إِذْ جَاءَهُ الْعَاصِ بْنُ وَائِلٍ السَّهْمِيُّ أَبُو عَمْرٍو، عَلَيْهِ حُلَّةُ حِبَرَةٍ، وَقَمِيصٌ مَكْفُوفٌ بِحَرِيرٍ، وَهُوَ مِنْ بَنِي سَهْمٍ، وَهُمْ حُلَفَاؤُنَا فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، فَقَالَ لَهُ: مَا بَالُكَ؟ قَالَ: زَعَمَ قَوْمُكَ أَنَّهُمْ سَيَقْتُلُونِي إِنْ أَسْلَمْتُ. قَالَ لاَ سَبِيلَ إِلَيْكَ. بَعْدَ أَنْ قَالَهَا أَمِنْتُ، فَخَرَجَ الْعَاصِ، فَلَقِيَ النَّاسَ قَدْ سَالَ بِهِمُ الْوَادِي، فَقَالَ: أَيْنَ تُرِيدُونَ؟ فَقَالُوا: نُرِيدُ هَذَا ابْنَ الْخَطَّابِ الَّذِي صَبَا. قَالَ: لاَ سَبِيلَ إِلَيْهِ. فَكَرَّ النَّاسُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3864) عن يحيى بن سليمان قال: ثني ابن وهب قال: ثني عمر بن محمد قال: فأخبرني جدي زيد بن عبد الله بن عمر، عن أبيه، قال: بينما فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ لإسلام عمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3864).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Supplication for ʿUmar to Embrace Islam","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported: While ʿUmar was at home in fear, al-ʿĀṣ ibn Wā’il al-Sahmī, Abū ʿAmr, came to him. He was wearing an embroidered cloak and a shirt edged with silk. He belonged to Banū Sahm, who had been our allies during the pre-Islamic period. He asked ʿUmar: “What is the matter with you?” ʿUmar replied: “Your people claim that they will kill me if I embrace Islam.” Al-ʿĀṣ said: “No one can reach you.” After he said this, I felt safe. Al-ʿĀṣ went out and encountered a crowd of people so numerous that they filled and flowed through the valley. He asked: “Where are you going?” They replied: “We are going after this Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb who has abandoned his religion.” He said: “No one can reach him.” The people then turned back."]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording:","“When ʿUmar embraced Islam, the people gathered at his house and said, ‘ʿUmar has abandoned his religion!’ I was a young boy on the roof of my house. A man wearing a silk cloak came and said, ‘ʿUmar has abandoned his religion—so what? He is under my protection.’ I then saw the people disperse and leave him. I asked, ‘Who is this?’ They replied, ‘Al-ʿĀṣ ibn Wā’il.’”","Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3865)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",61],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3864)."},{"num":9862,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن هِشَامٍ قَالَ: كُنَّا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَهْوَ آخِذٌ بِيَدِ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ، فَقَالَ لَهُ عُمَرُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، لأَنْتَ أَحَبُّ إِلَىَّ مِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ إِلاَّ مِنْ نَفْسِي. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لاَ، وَالَّذِي نَفْسِي بِيَدِهِ حَتَّى أَكُونَ أَحَبَّ إِلَيْكَ مِنْ نَفْسِكَ. فَقَالَ لَهُ عُمَرُ: فَإِنَّهُ الْآنَ وَاللَّهِ لأَنْتَ أَحَبُّ إِلَىَّ مِنْ نَفْسِي. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الْآنَ يَا عُمَرُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الأيمان والنذور (6632) عن يحيى بن سليمان، ثني ابن وهب، أخبرني حيوة قال: ثني أبو عقيل زهرة بن معبد، أنه سمع جده عبد الله بن هشام قال:فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن النبي ﷺ كان أحب الناس إلى عمر بن الخطاب من كل شيء حتى من نفسه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6632).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Was More Beloved to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb Than Everything, Even His Own Self","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Hishām reported: We were with the Prophet ﷺ while he was holding ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb by the hand. ʿUmar said to him: “O Messenger of Allah, you are certainly more beloved to me than everything except myself.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “No, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, not until I am more beloved to you than your own self.” ʿUmar then said: “Now, by Allah, you are more beloved to me than my own self.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Now, O ʿUmar.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",62],"full":1,"rep":[742,12442],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (6632)."},{"num":9863,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَقَدْ كَانَ فِيمَا قَبْلَكُمْ مِنَ الأُمَمِ مُحَدَّثُونَ، فَإِنْ يَكُ فِي أُمَّتِي أَحَدٌ فَإِنَّهُ عُمَرُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3689) عن يحيى بن قزعة، ثنا إبراهيم بن سعد، عن أبيه، عن أ بي سلمة، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لو كان في هذه الأمة محدَّثًا لكان عمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3689).","chapter_en":"If There Were a Muḥaddath in This Nation, It Would Be ʿUmar","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Among the nations before you were people who were divinely inspired. If there is anyone of this kind in my nation, it is ʿUmar.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",63],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3689)."},{"num":9864,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ كَانَ يَقُولُ:  قَدْ كَانَ يَكُونُ فِي الْأُمَمِ قَبْلَكُمْ مُحَدَّثُونَ، فَإِنْ يَكُنْ فِي أُمَّتِي مِنْهُمْ أَحَدٌ فَإِنَّ عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ مِنْهُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2398) عن أبي الطاهر أحمد بن عمرو بن سرح، ثنا عبد الله بن وهب، عن إبراهيم بن سعد، عن أبيه سعد بن إبراهيم، عن أ بي سلمة، عن عائشة، عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم.وكذلك رواه من وجهين آخرين عن ابن عجلان، عن سعد بن إبراهيم بهذا الإسناد مثله.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لو كان في هذه الأمة محدَّثًا لكان عمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2398).","chapter_en":"If There Were a Muḥaddath in This Nation, It Would Be ʿUmar","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported that the Prophet ﷺ used to say: “There were divinely inspired people among the nations before you. If there is anyone among my nation who is one of them, it is ʿUmar, for ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb is one of them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",64],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2398)."},{"num":9865,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ يَقُولُ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: بَيْنَمَا أَنَا نَائِمٌ رَأَيْتُ النَّاسَ يُعْرَضُونَ عليَّ وَعَلَيْهِمْ قُمُصٌ، مِنْهَا مَا يَبْلُغُ الثدي، وَمِنْهَا مَا يَبْلُغُ دُونَ ذَلِكَ، ومرَّ عليَّ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ، وَعَلَيْهِ قَمِيصٌ يجرُّه، قَالُوا: مَا أوَّلته يار سول اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: الدِّينَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التعبير (7008)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2390) كلاهما من طريق يعقوب بن إبراهيم، ثني أبي، عن صالح، عن ابن شهاب، ثني أبو أمامة بن سهل، أنه سمع أبا سعيد الخدري فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في صلابة عمر في الدين ونشره في أقطار الأرض","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7008) and Muslim (2390).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning ʿUmar’s Firmness in the Religion and Its Spread Throughout the Regions of the Earth","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “While I was sleeping, I saw the people being presented before me wearing shirts. Some of them reached their chests, while others were shorter than that. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb passed before me wearing a shirt which he was dragging.” They asked: “How did you interpret it, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “The religion.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “wearing a shirt which he was dragging,” contains an indication of the Islamic conquests that would occur during his caliphate and whose effects would remain for those who came after him.","Ibn Ḥajar related in Fatḥ al-Bārī (12/396) that the interpreters of dreams agreed that a shirt represents religion and that its length indicates the lasting influence of its wearer after his death."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",65],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7008)، ومسلم (2390)."},{"num":9866,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عُمَرَ أَنَّ ابْنَ عُمَرَ، قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: بَيْنَا أَنَا نَائِمٌ أُتِيتُ بِقَدَحِ لَبَنٍ، فَشَرِبْتُ حَتَّى إِنِّي لأَرَى الرِّيَّ يَخْرُجُ فِي أَظْفَارِي، ثُمَّ أَعْطَيْتُ فَضْلِي عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ. قَالُوا: فَمَا أَوَّلْتَهُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: الْعِلْمَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في العلم (82)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2391) كلاهما من طريق ابن شهاب، عن حمزة بن عبد الله بن عمر، أن ابن عمر قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في غزارة علم عمر بن الخطاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (82) and Muslim (2391).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Abundance of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Knowledge","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “While I was sleeping, I was brought a cup of milk. I drank from it until I could see the signs of satiation emerging through my fingernails. I then gave what remained of it to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.” They asked: “How did you interpret it, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Knowledge.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",66],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (82)، ومسلم (2391)."},{"num":9867,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابْنِ عُمَرَأَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ فِي النَّوْمِ أَنِّي أُعْطِيتُ عُسًّا مَمْلُوءًا لَبَنًا، فَشَرِبْتُ حَتَّى تَمَلَّأْتُ، حَتَّى رَأَيْتُهُ يَجْرِي فِي عُرُوقِي بَيْنَ الْجِلْدِ وَاللَّحْمِ، فَفَضَلَتْ فَضْلَةٌ فَأَعْطَيْتُهَا عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ. فَأَوَّلُوهَا، قَالُوا: يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ، هَذَا عِلْمٌ أَعْطَاكَهُ اللَّهُ فَمَلَأَكَ مِنْهُ، فَفَضَلَتْ فَضْلَةٌ فَأَعْطَيْتَهَا عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ. فَقَالَ: أَصَبْتُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه عبد الله بن أحمد في زوائده على فضائل الصحابة (319) عن محمد بن أبي بكر بن علي المقدمي-، ورواه الطبراني في الكبير (13155)، وصحّحه الحاكم (4496) من طريق عمرو بن عون الأوسطي كلاهما (محمد المقدمي وعمرو الواسطي)، من طريق معتمر بن سليمان قال: سمعت عبيد الله بن عمر يحدث عن أبي بكر بن سالم (هو ابن عبد الله بن عمر)، عن أبيه، عن ابن عمر فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في غزارة علم عمر بن الخطاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad in his additions to Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (319).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Abundance of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Knowledge","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I saw in a dream that I was given a large vessel filled with milk. I drank until I was completely filled, to the point that I saw it flowing through my veins between my skin and flesh. Some remained, so I gave it to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb. Interpret it.” They said: “O Prophet of Allah, this is knowledge which Allah gave you and with which He filled you. Some of it remained, so you gave it to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.” He said: “You are correct.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",67],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه عبد الله بن أحمد في زوائده على «فضائل الصحابة» (319)."},{"num":9868,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سَعْدِ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ قَالَ: اسْتَأْذَنَ عُمَرُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَعِنْدَهُ نِسَاءٌ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ يُكَلِّمْنَهُ وَيَسْتَكْثِرْنَهُ، عَالِيَةً أَصْوَاتُهُنَّ، فَلَمَّا اسْتَأْذَنَ عُمَرُ، قُمْنَ يَبْتَدِرْنَ الْحِجَابَ، فَأَذِنَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَضْحَكُ، فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: أَضْحَكَ اللَّهُ سِنَّكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. قَالَ: عَجِبْتُ مِنْ هَؤُلاَءِ اللاَّتِي كُنَّ عِنْدِي، فَلَمَّا سَمِعْنَ صَوْتَكَ ابْتَدَرْنَ الْحِجَابَ. قَالَ عُمَرُ: فَأَنْتَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ كُنْتَ أَحَقَّ أَنْ يَهَبْنَ. ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَىْ عَدُوَّاتِ أَنْفُسِهِنَّ، أَتَهَبْنَنِي وَلاَ تَهَبْنَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ قُلْنَ: نَعَمْ، أَنْتَ أَفَظُّ وَأَغْلَظُ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: وَالَّذِي نَفْسِي بِيَدِهِ، مَا لَقِيَكَ الشَّيْطَانُ قَطُّ سَالِكًا فَجًّا إِلاَّ سَلَكَ فَجًّا غَيْرَ فَجِّكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في بدء الخلق (3294)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2396) كلاهما من طريق إبراهيم بن سعد، عن صالح، عن ابن شهاب، أخبرني عبد الحميد بن عبد الرحمن بن زيد، أن محمد بن سعد بن أبي وقاص أخبره، أن أباه سعد بن أبي وقاص قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب هيبة عمر بن الخطاب في الجن والإنس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3294) and Muslim (2396).","chapter_en":"The Awe That ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb Inspired Among Jinn and Humankind","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ reported: ʿUmar sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while some women of Quraysh were with him, speaking to him, asking him for more and raising their voices over his voice. When ʿUmar sought permission to enter, they hurried to conceal themselves behind the curtain. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted him to enter while laughing. ʿUmar said: “May Allah keep you smiling, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “I was astonished by these women who were with me. As soon as they heard your voice, they hurried behind the curtain.” ʿUmar said: “You, O Messenger of Allah, were more deserving of being held in awe by them.” He then addressed the women: “O enemies of your own souls! Do you fear me but do not fear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” They replied: “Yes, for you are harsher and sterner than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in Whose hand is my soul, Satan has never encountered you travelling along a mountain pass except that he took a different pass from yours.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",68],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3294)، ومسلم (2396)."},{"num":9869,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ أَنَّ عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ جَاءَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَعِنْدَهُ نِسْوَةٌ قَدْ رَفَعْنَ أَصْوَاتَهُنَّ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَلَمَّا اسْتَأْذَنَ عُمَرُ ابْتَدَرْنَ الْحِجَابَ، فَذَكَرَ نَحْوَ حَدِيثِ سعد بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ المتقدم."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2397) عن هارون بن معروف، حدثنا به عبد العزيز بن محمد، أخبرني سهيل، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب هيبة عمر بن الخطاب في الجن والإنس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2397).","chapter_en":"The Awe That ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb Inspired Among Jinn and Humankind","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while some women were with him and had raised their voices in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When ʿUmar sought permission to enter, they hurried behind the curtain. He then related a report similar to the preceding hadith of Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",69],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2397)."},{"num":9870,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ: كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جَالِسًا فَسَمِعْنَا لَغَطًا وَصَوْتَ صِبْيَانٍ، فَقَامَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَإِذَا حَبَشِيَّةٌ تُزْفِنُ وَالصِّبْيَانُ حَوْلَهَا، فَقَالَ: يَا عَائِشَةُ تَعَالَىْ فَانْظُرِي. فَجِئْتُ فَوَضَعْتُ لَحْيَىَّ عَلَى مَنْكِبِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَجَعَلْتُ أَنْظُرَ إِلَيْهَا مَا بَيْنَ الْمَنْكِبِ إِلَى رَأْسِهِ، فَقَالَ لِي: أَمَا شَبِعْتِ، أَمَا شَبِعْتِ. قَالَتْ فَجَعَلْتُ أَقُولُ لاَ لأَنْظُرَ مَنْزِلَتِي عِنْدَهُ، إِذْ طَلَعَ عُمَرُ قَالَ فَارْفَضَّ النَّاسُ عَنْهَا، قَالَتْ: فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنِّي لأَنْظُرُ إِلَى شَيَاطِينِ الإِنْسِ وَالْجِنِّ قَدْ فَرُّوا مِنْ عُمَرَ. قَالَتْ فَرَجَعْتُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3691)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8908) كلاهما من طريق زيد بن حباب، أخبرني خارجة بن عبد الله بن سليمان بن زيد بن ثابت، أخبرنا يزيد بن رومان، عن عروة، عن عائشة فذكرته.وقال الترمذي: \" حسن صحيح غريب من هذا الوجه\".","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب هيبة عمر بن الخطاب في الجن والإنس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3691) and al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8908). Al-Tirmidhī said: “good authentic hadith.”","chapter_en":"The Awe That ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb Inspired Among Jinn and Humankind","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting when we heard a commotion and the voices of children. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and saw an Abyssinian woman dancing while the children were gathered around her. He said: “O ʿĀ’ishah, come and watch.” I came and placed my chin upon the shoulder of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I began watching her from the space between his shoulder and his head. He asked me: “Have you not had enough? Have you not had enough?” I continued saying, “No,” because I wanted to see my standing with him. Then ʿUmar appeared, and the people scattered from around her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I can indeed see the devils among humankind and the jinn fleeing from ʿUmar.” She said: “I then returned.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word “tazfin” means that she was dancing. The original meaning of zafn is play and vigorous movement. The phrase “the people scattered from around her” means that they dispersed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",70],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3691)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8908). وقال الترمذي: «حسن صحيح»."},{"num":9871,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رضي الله عنه، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللهِ ﷺ: مَا سَلَكَ عُمَرُ فَجًّا إِلَّا سَلَكَ الشَّيْطَانُ فَجًّا غَيْرَهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي عاصم في السنة (1295)، والبزار (9088) كلاهما من طرق عن عبد العزيز بن محمد (هو الدراوردي)، عن سهيل بن أبي صالح، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب هيبة عمر بن الخطاب في الجن والإنس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (1295) and al-Bazzār (9088).","chapter_en":"The Awe That ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb Inspired Among Jinn and Humankind","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “ʿUmar never travelled along a mountain pass except that Satan took a different pass.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",71],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي عاصم في «السنة» (1295)، والبزار (9088)."},{"num":9872,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: رَأَيْتُنِي دَخَلْتُ الْجَنَّةَ، فَإِذَا أَنَا بِالرُّمَيْصَاءِ امْرَأَةِ أَبِي طَلْحَةَ، وَسَمِعْتُ خَشَفَةً، فَقُلْتُ: مَنْ هَذَا؟ فَقَالَ: هَذَا بِلاَلٌ. وَرَأَيْتُ قَصْرًا بِفِنَائِهِ جَارِيَةٌ، فَقُلْتُ: لِمَنْ هَذَا؟ فَقَالَ: لِعُمَرَ. فَأَرَدْتُ أَنْ أَدْخُلَهُ، فَأَنْظُرَ إِلَيْهِ، فَذَكَرْتُ غَيْرَتَكَ. فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: بِأُمِّي وَأَبِي يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَعَلَيْكَ أَغَارُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3679) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2394-20) كلاهما من حديث محمد بن المنكدر، عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره. وهذا لفظ البخاري، ولفظ مسلم نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في قصر عمر بن الخطاب في الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3679) and Muslim (2394, no. 20). This is the wording of al-Bukhārī, while Muslim’s wording is similar.","chapter_en":"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Palace in Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I saw myself entering Paradise, where I encountered al-Rumayṣāʾ, the wife of Abū Ṭalḥah. I heard the sound of footsteps and asked, ‘Who is this?’ He replied, ‘This is Bilāl.’ I also saw a palace with a young woman in its courtyard. I asked, ‘To whom does this belong?’ He replied, ‘To ʿUmar.’ I wanted to enter it and look inside, but I remembered your jealousy.” ʿUmar said: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! Would I be jealous concerning you?”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["It contains the wording:","“I entered Paradise and saw within it a house—or a palace…”","At its conclusion:","“ʿUmar wept and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, could anyone be jealous concerning you?’”","In another wording narrated by al-Bukhārī:","“I entered Paradise—or came to Paradise—and saw a palace. I asked, ‘To whom does this belong?’ They replied, ‘To ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.’ I wanted to enter it, and nothing prevented me except my knowledge of your jealousy.”","Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5226).","In another wording narrated by al-Bukhārī:","“I entered Paradise and found myself before a palace made of gold. I asked, ‘To whom does this belong?’ They replied, ‘To a man from Quraysh.’ Nothing prevented me from entering it…”","Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7024)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",72],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[16293],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3679)، ومسلم (20-2394)، وهذا لفظ البخاري، ولفظ مسلم نحوه."},{"num":9873,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: بَيْنَمَا نَحْنُ عِنْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جُلُوسٌ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: بَيْنَمَا أَنَا نَائِمٌ رَأَيْتُنِي فِي الْجَنَّةِ، فَإِذَا امْرَأَةٌ تَتَوَضَّأُ إِلَى جَانِبِ قَصْرٍ، فَقُلْتُ: لِمَنْ هَذَا؟ قَالَ هَذَا لِعُمَرَ. فَذَكَرْتُ غَيْرَتَهُ، فَوَلَّيْتُ مُدْبِرًا. فَبَكَى عُمَرُ وَهْوَ فِي الْمَجْلِسِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَوَعَلَيْكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَغَارُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في النكاح (5227)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2395) كلاهما من طريق عبد الله بن وهب، عن يونس، عن الزهري قال: أخبرني ابن المسيب، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.واللفظ للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في قصر عمر بن الخطاب في الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5227) and Muslim (2395). The wording is that of al-Bukhārī.","chapter_en":"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Palace in Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “While I was sleeping, I saw myself in Paradise. There was a woman performing ablution beside a palace. I asked, ‘To whom does this belong?’ They replied, ‘It belongs to ʿUmar.’ I remembered his jealousy, so I turned away.” ʿUmar, who was present in the gathering, wept and said: “Would I be jealous concerning you, O Messenger of Allah?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",73],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5227)، ومسلم (2395). واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":9874,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: دَخَلْتُ الْجَنَّةَ، فَإِذَا أَنَا بِقَصْرٍ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ، فَقُلْتُ: لِمَنْ هَذَا الْقَصْرُ؟ قَالُوا: لِشَابٍّ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ، فَظَنَنْتُ أني أَنَا هُوَ، فَقُلْتُ: لِمَنْ هُوَ؟ فَقَالُوا: لِعُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ، قَالَ: فَلَوْلَا مَا عَلِمْتُ مِنْ غَيْرَتِكَ لَدَخَلْتُهُ، فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: عَلَيْكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَغَارُ؟"],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3688)، والنسائي في فضائل الصحابة (26)، وأحمد (12046) - واللفظ له -، وصحّحه ابن حبان (6887) كلهم من طرق عن حميد، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في قصر عمر بن الخطاب في الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3688), who authenticated it, and Aḥmad (12046), whose wording is cited here.","chapter_en":"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Palace in Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I entered Paradise and found myself before a palace made of gold. I asked, ‘To whom does this palace belong?’ They replied, ‘To a young man from Quraysh.’ I thought that I was that man, so I asked, ‘To whom does it belong?’ They replied, ‘To ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.’” He continued: “Had it not been for what I knew of your jealousy, I would have entered it.” ʿUmar said: “Would I be jealous concerning you, O Messenger of Allah?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",74],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[16294],"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3688)، وصححه، وأحمد (12046) -واللفظ له-."},{"num":9875,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ بُرَيْدَةَ بْنِ الحصيب قَالَ: أَصْبَحَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَدَعَا بِلَالًا فَقَالَ: يَا بِلَالُ، بِمَ سَبَقْتَنِي إِلَى الْجَنَّةِ؟ مَا دَخَلْتُ الْجَنَّةَ قَطُّ إِلَّا سَمِعْتُ خَشْخَشَتَكَ أَمَامِي، إِنِّي دَخَلْتُ الْبَارِحَةَ الْجَنَّةَ فَسَمِعْتُ خَشْخَشَتَكَ، فَأَتَيْتُ عَلَى قَصْرٍ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ مُرْتَفِعٍ مشرَّف، فَقُلْتُ: لِمَنْ هَذَا الْقَصْرُ؟ فَقَالُوا: لِرَجُلٍ مِنَ الْعَرَبِ.قُلْتُ: أَنَا عَرَبِيٌّ، لِمَنْ هَذَا الْقَصْرُ؟ قَالُوا: لِرَجُلٍ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ مِنْ أُمَّةِ مُحَمَّدٍ، قُلْتُ: فَأَنَا مُحَمَّدٌ، لِمَنْ هَذَا الْقَصْرُ؟ قَالُوا: لِعُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ.فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَوْلَا غَيْرَتُكَ يَا عُمَرُ، لَدَخَلْتُ الْقَصْرَ.فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، مَا كُنْتُ لِأَغَارَ عَلَيْكَ.","قَالَ: وَقَالَ لِبِلالٍ: بِمَ سَبَقْتَنِي إِلَى الجنة؟.قال: مَا أَحْدَثْتَ إِلَّا تَوَضَّأْتَ، وَصَلَّيْتُ ركعتين.فقال رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّم: بِهَذَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3689)، و أحمد (22996)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (7086) كلهم من طريق حسين بن واقد قال: حدثني عبد الله بن بريدة، حدثني أبي بريدة (هو ابن الحصيب) فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في قصر عمر بن الخطاب في الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3689) and Aḥmad (22996), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7086), through Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Buraydah, from his father Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb.","chapter_en":"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Palace in Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb reported: One morning, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned Bilāl and said: “O Bilāl, by what deed did you precede me into Paradise? I have never entered Paradise without hearing the sound of your footsteps before me. Last night, I entered Paradise and heard your footsteps. I then came upon a lofty, elevated palace made of gold. I asked, ‘To whom does this palace belong?’ They replied, ‘To an Arab man.’ I said, ‘I am an Arab. To whom does this palace belong?’ They replied, ‘To a Muslim man from the nation of Muḥammad.’ I said, ‘I am Muḥammad. To whom does this palace belong?’ They replied, ‘To ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “Had it not been for your jealousy, O ʿUmar, I would have entered the palace.” ʿUmar said: “O Messenger of Allah, I would never be jealous concerning you.” He then asked Bilāl: “By what deed did you precede me into Paradise?” Bilāl replied: “Whenever I entered a state of minor ritual impurity, I performed ablution and prayed two rakʿahs.”","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It was because of this.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["He also said:","“The meaning of the statement in this hadith, ‘Last night, I entered Paradise,’ is that he saw in a dream that he had entered Paradise. This is how it has been narrated in some versions of the hadith.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",75],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3689)، وأحمد (22996)، وصححه ابن حبان (7086)."},{"num":9876,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ عُمَرُ: وَافَقْتُ رَبِّي فِي ثَلاَثٍ، فَقُلْتُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، لَوِ اتَّخَذْنَا مِنْ مَقَامِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ مُصَلًّى، فَنَزَلَتْ: ﴿وَاتَّخِذُوا مِنْ مَقَامِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ مُصَلًّى﴾ [سورة البقرة: 125]} وَآيَةُ الْحِجَابِ، قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، لَوْ أَمَرْتَ نِسَاءَكَ أَنْ يَحْتَجِبْنَ، فَإِنَّهُ يُكَلِّمُهُنَّ الْبَرُّ وَالْفَاجِرُ. فَنَزَلَتْ آيَةُ الْحِجَابِ، وَاجْتَمَعَ نِسَاءُ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي الْغَيْرَةِ عَلَيْهِ، فَقُلْتُ لَهُنَّ: عَسَى رَبُّهُ إِنْ طَلَّقَكُنَّ أَنْ يُبَدِّلَهُ أَزْوَاجًا خَيْرًا مِنْكُنَّ. فَنَزَلَتْ هَذِهِ الآيَةُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الصلاة (402) عن عمرو بن عون، ثنا هشيم، عن حميد، عن أنس قال: فذكره، واللفظ له.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في موافقات عمر بن الخطاب ربه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (402) and Muslim (2399).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Instances in Which ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Opinions Corresponded with His Lord’s Revelation","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas reported that ʿUmar said: “My opinion corresponded with my Lord’s revelation on three occasions. I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, if only we were to take the Station of Abraham as a place of prayer.’ Then the following was revealed: ‘Take the Station of Abraham as a place of prayer.’ [Al-Baqarah 2:125] Regarding the verse of the veil, I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, if only you would command your wives to observe the veil, for both the righteous and the wicked speak to them.’ Then the verse of the veil was revealed. The wives of the Prophet ﷺ also united in their jealousy concerning him, so I said to them: ‘Perhaps, if he divorces you, his Lord will replace you with wives better than you.’ [Al-Taḥrīm 66:5] Then this verse was revealed.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording narrated by al-Bukhārī (4483):","“I heard that the Prophet ﷺ had reproached some of his wives, so I entered upon them and said:","‘Either you desist, or Allah will certainly give His Messenger ﷺ wives better than you in your place.’","I continued until I came to one of his wives. She said:","‘O ʿUmar, does the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not possess sufficient ability to admonish his wives, such that you must admonish them?’","Allah then revealed:","‘Perhaps, if he divorces you, his Lord will replace you with wives better than you…’ [Al-Taḥrīm 66:5]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13589],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (402)، ومسلم (2399)."},{"num":9877,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: خَرَجَتْ سَوْدَةُ بَعْدَ مَا ضُرِبَ الْحِجَابُ لِحَاجَتِهَا، وَكَانَتِ امْرَأَةً جَسِيمَةً، لاَ تَخْفَى عَلَى مَنْ يَعْرِفُهَا، فَرَآهَا عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ، فَقَالَ: يَا سَوْدَةُ أَمَا وَاللَّهِ مَا تَخْفَيْنَ عَلَيْنَا، فَانْظُرِي كَيْفَ تَخْرُجِينَ، قَالَتْ فَانْكَفَأَتْ رَاجِعَةً، وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي بَيْتِي، وَإِنَّهُ لَيَتَعَشَّى. وَفِي يَدِهِ عَرْقٌ، فَدَخَلَتْ فَقَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنِّي خَرَجْتُ لِبَعْضِ حَاجَتِي، فَقَالَ لِي عُمَرُ: كَذَا وَكَذَا. قَالَتْ فَأَوْحَى اللَّهُ إِلَيْهِ، ثُمَّ رُفِعَ عَنْهُ، وَإِنَّ الْعَرْقَ فِي يَدِهِ مَا وَضَعَهُ، فَقَالَ: إِنَّهُ قَدْ أُذِنَ لَكُنَّ أَنْ تَخْرُجْنَ لِحَاجَتِكُنَّ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4795)، ومسلم في السلام (2170-17) كلاهما من طرق عن أبي أسامة، عن هشام، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في موافقات عمر بن الخطاب ربه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4795) and Muslim (2170, no. 17).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Instances in Which ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Opinions Corresponded with His Lord’s Revelation","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reported: Sawdah went out to attend to her needs after the command concerning the veil had been revealed. She was a large woman and could not remain unrecognized by anyone who knew her. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb saw her and said: “O Sawdah, by Allah, you cannot remain unrecognized by us, so consider carefully how you go out.” She turned back while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in my house, eating his evening meal and holding a bone with meat upon it. She entered and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I went out to attend to some of my needs, and ʿUmar said such-and-such to me.” Allah then sent revelation to him. When the state of revelation had passed, the bone was still in his hand, and he had not put it down. He said: “You have been granted permission to go out to attend to your needs.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["This is the wording of al-Bukhārī, while Muslim’s wording is similar. It contains:","“She was a woman who surpassed other women in physical stature.”","In another wording:","“The wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go out at night when they needed to relieve themselves, proceeding to al-Manāṣiʿ, which was a wide, open plain. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb used to say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ:","‘Veil your wives.’","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do so. One night, Sawdah bint Zamʿah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, went out at the time of the evening prayer. She was a tall woman. ʿUmar called out to her:","‘Take heed, Sawdah! We have recognized you.’","He did so out of his desire that the command concerning the veil be revealed. Allah Almighty then revealed the command concerning the veil.”","Narrated by al-Bukhārī (146) and Muslim (2170, no. 18)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",77],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13092],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4795)، ومسلم (17-2170)."},{"num":9878,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ قَالَ: لَمَّا تُوُفِّيَ عبدالله بْنُ أُبَيٍّ ابْنُ سَلُولَ جَاءَ ابْنُهُ عبدالله بْنُ عبدالله إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَسَأَلَهُ أَنْ يُعْطِيَهُ قَمِيصَهُ أَنْ يُكَفِّنَ فِيهِ أَبَاهُ، فَأَعْطَاهُ، ثُمَّ سَأَلَهُ أَنْ يُصَلِّيَ عَلَيْهِ، فَقَامَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِيُصَلِّيَ عَلَيْهِ، فَقَامَ عُمَرُ فَأَخَذَ بِثَوْبِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَتُصَلِّي عَلَيْهِ، وَقَدْ نَهَاكَ اللهُ أَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلَيْهِ؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّمَا خيرَّني اللَّهُ، فَقَالَ: ﴿اسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ أَوْ لَا تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ إِنْ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ سَبْعِينَ مَرَّةً﴾ [التوبة: ٨٠] الآية، وسأزيده عَلَى سَبْعِينَ.قَالَ: إِنَّهُ مُنَافِقٌ، فَصَلَّى عَلَيْهِ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: ﴿لَا تُصَلِّ عَلَى أَحَدٍ مِنْهُمْ مَاتَ أَبَدًا وَلَا تَقُمْ عَلَى قَبْرِهِ﴾ [التوبة: ٨٤]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4670)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2400) كلاهما من طريق أبي أسامة، ثنا عبيد الله، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في موافقات عمر بن الخطاب ربه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4670) and Muslim (2400).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Instances in Which ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Opinions Corresponded with His Lord’s Revelation","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported: When ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl died, his son, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him to give him his shirt so that he could shroud his father in it. He gave it to him. He then asked him to perform the funeral prayer over his father. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to perform the prayer over him, but ʿUmar stood and took hold of the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: “O Messenger of Allah, will you pray over him when Allah has forbidden you to pray over him?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Allah has only given me a choice, for He said: ‘Ask forgiveness for them, or do not ask forgiveness for them. Even if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times…’ [Al-Tawbah 9:80]—and I shall ask more than seventy times.” ʿUmar said: “He is a hypocrite.” Nevertheless, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the funeral prayer over him. Allah Almighty then revealed: “Never perform the funeral prayer over any of them who dies, nor stand at his grave.” [Al-Tawbah 9:84]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4670)، ومسلم (2400)."},{"num":9879,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: لَمَّا مَاتَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ أُبَىٍّ ابْنُ سَلُولَ دُعِيَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِيُصَلِّيَ عَلَيْهِ، فَلَمَّا قَامَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَثَبْتُ إِلَيْهِ، فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَتُصَلِّي عَلَى ابْنِ أُبَىٍّ، وَقَدْ قَالَ يَوْمَ كَذَا: كَذَا وَكَذَا، قَالَ: أُعَدِّدُ عَلَيْهِ قَوْلَهُ، فَتَبَسَّمَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَقَالَ: أَخِّرْ عَنِّي، يَا عُمَرُ. فَلَمَّا أَكْثَرْتُ عَلَيْهِ قَالَ: إِنِّي خُيِّرْتُ فَاخْتَرْتُ، لَوْ أَعْلَمُ أَنِّي إِنْ زِدْتُ عَلَى السَّبْعِينَ يُغْفَرْ لَهُ لَزِدْتُ عَلَيْهَا. قَالَ فَصَلَّى عَلَيْهِ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ، فَلَمْ يَمْكُثْ إِلاَّ يَسِيرًا حَتَّى نَزَلَتِ الآيَتَانِ مِنْ بَرَاءَةَ: ﴿وَلاَ تُصَلِّ عَلَى أَحَدٍ مِنْهُمْ مَاتَ أَبَدًا} إِلَى﴾ [سورة التوبة: 84] قَوْلِهِ: {وَهُمْ فَاسِقُونَ} قَالَ: فَعَجِبْتُ بَعْدُ مِنْ جُرْأَتِي عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَاللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4671) عن يحيى بن بكير، ثنا الليث، عن عُقيل، وقال غيره: حدثني الليث، ثني عُقيل، عن ابن شهاب قال: أخبرني عبيد الله بن عبد الله، عن ابن عباس، عن عمر بن الخطاب قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في موافقات عمر بن الخطاب ربه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4671).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Instances in Which ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Opinions Corresponded with His Lord’s Revelation","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb reported: When ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was called to perform the funeral prayer over him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to do so, I sprang toward him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you pray over Ibn Ubayy when he said such-and-such on such-and-such a day?” I began recounting his statements to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said: “Stand back from me, O ʿUmar.” When I persisted, he said: “I was given a choice, and I have chosen. If I knew that he would be forgiven if I asked more than seventy times, I would ask more than seventy times.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then performed the funeral prayer over him and departed. Only a short time passed before the two verses from Sūrat Barā’ah were revealed: “Never perform the funeral prayer over any of them who dies…” through His words: “…while they were defiantly disobedient.” [Al-Tawbah 9:84] ʿUmar said: “Afterward, I was astonished at my boldness toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Allah and His Messenger know best.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[12502],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4671)."},{"num":9880,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ جَعَلَ الْحَقَّ عَلَى قَلْبِ عُمَرَ وَلِسَانِهِ قَالَ: وَقَالَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ: مَا نَزَلَ بِالنَّاسِ أَمْرٌ قَطُّ فَقَالُوا فِيهِ: وَقَالَ فِيهِ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ: - أَوْ قَالَ عُمَرُ، - إِلَّا نَزَلَ الْقُرْآنُ عَلَى نَحْوٍ مِمَّا قَالَ عُمَرُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3682) وأحمد (5697، 5145) وابنه في زوائد الفضائل (395) وصحّحه ابن حبان (6895) كلهم من طرق عن نافع، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إن الله جعل الحق على لسان عمر وقلبه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3682), Aḥmad (5145, 5697), and ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad in his additions to al-Faḍāʾil (395), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6895), through routes from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar.","chapter_en":"Allah Placed the Truth upon ʿUmar’s Tongue and in His Heart","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah Almighty has placed the truth in ʿUmar’s heart and upon his tongue.” Ibn ʿUmar also said: “Whenever an issue arose among the people and they expressed an opinion concerning it, and ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb also expressed his opinion—or whenever ʿUmar expressed an opinion—the Qur’an was revealed in accordance with what ʿUmar had said.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The meaning of the hadith is that Allah inspired him with the truth and enabled him to speak it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",80],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3682)، وأحمد (5145، 5697)، وعبد الله بن أحمد في زوائد الفضائل (395)، وصححه ابن حبان (6895)."},{"num":9881,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ غُضَيْفِ بْنِ الْحَارِثِ، أَنَّهُ مَرَّ بِعُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ، فَقَالَ: نِعْمَ الْفَتَى غُضَيْفٌ، فَلَقِيَهُ أَبُو ذَرٍّ، فَقَالَ: أَيْ أُخَيَّ اسْتَغْفِرْ لِي. قَالَ: أَنْتَ صَاحِبُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَأَنْتَ أَحَقُّ أَنْ تَسْتَغْفِرَ لِي! فَقَالَ: إِنِّي سَمِعْتُ عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ يَقُولُ: نِعْمَ الْفَتَى غُضَيْفٌ، وَقَدْ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ ضَرَبَ بِالْحَقِّ عَلَى لِسَانِ عُمَرَ وَقَلْبِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2962) وابن ماجه (108) وأحمد (21295، 21457) واللفظ له، وصحّحه الحاكم (3/87) كلهم من طرق عن غضيف بن الحارث، فذكره.وبعضهم لم يذكر القصة.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إن الله جعل الحق على لسان عمر وقلبه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (2962), Ibn Mājah (108), and Aḥmad (21295, 21457)—whose wording is cited here—and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (3/87), through routes from Ghuḍayf ibn al-Ḥārith. Some routes omit the story; the chain is sound.","chapter_en":"Allah Placed the Truth upon ʿUmar’s Tongue and in His Heart","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ghuḍayf ibn al-Ḥārith reported that he passed by ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, who said: “What an excellent young man Ghuḍayf is!” Ghuḍayf later met Abū Dharr, who said to him: “My brother, ask Allah to forgive me.” Ghuḍayf replied: “You are a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you are more deserving of asking forgiveness for me!” Abū Dharr said: “I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb say, ‘What an excellent young man Ghuḍayf is!’ And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Allah has firmly established the truth upon ʿUmar’s tongue and in his heart.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",81],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2962)، وابن ماجه (108)، وأحمد (21295، 21457) -واللفظ له-، وصححه الحاكم (3/87)."},{"num":9882,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ جَعَلَ الْحَقَّ عَلَى لِسَانِ عُمَرَ وَقَلْبِهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه عبد الله بن أحمد في زوائده على الفضائل (315) وصحّحه ابن حبان (6889) كلاهما من طريق عبد العزيز بن محمد الدراوردي، أخبرني سهيل بن أبي صالح، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب إن الله جعل الحق على لسان عمر وقلبه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad in his additions to al-Faḍāʾil (315), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6889).","chapter_en":"Allah Placed the Truth upon ʿUmar’s Tongue and in His Heart","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has placed the truth upon ʿUmar’s tongue and in his heart.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",82],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه عبد الله بن أحمد في زوائده على «الفضائل» (315)، وصححه ابن حبان (6889)."},{"num":9883,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، - أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَا كَانَ نَبِيٌّ قَطُّ إِلَّا فِي أُمَّتِهِ مُعَلِّمٌ أَوْ مُعَلِّمَانِ، وَإِنْ يَكُنْ فِي أُمَّتِي مِنْهُمْ أَحَدٌ فَهُوَ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ، إِنَّ الْحَقَّ عَلَى لِسَانِ عُمَرَ وَقَلْبِهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه القطيعي في زوائده على فضائل الصحابة (518) والطبراني في الأوسط (9133) كلاهما من طريق عبد الرحمن بن أبي الزناد، عن عبد الله بن محمد بن أبي عتيق، عن أبيه، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب إن الله جعل الحق على لسان عمر وقلبه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Qaṭīʿī in his additions to Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (518), and by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (9133).","chapter_en":"Allah Placed the Truth upon ʿUmar’s Tongue and in His Heart","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There has never been a prophet except that within his nation there was one man—or two men—who were divinely instructed. If there is anyone of this kind in my nation, it is ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb. Indeed, the truth is upon ʿUmar’s tongue and in his heart.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",83],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه القطيعي في زوائده على «فضائل الصحابة» (518)، والطبراني في «الأوسط» (9133)."},{"num":9884,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حُذَيْفَةَ قَالَ:  كُنَّا عِنْدَ عُمَرَ فَقَالَ: أَيُّكُمْ يَحْفَظُ حَدِيثَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي الْفِتْنَةِ كَمَا قَالَ؟ قَالَ: فَقُلْتُ: أَنَا. قَالَ: إِنَّكَ لَجَرِيءٌ، وَكَيْفَ قَالَ؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: فِتْنَةُ الرَّجُلِ فِي أَهْلِهِ وَمَالِهِ وَنَفْسِهِ وَوَلَدِهِ وَجَارِهِ، يُكَفِّرُهَا الصِّيَامُ وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالصَّدَقَةُ وَالْأَمْرُ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَالنَّهْيُ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ. فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: لَيْسَ هَذَا أُرِيدُ، إِنَّمَا أُرِيدُ الَّتِي تَمُوجُ كَمَوْجِ الْبَحْرِ. قَالَ: فَقُلْتُ: مَا لَكَ وَلَهَا؟ يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ؟ إِنَّ بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَهَا بَابًا مُغْلَقًا. قَالَ: أَفَيُكْسَرُ الْبَابُ أَمْ يُفْتَحُ؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: لَا، بَلْ يُكْسَرُ. قَالَ: ذَلِكَ أَحْرَى أَنْ لَا يُغْلَقَ أَبَدًا.","قَالَ: فَقُلْنَا لِحُذَيْفَةَ: هَلْ كَانَ عُمَرُ يَعْلَمُ مَنِ الْبَابُ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ كَمَا يَعْلَمُ أَنَّ دُونَ غَدٍ اللَّيْلَةَ، إِنِّي حَدَّثْتُهُ حَدِيثًا لَيْسَ بالأغاليط.قال: فَهِبْنَا أَنْ نَسْأَلَ حُذَيْفَةَ: مَنِ الْبَابُ؟ فَقُلْنَا لِمَسْرُوقٍ: سَلْهُ، فَسَأَلَهُ، فَقَالَ: عُمَرُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في علامات النبوة (3568) ومسلم في الفتن (144: 26) كلاهما من طريق سليمان الأعمش، عن أبي وائل شقيق بن سلمة، عن حذيفة فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن عمر باب مغلق دون الفتن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3586) and Muslim (26, no. 144).","chapter_en":"ʿUmar Was a Closed Door against Tribulations","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥudhayfah reported: We were with ʿUmar when he asked: “Which of you has preserved the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning tribulation exactly as he stated it?” I replied: “I have.” He said: “You are certainly bold! How did he state it?” I replied: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘A man’s trials concerning his family, wealth, self, children, and neighbor are expiated by fasting, prayer, charity, enjoining what is right, and forbidding what is wrong.’” ʿUmar said: “That is not what I mean. I mean the tribulation that will surge like the waves of the sea.” I said: “Why should you be concerned about it, O Commander of the Believers? Between you and it is a closed door.” He asked: “Will the door be broken or opened?” I replied: “No, it will be broken.” He said: “Then it is more likely never to be closed again.” We later asked Ḥudhayfah: “Did ʿUmar know who the door was?” He replied: “Yes, just as he knew that tonight comes before tomorrow. I narrated to him a report containing no errors or riddles.”","We were too apprehensive to ask Ḥudhayfah who the door was, so we said to Masrūq: “Ask him.” Masrūq asked him, and he replied: “ʿUmar.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",84],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3568)، ومسلم (144: 26)."},{"num":9885,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي بُرْدَةَ بن أَبِي مُوسَى الأشعري قَالَ: قَالَ لِي عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ عُمَرَ: هَلْ تَدْرِي مَا قَالَ أَبِي لأَبِيكَ؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: لاَ.قَالَ: فَإِنَّ أَبِي قَالَ لأَبِيكَ: يَا أَبَا مُوسَى هَلْ يسرَُك إِسْلاَمُنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَهِجْرَتُنَا مَعَهُ، وَجِهَادُنَا مَعَهُ، وَعَمَلُنَا كُلُّهُ مَعَهُ، بَرَدَ لَنَا، وَأَنَّ كُلَّ عَمَلٍ عَمِلْنَاهُ بَعْدَهُ نَجَوْنَا مِنْهُ كَفَافًا رَأْسًا بِرَأْسٍ؟ فَقَالَ أَبِي: لاَ وَاللَّهِ، قَدْ جَاهَدْنَا بَعْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَصَلَّيْنَا، وَصُمْنَا، وَعَمِلْنَا خَيْرًا كَثِيرًا، وَأَسْلَمَ عَلَى أَيْدِينَا بَشَرٌ كَثِيرٌ، وَإِنَّا لَنَرْجُو ذَلِكَ، فَقَالَ أَبِي: لَكِنِّي أَنَا وَالَّذِي نَفْسُ عُمَرَ بِيَدِهِ لَوَدِدْتُ أَنَّ ذَلِكَ بَرَدَ لَنَا، وَأَنَّ كُلَّ شيء عَمِلْنَاهُ بعدُ نَجَوْنَا مِنْهُ كَفَافًا رَأْسًا بِرَأْسٍ.فَقُلْتُ: إِنَّ أَبَاكَ وَاللَّهِ خَيْرٌ مِنْ أَبِي."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3915) عن يحيى بن بشر، حدثنا روح، حدثنا عوف، عن معاوية بن قرة قال: حدثني أبو بردة بن أبي موسى الأشعري قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب تخوف عمر بعد رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3915). The phrase “was secured for us” means that it was firmly established for us. “Simply even” means equal, with neither gain nor loss.","chapter_en":"ʿUmar’s Fear concerning His Deeds after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Burdah ibn Abī Mūsā al-Ashʿarī reported: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar asked me: “Do you know what my father said to your father?” I replied: “No.” He said: “My father said to your father: ‘O Abū Mūsā, would it please you if our acceptance of Islam with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, our migration with him, our striving alongside him, and all our deeds with him were secured for us, while we escaped from every deed we performed after him neither rewarded nor punished—simply even, with nothing for us and nothing against us?’ “My father replied: ‘No, by Allah! After the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we fought in Allah’s cause, prayed, fasted, performed much good, and many people accepted Islam at our hands. We certainly hope to be rewarded for that.’ “Then my father said: ʿAs for me, by the One in Whose hand is ʿUmar’s soul, I wish that what we did with him had been secured for us and that we escaped from everything we did afterward simply even—with nothing for us and nothing against us.’” I said: “By Allah, your father was better than mine.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",85],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3915). قوله: «برد لنا» أي: ثبت لنا. وقوله: «كفافا» سواء بسواء."},{"num":9886,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سَعِيدِ بْنِ زَيْدٍ بن عمرو بْنِ نُفَيْلٍ فِي مَسْجِدِ الْكُوفَةِ: يَقُولُ وَاللَّهِ لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنِي وَإِنَّ عُمَرَ لَمُوثِقِي عَلَى الإِسْلاَمِ قَبْلَ أَنْ يُسْلِمَ، عُمَرُ، وَلَوْ أَنَّ أُحُدًا ارْفَضَّ لِلَّذِي صَنَعْتُمْ بِعُثْمَانَ لَكَانَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3862) عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا سفيان، عن إسماعيل، عن قيس قال: سمعت سعيد بن زيد بن عمرو بن نفيل في مسجد الكوفة يقول: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار عمر بن الخطاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3862).","chapter_en":"Reports concerning ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿīd ibn Zayd ibn ʿAmr ibn Nufayl said in the mosque of Kūfah: “By Allah, I remember when ʿUmar had bound me because of my acceptance of Islam, before he himself became Muslim. If Mount Uḥud had collapsed because of what you did to ʿUthmān, it would have been justified.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Another wording states:","“If only you had seen me when ʿUmar had bound me and his sister because of our acceptance of Islam, while he had not yet become Muslim! If Mount Uḥud had collapsed because of what you did to ʿUthmān, it would have been fully justified in collapsing.”","Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3867).","The phrase “had bound me because of Islam” means that he would tie him up because he had accepted Islam and beat him in an attempt to make him renounce it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",86],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9902],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3862). وفي لفظ: «لو رأيتني موثقي عمر على الإسلام أنا وأخته وما أسلم، ولو أن أحدا انقض لما صنعتم بعثمان لكان محقوقا أن ينقض». رواه البخاري (3867)."},{"num":9887,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبدالله بن مسعود قال: مَا زِلْنَا أَعِزَّةً مُنْذُ أَسْلَمَ عُمَرُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3684) عن محمد بن المثنى، ثنا يحيى، عن إسماعيل، ثنا قيس قال: قال عبد الله: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار عمر بن الخطاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3684).","chapter_en":"Reports concerning ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd said: “We have remained strong and honored ever since ʿUmar accepted Islam.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",87],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3684)."},{"num":9888,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي عُثْمَانَ، قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ ابْنَ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا إِذَا قِيلَ لَهُ: هَاجَرَ قَبْلَ أَبِيهِ يَغْضَبُ، قَالَ وَقَدِمْتُ أَنَا وَعُمَرُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَوَجَدْنَاهُ قَائِلاً، فَرَجَعْنَا إِلَى الْمَنْزِلِ، فَأَرْسَلَنِي عُمَرُ، وَقَالَ: اذْهَبْ فَانْظُرْ هَلِ اسْتَيْقَظَ، فَأَتَيْتُهُ، فَدَخَلْتُ عَلَيْهِ فَبَايَعْتُهُ، ثُمَّ انْطَلَقْتُ إِلَى عُمَرَ، فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ أَنَّهُ قَدِ اسْتَيْقَظَ، فَانْطَلَقْنَا إِلَيْهِ نُهَرْوِلُ هَرْوَلَةً حَتَّى دَخَلَ عَلَيْهِ فَبَايَعَهُ ثُمَّ بَايَعْتُهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3916) عن محمد بن صباح، أو بلغني عنه، حدثنا إسماعيل، عن عاصم، عن أبي عثمان قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار عمر بن الخطاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3916).","chapter_en":"Reports concerning ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū ʿUthmān reported: I heard Ibn ʿUmar become angry whenever it was said to him: “He migrated before his father.” He explained: “ʿUmar and I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found him taking his midday rest, so we returned home. ʿUmar then sent me, saying: ‘Go and see whether he has awakened.’ “I went to him, entered upon him, and pledged allegiance to him. I then went to ʿUmar and informed him that the Prophet ﷺ had awakened. We hurried to him at a brisk pace. ʿUmar entered and pledged allegiance to him, and then I pledged allegiance to him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",88],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3916)."},{"num":9889,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حُذَيْفَةَ، قَالَ: دُعِيَ عُمَرُ لِجِنَازَةٍ، فَخَرَجَ فِيهَا أَوْ يُرِيدُهَا، فَتَعَلَّقْتُ بِهِ، فَقُلْتُ: اجْلِسْ يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ! فَانْهَ عَنْ أُولئِكَ، فَقَالَ: نَشَدْتُكُ بِاللَّهِ أَنَا مِنْهُمْ؟ فَقَالَ: لا، وَلا أُبْرِئُ أَحَدًا بَعْدَكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البزار (2885) عن عبد الواحد بن غياث، أخبرنا عبد العزيز بن مسلم(هو القسملي)، أخبرنا الأعمش، عن أبي وائل، عن حذيفة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار عمر بن الخطاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bazzār (2885).","chapter_en":"Reports concerning ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān reported: ʿUmar was invited to attend a funeral. As he went out to attend it—or was about to do so—I took hold of him and said: “Remain seated, O Commander of the Believers, for the deceased is one of those people.” ʿUmar said: “I adjure you by Allah: am I one of them?” Ḥudhayfah replied: “No, but I will not declare anyone after you free of suspicion.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["This hadith contains an evident virtue of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb: his freedom from hypocrisy. The Prophet ﷺ had disclosed the names of the hypocrites to Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān and instructed him not to reveal them. For this reason, Ḥudhayfah was known as the keeper of the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The phrase “one of those people” means one of the hypocrites."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",89],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البزار (2885)."},{"num":9890,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ: يَقُولُ كَانَ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ إِذَا صَلَّى صَلَاةً جَلَسَ لِلنَّاسِ فَمَنْ كَانَتْ لَهُ حَاجَةٌ، كَلَّمَهُ، وَإِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ لِأَحَدٍ حَاجَةٌ قَامَ فَدَخَلَ، قَالَ: فَصَلَّى صَلَوَاتٍ لَا يَجْلِسُ لِلنَّاسِ فِيهِنَّ، قَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: فَحَضَرْتُ الْبَابَ، فَقُلْتُ: يَا يَرْفَأُ، أَبِأَمِيرِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ شَكَاةٌ؟ فَقَالَ: مَا بِأَمِيرِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ مِنْ شَكْوًى، فَجَلَسْتُ، فَجَاءَ عُثْمَانُ بْنُ عَفَّانَ فَجَلَسَ، فَخَرَجَ يَرْفَأُ، فَقَالَ: قُمْ يَا ابْنَ عَفَّانَ، قُمْ يَا ابْنَ عَبَّاسٍ، فَدَخَلْنَا عَلَى عُمَرَ، فَإِذَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ صُبَرٌ مِنْ مَالٍ، عَلَى كُلِّ صُبْرَةٍ مِنْهَا كِنْفٌ فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: إِنِّي نَظَرْتُ فِي أَهْلِ الْمَدِينَةِ، وَجَدْتُكُمَا مِنْ أَكْثَرِ أَهْلِهَا عَشِيرَةً، فَخُذَا هَذَا الْمَالَ فَاقْتَسِمَاهُ، فَمَا كَانَ مِنْ فَضْلٍ فَرُدَّا، فَأَمَّا عُثْمَانُ فَحَثَا، وَأَمَّا أَنَا فَجَثَوْتُ لِرُكْبَتَيَّ، وَقُلْتُ: وَإِنْ كَانَ نُقْصَانٌ رَدَدْتَ عَلَيْنَا، فَقَالَ: عُمَرُ نَشْنَشَةٌ مِنْ أَخْشَنَ، - يَعْنِي حَجَرًا مِنْ جَبَلٍ، - أَمَا كَانَ هَذَا عِنْدَ اللَّهِ إِذْ مُحَمَّدٌ وَأَصْحَابُهُ يَأْكُلُونَ الْقَدَّ، فَقُلْتُ: بَلَى، وَاللَّهِ لَقَدْ كَانَ هَذَا عِنْدَ اللَّهِ وَمُحَمَّدٌ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَيٌّ، وَلَوْ عَلَيْهِ فُتِحَ لَصَنَعَ فِيهِ غَيْرَ الَّذِي تَصْنَعُ، قَالَ: فَغَضِبَ عُمَرُ وَقَالَ: أَوْ صَنَعَ مَاذَا؟ قُلْتُ: إِذًا لَأَكَلَ وَأَطْعَمَنَا، قَالَ: فَنَشَجَ عُمَرُ حَتَّى اخْتَلَفَتْ أَضْلَاعُهُ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: وَدِدْتُ أَنِّي خَرَجْتُ مِنْهَا كَفَافًا لَا لِيَ وَلَا عَلَيَّ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الحميدي (30)، والبزار (209) كلاهما من طريق سفيان بن عيينة، عن عاصم بن كليب، عن أبيه، عن ابن عباس فذكره.واللفظ للحميدي.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار عمر بن الخطاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ḥumaydī (30) and al-Bazzār (209). The wording is that of al-Ḥumaydī.","chapter_en":"Reports concerning ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās reported: Whenever ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb finished a prayer, he would sit with the people so that anyone who had a need could speak to him. If no one had a need, he would rise and enter his residence. On several occasions, however, he prayed without sitting with the people afterward. Ibn ʿAbbās said: “I came to his door and asked, ‘O Yarfaʾ, is the Commander of the Believers ill?’ “He replied, ‘There is nothing wrong with the Commander of the Believers.’ “I sat down, and then ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān arrived and sat as well. Yarfaʾ came out and said, ‘Rise, Ibn ʿAffān; rise, Ibn ʿAbbās.’ “We entered upon ʿUmar and found piles of wealth before him, with a shoulder blade placed upon each pile. ʿUmar said: “‘I have considered the people of Madinah and found that you have two of its largest clans. Take this wealth and divide it between yourselves. If anything remains, return it.’ “ʿUthmān began scooping up the wealth, but I knelt upon my knees and asked: “‘If it falls short, will you give us more?’ “He replied: “‘A trait from Akhshan—a stone from a mountain! Was this wealth not with Allah when Muḥammad ﷺ and his Companions were eating dried strips of hide?’ “I said: “‘Yes, by Allah, this wealth was with Allah Almighty while Muḥammad ﷺ was alive. Had it been granted to him, he would have dealt with it differently from the way you are dealing with it.’ “ʿUmar became angry and said: “‘Tell me, what would he have done?’ “I replied: “‘He would have eaten from it and fed us as well.’ “ʿUmar then sobbed so intensely that his ribs shook, and he said: “‘I wish I could leave this matter simply even—with nothing for me and nothing against me.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",90],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الحميدي (30)، والبزار (209)، واللفظ للحميدي."},{"num":9891,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن زَيْدِ بن أَسْلَمَ حدَّث حَدَّثَهُ عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: سَأَلَنِي ابْنُ عُمَرَ عَنْ بَعْضِ، شَأْنِهِ ـ يَعْنِي عُمَرَ ـ فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ. فَقَالَ، مَا رَأَيْتُ أَحَدًا قَطُّ بَعْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ حِينَ قُبِضَ كَانَ أَجَدَّ وَأَجْوَدَ حَتَّى انْتَهَى مِنْ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3687) عن يحيى بن سليمان، ثني ابن وهب، ثني عمر بن محمد، أن زيد بن أسلم حدَّثه عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في جود عمر بن الخطاب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3687).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Generosity of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zayd ibn Aslam reported from his father: Ibn ʿUmar asked me about some of his father ʿUmar’s affairs, so I informed him. He then said: “Since the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, I have never seen anyone work with greater diligence and generosity, persevering until he completed what he undertook, than ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",91],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3687)."},{"num":9892,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَمْرِو بْنِ مَيْمُونٍ، قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَبْلَ أَنْ يُصَابَ بِأَيَّامٍ بِالْمَدِينَةِ وَقَفَ عَلَى حُذَيْفَةَ بْنِ الْيَمَانِ وَعُثْمَانَ بْنِ حُنَيْفٍ، قَالَ كَيْفَ فَعَلْتُمَا، أَتَخَافَانِ أَنْ تَكُونَا قَدْ حَمَّلْتُمَا الأَرْضَ مَا لاَ تُطِيقُ؟ قَالاَ: حَمَّلْنَاهَا أَمْرًا هِيَ لَهُ مُطِيقَةٌ، مَا فِيهَا كَبِيرُ فَضْلٍ. قَالَ انْظُرَا أَنْ تَكُونَا حَمَّلْتُمَا الأَرْضَ مَا لاَ تُطِيقُ، قَالَ: قَالاَ: لاَ. فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: لَئِنْ سَلَّمَنِي اللَّهُ لأَدَعَنَّ أَرَامِلَ أَهْلِ الْعِرَاقِ لاَ يَحْتَجْنَ إِلَى رَجُلٍ بَعْدِي أَبَدًا. قَالَ: فَمَا أَتَتْ عَلَيْهِ إِلاَّ رَابِعَةٌ حَتَّى أُصِيبَ. قَالَ: إِنِّي لَقَائِمٌ مَا بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَهُ إِلاَّ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ عَبَّاسٍ غَدَاةَ أُصِيبَ، وَكَانَ إِذَا مَرَّ بَيْنَ الصَّفَّيْنِ قَالَ: اسْتَوُوا. حَتَّى إِذَا لَمْ يَرَ فِيهِنَّ خَلَلاً تَقَدَّمَ فَكَبَّرَ، وَرُبَّمَا قَرَأَ سُورَةَ يُوسُفَ، أَوِ النَّحْلَ، أَوْ نَحْوَ ذَلِكَ، فِي الرَّكْعَةِ الْأُولَى حَتَّى يَجْتَمِعَ النَّاسُ، فَمَا هُوَ إِلاَّ أَنْ كَبَّرَ فَسَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ: قَتَلَنِي ـ أَوْ أَكَلَنِي ـ الْكَلْبُ. حِينَ طَعَنَهُ، فَطَارَ الْعِلْجُ بِسِكِّينٍ ذَاتِ طَرَفَيْنِ، لاَ يَمُرُّ عَلَى أَحَدٍ يَمِينًا وَلاَ شِمَالاً إِلاَّ طَعَنَهُ، حَتَّى طَعَنَ ثَلاَثَةَ عَشَرَ رَجُلاً، مَاتَ مِنْهُمْ سَبْعَةٌ، فَلَمَّا رَأَى ذَلِكَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ، طَرَحَ عَلَيْهِ بُرْنُسًا، فَلَمَّا ظَنَّ الْعِلْجُ أَنَّهُ مَأْخُوذٌ نَحَرَ نَفْسَهُ، وَتَنَاوَلَ عُمَرُ يَدَ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ عَوْفٍ فَقَدَّمَهُ، فَمَنْ يَلِي عُمَرَ فَقَدْ رَأَى الَّذِي أَرَى، وَأَمَّا نَوَاحِي الْمَسْجِدِ فَإِنَّهُمْ لاَ يَدْرُونَ، غَيْرَ أَنَّهُمْ قَدْ فَقَدُوا صَوْتَ عُمَرَ، وَهُمْ يَقُولُونَ: سُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ، سُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ. فَصَلَّى بِهِمْ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ صَلاَةً خَفِيفَةً، فَلَمَّا انْصَرَفُوا. قَالَ: يَا ابْنَ عَبَّاسٍ، انْظُرْ مَنْ قَتَلَنِي. فَجَالَ سَاعَةً، ثُمَّ جَاءَ، فَقَالَ: غُلاَمُ الْمُغِيرَةِ. قَالَ الصَّنَعُ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ قَاتَلَهُ اللَّهُ، لَقَدْ أَمَرْتُ بِهِ مَعْرُوفًا، الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي لَمْ يَجْعَلْ مَنِيَّتِي بِيَدِ رَجُلٍ يَدَّعِي الإِسْلاَمَ، قَدْ كُنْتَ أَنْتَ وَأَبُوكَ تُحِبَّانِ أَنْ تَكْثُرَ الْعُلُوجُ بِالْمَدِينَةِ، وَكَانَ {الْعَبَّاسُ} أَكْثَرَهُمْ رَقِيقًا. فَقَالَ: إِنْ شِئْتَ فَعَلْتُ. أَىْ: إِنْ شِئْتَ قَتَلْنَا. قَالَ: كَذَبْتَ، بَعْدَ مَا تَكَلَّمُوا بِلِسَانِكُمْ، وَصَلَّوْا قِبْلَتَكُمْ، وَحَجُّوا حَجَّكُمْ، فَاحْتُمِلَ إِلَى بَيْتِهِ، فَانْطَلَقْنَا مَعَهُ، وَكَأَنَّ النَّاسَ لَمْ تُصِبْهُمْ مُصِيبَةٌ قَبْلَ يَوْمَئِذٍ، فَقَائِلٌ يَقُولُ: لاَ بَأْسَ. وَقَائِلٌ يَقُولُ: أَخَافُ عَلَيْهِ، فَأُتِيَ بِنَبِيذٍ فَشَرِبَهُ، فَخَرَجَ مِنْ جَوْفِهِ، ثُمَّ أُتِيَ بِلَبَنٍ فَشَرِبَهُ، فَخَرَجَ مِنْ جُرْحِهِ، فَعَلِمُوا أَنَّهُ مَيِّتٌ، فَدَخَلْنَا عَلَيْهِ، وَجَاءَ النَّاسُ يُثْنُونَ عَلَيْهِ، وَجَاءَ رَجُلٌ شَابٌّ، فَقَالَ: أَبْشِرْ يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ بِبُشْرَى اللَّهِ لَكَ، مِنْ صُحْبَةِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَقَدَمٍ فِي الإِسْلاَمِ مَا قَدْ عَلِمْتَ، ثُمَّ وَلِيتَ فَعَدَلْتَ، ثُمَّ شَهَادَةٌ. قَالَ: وَدِدْتُ أَنَّ ذَلِكَ كَفَافٌ، لاَ عَلَىَّ وَلاَ لِي. فَلَمَّا أَدْبَرَ، إِذَا إِزَارُهُ يَمَسُّ الأَرْضَ. قَالَ: رُدُّوا عَلَىَّ الْغُلاَمَ، قَالَ: ابْنَ أَخِي ارْفَعْ ثَوْبَكَ، فَإِنَّهُ أَبْقَى لِثَوْبِكَ، وَأَتْقَى لِرَبِّكَ، يَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عُمَرَ، انْظُرْ مَا عَلَىَّ مِنَ الدَّيْنِ. فَحَسَبُوهُ فَوَجَدُوهُ سِتَّةً وَثَمَانِينَ أَلْفًا أَوْ نَحْوَهُ، قَالَ: إِنْ وَفَى لَهُ مَالُ آلِ عُمَرَ، فَأَدِّهِ مِنْ أَمْوَالِهِمْ، وَإِلاَّ فَسَلْ فِي بَنِي عَدِيِّ بْنِ كَعْبٍ، فَإِنْ لَمْ تَفِ أَمْوَالُهُمْ فَسَلْ فِي قُرَيْشٍ، وَلاَ تَعْدُهُمْ إِلَى غَيْرِهِمْ، فَأَدِّ عَنِّي هَذَا الْمَالَ، انْطَلِقْ إِلَى عَائِشَةَ أُمِّ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ فَقُلْ: يَقْرَأُ عَلَيْكِ عُمَرُ السَّلاَمَ. وَلاَ تَقُلْ أَمِيرُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ. فَإِنِّي لَسْتُ الْيَوْمَ لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَمِيرًا، وَقُلْ: يَسْتَأْذِنُ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ أَنْ يُدْفَنَ مَعَ صَاحِبَيْهِ. فَسَلَّمَ وَاسْتَأْذَنَ، ثُمَّ دَخَلَ عَلَيْهَا، فَوَجَدَهَا قَاعِدَةً تَبْكِي، فَقَالَ: يَقْرَأُ عَلَيْكِ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ السَّلاَمَ، وَيَسْتَأْذِنُ أَنْ يُدْفَنَ مَعَ صَاحِبَيْهِ. فَقَالَتْ: كُنْتُ أُرِيدُهُ لِنَفْسِي، وَلأُوثِرَنَّ بِهِ الْيَوْمَ عَلَى نَفْسِي. فَلَمَّا أَقْبَلَ قِيلَ: هَذَا عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ عُمَرَ قَدْ جَاءَ. قَالَ: ارْفَعُونِي، فَأَسْنَدَهُ رَجُلٌ إِلَيْهِ، فَقَالَ: مَا لَدَيْكَ؟ قَالَ: الَّذِي تُحِبُّ يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَذِنَتْ. قَالَ الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ، مَا كَانَ مِنْ شَىْءٍ أَهَمُّ إِلَىَّ مِنْ ذَلِكَ، فَإِذَا أَنَا قَضَيْتُ فَاحْمِلُونِي، ثُمَّ سَلِّمْ، فَقُلْ: يَسْتَأْذِنُ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ، فَإِنْ أَذِنَتْ لِي فَأَدْخِلُونِي، وَإِنْ رَدَّتْنِي رُدُّونِي إِلَى مَقَابِرِ الْمُسْلِمِينَ. وَجَاءَتْ أُمُّ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ حَفْصَةُ وَالنِّسَاءُ تَسِيرُ مَعَهَا، فَلَمَّا رَأَيْنَاهَا قُمْنَا، فَوَلَجَتْ عَلَيْهِ فَبَكَتْ عِنْدَهُ سَاعَةً، وَاسْتَأْذَنَ الرِّجَالُ، فَوَلَجَتْ دَاخِلاً لَهُمْ، فَسَمِعْنَا بُكَاءَهَا مِنَ الدَّاخِلِ. فَقَالُوا أَوْصِ يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ اسْتَخْلِفْ. قَالَ مَا أَجِدُ أَحَقَّ بِهَذَا الأَمْرِ مِنْ هَؤُلاَءِ النَّفَرِ أَوِ الرَّهْطِ الَّذِينَ تُوُفِّيَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهْوَ عَنْهُمْ رَاضٍ. فَسَمَّى عَلِيًّا وَعُثْمَانَ وَالزُّبَيْرَ وَطَلْحَةَ وَسَعْدًا وَعَبْدَ الرَّحْمَنِ وَقَالَ يَشْهَدُكُمْ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ عُمَرَ وَلَيْسَ لَهُ مِنَ الأَمْرِ شَىْءٌ ـ كَهَيْئَةِ التَّعْزِيَةِ لَهُ ـ فَإِنْ أَصَابَتِ الإِمْرَةُ سَعْدًا فَهْوَ ذَاكَ، وَإِلاَّ فَلْيَسْتَعِنْ بِهِ أَيُّكُمْ مَا أُمِّرَ، فَإِنِّي لَمْ أَعْزِلْهُ عَنْ عَجْزٍ وَلاَ خِيَانَةٍ وَقَالَ أُوصِي الْخَلِيفَةَ مِنْ بَعْدِي بِالْمُهَاجِرِينَ الأَوَّلِينَ أَنْ يَعْرِفَ لَهُمْ حَقَّهُمْ، وَيَحْفَظَ لَهُمْ حُرْمَتَهُمْ، وَأُوصِيهِ بِالأَنْصَارِ خَيْرًا، الَّذِينَ تَبَوَّءُوا الدَّارَ وَالإِيمَانَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ، أَنْ يُقْبَلَ مِنْ مُحْسِنِهِمْ، وَأَنْ يُعْفَى عَنْ مُسِيئِهِمْ، وَأُوصِيهِ بِأَهْلِ الأَمْصَارِ خَيْرًا فَإِنَّهُمْ رِدْءُ الإِسْلاَمِ، وَجُبَاةُ الْمَالِ، وَغَيْظُ الْعَدُوِّ، وَأَنْ لاَ يُؤْخَذَ مِنْهُمْ إِلاَّ فَضْلُهُمْ عَنْ رِضَاهُمْ، وَأُوصِيهِ بِالأَعْرَابِ خَيْرًا، فَإِنَّهُمْ أَصْلُ الْعَرَبِ وَمَادَّةُ الإِسْلاَمِ أَنْ يُؤْخَذَ مِنْ حَوَاشِي أَمْوَالِهِمْ وَتُرَدَّ عَلَى فُقَرَائِهِمْ، وَأُوصِيهِ بِذِمَّةِ اللَّهِ وَذِمَّةِ رَسُولِهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنْ يُوفَى لَهُمْ بِعَهْدِهِمْ، وَأَنْ يُقَاتَلَ مِنْ وَرَائِهِمْ، وَلاَ يُكَلَّفُوا إِلاَّ طَاقَتَهُمْ. فَلَمَّا قُبِضَ خَرَجْنَا بِهِ فَانْطَلَقْنَا نَمْشِي فَسَلَّمَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ عُمَرَ قَالَ يَسْتَأْذِنُ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ. قَالَتْ أَدْخِلُوهُ. فَأُدْخِلَ، فَوُضِعَ هُنَالِكَ مَعَ صَاحِبَيْهِ، فَلَمَّا فُرِغَ مِنْ دَفْنِهِ اجْتَمَعَ هَؤُلاَءِ الرَّهْطُ، فَقَالَ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ اجْعَلُوا أَمْرَكُمْ إِلَى ثَلاَثَةٍ مِنْكُمْ. فَقَالَ الزُّبَيْرُ قَدْ جَعَلْتُ أَمْرِي إِلَى عَلِيٍّ. فَقَالَ طَلْحَةُ قَدْ جَعَلْتُ أَمْرِي إِلَى عُثْمَانَ. وَقَالَ سَعْدٌ قَدْ جَعَلْتُ أَمْرِي إِلَى عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ عَوْفٍ. فَقَالَ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ أَيُّكُمَا تَبَرَّأَ مِنْ هَذَا الأَمْرِ فَنَجْعَلُهُ إِلَيْهِ، وَاللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَالإِسْلاَمُ لَيَنْظُرَنَّ أَفْضَلَهُمْ فِي نَفْسِهِ. فَأُسْكِتَ الشَّيْخَانِ، فَقَالَ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ أَفَتَجْعَلُونَهُ إِلَىَّ، وَاللَّهُ عَلَىَّ أَنْ لاَ آلُوَ عَنْ أَفْضَلِكُمْ قَالاَ نَعَمْ، فَأَخَذَ بِيَدِ أَحَدِهِمَا فَقَالَ لَكَ قَرَابَةٌ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَالْقَدَمُ فِي الإِسْلاَمِ مَا قَدْ عَلِمْتَ، فَاللَّهُ عَلَيْكَ لَئِنْ أَمَّرْتُكَ لَتَعْدِلَنَّ، وَلَئِنْ أَمَّرْتُ عُثْمَانَ لَتَسْمَعَنَّ وَلَتُطِيعَنَّ. ثُمَّ خَلاَ بِالآخَرِ فَقَالَ لَهُ مِثْلَ ذَلِكَ، فَلَمَّا أَخَذَ الْمِيثَاقَ قَالَ ارْفَعْ يَدَكَ يَا عُثْمَانُ. فَبَايَعَهُ، فَبَايَعَ لَهُ عَلِيٌّ، وَوَلَجَ أَهْلُ الدَّارِ فَبَايَعُوهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3700) عن موسى بن إسماعيل، ثنا أبو عوانة، عن حصين، عن عمرو بن ميمون قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في قصة استشهاد عمر ووصاياه وكفنه ودفنه وقصة أمر الاستخلاف بعده واتفاقهم على عثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3700). Another wording narrated by him provides further clarification of the account of appointing the successor:","chapter_en":"Reports concerning the Martyrdom of ʿUmar, His Final Instructions, Shrouding and Burial, the Appointment of a Successor after Him, and Their Agreement upon ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAmr ibn Maymūn reported: A few days before ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, was attacked, I saw him in Madinah standing with Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān and ʿUthmān ibn Ḥunayf. He asked them: “How have you proceeded? Do you fear that you may have imposed upon the land more than it can bear?” They replied: “We have imposed upon it something it is capable of bearing, and there is no great excess in it.” He said: “Make certain that you have not imposed upon the land more than it can bear.” They replied: “No.” ʿUmar then said: “If Allah preserves me, I shall certainly leave the widows of Iraq in such a condition that they will never need to depend upon any man after me.” Only four days passed before he was attacked. On the morning when he was attacked, I was standing with no one between him and me except ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās. Whenever ʿUmar passed between the rows, he would say, “Straighten your rows.” When he saw no gap in them, he would step forward and pronounce the takbīr. He would sometimes recite Sūrat Yūsuf, Sūrat al-Naḥl, or something similar during the first rakʿah so that the people could gather. He had scarcely pronounced the takbīr when I heard him say: “The dog has killed me—or devoured me!” This was when the attacker stabbed him. The non-Arab assailant fled with a double-edged knife, stabbing everyone he passed on his right or left, until he had stabbed thirteen men, seven of whom died. When a Muslim man saw this, he threw a cloak over him. Realizing that he had been captured, the assailant cut his own throat. ʿUmar took the hand of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf and moved him forward to lead the prayer. Those close to ʿUmar saw what I saw, but those in the other parts of the mosque did not know what had happened. They only noticed that ʿUmar’s voice was absent, and they kept saying, “Subḥān Allah! Subḥān Allah!” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān therefore led them in a brief prayer. When they finished, ʿUmar said: “O Ibn ʿAbbās, find out who attacked me.” He went around for a while and then returned, saying: “It was al-Mughīrah’s slave.” ʿUmar asked: “The skilled craftsman?” He replied: “Yes.” ʿUmar said: “May Allah destroy him! I had commanded that he be treated well. Praise be to Allah, who did not cause my death to come at the hands of a man claiming Islam. You and your father used to favor increasing the number of non-Arabs in Madinah.” Most of them were slaves. Ibn ʿAbbās said: “If you wish, I will do it,” meaning: “If you wish, we will kill them.” ʿUmar replied: “You are mistaken! How could that be done after they have spoken your language, prayed toward your qiblah, and performed the pilgrimage as you do?” ʿUmar was carried to his home, and we went with him. It was as though the people had never suffered a calamity before that day. Some said, “There is nothing seriously wrong with him,” while others said, “I fear for him.” He was brought nabīdh and drank it, but it came out through his abdomen. He was then brought milk and drank it, but it emerged from his wound. They therefore knew that he was dying. We entered upon him, and people came praising him. A young man came and said: “Rejoice, O Commander of the Believers, in the glad tidings Allah has prepared for you: the companionship of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, your early precedence in Islam, which you know well, then your appointment as ruler and your governing with justice, and now martyrdom.” ʿUmar replied: “I wish that all of that would leave me even—with nothing against me and nothing in my favor.” When the young man turned away, his lower garment was dragging along the ground. ʿUmar said: “Bring the young man back to me.” He then told him: “O son of my brother, raise your garment, for that will preserve your garment and is more mindful of your Lord.” He then said: “O ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, determine how much debt I owe.” They calculated it and found it to be approximately eighty-six thousand dirhams. ʿUmar said: “If the wealth of the family of ʿUmar is sufficient to repay it, then repay it from their wealth. Otherwise, ask Banū ʿAdī ibn Kaʿb. If their wealth is insufficient, ask Quraysh, but do not go beyond them to anyone else. Repay this debt on my behalf.” He then said: “Go to ʿĀ’ishah, the Mother of the Believers, and say: ‘ʿUmar sends you greetings of peace.’ Do not say, ‘The Commander of the Believers,’ for today I am no longer the commander of the believers. Say: ‘ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb requests permission to be buried beside his two companions.’” ʿAbdullāh went, conveyed the greeting, and requested permission. He entered and found her sitting and weeping. He said: “ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb sends you greetings of peace and requests permission to be buried beside his two companions.” She replied: “I had wished that place for myself, but today I shall give him preference over myself.” When ʿAbdullāh returned, someone said: “ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar has arrived.” ʿUmar said: “Raise me.” A man supported him, and ʿUmar asked: “What news do you have?” He replied: “What you wished for, O Commander of the Believers. She has granted permission.” ʿUmar said: “Praise be to Allah. Nothing was more important to me than that. When I die, carry me there, then convey greetings of peace and say: ‘ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb requests permission to enter.’ If she grants me permission, take me inside; but if she refuses me, return me to the Muslim cemetery.” Ḥafṣah, the Mother of the Believers, then came accompanied by other women. When we saw her, we stood up. She entered upon him and wept beside him for a while. The men then requested permission to enter, so she went into an inner room, and we could hear her weeping from inside. They said: “Give your final instructions, O Commander of the Believers, and appoint a successor.” He replied: “I find no one more entitled to this matter than these men—or this group—with whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased when he died.” He named ʿAlī, ʿUthmān, al-Zubayr, Ṭalḥah, Saʿd, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. He said: “ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar shall attend your deliberations, but he shall have no share in the matter,” as a means of consoling him. “If authority falls to Saʿd, then so be it. Otherwise, whoever among you is appointed should seek his assistance, for I did not remove him because of incompetence or dishonesty.” He continued: “I instruct the caliph after me to honor the rights of the earliest Emigrants and preserve their sanctity. I instruct him to treat the Anṣār well—those who established their home and embraced the faith before them—to accept the good deeds of their virtuous members and pardon those who fall into error. “I instruct him to treat the inhabitants of the provinces well, for they are the support of Islam, the collectors of its wealth, and a source of rage to the enemy. Nothing should be taken from them beyond their surplus, and only with their consent. “I instruct him to treat the Bedouins well, for they are the origin of the Arabs and the strength of Islam. Zakāh should be taken from the outer portions of their wealth and returned to their poor. “I instruct him concerning those protected by the covenant of Allah Almighty and the covenant of His Messenger ﷺ: their covenant must be fulfilled, their enemies must be fought in their defense, and they must not be burdened beyond their capacity.” When ʿUmar passed away, we carried him out and proceeded with him. ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar conveyed greetings of peace and said: “ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb requests permission to enter.” ʿĀ’ishah said: “Bring him in.” He was brought inside and laid beside his two companions. When his burial was completed, the appointed group assembled. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: “Reduce the matter to three among you.” Al-Zubayr said: “I give my authority to ʿAlī.” Ṭalḥah said: “I give my authority to ʿUthmān.” Saʿd said: “I give my authority to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf.” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān then said to ʿAlī and ʿUthmān: “Which of you will withdraw from this matter so that we may entrust the decision to him? Allah and Islam shall be his witnesses that he must consider which of the two is better in his judgment.” The two elders remained silent. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: “Will you entrust the matter to me? By Allah, I shall spare no effort in selecting the better of you.” They replied: “Yes.” He took one of them by the hand and said: “You possess kinship with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the precedence in Islam that you know. I adjure you by Allah: if I appoint you, you must rule with justice; and if I appoint ʿUthmān, you must listen and obey.” He then spoke privately to the other and said the same to him. After securing their covenant, he said: “Raise your hand, O ʿUthmān.” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān pledged allegiance to him, then ʿAlī pledged allegiance to him, and the people of the house entered and pledged allegiance to him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",92],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3700). وفي لفظ له مزيد إيضاح لقصة الاستخلاف:."},{"num":9893,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن الْمِسْوَرِ بن مَخْرَمَةَ أَخْبَرَهُ. أَنَّ الرَّهْطَ الَّذِينَ وَلاَّهُمْ عُمَرُ اجْتَمَعُوا فَتَشَاوَرُوا، قَالَ لَهُمْ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ: لَسْتُ بِالَّذِي أُنَافِسُكُمْ عَلَى هَذَا الأَمْرِ، وَلَكِنَّكُمْ إِنْ شِئْتُمُ اخْتَرْتُ لَكُمْ مِنْكُمْ. فَجَعَلُوا ذَلِكَ إِلَى عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ، فَلَمَّا وَلَّوْا عَبْدَ الرَّحْمَنِ أَمْرَهُمْ، فَمَالَ النَّاسُ عَلَى عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ، حَتَّى مَا أَرَى أَحَدًا مِنَ النَّاسِ يَتْبَعُ أُولَئِكَ الرَّهْطَ وَلاَ يَطَأُ عَقِبَهُ، وَمَالَ النَّاسُ عَلَى عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ يُشَاوِرُونَهُ تِلْكَ اللَّيَالِيَ، حَتَّى إِذَا كَانَتِ اللَّيْلَةُ الَّتِي أَصْبَحْنَا مِنْهَا، فَبَايَعْنَا عُثْمَانَ، قَالَ الْمِسْوَرُ: طَرَقَنِي عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ بَعْدَ هَجْعٍ مِنَ اللَّيْلِ، فَضَرَبَ الْبَابَ حَتَّى اسْتَيْقَظْتُ، فَقَالَ: أَرَاكَ نَائِمًا، فَوَاللَّهِ مَا اكْتَحَلْتُ هَذِهِ اللَّيْلَةَ بِكَبِيرِ نَوْمٍ، انْطَلِقْ فَادْعُ الزُّبَيْرَ وَسَعْدًا، فَدَعَوْتُهُمَا لَهُ، فَشَاوَرَهُمَا، ثُمَّ دَعَانِي، فَقَالَ: ادْعُ لِي عَلِيًّا. فَدَعَوْتُهُ، فَنَاجَاهُ حَتَّى ابْهَارَّ اللَّيْلُ، ثُمَّ قَامَ عَلِيٌّ مِنْ عِنْدِهِ، وَهْوَ عَلَى طَمَعٍ، وَقَدْ كَانَ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ يَخْشَى مِنْ عَلِيٍّ شَيْئًا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: ادْعُ لِي عُثْمَانَ، فَدَعَوْتُهُ، فَنَاجَاهُ حَتَّى فَرَّقَ بَيْنَهُمَا الْمُؤَذِّنُ بِالصُّبْحِ، فَلَمَّا صَلَّى لِلنَّاسِ الصُّبْحَ، وَاجْتَمَعَ أُولَئِكَ الرَّهْطُ عِنْدَ الْمِنْبَرِ، فَأَرْسَلَ إِلَى مَنْ كَانَ حَاضِرًا مِنَ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ وَالأَنْصَارِ، وَأَرْسَلَ إِلَى أُمَرَاءِ الأَجْنَادِ، وَكَانُوا وَافَوْا تِلْكَ الْحَجَّةَ مَعَ عُمَرَ، فَلَمَّا اجْتَمَعُوا تَشَهَّدَ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَمَّا بَعْدُ، يَا عَلِيُّ، إِنِّي قَدْ نَظَرْتُ فِي أَمْرِ النَّاسِ فَلَمْ أَرَهُمْ يَعْدِلُونَ بِعُثْمَانَ، فَلاَ تَجْعَلَنَّ عَلَى نَفْسِكَ سَبِيلاً. فَقَالَ: أُبَايِعُكَ عَلَى سُنَّةِ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ وَالْخَلِيفَتَيْنِ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ. فَبَايَعَهُ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ، وَبَايَعَهُ النَّاسُ الْمُهَاجِرُونَ، وَالأَنْصَارُ، وَأُمَرَاءُ الأَجْنَادِ، وَالْمُسْلِمُونَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الأحكام (7207) عن عبدالله بن محمد بن أسماء، ثنا جويرية، عن مالك، عن الزهري، عن حميد بن عبدالرحمن، عن المسور بن مخرمة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في قصة استشهاد عمر ووصاياه وكفنه ودفنه وقصة أمر الاستخلاف بعده واتفاقهم على عثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7207).","chapter_en":"Reports concerning the Martyrdom of ʿUmar, His Final Instructions, Shrouding and Burial, the Appointment of a Successor after Him, and Their Agreement upon ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah reported: The group whom ʿUmar had appointed assembled and consulted one another. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said to them: “I am not one who will compete with you for this authority. However, if you wish, I will choose one of you on your behalf.” They therefore entrusted the matter to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. Once they entrusted their affair to him, the people turned toward ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. I saw scarcely anyone following the other members of the council or treading at their heels. Instead, the people approached ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and consulted with him throughout those nights. On the night preceding the morning on which we pledged allegiance to ʿUthmān, al-Miswar said: “ʿAbd al-Raḥmān came to me after part of the night had passed and knocked on the door until I awoke. He said: “‘I see that you are sleeping! By Allah, I have hardly slept at all tonight. Go and call al-Zubayr and Saʿd for me.’ “I called them, and he consulted them. He then called me and said: “‘Call ʿAlī for me.’ “I called him, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān spoke privately with him until the night had grown very late. ʿAlī then left him while still hoping to be selected, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān had certain concerns regarding ʿAlī. “He then said: “‘Call ʿUthmān for me.’ “I called him, and he spoke privately with him until the caller to the dawn prayer separated them.” After ʿAbd al-Raḥmān led the people in the dawn prayer and the members of the council gathered near the pulpit, he summoned the Emigrants and the Anṣār who were present. He also summoned the commanders of the armies, who had come to perform that year’s pilgrimage with ʿUmar. When they had assembled, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān recited the testimony of faith and said: “To proceed: O ʿAlī, I have examined the people’s affair and have not found them regarding anyone as equal to ʿUthmān. Therefore, do not give anyone grounds to act against you.” He then said to ʿUthmān: “I pledge allegiance to you upon the way of Allah, His Messenger, and the two caliphs after him.” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān pledged allegiance to him, followed by the people—the Emigrants, the Anṣār, the commanders of the armies, and the Muslims."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[7699],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (7207)."},{"num":9894,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْمِسْوَرِ بْنِ مَخْرَمَةَ، قَالَ: لَمَّا طُعِنَ عُمَرُ جَعَلَ يَأْلَمُ، فَقَالَ لَهُ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ، ـ وَكَأَنَّهُ يُجَزِّعُهُ: ـ يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، وَلَئِنْ كَانَ ذَاكَ، لَقَدْ صَحِبْتَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَحْسَنْتَ صُحْبَتَهُ، ثُمَّ فَارَقْتَهُ وَهْوَ عَنْكَ رَاضٍ، ثُمَّ صَحِبْتَ أَبَا بَكْرٍ فَأَحْسَنْتَ صُحْبَتَهُ، ثُمَّ فَارَقْتَهُ وَهْوَ عَنْكَ رَاضٍ، ثُمَّ صَحِبْتَ صَحَبَتَهُمْ فَأَحْسَنْتَ صُحْبَتَهُمْ، وَلَئِنْ فَارَقْتَهُمْ لَتُفَارِقَنَّهُمْ وَهُمْ عَنْكَ رَاضُونَ. قَالَ أَمَّا مَا ذَكَرْتَ مِنْ صُحْبَةِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَرِضَاهُ، فَإِنَّمَا ذَاكَ مَنٌّ مِنَ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى مَنَّ بِهِ عَلَىَّ، وَأَمَّا مَا ذَكَرْتَ مِنْ صُحْبَةِ أَبِي بَكْرٍ وَرِضَاهُ، فَإِنَّمَا ذَاكَ مَنٌّ مِنَ اللَّهِ جَلَّ ذِكْرُهُ مَنَّ بِهِ عَلَىَّ، وَأَمَّا مَا تَرَى مِنْ جَزَعِي، فَهْوَ مِنْ أَجْلِكَ وَأَجْلِ أَصْحَابِكَ، وَاللَّهِ لَوْ أَنَّ لِي طِلاَعَ الأَرْضِ ذَهَبًا لاَفْتَدَيْتُ بِهِ مِنْ عَذَابِ اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ قَبْلَ أَنْ أَرَاهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3692) عن الصلت بن محمد، ثنا إسماعيل بن إبراهيم، ثنا أيوب، عن ابن أبي مليكة، عن المسور بن مخرمة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في قصة استشهاد عمر ووصاياه وكفنه ودفنه وقصة أمر الاستخلاف بعده واتفاقهم على عثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3692).","chapter_en":"Reports concerning the Martyrdom of ʿUmar, His Final Instructions, Shrouding and Burial, the Appointment of a Successor after Him, and Their Agreement upon ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah reported: When ʿUmar was stabbed, he began to suffer pain. Ibn ʿAbbās said to him, as though seeking to console him: “O Commander of the Believers, even if this has happened, you accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and were an excellent companion to him. Then you parted from him while he was pleased with you. You accompanied Abū Bakr and were an excellent companion to him. Then you parted from him while he was pleased with you. You then accompanied their Companions and treated them well. If you now part from them, you will certainly leave them while they are pleased with you.” ʿUmar replied: “As for what you mentioned concerning my companionship with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his pleasure with me, that was only a favor Allah Almighty bestowed upon me. As for what you mentioned concerning my companionship with Abū Bakr and his pleasure with me, that too was only a favor Allah—Majestic is His remembrance—bestowed upon me. “As for the distress you see in me, it is on account of you and your companions. By Allah, if I possessed enough gold to fill the earth, I would use it to ransom myself from the punishment of Allah Almighty before seeing it.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",93],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3692)."},{"num":9895,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ قَالَ: لَمَّا طَعَنَ أَبُو لُؤْلُؤَةَ عُمَرَ، طَعَنَهُ طَعْنَتَيْنِ، فَظَنَّ عُمَرُ أَنَّ لَهُ ذَنْبًا فِي النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُهُ، فَدَعَا ابْنَ عَبَّاسٍ وَكَانَ يُحِبُّهُ، ويُدْنِيهِ، ويَسْتَمِعُ مِنْهُ، فَقَالَ لَهُ: أَحَبُّ أَنْ تَعْلَمَ عَنْ مَلَأٍ مِنَ النَّاسِ كَانَ هَذَا؟ فَخَرَجَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ، فَجَعَلَ لَا يَمُرُّ بِمَلَإٍ مِنَ النَّاسِ إِلَّا وَهُمْ يَبْكُونَ، فَرَجَعَ إِلَيْهِ، فَقَالَ: يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ: مَا أَتَيْتُ عَلَى مَلَإٍ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ إِلَّا وَهُمْ يَبْكُونَ، كَأَنَّمَا فَقَدُوا الْيَوْمَ أبكارَ أَوْلَادِهِمْ. فَقَالَ: مَنْ قَتَلَنِي؟ قَالَ: أَبُو لُؤْلُؤَةَ الْمَجُوسِيُّ عَبْدُ الْمُغِيرَةِ بْنِ شُعْبَةَ. قَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: فَرَأَيْتُ الْبِشْرَ فِي وَجْهِهِ. فَقَالَ: الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي لَمْ يَبْتَلِنِي بِقَوْلِ أَحَدٍ يُحَاجُّنِي بِقَوْلِ: لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، أَمَا إِنِّي كُنْتُ قَدْ نَهَيْتُكُمْ أَنْ تَجْلِبُوا إِلَيْنَا مِنَ الْعُلُوجِ أَحَدًا، فَعَصَيتُمُونِي. ثُمَّ قَالَ: ادْعُوا لِي إِخْوَانِي. قَالُوا: وَمَنْ؟ قَالَ: عُثْمَانُ، وَعَلِيٌّ، وَطَلْحَةُ، وَالزُّبَيْرُ، وَعَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنُ عَوْفٍ، وَسَعْدُ بْنُ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ. فَأَرْسَلَ إِلَيْهِمْ، ثُمَّ وَضَعَ رَأْسَهُ فِي حَجْرِي، فَلَمَّا جَاءُوا، قُلْتُ: هَؤُلَاءِ قَدْ حَضَرُوا. فَقَالَ: نَعَمْ، نَظَرْتُ فِي أَمْرِ الْمُسْلِمِينَ، فَوَجَدْتُكُمْ أَيُّهَا السِّتَّةُ رُءُوسَ النَّاسِ، وَقَادَتَهُمْ، وَلَا يَكُونُ هَذَا الْأَمْرُ إِلَّا فِيكُمْ مَا اسْتَقَمْتُمْ يَسْتَقِيمُ أَمْرُ النَّاسِ، وَإِنْ يَكُنِ اخْتِلَافٌ يَكُنْ فِيكُمْ، فَلَمَّا سَمِعْتُ ذِكْرَ الِاخْتِلَافِ، وَالشِّقَاقِ ظَنَنْتُ أَنَّهُ كَائِنٌ، لِأَنَّهُ قَلَّ مَا قَالَ شَيْئًا إِلَّا رَأَيْتُهُ، ثُمَّ نَزَفَ الدَّمَ، فَهَمَسُوا بَيْنَهُمْ حَتَّى خَشِيتُ أَنْ يُبَايِعُوا رَجُلًا مِنْهُمْ، فَقُلْتُ: إِنَّ أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ حَيٌّ بَعْدُ، وَلَا يَكُونُ خَلِيفَتَانِ يَنْظُرُ أَحَدُهُمَا إِلَى الْآخَرِ. فَقَالَ: احْمِلُونِي، فَحَمَلْنَاهُ، فَقَالَ: تَشَاوِرُوا ثَلَاثًا. وَيُصَلِّي بِالنَّاسِ صُهَيْبٌ. قَالَ: مَنْ نُشَاوِرُ يَا أَمِيرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ؟ فَقَالَ: شَاوِرُوا الْمُهَاجِرِينَ وَالْأَنْصَارَ، وسَرَاةَ مَنْ هُنَا مِنَ الْأَجْنَادِ. ثُمَّ دَعَا بِشَرْبَةٍ مِنْ لَبَنٍ، فَشَرِبَ، فَخَرَجَ بَيَاضُ اللَّبَنِ مِنَ الْجُرْحَيْنِ، فَعُرِفَ أَنَّهُ الْمَوْتُ، فَقَالَ: الْآنَ لَوْ أَنَّ لِيَ الدُّنْيَا كُلَّهَا لَافْتَدَيْتُ بِهَا مِنْ هَوْلِ الْمَطْلَعِ، وَمَا ذَاكَ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ إِنْ أَكُونُ رَأَيْتُ إِلَّا خَيْرًا. فَقَالَ ابْنُ عَبَّاسٍ: وَإنْ قُلْتَ ذَلِكَ، فَجَزَاكَ اللَّهُ خَيْرًا، أَلَيْسَ قَدْ دَعَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنْ يُعِزَّ اللَّهُ بِكَ الدِّينَ وَالْمُسْلِمِينَ إِذْ يَخَافُونَ بِمَكَّةَ، فَلَمَّا أَسْلَمْتَ كَانَ إسْلَامُكَ عِزًّا، وَظَهَرَ بِكَ الْإِسْلَامُ وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَصْحَابُهُ، وَهَاجَرْتَ إِلَى الْمَدِينَةِ، فَكَانَتْ هِجْرَتُكَ فَتْحًا، ثُمَّ لَمْ تَغِبْ عَنْ مَشْهَدٍ شَهِدَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ قِتَالِ الْمُشْرِكِينَ مِنْ يَوْمِ كَذَا وَيَوْمِ كَذَا، ثُمَّ قُبِضَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُوَ عَنْكَ رَاضٍ، فَوَازَرْتَ الْخَلِيفَةَ بَعْدَهُ عَلَى مِنْهَاجِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَضَرَبْتِ مَنْ أَدْبَرَ بِمَنْ أَقْبَلَ حَتَّى دَخَلَ النَّاسُ فِي الْإِسْلَامِ طَوْعًا أَوْ كَرْهًا، ثُمَّ قُبِضَ الْخَلِيفَةُ وَهُوَ عَنْكَ رَاضٍ، ثُمَّ وُلِّيتَ بِخَيْرِ مَا وُلِّيَ النَّاسُ، مَصَّرَ اللَّهُ بِكَ الْأَمْصَارَ، وَجَبَى بِكَ الْأَمْوَالَ، وَنَفَى بِكَ الْعَدُوَّ، وَأَدْخَلَ اللَّهُ بِكَ عَلَى كُلِّ أَهْلِ بَيْتٍ مِنْ تَوَسُّعِهِمْ فِي دِينِهِمْ، وتَوَسُّعِهِمْ فِي أَرْزَاقِهِمْ، ثُمَّ خَتَمَ لَكَ بِالشَّهَادَةِ، فَهَنِيئًا لَكَ. فَقَالَ: وَاللَّهِ إِنَّ الْمغرورَ مَنْ تَغُرُّونَهُ. ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَتَشْهَدُ لِي يَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ؟ فَقَالَ: نَعَمْ. فَقَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ، أَلْصِقْ خَدِّي بِالْأَرْضِ يَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ ابْنَ عُمَرَ، فَوَضَعْتُهُ مِنْ فَخِذِي عَلَى سَاقِي. فَقَالَ: أَلْصِقْ خَدِّي بِالْأَرْضِ، فَتَرَكَ لِحْيَتَهُ وَخَدَّهُ حَتَّى وَقَعَ بِالْأَرْضِ، فَقَالَ: وَيْلَكَ وَوَيْلَ أُمِّكَ يَا عُمَرُ إِنْ لَمْ يَغْفِرِ اللَّهُ لَكَ. ثُمَّ قُبِضَ رحمه اللَّهُ. فَلَمَّا قُبِضَ أَرْسَلُوا إِلَى عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ، فَقَالَ: لَا آتِيكُمْ إِنْ لَمْ تَفْعَلُوا مَا أَمَرَكُمْ بِهِ مِنْ مُشَاوَرَةِ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ، وَالْأَنْصَارِ، وسَرَاةِ مَنْ هَاهُنَا مِنَ الْأَجْنَادِ.","قَالَ الْحَسَنُ -وَذُكِرَ لَهُ فِعْلُ عُمَرَ عِنْدَ مَوْتِهِ وخَشْيَتُهُ مِنْ رَبِّهِ- فَقَالَ: هَكَذَا الْمُؤْمِنُ جَمَعَ إِحْسَانًا وَشَفَقَةً، وَالْمُنَافِقُ جَمَعَ إساءةً وَغِرَّةً، وَاللَّهِ مَا وَجَدْتُ فِيمَا مَضَى، وَلَا فِيمَا بَقِيَ عَبْدًا ازْدَادَ إِحْسَانًا إِلَّا ازْدَادَ مَخَافَةً وَشَفَقَةً مِنْهُ، وَلَا وَجَدْتُ فِيمَا مَضَى، وَلَا فِيمَا بَقِيَ عَبْدًا ازْدَادَ إساءةً إِلَّا ازْدَادَ غِرَّةٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (583) عن أحمد (هو القاسم بن مساور)، حدثنا سعيد بن سليمان الواسطي، قال: حدثنا مبارك بن فضالة، قال: حدثنا عبيدالله بن عمر، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر فذكره. وإسناده حسن من أجل مبارك بن فضالة فإنه حسن الحديث وقد حسَّنه الهيثمي في المجمع (14463).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في قصة استشهاد عمر ووصاياه وكفنه ودفنه وقصة أمر الاستخلاف بعده واتفاقهم على عثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in Al-Awsaṭ (583).","chapter_en":"Reports concerning the Martyrdom of ʿUmar, His Final Instructions, Shrouding and Burial, the Appointment of a Successor after Him, and Their Agreement upon ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل عمر بن الخطاب وأخباره","group_en":"Collection of Reports Concerning the Virtues and Accounts of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb","part_no":49,"group_no":3,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar reported: When Abū Luʾluʾah stabbed ʿUmar, he stabbed him twice. ʿUmar feared that he might have committed some wrong against the people of which he was unaware. He therefore summoned Ibn ʿAbbās—whom he loved, kept close, and listened to—and said: “I want you to find out from the gatherings of the people whether this happened because of something they held against me.” Ibn ʿAbbās went out, and he did not pass any gathering of people without finding them weeping. He returned and said: “O Commander of the Believers, I did not come upon any gathering of Muslims without finding them weeping as though they had lost the firstborn of their children today.” ʿUmar asked: “Who attacked me?” He replied: “Abū Luʾluʾah the Magian, the slave of al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah.” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “I saw joy appear upon his face.” ʿUmar said: “Praise be to Allah, who did not test me through someone who could dispute with me by saying, ‘There is no deity except Allah.’ I had forbidden you from bringing any of these non-Arabs among us, but you disobeyed me.” He then said: “Call my brothers for me.” They asked: “Who are they?” He replied: “ʿUthmān, ʿAlī, Ṭalḥah, al-Zubayr, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, and Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ.” They sent for them, and ʿUmar placed his head in my lap. When they arrived, I said: “They are all present.” He said: “Yes. I have considered the Muslims’ affair and found that you six are the leaders and commanders of the people. This authority will belong only to you. So long as you remain upright, the people’s affairs will remain upright; but if disagreement arises, it will arise among you.” When I heard him mention disagreement and division, I became convinced that it would occur, for he rarely said anything without my later seeing it come to pass. He then began losing blood. The six men whispered among themselves until I feared that they might pledge allegiance to one of them. I said: “The Commander of the Believers is still alive, and there cannot be two caliphs looking at one another.” ʿUmar said: “Carry me.” So we carried him. He said: “Consult one another for three days, and let Ṣuhayb lead the people in prayer.” They asked: “Whom should we consult, O Commander of the Believers?” He replied: “Consult the Emigrants, the Anṣār, and the prominent commanders of the armies who are present here.” He then called for a cup of milk and drank it. The whiteness of the milk emerged from both wounds, so he knew that death had come. He said: “Now, if I possessed the entire world, I would use it to ransom myself from the terror of what lies ahead. Yet, praise be to Allah, I do not believe that I have seen anything but good.” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “Even if you say that, may Allah reward you with goodness! Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not supplicate that Allah strengthen the religion and the Muslims through you when they were living in fear in Makkah? When you accepted Islam, your Islam was a source of strength, and through you Islam, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his Companions became publicly manifest. “You migrated to Madinah, and your migration was a victory. You were never absent from any battle in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fought the polytheists, on such-and-such a day and such-and-such a day. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while pleased with you. “You supported the caliph after him upon the way of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. You confronted those who turned away with the help of those who advanced, until people entered Islam willingly or unwillingly. Then that caliph passed away while pleased with you. “You were then entrusted with authority in the best manner in which anyone has governed the people. Through you, Allah established the garrison cities, collected wealth, and drove back the enemy. Through you, Allah brought into every household an expansion in their religion and an increase in their provision. Then He concluded your life with martyrdom. So congratulations to you!” ʿUmar replied: “By Allah, the truly deceived person is the one whom you cause to become deceived by such praise.” He then asked: “Will you testify to this for me before Allah on the Day of Resurrection, O ʿAbdullāh?” Ibn ʿAbbās replied: “Yes.” ʿUmar said: “O Allah, to You belongs all praise. Place my cheek upon the ground, O ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās.” I lowered his head from my thigh to my shin. He again said: “Place my cheek upon the ground.” He allowed his beard and cheek to rest upon the earth and said: “Woe to you—and woe to your mother, O ʿUmar—if Allah does not forgive you!” He then passed away, may Allah have mercy upon him. After his death, they sent for ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar. He said: “I will not come to you unless you carry out his command to consult the Emigrants, the Anṣār, and the prominent commanders of the armies who are present here.” When al-Ḥasan was told about ʿUmar’s conduct at the time of his death and his fear of his Lord, he said: “Such is the believer: he combines righteous deeds with fear and apprehension. The hypocrite combines wrongdoing with deluded confidence. By Allah, I have never found—among those of the past or those who remain—a servant who increased in righteousness without also increasing in fear and apprehension of Him. Nor have I found a servant who increased in wrongdoing without also increasing in deluded confidence.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Note: The printed edition reads, “Place my cheek upon the ground, O ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar.” The correct wording is, “ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās,” because ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar was not present with him at that time, as indicated by the end of the hadith: “He then passed away, may Allah have mercy upon him. After his death, they sent for ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",94],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (583)."},{"num":9896,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: كَانَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مُضْطَجِعًا فِي بَيْتِي، كَاشِفًا عَنْ فَخِذَيْهِ -أَوْ سَاقَيْهِ- فَاسْتَأْذَنَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَأَذِنَ لَهُ، وَهُوَ عَلَى تِلْكَ الْحَالِ، فَتَحَدَّثَ، ثُمَّ اسْتَأْذَنَ عُمَرُ فَأَذِنَ لَهُ، وَهُوَ كَذَلِكَ، فَتَحَدَّثَ، ثُمَّ اسْتَأْذَنَ عُثْمَانُ، فَجَلَسَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَسَوَّى ثِيَابَهُ- قَالَ مُحَمَّدٌ: وَلَا أَقُولُ ذَلِكَ فِي يَوْمٍ وَاحِدٍ -- فَدَخَلَ فَتَحَدَّثَ، فَلَمَّا خَرَجَ قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: دَخَلَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ فَلَمْ تَهْتَشَّ لَهُ وَلَمْ تُبَالِهِ، ثُمَّ دَخَلَ عُمَرُ فَلَمْ تَهْتَشَّ لَهُ وَلَمْ تُبَالِهِ، ثُمَّ دَخَلَ عُثْمَانُ فَجَلَسْتَ وَسَوَّيْتَ ثِيَابَكَ، فَقَالَ: أَلَا أَسْتَحِي مِنْ رَجُلٍ تَسْتَحِي مِنْهُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2401: 26) من طرق عن إسماعيل بن جعفر، عن محمد بن أبي حرملة، عن عطاء وسليمان بن يسار وأبي سلمة بن عبد الرحمن، أن عائشة قالت: فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن عثمان رجل حيي تستحي منه الملائكة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim in Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (2401, no. 26), through routes from Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar, from Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥarmalah, from ʿAṭāʾ, Sulaymān ibn Yasār, and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿĀ’ishah.","chapter_en":"That ʿUthmān Was a Man of Such Modesty That Even the Angels Feel Shy Before Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reclining in my house with his thighs—or his lower legs—uncovered. Abū Bakr sought permission to enter, and he permitted him while remaining in that state, and they spoke. Then ʿUmar sought permission to enter, and he permitted him while remaining in the same state, and they spoke. Then ʿUthmān sought permission to enter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat up and adjusted his clothes. Muḥammad said: “I do not say that all of this occurred on the same day.” ʿUthmān entered and spoke with him. After he left, ʿĀ’ishah said: “Abū Bakr entered, yet you did not become especially animated or concerned about his entrance. Then ʿUmar entered, and you likewise did not. But when ʿUthmān entered, you sat up and adjusted your clothes.” He ﷺ said: “Should I not feel shy before a man before whom the angels feel shy?”"]},"intro_majmu":{"ar":["هو عثمان بن عفان بن أبي العاص القرشي الأموي أمير المؤمنين.","وُلِدَ بعد عام الفيل بست سنين على الصحيح، وكان ربعة (أي لا بالطويل ولا بالقصير) حسن الوجه، رقيق البشرة، عظيم اللحية، بعيد ما بين المنكبين، زوَّجه النبي ﷺ ابنته رقية، فماتت عنده أيام بدر، فزوَّجه بعدها أختها أم كلثوم، فلذلك كان يلقب ذا النورين.","قال ابن مسعود: “لما بويع بايعنا خيرنا، ولم نأل”.","وقال علي: “كان عثمان أوصلنا للرحم”.","وكذا قالت عائشة لما بلغها قتله: “قتلوه، وإنه لأوصلهم للرحم، وأتقاهم للرب”.","قُتل على رأس إحدى عشرة سنة وأحد عشر شهراً واثنين وعشرين يوماً من خلافته، فيكون ذلك في ثاني وعشرين ذي الحجة سنة خمس وثلاثين، قاله ابن إسحاق.","الإصابة (٥٤٧٣)."],"en":["He was ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān ibn Abī al-ʿĀṣ al-Qurashī al-Umawī, the Commander of the Believers.","According to the sounder opinion, he was born six years after the Year of the Elephant. He was of medium height (neither tall nor short), handsome in appearance, fair-skinned, with a full beard and broad shoulders. The Prophet ﷺ married his daughter Ruqayyah to him. When she passed away during the days of the Battle of Badr, the Prophet ﷺ married him to her sister, Umm Kulthūm. For this reason, he became known as Dhū al-Nūrayn (The Possessor of the Two Lights).","Ibn Masʿūd said:","“When ʿUthmān was given the pledge of allegiance, we pledged allegiance to the best among us, and we did not fall short in doing so.”","ʿAlī said:","“ʿUthmān was the one among us who maintained family ties the most.”","Likewise, when news of his murder reached ʿĀ’ishah, she said:","“They have killed him, though he was the one who maintained family ties the most among them and was the most God-fearing toward his Lord.”","He was martyred after completing eleven years, eleven months, and twenty-two days of his caliphate. Thus, his martyrdom occurred on the twenty-second of Dhū al-Ḥijjah in the year 35 AH, as stated by Ibn Isḥāq.","Al-Iṣābah (5473)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",95],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2401: 26)."},{"num":9897,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَةَ زَوْجَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَعُثْمَانَ أَنَّ أَبَا بَكْرٍ اسْتَأْذَنَ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَهُوَ مُضْطَجِعٌ عَلَى فِرَاشِهِ، لَابِسٌ مِرْطَ عَائِشَةَ، فَأَذِنَ لِأَبِي بَكْرٍ وَهُوَ كَذَلِكَ، فَقَضَى إِلَيْهِ حَاجَتَهُ ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ، ثُمَّ اسْتَأْذَنَ عُمَرُ فَأَذِنَ لَهُ وَهُوَ عَلَى تِلْكَ الْحَالِ، فَقَضَى إِلَيْهِ حَاجَتَهُ، ثُمَّ انصرف.قال عُثْمَانُ: ثُمَّ اسْتَأْذَنْتُ عَلَيْهِ، فَجَلَسَ، وَقَالَ لِعَائِشَةَ: اجْمَعِي عَلَيْكِ ثيابك.فقضيت إِلَيْهِ حَاجَتِي ثُمَّ انْصَرَفْتُ، فَقَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللهِ مَا لِي لَمْ أَرَكَ فَزِعْتَ لِأَبِي بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا كَمَا فَزِعْتَ لِعُثْمَانَ؟ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ عُثْمَانَ رَجُلٌ حَيِيٌّ وَإِنِّي خَشِيتُ إِنْ أَذِنْتُ لَهُ عَلَى تِلْكَ الْحَالِ أَنْ لَا يَبْلُغَ إِلَيَّ فِي حَاجَتِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2402: 27) عن عبد الملك بن شعيب بن الليث بن سعد، حدثني أبي، عن جدي، حدثني عُقيل بن خالد، عن ابن شهاب، عن يحيى بن سعيد بن العاص أن سعيد بن العاص أخبره أن عائشة زوج النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم وعثمان حدثاه فذكراه.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن عثمان رجل حيي تستحي منه الملائكة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim in Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (2402, no. 27), through ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth ibn Saʿd, from his father, from his grandfather, from ʿUqayl ibn Khālid, from Ibn Shihāb, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ, from Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ, from ʿĀ’ishah and ʿUthmān.","chapter_en":"That ʿUthmān Was a Man of Such Modesty That Even the Angels Feel Shy Before Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and ʿUthmān narrated that Abū Bakr sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reclining on his bed, wearing the outer garment of ʿĀ’ishah. The Prophet ﷺ admitted Abū Bakr while remaining in that state. Abū Bakr fulfilled the purpose for which he had come and then departed. After that, ʿUmar sought permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ admitted him while remaining in the same state. He fulfilled his need and then departed. ʿUthmān said: Then I sought permission to enter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat upright and said to ʿĀ’ishah: “Gather your garments around yourself.” I fulfilled my need and then left. ʿĀ’ishah asked: “O Messenger of Allah, why did I not see you become concerned for Abū Bakr and ʿUmar as you did for ʿUthmān?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Indeed, ʿUthmān is a man of great modesty, and I feared that if I admitted him while I was in that condition, he would not be able to express the purpose for which he had come.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",96],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2402: 27) عن عبد الملك بن شعيب بن الليث بن سعد، حدثني أبي، عن جدي، حدثني عقيل بن خالد، عن ابن شهاب، عن يحيى بن سعيد بن العاص، أن سعيد بن العاص أخبره أن عائشة زوج النبي ﷺ وعثمان حدثاه فذكراه."},{"num":9898,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: إِنَّمَا تَغَيَّبَ عُثْمَانُ عَنْ بَدْرٍ، فَإِنَّهُ كَانَتْ تَحْتَهُ بِنْتُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَكَانَتْ مَرِيضَةً. فَقَالَ لَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ لَكَ أَجْرَ رَجُلٍ مِمَّنْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا وَسَهْمَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3130) عن موسى بن إسماعيل، ثنا أبو عوانة، ثنا عثمان بن موهب، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن عثمان أدرك فضل من شهد بدرًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (3130), from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl, from Abū ʿAwānah, from ʿUthmān ibn Mawhab, from Ibn ʿUmar.","chapter_en":"That ʿUthmān Attained the Virtue of Those Who Participated in the Battle of Badr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ʿUthmān was absent from the Battle of Badr only because the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who was his wife, was ill. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “You shall have the reward of a man who participated in the Battle of Badr, as well as his share of the spoils.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[8033],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3130)."},{"num":9899,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عُثْمَانَ بن مَوْهَبٍ قَالَ: جَاءَ رَجُلٌ مَنْ أَهْلِ مِصْرَ حَجَّ الْبَيْتَ، فَرَأَى قَوْمًا جُلُوسًا، فَقَالَ: مَنْ هَؤُلاَءِ الْقَوْمُ؟ قَالَ هَؤُلاَءِ قُرَيْشٌ. قَالَ فَمَنِ الشَّيْخُ فِيهِمْ؟ قَالُوا: عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ عُمَرَ. قَالَ يَا ابْنَ عُمَرَ، إِنِّي سَائِلُكَ عَنْ شَىْءٍ فَحَدِّثْنِي، هَلْ تَعْلَمُ أَنَّ عُثْمَانَ فَرَّ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ تَعْلَمُ أَنَّهُ تَغَيَّبَ عَنْ بَدْرٍ وَلَمْ يَشْهَدْ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ تَعْلَمُ أَنَّهُ تَغَيَّبَ عَنْ بَيْعَةِ الرُّضْوَانِ فَلَمْ يَشْهَدْهَا؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ اللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ. قَالَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ: تَعَالَ أُبَيِّنْ لَكَ، أَمَّا فِرَارُهُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ فَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَفَا عَنْهُ وَغَفَرَ لَهُ، وَأَمَّا تَغَيُّبُهُ عَنْ بَدْرٍ، فَإِنَّهُ كَانَتْ تَحْتَهُ بِنْتُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَكَانَتْ مَرِيضَةً، فَقَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ لَكَ أَجْرَ رَجُلٍ مِمَّنْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا وَسَهْمَهُ. وَأَمَّا تَغَيُّبُهُ عَنْ بَيْعَةِ الرُّضْوَانِ فَلَوْ كَانَ أَحَدٌ أَعَزَّ بِبَطْنِ مَكَّةَ مِنْ عُثْمَانَ لَبَعَثَهُ مَكَانَهُ، فَبَعَثَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عُثْمَانَ، وَكَانَتْ بَيْعَةُ الرُّضْوَانِ بَعْدَ مَا ذَهَبَ عُثْمَانُ إِلَى مَكَّةَ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِيَدِهِ الْيُمْنَى: هَذِهِ يَدُ عُثْمَانَ. فَضَرَبَ بِهَا عَلَى يَدِهِ، فَقَالَ: هَذِهِ لِعُثْمَانَ. فَقَالَ لَهُ ابْنُ عُمَرَ: اذْهَبْ بِهَا الْآنَ مَعَكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3698) عن موسى بن إسماعيل، ثنا أبو عوانة، ثنا عثمان بن موهب قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إن بيعة الرضوان كانت من أجل عثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (3698).","chapter_en":"That the Pledge of al-Riḍwān Was Given on Account of ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUthmān ibn Mawhab narrated: A man from the people of Egypt came to perform Ḥajj. He saw a group of people sitting together and asked, “Who are these people?” They replied, “They are Quraysh.” He asked, “Who is the elder among them?” They answered, “ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar.” The man said, “O Ibn ʿUmar, I wish to ask you about something, so tell me. Do you know that ʿUthmān fled on the Day of Uḥud?” He replied, “Yes.” The man asked, “Do you know that he was absent from Badr and did not participate?” He replied, “Yes.” The man asked, “Do you know that he was absent from the Pledge of al-Riḍwān and did not attend it?” He replied, “Yes.” The man exclaimed, “Allāhu Akbar!” Ibn ʿUmar said: “Come, and I will explain it to you. As for his retreat on the Day of Uḥud, I testify that Allah pardoned him and forgave him. As for his absence from Badr, it was because the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who was his wife, was ill. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: ‘You shall have the reward of a man who participated in Badr, along with his share of the spoils.’ As for his absence from the Pledge of al-Riḍwān, if there had been anyone in the heart of Makkah more honored than ʿUthmān, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have sent him instead. However, he sent ʿUthmān. The Pledge of al-Riḍwān took place after ʿUthmān had gone to Makkah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took his right hand and said: ‘This is the hand of ʿUthmān.’ Then he struck it upon his other hand and said: ‘This is on behalf of ʿUthmān.’” Ibn ʿUmar then said to the man: “Now take this answer with you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",98],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3698)."},{"num":9900,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ سَمُرَةَ، قَالَ: جَاءَ عُثْمَانُ بْنُ عَفَّانَ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِأَلْفِ دِينَارٍ فِي ثَوْبِهِ، حِينَ جَهَّزَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جَيْشَ الْعُسْرَةِ، قَالَ: فَصَبَّهَا فِي حِجْرِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَجَعَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، يُقَلِّبُهَا بِيَدِهِ، وَيَقُولُ: مَا ضَرَّ ابْنُ عَفَّانَ مَا عَمِلَ بَعْدَ الْيَوْمِ، يُرَدِّدُهَا مِرَارًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3701)، وأحمد (20630)، وابن أبي عاصم في الجهاد (82)، والحاكم (4553) كلهم من حديث ضمرة بن ربيعة، عن عبد الله بن شؤذب، عن عبد الله بن القاسم، عن كثير مولى عبد الرحمن بن سمرة، عن عبدالرحمن بن سمرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قوله: ما ضرَّ عثمانَ ما عمل بعد تجهيز جيش العسرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3701), Aḥmad (20630), Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Jihād (82), and al-Ḥākim (3/102).","chapter_en":"The Statement,\n“Nothing that ʿUthmān Does After Equipping the Army of Hardship Will Harm Him”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān came to the Prophet ﷺ carrying one thousand dinars wrapped in his garment when the Prophet ﷺ was preparing the Army of Hardship. He poured them into the lap of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ began turning the coins over with his hand while repeatedly saying: “Nothing that Ibn ʿAffān does after this day will harm him.” He repeated these words several times."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",99],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9255],"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3701)، وأحمد (20630)، وابن أبي عاصم في الجهاد (82)، والحاكم (4553)."},{"num":9901,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ، أَنَّ عُثْمَانَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ حَيْثُ حُوصِرَ أَشْرَفَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَقَالَ: أَنْشُدُكُمْ، وَلاَ أَنْشُدُ إِلاَّ أَصْحَابَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، أَلَسْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَنْ حَفَرَ رُومَةَ فَلَهُ الْجَنَّةُ. فَحَفَرْتُهَا، أَلَسْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: مَنْ جَهَّزَ جَيْشَ الْعُسْرَةِ فَلَهُ الْجَنَّةُ. فَجَهَّزْتُهُمْ. قَالَ: فَصَدَّقُوهُ بِمَا قَالَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الوصايا (778) قال: قال عبدان، أخبرني أبي، عن شعبة، عن أبي إسحاق، عن أبي عبد الرحمن السلمي أن عثمان فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قوله: ما ضرَّ عثمانَ ما عمل بعد تجهيز جيش العسرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2778).","chapter_en":"The Statement,\n“Nothing that ʿUthmān Does After Equipping the Army of Hardship Will Harm Him”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated: When ʿUthmān was under siege, he addressed the people from above and said: “I adjure you by Allah—and I ask only the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ— Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Whoever develops the Well of Rūmah shall have Paradise,’ and I was the one who developed it? Do you not know that he also said: ‘Whoever equips the Army of Hardship shall have Paradise,’ and I was the one who equipped it?” The people acknowledged that what he had said was true."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",100],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (778)."},{"num":9902,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سَعِيدِ بْنِ زَيْدٍ بن عمرو بْنِ نُفَيْلٍ فِي مَسْجِدِ الْكُوفَةِ: يَقُولُ وَاللَّهِ لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنِي وَإِنَّ عُمَرَ لَمُوثِقِي عَلَى الإِسْلاَمِ قَبْلَ أَنْ يُسْلِمَ، عُمَرُ، وَلَوْ أَنَّ أُحُدًا ارْفَضَّ لِلَّذِي صَنَعْتُمْ بِعُثْمَانَ لَكَانَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3862) عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا سفيان، عن إسماعيل، عن قيس قال: سمعت سعيد بن زيد بن عمرو بن نفيل في مسجد الكوفة يقول: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار عثمان بن عفان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3862). Another wording is recorded by al-Bukhārī (3867).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿīd ibn Zayd ibn ʿAmr ibn Nufayl said in the Mosque of Kūfah: “By Allah, I remember the time when ʿUmar had me bound because I had accepted Islam, before he himself embraced Islam. If Mount Uḥud had collapsed because of what you have done to ʿUthmān, it would have been justified.” Another wording states: “If you had seen me when ʿUmar had both me and his own sister bound because of Islam before he embraced Islam! If Mount Uḥud had collapsed because of what you have done to ʿUthmān, it would certainly have had every right to collapse.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",101],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9886],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3862). وفي لفظ: رواه البخاري (3867)."},{"num":9903,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ بن عدي بْنِ الْخِيَارِ أَخْبَرَهُ: أَنَّ الْمِسْوَرَ بْنَ مَخْرَمَةَ وَعَبْدَ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنَ الأَسْوَدِ بْنِ عَبْدِ يَغُوثَ قَالاَ لَهُ: مَا يَمْنَعُكَ أَنْ تُكَلِّمَ خَالَكَ عُثْمَانَ فِي أَخِيهِ الْوَلِيدِ بْنِ عُقْبَةَ، وَكَانَ أَكْثَرَ النَّاسُ فِيمَا فَعَلَ بِهِ. قَالَ عُبَيْدُ اللَّهِ: فَانْتَصَبْتُ لِعُثْمَانَ حِينَ خَرَجَ إِلَى الصَّلاَةِ، فَقُلْتُ لَهُ: إِنَّ لِي إِلَيْكَ حَاجَةً، وَهْىَ نَصِيحَةٌ. فَقَالَ: أَيُّهَا الْمَرْءُ، أَعُوذُ بِاللَّهِ مِنْكَ، فَانْصَرَفْتُ، فَلَمَّا قَضَيْتُ الصَّلاَةَ جَلَسْتُ إِلَى الْمِسْوَرِ وَإِلَى ابْنِ عَبْدِ يَغُوثَ، فَحَدَّثْتُهُمَا بِالَّذِي قُلْتُ لِعُثْمَانَ وَقَالَ لِي. فَقَالاَ: قَدْ قَضَيْتَ الَّذِي كَانَ عَلَيْكَ. فَبَيْنَمَا أَنَا جَالِسٌ مَعَهُمَا، إِذْ جَاءَنِي رَسُولُ عُثْمَانَ، فَقَالاَ لِي: قَدِ ابْتَلاَكَ اللَّهُ. فَانْطَلَقْتُ حَتَّى دَخَلْتُ عَلَيْهِ، فَقَالَ: مَا نَصِيحَتُكَ الَّتِي ذَكَرْتَ آنِفًا قَالَ فَتَشَهَّدْتُ، ثُمَّ قُلْتُ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ بَعَثَ مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَأَنْزَلَ عَلَيْهِ الْكِتَابَ، وَكُنْتَ مِمَّنِ اسْتَجَابَ لِلَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَآمَنْتَ بِهِ، وَهَاجَرْتَ الْهِجْرَتَيْنِ الأُولَيَيْنِ، وَصَحِبْتَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَرَأَيْتَ هَدْيَهُ، وَقَدْ أَكْثَرَ النَّاسُ فِي شَأْنِ الْوَلِيدِ بْنِ عُقْبَةَ، فَحَقٌّ عَلَيْكَ أَنْ تُقِيمَ عَلَيْهِ الْحَدَّ. فَقَالَ لِي: يَا ابْنَ أَخِي أَدْرَكْتَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: لاَ، وَلَكِنْ قَدْ خَلَصَ إِلَىَّ مِنْ عِلْمِهِ مَا خَلَصَ إِلَى الْعَذْرَاءِ فِي سِتْرِهَا. قَالَ فَتَشَهَّدَ عُثْمَانُ، فَقَالَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ بَعَثَ مُحَمَّدًا صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْحَقِّ، وَأَنْزَلَ عَلَيْهِ الْكِتَابَ، وَكُنْتُ مِمَّنِ اسْتَجَابَ لِلَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَآمَنْتُ بِمَا بُعِثَ بِهِ مُحَمَّدٌ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. وَهَاجَرْتُ الْهِجْرَتَيْنِ الأُولَيَيْنِ كَمَا قُلْتَ، وَصَحِبْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَبَايَعْتُهُ، وَاللَّهِ مَا عَصَيْتُهُ وَلاَ غَشَشْتُهُ حَتَّى تَوَفَّاهُ اللَّهُ، ثُمَّ اسْتَخْلَفَ اللَّهُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ، فَوَاللَّهِ مَا عَصَيْتُهُ وَلاَ غَشَشْتُهُ، ثُمَّ اسْتُخْلِفَ عُمَرُ، فَوَاللَّهِ مَا عَصَيْتُهُ وَلاَ غَشَشْتُهُ، ثُمَّ اسْتُخْلِفْتُ، أَفَلَيْسَ لِي عَلَيْكُمْ مِثْلُ الَّذِي كَانَ لَهُمْ عَلَىَّ؟ قَالَ: بَلَى. قَالَ فَمَا هَذِهِ الأَحَادِيثُ الَّتِي تَبْلُغُنِي عَنْكُمْ؟ فَأَمَّا مَا ذَكَرْتَ مِنْ شَأْنِ الْوَلِيدِ بْنِ عُقْبَةَ، فَسَنَأْخُذُ فِيهِ إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ بِالْحَقِّ، قَالَ: فَجَلَدَ الْوَلِيدَ أَرْبَعِينَ جَلْدَةً، وَأَمَرَ عَلِيًّا أَنْ يَجْلِدَهُ، وَكَانَ هُوَ يَجْلِدُهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3872) عن عبد الله بن محمد الجعفي، ثنا هشام، أنا معمر، عن الزهري، ثنا عروة بن الزبير، أن عبيد الله بن عدي بن الخيار أخبره فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار عثمان بن عفان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3872).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAdī ibn al-Khiyār reported that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad ibn ʿAbd Yaghūth said to him: “Why do you not speak to your maternal uncle, ʿUthmān, concerning his brother al-Walīd ibn ʿUqbah? The people have spoken much about what happened regarding him.” ʿUbaydullāh said: I stood waiting for ʿUthmān as he came out for the prayer and said, “I have something to say to you as sincere advice.” He replied, “O man, I seek refuge in Allah from you.” So I withdrew. After the prayer I sat with al-Miswar and Ibn ʿAbd Yaghūth and informed them of what had occurred. They said: “You have fulfilled your duty.” While I was sitting with them, a messenger from ʿUthmān came to summon me. They said: “Allah has now put you to the test.” I entered upon ʿUthmān, who asked: “What was the advice you mentioned earlier?” I praised Allah and testified to the faith, then said: “Allah sent Muḥammad ﷺ with the truth and revealed the Book to him. You were among those who responded to Allah and His Messenger, believed in him, migrated the two migrations, accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and witnessed his guidance. The people have spoken much regarding al-Walīd ibn ʿUqbah, so it is your duty to carry out the prescribed punishment upon him.” ʿUthmān asked: “My nephew, did you meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” I replied: “No, but knowledge of him has reached me just as surely as it reaches a secluded virgin behind her curtain.” ʿUthmān then praised Allah and said: “Allah sent Muḥammad ﷺ with the truth and revealed the Book to him. I responded to Allah and His Messenger, believed in what Muḥammad ﷺ was sent with, made the two migrations as you have mentioned, accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and pledged allegiance to him. By Allah, I never disobeyed him nor betrayed him until Allah took him in death. Then Allah appointed Abū Bakr as Caliph, and by Allah, I neither disobeyed him nor betrayed him. Then ʿUmar became Caliph, and by Allah, I neither disobeyed him nor betrayed him. Then I became Caliph. Do I not deserve from you the same loyalty that they deserved from me?” They replied: “Indeed.” He continued: “Then what are these reports that reach me from among you? As for what you have mentioned concerning al-Walīd ibn ʿUqbah, we shall, Allah willing, deal with him according to the truth.” The narrator said: Al-Walīd was then flogged with forty lashes, and ʿUthmān instructed ʿAlī to carry out the punishment, and ʿAlī himself administered the lashes."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",102],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3872)."},{"num":9904,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بْنِ عُبَيْدَةَ، قَالَ: جَاءَ رَجُلٌ إِلَى ابْنِ عُمَرَ، فَسَأَلَهُ عَنْ عُثْمَانَ،، فَذَكَرَ عَنْ مَحَاسِنِ، عَمَلِهِ، قَالَ: لَعَلَّ ذَاكَ يَسُوؤُكَ. قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ فَأَرْغَمَ اللَّهُ بِأَنْفِكَ. ثُمَّ سَأَلَهُ عَنْ عَلِيٍّ، فَذَكَرَ مَحَاسِنَ عَمَلِهِ، قَالَ: هُوَ ذَاكَ، بَيْتُهُ أَوْسَطُ بُيُوتِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. ثُمَّ قَالَ: لَعَلَّ ذَاكَ يَسُوؤُكَ. قَالَ: أَجَلْ. قَالَ فَأَرْغَمَ اللَّهُ بِأَنْفِكَ، انْطَلِقْ فَاجْهَدْ عَلَىَّ جَهْدَكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3704) عن محمد بن رافع، ثنا حسين، عن زائدة، عن أبي حصين، عن سعد بن عبيدة قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار عثمان بن عفان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3704).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah said: A man came to Ibn ʿUmar and asked him about ʿUthmān. Ibn ʿUmar mentioned his good qualities and virtuous deeds. He then said: “Perhaps that displeases you?” The man replied: “Yes.” Ibn ʿUmar said: “May Allah humble you.” Then the man asked him about ʿAlī. Ibn ʿUmar mentioned his virtues and good qualities and then pointed toward his house, saying: “That is his house, situated among the houses of the Prophet ﷺ.” He then asked: “Perhaps that displeases you?” The man replied: “Yes.” Ibn ʿUmar said: “May Allah humble you. Go and do whatever you can against me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",103],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9930],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3704)."},{"num":9905,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ قَالَ: ذَكَرَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِتْنَةً، فَمَرَّ رَجُلٌ، فَقَالَ: يُقْتَلُ فِيهَا هَذَا الْمُقَنَّعُ يَوْمَئِذٍ مَظْلُومًا، قَالَ: فَنَظَرْتُ، فَإِذَا هُوَ عُثْمَانُ بْنُ عَفَّانَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3708)، وأحمد (5953) كلاهما من حديث الأسود بن عامر، عن سنان بن هارون(هو البرجمي)، عن كليب بن وائل، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قوله: إن عثمان يقتل مظلومًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3708) and Aḥmad (5953).","chapter_en":"The Statement,\n“Indeed, ʿUthmān Will Be Killed While Wronged”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once mentioned a coming trial (fitnah). As he was speaking, a man passed by. The Prophet ﷺ said: “This veiled man will be killed during that trial while being wronged.” Ibn ʿUmar said: I looked, and it was ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3708)، وأحمد (5953)."},{"num":9906,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي الأَشْعَثِ الصَّنْعَانِيِّ، أَنَّ خُطَبَاءَ، قَامَتْ بِالشَّامِ، وَفِيهِمْ رِجَالٌ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَامَ آخِرُهُمْ رَجُلٌ يُقَالُ لَهُ: مُرَّةُ بْنُ كَعْبٍ، فَقَالَ: لَوْلاَ حَدِيثٌ سَمِعْتُهُ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَا قُمْتُ. وَذَكَرَ الْفِتَنَ فَقَرَّبَهَا، فَمَرَّ رَجُلٌ مُقَنَّعٌ فِي ثَوْبٍ فَقَالَ: هَذَا يَوْمَئِذٍ عَلَى الْهُدَى، فَقُمْتُ إِلَيْهِ فَإِذَا هُوَ عُثْمَانُ بْنُ عَفَّانَ. قَالَ فَأَقْبَلْتُ عَلَيْهِ بِوَجْهِهِ، فَقُلْتُ: هَذَا؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3704)، وأحمد (18068)، وصحّحه الحاكم (4552) كلهم من طريق أيوب، عن أبي قلابة، عن أبي الأشعث (وهو شراحيل بن آده) قال: فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قوله: إن عثمان يقتل مظلومًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3704), Aḥmad (18068), and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (4552), all through Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Abū al-Ashʿath—Shurāḥīl ibn Ādah—who related the report. Its chain is authentic.","chapter_en":"The Statement,\n“Indeed, ʿUthmān Will Be Killed While Wronged”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū al-Ashʿath al-Ṣanʿānī narrated: A group of speakers addressed the people in Syria, among whom were several Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The last to stand was a man named Murrah ibn Kaʿb. He said: “Had I not heard a statement from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would not have stood to speak.” He then mentioned the future trials and said they were drawing near. At that moment, a man passed by with his face covered by his garment. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This man, on that day, will be upon true guidance.” I went toward him and looked at his face. It was ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān. I turned him toward me and asked: “This man?” He replied: “Yes.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",105],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3704)، وأحمد (18068)، وصححه الحاكم (4552). وإسناده صحيح."},{"num":9907,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، قَالَتْ: أَرْسَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى عُثْمَانَ بْنِ عَفَّانَ، فَأَقْبَلَ عَلَيْهِ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَلَمَّا رَأَيْنَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، أَقْبَلَتْ إِحْدَانَا عَلَى الْأُخْرَى، فَكَانَ مِنْ آخِرِ كَلَامٍ كَلَّمَهُ، أَنْ ضَرَبَ مَنْكِبَهُ، وَقَالَ: يَا عُثْمَانُ، إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ عَسَى أَنْ يُلْبِسَكَ قَمِيصًا، فَإِنْ أَرَادَكَ الْمُنَافِقُونَ عَلَى خَلْعِهِ، فَلَا تَخْلَعْهُ حَتَّى تَلْقَانِي، يَا عُثْمَانُ، إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَسَى أَنْ يُلْبِسَكَ قَمِيصًا، فَإِنْ أَرَادَكَ الْمُنَافِقُونَ عَلَى خَلْعِهِ، فَلَا تَخْلَعْهُ حَتَّى تَلْقَانِي ثَلَاثًا، فَقُلْتُ لَهَا: يَا أُمَّ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، فَأَيْنَ كَانَ هَذَا عَنْكِ؟ قَالَتْ: نَسِيتُهُ، وَاللهِ فَمَا ذَكَرْتُهُ. قَالَ: فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ مُعَاوِيَةَ بْنَ أَبِي سُفْيَانَ، فَلَمْ يَرْضَ بِالَّذِي أَخْبَرْتُهُ حَتَّى كَتَبَ إِلَى أُمِّ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَنْ اكْتُبِي إِلَيَّ بِهِ، فَكَتَبَتْ إِلَيْهِ بِهِ كِتَابًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3705)، و أحمد (24566) كلاهما من طريق ربيعة بن يزيد، عن عبد الله بن عامر، عن النعمان بن بشير، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قوله: إن عثمان يقتل مظلومًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3705) and Aḥmad (24566).","chapter_en":"The Statement,\n“Indeed, ʿUthmān Will Be Killed While Wronged”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān. When ʿUthmān came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke privately with him. When we saw this, we turned our attention away from them toward one another. Among the last things the Prophet ﷺ said to him was that he struck him gently on the shoulder and said: “O ʿUthmān, perhaps Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will clothe you with a garment. If the hypocrites seek to make you remove it, then do not remove it until you meet me. O ʿUthmān, perhaps Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will clothe you with a garment. If the hypocrites seek to make you remove it, then do not remove it until you meet me.” He repeated this three times. The narrator said: I asked her, “O Mother of the Believers, where was this narration all this time?” She replied: “By Allah, I had forgotten it, so I never mentioned it.” The narrator said: I informed Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān of this narration, but he was not satisfied with merely hearing it from me. Instead, he wrote to the Mother of the Believers requesting that she write it to him herself. So she wrote it to him in a letter."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",106],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3705)، وأحمد (24566)."},{"num":9908,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي مَرَضِهِ: وَدِدْتُ أَنَّ عِنْدِي بَعْضَ أَصْحَابِي قُلْنَا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَلاَ نَدْعُو لَكَ أَبَا بَكْرٍ؟ فَسَكَتَ.قُلْنَا: أَلاَ نَدْعُو لَكَ عُمَرَ؟ فَسَكَتَ.قُلْنَا: أَلاَ نَدْعُو لَكَ عُثْمَانَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ فَجَاءَ فَخَلاَ بِهِ، فَجَعَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُكَلِّمُهُ، وَوَجْهُ عُثْمَانَ يَتَغَيَّرُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (113)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (6918) كلاهما من طريق إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن قيس بن أبي حازم، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قوله: إن عثمان يقتل مظلومًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (113), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6918).","chapter_en":"The Statement,\n“Indeed, ʿUthmān Will Be Killed While Wronged”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: During his illness, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I wish that one of my companions were with me.” We said: “O Messenger of Allah, shall we call Abū Bakr for you?” He remained silent. We said: “Shall we call ʿUmar?” Again, he remained silent. We said: “Shall we call ʿUthmān?” He replied: “Yes.” So ʿUthmān came, and the Prophet ﷺ spoke privately with him. As the Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued speaking, the expression on ʿUthmān’s face began to change."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",107],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (113)، وصححه ابن حبان (6918)."},{"num":9909,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سهلة مولى عُثْمَانَ: أَنَّ عُثْمَانَ بْنِ عَفَّانَ قَالَ يَوْمَ الدَّارِ: إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَهِدَ إليَّ عَهْدًا، فَأَنَا صَابِرٌ عَلَيْهِ.قَالَ قَيْسٌ: فَكَانُوا يَرَوْنَهُ ذَلِكَ الْيَوْمَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3711)، وأحمد (407)، والبزار (402) كلهم من طريق إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن قيس بن أبي حازم، قال: حدثني أبو سهلة قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قوله: إن عثمان يقتل مظلومًا","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3711), Aḥmad (407), and al-Bazzār (402).","chapter_en":"The Statement,\n“Indeed, ʿUthmān Will Be Killed While Wronged”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Sahlah, the freed servant of ʿUthmān, narrated that on the day his house was surrounded, ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrusted me with a matter, and I shall remain patient upon it.” Qays said: “They understood that this was what he was referring to on that day.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Qays’ statement,","“They understood that this was what he was referring to on that day,”","refers to the previously mentioned narration of ʿĀ’ishah regarding the Prophet’s ﷺ private conversation with ʿUthmān. Although the two reports occurred at different times—as is evident from their contexts—Ibn Mājah and Ibn Ḥibbān narrated them together because they relate to the same incident."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",108],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3711)، وأحمد (407)، والبزار (402)."},{"num":9910,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ ابْنِ الحَنَفِيَّةِ قَالَ: لَوْ كَانَ عَلِيٌّ رَضِيَ الله عنه ذَاكِرًا عُثْمَانَ رَضِيَ الله عنه ذَكَرَهُ يَوْمَ جَاءَهُ نَاسٌ فَشَكَوْا سُعَاةَ عُثْمَانَ، فَقَالَ لِي عَلِيٌّ: اذْهَبْ إِلَى عُثْمَانَ، فَأَخْبِرْهُ أَنَّهَا صَدَقَةُ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَمُرْ سُعَاتَكَ يَعْمَلُونَ فِيهَا، فَأَتَيْتُهُ بِهَا، فَقَالَ: أَغْنِهَا عَنَّا، فَأَتَيْتُ بِهَا عَلِيًّا، فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ، فَقَالَ: ضَعْهَا حَيْثُ أَخَذْتَهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فرض الخمس (3111) عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا سفيان، عن محمد بن سوقة، عن منذر، عن ابن الحنفية قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في أخبار عثمان بن عفان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3111).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب عثمان بن عفان وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān","part_no":49,"group_no":4,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah said: Had ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) ever wished to speak ill of ʿUthmān, he would have done so on the day when some people came to him complaining about ʿUthmān’s zakāh collectors. Instead, ʿAlī said to me: “Go to ʿUthmān and inform him that this is the instruction of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the collection of charity. Tell him to instruct his collectors to act according to it.” I brought it to ʿUthmān. He said: “We have no need of it.” So I returned to ʿAlī and informed him. He replied: “Put it back where you took it from.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Imām Aḥmad also narrated it (1196) through another chain from Muḥammad ibn Sawqah with additional wording from Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah.","This report demonstrates that a ruler is not obligated to act upon every complaint that reaches him. Rather, he has the right to judge each matter according to what best serves the public interest.","For this reason, ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) excused ʿUthmān and did not speak ill of him.","It also teaches an important etiquette for anyone advising a ruler: one should not become angry if one’s sincere advice is not accepted."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",109],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3111)."},{"num":9911,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سَعْدِ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ قَالَ:  أَمَرَ مُعَاوِيَةُ بْنُ أَبِي سُفْيَانَ سَعْدًا، فَقَالَ: مَا مَنَعَكَ أَنْ تَسُبَّ أَبَا التُّرَابِ؟ فَقَالَ: أَمَّا مَا ذَكَرْتُ ثَلَاثًا قَالَهُنَّ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَلَنْ أَسُبَّهُ لَأَنْ تَكُونَ لِي وَاحِدَةٌ مِنْهُنَّ أَحَبُّ إِلَيَّ مِنْ حُمْرِ النَّعَمِ، سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ لَهُ، خَلَّفَهُ فِي بَعْضِ مَغَازِيهِ، فَقَالَ لَهُ عَلِيٌّ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، خَلَّفْتَنِي مَعَ النِّسَاءِ وَالصِّبْيَانِ! فَقَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَمَا تَرْضَى أَنْ تَكُونَ مِنِّي بِمَنْزِلَةِ هَارُونَ مِنْ مُوسَى، إِلَّا أَنَّهُ لَا نُبُوَّةَ بَعْدِي. وَسَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ يَوْمَ خَيْبَرَ: لَأُعْطِيَنَّ الرَّايَةَ رَجُلًا يُحِبُّ اللهَ وَرَسُولَهُ وَيُحِبُّهُ اللهُ وَرَسُولُهُ. قَالَ: فَتَطَاوَلْنَا لَهَا، فَقَالَ: ادْعُوا لِي عَلِيًّا! فَأُتِيَ بِهِ أَرْمَدَ، فَبَصَقَ فِي عَيْنِهِ، وَدَفَعَ الرَّايَةَ إِلَيْهِ، فَفَتَحَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ، وَلَمَّا نَزَلَتْ هَذِهِ الْآيَةُ: ﴿فَقُلْ تَعَالَوْا نَدْعُ أَبْنَاءَنَا وَأَبْنَاءَكُمْ﴾ دَعَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلِيًّا وَفَاطِمَةَ وَحَسَنًا وَحُسَيْنًا فَقَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ هَؤُلَاءِ أَهْلِي."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2404-32) من طرق عن حاتم بن إسماعيل، عن بكير بن مسمار، عن عامر بن سعد بن أبي وقاص، عن أبيه قال: أمر معاوية فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن علي بن أبي طالب من أهل بيت النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2404, Hadith 32).","chapter_en":"That ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib Is Among the Household of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān asked Saʿd, “What prevents you from reviling Abū Turāb (ʿAlī)?” Saʿd replied: “As long as I remember three statements that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about him, I will never revile him. Possessing even one of those virtues would be more beloved to me than red camels. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to him when he left him behind during one of his military expeditions. ʿAlī said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, are you leaving me behind with the women and children?’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: ‘Are you not pleased that your position to me is like the position of Hārūn (Aaron) to Mūsā (Moses), except that there will be no prophet after me?’ I also heard him say on the Day of Khaybar: ‘Tomorrow I will certainly give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love.’ We all hoped it would be given to us. Then he said: ‘Call ʿAlī for me.’ He was brought while suffering from an eye ailment. The Prophet ﷺ applied his saliva to his eyes and handed him the banner, and Allah granted victory through him. And when the following verse was revealed: “Say, ‘Come, let us call our sons and your sons…’” (Āl ʿImrān 3:61), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called ʿAlī, Fāṭimah, al-Ḥasan, and al-Ḥusayn, and said: “O Allah, these are my family.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (32-2404)."},{"num":9912,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن يَزِيدَ بْنِ حَيَّانَ قَالَ:  انْطَلَقْتُ أَنَا وَحُصَيْنُ بْنُ سَبْرَةَ وَعُمَرُ بْنُ مُسْلِمٍ إِلَى زَيْدِ بْنِ أَرْقَمَ، فَلَمَّا جَلَسْنَا إِلَيْهِ قَالَ لَهُ حُصَيْنٌ: لَقَدْ لَقِيتَ يَا زَيْدُ خَيْرًا كَثِيرًا، رَأَيْتَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَسَمِعْتَ حَدِيثَهُ، وَغَزَوْتَ مَعَهُ، وَصَلَّيْتَ خَلْفَهُ، لَقَدْ لَقِيتَ يَا زَيْدُ خَيْرًا كَثِيرًا، حَدِّثْنَا يَا زَيْدُ مَا سَمِعْتَ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. قَالَ: يَا ابْنَ أَخِي، وَاللهِ لَقَدْ كَبِرَتْ سِنِّي، وَقَدُمَ عَهْدِي، وَنَسِيتُ بَعْضَ الَّذِي كُنْتُ أَعِي مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَمَا حَدَّثْتُكُمْ فَاقْبَلُوا، وَمَا لَا فَلَا تُكَلِّفُونِيهِ. ثُمَّ قَالَ: قَامَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمًا فِينَا خَطِيبًا بِمَاءٍ يُدْعَى خُمًّا بَيْنَ مَكَّةَ وَالْمَدِينَةِ، فَحَمِدَ اللَّهَ، وَأَثْنَى عَلَيْهِ، وَوَعَظَ وَذَكَّرَ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَمَّا بَعْدُ، أَلَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، فَإِنَّمَا أَنَا بَشَرٌ يُوشِكُ أَنْ يَأْتِيَ رَسُولُ رَبِّي فَأُجِيبَ، وَأَنَا تَارِكٌ فِيكُمْ ثَقَلَيْنِ، أَوَّلُهُمَا كِتَابُ اللَّهِ، فِيهِ الْهُدَى وَالنُّورُ، فَخُذُوا بِكِتَابِ اللَّهِ وَاسْتَمْسِكُوا بِهِ - فَحَثَّ عَلَى كِتَابِ اللَّهِ، وَرَغَّبَ فِيهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: وَأَهْلُ بَيْتِي، أُذَكِّرُكُمُ اللهَ فِي أَهْلِ بَيْتِي، أُذَكِّرُكُمُ اللهَ فِي أَهْلِ بَيْتِي، أُذَكِّرُكُمُ اللهَ فِي أَهْلِ بَيْتِي. فَقَالَ لَهُ حُصَيْنٌ: وَمَنْ أَهْلُ بَيْتِهِ يَا زَيْدُ؟ أَلَيْسَ نِسَاؤُهُ مِنْ أَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ؟ قَالَ: نِسَاؤُهُ مِنْ أَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ، وَلَكِنْ أَهْلُ بَيْتِهِ مَنْ حُرِمَ الصَّدَقَةَ بَعْدَهُ. قَالَ: وَمَنْ هُمْ؟ قَالَ: هُمْ آلُ عَلِيٍّ، وَآلُ عَقِيلٍ، وَآلُ جَعْفَرٍ، وَآلُ عَبَّاسٍ. قَالَ: كُلُّ هَؤُلَاءِ حُرِمَ الصَّدَقَةَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2408-36) من طرق عن ابن علية، ثني أبو حيان، ثني يزيد بن حيان قال: انطلقت أنا فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن علي بن أبي طالب من أهل بيت النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2408, Hadith 36).","chapter_en":"That ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib Is Among the Household of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yazīd ibn Ḥayyān said: I, Ḥuṣayn ibn Sabrah, and ʿUmar ibn Muslim went to Zayd ibn Arqam. After we sat with him, Ḥuṣayn said: “O Zayd, you have been blessed with tremendous good. You saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, heard his narrations, fought alongside him, and prayed behind him. Tell us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Zayd replied: “My nephew, by Allah, I have become old, much time has passed, and I have forgotten some of what I once preserved from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Whatever I narrate to you, accept it, and whatever I do not narrate, do not burden me concerning it.” He then said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once stood among us delivering a sermon at a watering place called Khumm, between Makkah and Madinah. After praising Allah, glorifying Him, exhorting, and reminding the people, he said: “Indeed, I am only a human being. Soon the messenger of my Lord will come to me, and I will answer His call. I am leaving among you two weighty matters. The first of them is the Book of Allah, in which there is guidance and light. Therefore, hold firmly to the Book of Allah and cling to it.” He strongly encouraged adherence to the Book of Allah. Then he said: “And my household. I remind you by Allah concerning my household. I remind you by Allah concerning my household. I remind you by Allah concerning my household.” Ḥuṣayn then asked: “Who are the members of his household, O Zayd? Are not his wives included among his household?” Zayd replied: “His wives are indeed among his household. However, those specifically intended here are those for whom charity became unlawful after him.” He asked: “Who are they?” Zayd replied: “They are the family of ʿAlī, the family of ʿAqīl, the family of Jaʿfar, and the family of al-ʿAbbās.” He asked: “Was charity forbidden for all of them?” Zayd replied: “Yes.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Another wording recorded by Muslim states:","“Indeed, I am leaving among you two weighty matters. One of them is the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. It is the Rope of Allah. Whoever follows it is upon guidance, and whoever abandons it is upon misguidance.”","It also includes:","We asked:","“Who are the members of his household? His wives?”","He replied:","“No. By Allah, a woman may remain with a man for a long period of time, then he divorces her and she returns to her father and her people. Rather, his household here refers to his blood relatives and clan for whom charity was prohibited after him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",111],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9304],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (36-2408)."},{"num":9913,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَرَجَ إِلَى تَبُوكَ، وَاسْتَخْلَفَ عَلِيًّا، فَقَالَ: أَتُخَلِّفُنِي فِي الصِّبْيَانِ وَالنِّسَاءِ؟ قَالَ: أَلاَ تَرْضَى أَنْ تَكُونَ مِنِّي بِمَنْزِلَةِ هَارُونَ مِنْ مُوسَى؟ إِلاَّ أَنَّهُ لَيْسَ نَبِيٌّ بَعْدِي."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4416)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2404-31) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، عن الحكم، عن مصعب بن سعد، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب منزلة علي من النبي ﷺ كمنزلة هارون من موسى إلا أنه لا نبي بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4416) and Muslim (2404, Hadith 31).","chapter_en":"The Status of ʿAlī in Relation to the Prophet ﷺ Is Like the Status of Hārūn (Aaron) to Mūsā (Moses), Except That There Is No Prophet After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed for the expedition of Tabūk and appointed ʿAlī as his deputy in Madinah. ʿAlī said: “Are you leaving me behind with the women and the children?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Are you not pleased that your position in relation to me is like the position of Hārūn (Aaron) in relation to Mūsā (Moses), except that there is no prophet after me?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",112],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4416)، ومسلم (31-2404)."},{"num":9914,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ لِعَلِيٍّ: أَنْتَ مِنِّي بِمَنْزِلَةِ هَارُونَ مِنْ مُوسَى إِلاَّ أَنَّهُ لاَ نَبِيَّ بَعْدِي."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3730) عن محمود بن غيلان، حدثنا أبو أحمد الزبيري، حدثنا شريك، عن عبد الله بن محمد بن عقيل، عن جابر بن عبد الله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب منزلة علي من النبي ﷺ كمنزلة هارون من موسى إلا أنه لا نبي بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3730) and Aḥmad (14638).","chapter_en":"The Status of ʿAlī in Relation to the Prophet ﷺ Is Like the Status of Hārūn (Aaron) to Mūsā (Moses), Except That There Is No Prophet After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAlī: “You are to me in the position of Hārūn (Aaron) in relation to Mūsā (Moses), except that there is no prophet after me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",113],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[761],"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3730)، وأحمد (14638)."},{"num":9915,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أَسْمَاءَ بِنْتِ عُمَيْسٍ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ لِعَلِيٍّ: أَنْتَ مِنِّي بِمَنْزِلَةِ هَارُونَ مِنْ مُوسَى، إِلَّا أَنَّهُ لَيْسَ بَعْدِي نَبِيٌّ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (27081)، والنسائيّ في الكبرى (8143)، والطبرانيّ في الكبير (ج24/146-147)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (1381 - بتحقيق باسم) كلّهم من طريق موسى الجهنيّ قال: دخلتُ على فاطمة بنت عليّ، فقال لها رفيقي أبو مَهَل: كم لكِ؟ قالت: ستة وثمانون سنة.قال: ما سمعتِ من أبيك شيئاً؟ قالت: حدَّثتني أسماءُ بنتُ عميس فذكرت الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب منزلة علي من النبي ﷺ كمنزلة هارون من موسى إلا أنه لا نبي بعده","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (27081), al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8143), and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (24/146–147, no. 1470).","chapter_en":"The Status of ʿAlī in Relation to the Prophet ﷺ Is Like the Status of Hārūn (Aaron) to Mūsā (Moses), Except That There Is No Prophet After Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿAlī: “You are to me in the position of Hārūn (Aaron) in relation to Mūsā (Moses), except that there will be no prophet after me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[760],"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (27081)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8143)، والطبراني في الكبير (24/146-147، 1470)."},{"num":9916,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَهْلِ بْنِ سَعْدٍ قَالَ:  اسْتُعْمِلَ عَلَى الْمَدِينَةِ رَجُلٌ مِنْ آلِ مَرْوَانَ، قَالَ: فَدَعَا سَهْلَ بْنَ سَعْدٍ، فَأَمَرَهُ أَنْ يَشْتِمَ عَلِيًّا، قَالَ: فَأَبَى سَهْلٌ، فَقَالَ لَهُ: أَمَّا إِذْ أَبَيْتَ فَقُلْ: لَعَنَ اللَّهُ أَبَا التُّرَابِ! فَقَالَ سَهْلٌ: مَا كَانَ لِعَلِيٍّ اسْمٌ أَحَبَّ إِلَيْهِ مِنْ أَبِي التُّرَابِ، وَإِنْ كَانَ لَيَفْرَحُ إِذَا دُعِيَ بِهَا. فَقَالَ لَهُ: أَخْبِرْنَا عَنْ قِصَّتِهِ، لِمَ سُمِّيَ أَبَا تُرَابٍ؟ قَالَ: جَاءَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَيْتَ فَاطِمَةَ فَلَمْ يَجِدْ عَلِيًّا فِي الْبَيْتِ، فَقَالَ: أَيْنَ ابْنُ عَمِّكِ؟ فَقَالَتْ: كَانَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَهُ شَيْءٌ، فَغَاضَبَنِي فَخَرَجَ، فَلَمْ يَقِلْ عِنْدِي! فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِإِنْسَانٍ: انْظُرْ أَيْنَ هُوَ؟ فَجَاءَ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، هُوَ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ رَاقِدٌ. فَجَاءَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُوَ مُضْطَجِعٌ قَدْ سَقَطَ رِدَاؤُهُ عَنْ شِقِّهِ فَأَصَابَهُ تُرَابٌ، فَجَعَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَمْسَحُهُ عَنْهُ وَيَقُولُ: قُمْ أَبَا التُّرَابِ، قُمْ أَبَا التُّرَابِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الصلاة (441)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2409) كلاهما عن قتيبة بن سعيد، ثنا عبد العزيز بن أبي حازم، عن أبي حازم، عن سهل بن سعد فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب لقبه النبي ﷺ بأبي تراب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (441) and Muslim (2409).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Gave Him the Title “Abū Turāb”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A man from the family of Marwān was appointed governor over Madinah. He summoned Sahl ibn Saʿd and ordered him to revile ʿAlī. Sahl refused. The governor said: “If you refuse, then at least say: ‘May Allah curse Abū Turāb.’” Sahl replied: “There was no name more beloved to ʿAlī than Abū Turāb. In fact, he would become happy whenever he was called by it.” They asked him: “Tell us the story. Why was he called Abū Turāb?” He replied: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the house of Fāṭimah but did not find ʿAlī there. He asked: “Where is your cousin?” She replied: “Something occurred between us. He became upset with me and left without taking his midday rest here.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to someone: “Go and see where he is.” The man returned and said: “O Messenger of Allah, he is lying down in the mosque.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to him and found him reclining. His cloak had slipped from one side of his body, and dust had settled upon him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began brushing the dust off him while saying: “Get up, O Abū Turāb. Get up, O Abū Turāb.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording, al-Bukhārī adds after the words:","“He would become happy whenever he was called by it,”","the following statement:","“No one gave him the name ‘Abū Turāb’ except the Prophet ﷺ.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",115],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (441)، ومسلم (2409)."},{"num":9917,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَلَمَةَ، قَالَ: كَانَ عَلِيٌّ قَدْ تَخَلَّفَ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي خَيْبَرَ، وَكَانَ بِهِ رَمَدٌ، فَقَالَ: أَنَا أَتَخَلَّفُ عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَخَرَجَ عَلِيٌّ فَلَحِقَ بِالنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَلَمَّا كَانَ مَسَاءُ اللَّيْلَةِ الَّتِي فَتَحَهَا اللَّهُ فِي صَبَاحِهَا، قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لأُعْطِيَنَّ الرَّايَةَ ـ أَوْ لَيَأْخُذَنَّ الرَّايَةَ ـ غَدًا رَجُلاً يُحِبُّهُ اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ، ـ أَوْ قَالَ: يُحِبُّ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ، ـ يَفْتَحُ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ. فَإِذَا نَحْنُ بِعَلِيٍّ، وَمَا نَرْجُوهُ، فَقَالُوا: هَذَا عَلِيٌّ. فَأَعْطَاهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَفَتَحَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3702) وفي المغازي bukhari(4209)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2407) كلاهما من طريق حاتم بن إسماعيل، عن يزيد بن أبي عبيد، عن سلمة بن الأكوع قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بشارة النبي ﷺ أن الله يفتح خيبر على يد علي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3702 and 4209) and Muslim (2407).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Gave Glad Tidings That Allah Would Grant the Conquest of Khaybar Through the Hands of ʿAlī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ʿAlī had remained behind during the expedition to Khaybar because he was suffering from an eye inflammation. He said: “Should I remain behind while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ goes forth?” So ʿAlī set out and caught up with the Prophet ﷺ. On the evening before Allah granted the conquest the following morning, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Tomorrow I will surely give the banner—or tomorrow the banner will be taken—by a man whom Allah and His Messenger love, or he said, who loves Allah and His Messenger. Through him Allah will grant victory.” We looked around, not expecting ʿAlī because of his condition. Then it was said: “Here is ʿAlī.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ handed him the banner, and Allah granted victory through him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3702، 4209)، ومسلم (2407)."},{"num":9918,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سهل بْنِ سَعْدٍ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ يَوْمَ خَيْبَرَ: لَأُعْطِيَنَّ هَذِهِ الرَّايَةَ رَجُلًا يَفْتَحُ اللَّهُ عَلَى يَدَيْهِ، يُحِبُّ اللهَ وَرَسُولَهُ، وَيُحِبُّهُ اللهُ وَرَسُولُهُ! قَالَ: فَبَاتَ النَّاسُ يَدُوكُونَ لَيْلَتَهُمْ أَيُّهُمْ يُعْطَاهَا! قَالَ: فَلَمَّا أَصْبَحَ النَّاسُ غَدَوْا عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كُلُّهُمْ يَرْجُونَ أَنْ يُعْطَاهَا، فَقَالَ: أَيْنَ عَلِيُّ بْنُ أَبِي طَالِبٍ؟ فَقَالُوا: هُوَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ يَشْتَكِي عَيْنَيْهِ! قَالَ: فَأَرْسَِلُوا إِلَيْهِ. فَأُتِيَ بِهِ، فَبَصَقَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي عَيْنَيْهِ، وَدَعَا لَهُ فَبَرَأَ، حَتَّى كَأَنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ بِهِ وَجَعٌ، فَأَعْطَاهُ الرَّايَةَ، فَقَالَ عَلِيٌّ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أُقَاتِلُهُمْ حَتَّى يَكُونُوا مِثْلَنَا؟ فَقَالَ: انْفُذْ عَلَى رِسْلِكَ حَتَّى تَنْزِلَ بِسَاحَتِهِمْ، ثُمَّ ادْعُهُمْ إِلَى الْإِسْلَامِ، وَأَخْبِرْهُمْ بِمَا يَجِبُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِنْ حَقِّ اللَّهِ فِيهِ، فَوَاللهِ لَأَنْ يَهْدِيَ اللهُ بِكَ رَجُلًا وَاحِدًا خَيْرٌ لَكَ مِنْ أَنْ يَكُونَ لَكَ حُمْرُ النَّعَمِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الجهاد (2942) وفي فضائل الصحابة bukhari(3701) وفي المغازي bukhari(4210)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2406) كلاهما من طريق عبدالعزيز بن أبي حازم، عن أبيه، عن سهل بن سعد سمع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب بشارة النبي ﷺ أن الله يفتح خيبر على يد علي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2942, 3701, and 4210) and Muslim (2406).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Gave Glad Tidings That Allah Would Grant the Conquest of Khaybar Through the Hands of ʿAlī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that on the Day of Khaybar the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I will surely give this banner to a man through whose hands Allah will grant victory. He loves Allah and His Messenger, and Allah and His Messenger love him.” The people spent that night discussing among themselves, each hoping that he would be the one to receive it. The next morning they all came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hoping it would be given to them. He asked: “Where is ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib?” They replied: “O Messenger of Allah, he is suffering from pain in his eyes.” He said: “Send for him.” ʿAlī was brought before him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ applied his blessed saliva to ʿAlī’s eyes and supplicated for him. He was immediately cured, as though he had never suffered any pain. The Prophet ﷺ then gave him the banner. ʿAlī asked: “O Messenger of Allah, should I fight them until they become like us?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Proceed calmly until you reach their territory. Then invite them to Islam and inform them of the rights Allah has made obligatory upon them. By Allah, if Allah guides even one man through you, it is better for you than possessing red camels.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2942)، وbukhari(3701، 4210)، ومسلم (2406)."},{"num":9919,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ  أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ يَوْمَ خَيْبَرَ: لَأُعْطِيَنَّ هَذِهِ الرَّايَةَ رَجُلًا يُحِبُّ اللهَ وَرَسُولَهُ يَفْتَحُ اللَّهُ عَلَى يَدَيْهِ! قَالَ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ: مَا أَحْبَبْتُ الْإِمَارَةَ إِلَّا يَوْمَئِذٍ! قَالَ: فَتَسَاوَرْتُ لَهَا رَجَاءَ أَنْ أُدْعَى لَهَا. قَالَ: فَدَعَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلِيَّ بْنَ أَبِي طَالِبٍ فَأَعْطَاهُ إِيَّاهَا، وَقَالَ: امْشِ، وَلَا تَلْتَفِتْ حَتَّى يَفْتَحَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْكَ. قَالَ: فَسَارَ عَلِيٌّ شَيْئًا، ثُمَّ وَقَفَ وَلَمْ يَلْتَفِتْ، فَصَرَخَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، عَلَى مَاذَا أُقَاتِلُ النَّاسَ؟ قَالَ: قَاتِلْهُمْ حَتَّى يَشْهَدُوا أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، فَإِذَا فَعَلُوا ذَلِكَ فَقَدْ مَنَعُوا مِنْكَ دِمَاءَهُمْ وَأَمْوَالَهُمْ إِلَّا بِحَقِّهَا وَحِسَابُهُمْ عَلَى اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2405) عن قتيبة بن سعيد، ثنا يعقوب بن عبد الرحمن القارّي، عن سهيل، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بشارة النبي ﷺ أن الله يفتح خيبر على يد علي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2405).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Gave Glad Tidings That Allah Would Grant the Conquest of Khaybar Through the Hands of ʿAlī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that on the Day of Khaybar the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I will surely give this banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger. Allah will grant victory through his hands.” ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said: “I never desired leadership except on that day.” He continued: “I stretched myself forward, hoping that I would be called.” Instead, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib and gave him the banner, saying: “Go, and do not turn back until Allah grants you victory.” ʿAlī walked a short distance, then stopped without turning around and called out: “O Messenger of Allah, upon what should I fight the people?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Fight them until they testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah. If they do so, they have protected from you their lives and their property except by the right of Islam, and their reckoning rests with Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[7861,9043],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2405)."},{"num":9920,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عِمْرَانَ بْنِ حَصِينٍ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَأُعْطِيَنَّ الرَّايَةَ رَجُلًا يُحِبُّ اللهَ وَرَسُولَهُ أَوْ قَالَ: يُحِبُّهُ اللهُ وَرَسُولُهُ فَدَعَا عَلِيًّا، وَهُوَ أَرْمَدُ، فَفَتَحَ اللَّهُ عَلَى يَعْنِي يَدَيْهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (8094، 8353) والطبراني في الكبير (18/237) كلاهما من طريق معتمر بن سليمان، عن أبيه، عن منصور، عن ربعي بن حراش، عن عمران بن حصين قال: فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب بشارة النبي ﷺ أن الله يفتح خيبر على يد علي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8094, 8353) and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (18/237).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Gave Glad Tidings That Allah Would Grant the Conquest of Khaybar Through the Hands of ʿAlī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I will surely give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger”—or he said—“whom Allah and His Messenger love.” He then called ʿAlī, who was suffering from an eye inflammation, and Allah granted victory through his hands."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (8094، 8353)، والطبراني في الكبير (18/237)."},{"num":9921,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ بُرَيْدَةَ قَالَ: غَزَوْتُ مَعَ عَلِيٍّ الْيَمَنَ، فَرَأَيْتُ مِنْهُ جَفْوَةً، فَلَمَّا قَدِمْتُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ذَكَرْتُ عَلِيًّا، فَتَنَقَّصْتُهُ، فَرَأَيْتُ وَجْهَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَتَغَيَّرُ، فَقَالَ: يَا بُرَيْدَةُ، أَلَسْتُ أَوْلَى بِالْمُؤْمِنِينَ مِنْ أَنْفُسِهِمْ؟ قُلْتُ: بَلَى يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. قَالَ: مَنْ كُنْتُ مَوْلَاهُ فَعَلِيٌّ مَوْلَاهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (22945)، والنسائي في خصائص علي (82)، وصحّحه الحاكم (4578) كلهم من طريق أبي نعيم الفضل بن دكين، حدثنا عبد الملك بن أبي غنية، عن الحكم (هو ابن عتيبة)، عن سعيد بن جبير، عن ابن عباس، عن بريدة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قوله ﷺ: من كنت مولاه فعلي مولاه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (22945), al-Nasā’ī in Khaṣāʾiṣ ʿAlī (82), and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (4578).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Statement:\n“Whoever I Am His Mawlā, Then ʿAlī Is His Mawlā”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Buraydah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I participated with ʿAlī in the expedition to Yemen, and I experienced some harshness from him. When I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I mentioned ʿAlī and spoke critically of him. I saw the expression on the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ face change, and he said: “O Buraydah, am I not closer to the believers than they are to themselves?” I replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He then said: “Whoever I am his Mawlā, then ʿAlī is his Mawlā.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",120],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (22945)، والنسائي في خصائص علي (82)، وصححه الحاكم (4578)."},{"num":9922,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي الطُّفَيْلِ، عَنْ زَيْدِ بْنِ أَرْقَمَ أَوْ حُذَيْفَةَ بْنِ أَسِيدٍ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  قَالَ: مَنْ كُنْتُ مَوْلَاهُ فَعَلَيٌّ مَوْلَاهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3713)، وأحمد في فضائل الصحابة (959)، والطبراني في الكبير (3049) كلهم من طريق محمد بن جعفر، حدثنا شعبة، عن سلمة بن كهيل قال: سمعت أبا الطفيل يحدث عن أبي سريحة (واسمه: حذيفة بن أسيد) أو - زيد بن أرقم - قال: فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قوله ﷺ: من كنت مولاه فعلي مولاه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3713), Aḥmad in Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (959), and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (3/199).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Statement:\n“Whoever I Am His Mawlā, Then ʿAlī Is His Mawlā”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Surayḥah Ḥudhayfah ibn Usayd—or, according to another narration, Zayd ibn Arqam—reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever I am his Mawlā, then ʿAlī is his Mawlā.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",121],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3713)، وأحمد في فضائل الصحابة (959)، والطبراني في الكبير (3049)."},{"num":9923,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سَعِيدِ بْنِ وَهْبٍ قَالَ: نَشَدَ عَلِيٌّ النَّاسَ، فَقَامَ خَمْسَةٌ أَوْ سِتَّةٌ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَشَهِدُوا أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَنْ كُنْتُ مَوْلَاهُ فَعَلِيٌّ مَوْلَاهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (23107)، والنسائي في خصائص علي (86) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، عن أبي إسحاق قال: سمعت سعيد بن وهب قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قوله ﷺ: من كنت مولاه فعلي مولاه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (23107) and al-Nasā’ī in Khaṣāʾiṣ ʿAlī (86).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Statement:\n“Whoever I Am His Mawlā, Then ʿAlī Is His Mawlā”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿīd ibn Wahb said: ʿAlī called upon the people to testify, whereupon five or six of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ stood and bore witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said: “Whoever I am his Mawlā, then ʿAlī is his Mawlā.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The author’s statement,","“ʿAlī called upon the people to testify,”","means:","“Who among you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever I am his Mawlā, then ʿAlī is his Mawlā’?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (23107)، والنسائي في خصائص علي (86)."},{"num":9924,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ رِيَاحِ بْنِ الْحَارِثِ، قَالَ: جَاءَ رَهْطٌ إِلَى عَلِيٍّ بالرَّحْبَةِ فَقَالُوا: السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَوْلَانَا قَالَ: كَيْفَ أَكُونُ مَوْلَاكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ عَرَبٌ؟ قَالُوا: سَمِعْنَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ غَدِيرِ خُمٍّ يَقُولُ: مَنْ كُنْتُ مَوْلَاهُ، فَإِنَّ هَذَا مَوْلَاهُ.","قَالَ رَبَاحٌ: فَلَمَّا مَضَوْا تَبِعْتُهُمْ، فَسَأَلْتُ مَنْ هَؤُلاءِ؟ قَالُوا: نَفَرَ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ فِيهِمْ أَبُو أَيُّوبَ الأَنْصَارِىُّ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (23563، 23564)، وابن أبي شيبة (32736) كلاهما من طرق عن حنش بن الحارث بن لقيط النخعي الأشجعي، عن رباح بن الحارث قال: فذكره.وإسناده حسن من أجل حنش بن الحارث فإنه حسن الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قوله ﷺ: من كنت مولاه فعلي مولاه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (23563, 23564) and Ibn Abī Shaybah (32736).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Statement:\n“Whoever I Am His Mawlā, Then ʿAlī Is His Mawlā”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Rabāḥ ibn al-Ḥārith reported: A group of men came to ʿAlī at al-Raḥbah and said: “Peace be upon you, our Mawlā.” He said: “How can I be your Mawlā when you are Arab men?” They replied: “We heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of Ghadīr Khumm: ‘Whoever I am his Mawlā, then this man is his Mawlā.’” Rabāḥ said: After they left, I followed them and asked: “Who are these men?” They replied: “A group from the Anṣār, among whom was Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (23563، 23564)، وابن أبي شيبة (32736)."},{"num":9925,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: كُنَّا بِالْجُحْفَةِ بِغَدِيرِ خَمٍّ، إِذْ خَرَجَ عَلَيْنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَخَذَ بِيَدِ عَلِيٍّ فَقَالَ: مَنْ كُنْتُ مَوْلَاهُ فَعَلِيٌّ مَوْلَاهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي شيبة (32735) عن مطلب بن زياد، عن عبد الله بن محمد بن عقيل، عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قوله ﷺ: من كنت مولاه فعلي مولاه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah (32735).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Statement:\n“Whoever I Am His Mawlā, Then ʿAlī Is His Mawlā”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We were at al-Juḥfah, at Ghadīr Khumm, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us. He took ʿAlī by the hand and said: “Whoever I am his Mawlā, then ʿAlī is his Mawlā.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",124],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي شيبة (32735)."},{"num":9926,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بْنِ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ، قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : مَنْ كُنْتُ مَوْلَاهُ فَعَلِيٌّ مَوْلَاهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي عاصم في السنة (1393) والنسائي في الكبرى (8414) كلاهما من طريق عبد الله بن دواد، عن عبد الواحد ين أيمن، عن أبيه أن سعدا قال: فذكره.وإسناده حسن من أجل عبد الواحد بن أيمن.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قوله ﷺ: من كنت مولاه فعلي مولاه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (1393) and al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8414).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Statement:\n“Whoever I Am His Mawlā, Then ʿAlī Is His Mawlā”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever I am his Mawlā, then ʿAlī is his Mawlā.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Shaykh al-Islām Ibn Taymiyyah wrote in his Fatāwā (4/417):","“As for the wording, ‘Whoever I am his Mawlā, then ʿAlī is his Mawlā; O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him…,’ this is not found in any of the principal collections except al-Tirmidhī, and what is found there is only: ‘Whoever I am his Mawlā, then ʿAlī is his Mawlā.’ As for the additional wording, it is not part of the hadith. Aḥmad was asked about it and said: ‘It is a Kūfan addition.’","There is no doubt that these additions are false for several reasons.","First: the truth does not revolve around any particular person except the Prophet ﷺ, because if that were so, it would be obligatory to follow him in everything he said. It is well known that the Companions disagreed with ʿAlī, and there are revealed texts that agree with those who opposed him in certain issues, such as the case of a woman whose husband dies while she is pregnant.","The wording, ‘O Allah, grant victory to whoever supports him…,’ is contrary to what actually occurred. Some people fought alongside him on the Day of Ṣiffīn yet were not victorious, while others did not fight alongside him and were not forsaken—such as Saʿd, who conquered Iraq and did not fight with him. Likewise, the supporters of Muʿāwiyah and Banū Umayyah, who fought him, conquered many lands of the disbelievers, and Allah granted them victory.","Likewise, the wording, ‘O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him,’ is contrary to a foundational principle of Islam, for the Qur’an has made clear that the believers are brothers even when some of them fight and transgress against others.","As for the wording, ‘Whoever I am his Mawlā, then ʿAlī is his Mawlā,’ some scholars of hadith criticized it, such as al-Bukhārī and others, while others graded it good. If he did say it, he did not intend by it an exclusive authority, but rather the shared loyalty of faith that belongs among the believers. Loyalty is the opposite of hostility, and there is no doubt that believers must show loyalty to the believers over others. Thus, it contains a refutation of the Nawāṣib.” End quote.","The compiler concludes:","What Shaykh al-Islām stated is correct without doubt. Those who authenticated the narration did not take sufficient notice of the aspect he pointed out. Moreover, the authenticity of a chain of transmission does not necessarily entail the authenticity of the text itself, because irregularity (shudhūdh) and other defects may still exist. This is a well-known principle among the scholars of hadith. Allah is the Granter of success."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",125],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي عاصم في السنة (1393)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8414)."},{"num":9927,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: كُنَّا جُلُوسًا نَنْتَظِرُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَخَرَجَ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ بَعْضِ بُيُوتِ نِسَائِهِ، قَالَ: فَقُمْنَا مَعَهُ، فَانْقَطَعَتْ نَعْلُهُ، فَتَخَلَّفَ عَلَيْهَا عَلِيٌّ يَخْصِفُهَا، فَمَضَى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَمَضَيْنَا مَعَهُ، ثُمَّ قَامَ يَنْتَظِرُهُ وَقُمْنَا مَعَهُ فَقَالَ: إِنَّ مِنْكُمْ مَنْ يُقَاتِلُ عَلَى تَأْوِيلِ هَذَا الْقُرْآنِ، كَمَا قَاتَلْتُ عَلَى تَنْزِيلِهِ.فَاسْتَشْرَفْنَا وَفِينَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ فَقَالَ: لَا، وَلَكِنَّهُ خَاصِفُ النَّعْلِ.قَالَ: فَجِئْنَا نُبَشِّرُهُ، قَالَ: وَكَأَنَّهُ قَدْ سَمِعَهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (11773) -واللفظ له-، والنسائي في الكبرى (8488)، وأبو يعلى (1086)، والطحاوي في مشكله (4058)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (6937)، والحاكم (3/122-123) كلهم من طرق عن إسماعيل بن رجاء الزبيدي، عن أبيه (هو رجاء بن ربيعة) قال: سمعت أبا سعيد الخدري يقول: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب إخبار النبي ﷺ أنه يقاتل الخوارج","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (11773)—this wording is his—al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8488), and Abū Yaʿlā (1086).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Foretelling That ʿAlī Would Fight the Khawārij","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We were sitting, waiting for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he came out to us from one of his wives’ houses. We stood and accompanied him. On the way, one of his sandals broke, so ʿAlī stayed behind to repair it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued walking, and we walked with him. Then he stopped and waited for ʿAlī, and we waited with him. The Prophet ﷺ then said: “Indeed, among you is one who will fight for the correct interpretation of this Qur’an just as I fought for its revelation.” We looked toward one another, hoping it referred to one of us. Among those present were Abū Bakr and ʿUmar. The Prophet ﷺ said: “No. Rather, it is the one repairing the sandal.” Abū Saʿīd said: We went to give ʿAlī the glad tidings, but it was as though he had already heard it."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The Prophet’s ﷺ statement,","“Indeed, among you is one who will fight for the correct interpretation of the Qur’an,”","contains an indication of ʿAlī’s later battle against the Khawārij, whom the author describes as among the worst of Allah’s creation because they took verses that had been revealed concerning the disbelievers and applied them to the believers, as Ibn ʿUmar explained.","Their movement first emerged during the caliphate of ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him). He fought them at the Battle of Nahrawān, where many of them were killed. It is said that they numbered around six thousand, while another report estimates between eight thousand and ten thousand. Fewer than ten of them reportedly survived.","Thus, this became one of the fulfilled prophecies and miracles of the Prophet ﷺ.","Supporting Narration","Rabʿī ibn Ḥirāsh narrated:","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib related to us at al-Raḥbah:","On the Day of al-Ḥudaybiyah, a delegation of the polytheists—including Suhayl ibn ʿAmr and several of their leaders—came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said:","“Some of our sons, brothers, and slaves have come to you. They possess no real understanding of the religion; they merely fled with our property and possessions. Return them to us. If they lack understanding of the religion, we will teach them.”","The Prophet ﷺ replied:","“O people of Quraysh! Either you cease, or Allah will surely send against you a man who will strike your necks with the sword for the sake of this religion—a man whose heart Allah has tested for faith.”","They asked:","“Who is he, O Messenger of Allah?”","Abū Bakr asked:","“Who is he, O Messenger of Allah?”","ʿUmar also asked:","“Who is he, O Messenger of Allah?”","The Prophet ﷺ answered:","“He is the one repairing the sandal.”","At that moment, he had given his sandal to ʿAlī, who was repairing it.","Then ʿAlī turned to us and said:","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, let him prepare his seat in the Fire.’”","Recorded by al-Tirmidhī (3715), al-Nasā’ī in Khaṣāʾiṣ ʿAlī (31), and al-Ṭaḥāwī in Sharḥ Mushkil al-Āthār (4053)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",126],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (11773) – واللفظ له –، والنسائي في الكبرى (8488)، وأبو يعلى (1086)."},{"num":9928,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سِنَانٍ يَزِيدَ بْنِ أُمَيَّةَ الدِّيلِيِّ، قَالَ: مَرِضَ عَلِيُّ بْنُ أَبِي طَالِبٍ مَرَضًا شَدِيدًا حَتَّى أَدْنَفَ وَخِفْنَا عَلَيْهِ، ثُمَّ إِنَّهُ بَرَأَ وَنَقِهَ، فَقُلْنَا: هَنِيئًا لَكَ أَبَا الْحَسَنِ، الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي عَافَاكَ، قَدْ كُنَّا نَخَافُ عَلَيْكَ، قَالَ: لَكِنِّي لَمْ أَخَفْ عَلَى نَفْسِي، أَخْبَرَنِي الصَّادِقُ الْمُصَدَّقُ أَنِّي لَا أَمُوتُ حَتَّى أُضْرَبَ عَلَى هَذِهِ، وَأَشَارَ إِلَى مُقَدَّمِ رَأْسِهِ الْأَيْسَرِ، فَتَخَضَّبُ هَذِهِ مِنْهَا بِدَمٍ، وَأَخَذَ بِلِحْيَتِهِ، وَقَالَ لِي: يَقْتُلُكَ أَشْقَى هَذِهِ الْأُمَّةِ كَمَا عَقَرَ نَاقَةَ اللَّهِ أَشْقَى بَنِي فُلَانٍ مِنْ ثَمُودَ.","قَالَ: فَنَسَبَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم إِلَى فَخِذِهِ الدُّنْيَا دُونَ ثَمُودَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (569) عن عبيد الله (هو القواريري)، حدثنا عبد الله بن جعفر (وهو ابن أبي نجيح)، أخبرني زيد بن أسلم، عن أبي سنان يزيد بن أمية قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب إخبار النبي ﷺ بأن علي بن أبي طالب يقتله أشقى هذه الأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā (569) and ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd (92).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Foretelling That the Most Wretched Man of This Nation Would Kill ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Sinān Yazīd ibn Umayyah al-Duʾalī said: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib became gravely ill until he was near death, and we feared for him. Then Allah cured him, and he recovered. We said: “Congratulations, O Abū al-Ḥasan! Praise be to Allah who has restored your health. We truly feared for you.” ʿAlī replied: “But I was never afraid for myself. The truthful one, whose truth is always confirmed, informed me that I will not die until I am struck here”— and he pointed to the front left side of his head— “and this”— while taking hold of his beard— “will be dyed with blood from it.” Then he said: “The most wretched man of this nation will kill you, just as the most wretched man of Thamūd hamstrung the she-camel of Allah.” The narrator said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ likened his killer to the most wretched man among the people of Thamūd."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",127],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (569)، وعبد بن حميد (92)."},{"num":9929,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيٍّ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: اقْضُوا كَمَا كُنْتُمْ تَقْضُونَ، فَإِنِّي أَكْرَهُ الاِخْتِلاَفَ، حَتَّى يَكُونَ لِلنَّاسِ جَمَاعَةٌ، أَوْ أَمُوتَ كَمَا مَاتَ أَصْحَابِي. فَكَانَ ابْنُ سِيرِينَ يَرَى أَنَّ عَامَّةَ مَا يُرْوَى عَلَى عَلِيٍّ الْكَذِبُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3707) عن علي بن الجعد، أنا شعبة، عن أيوب، عن ابن سيرين، عن عبيدة، عن علي قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار علي بن أبي طالب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3707).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “Judge cases as you have always judged them, for I dislike disagreement until the people become united, or until I die as my companions died.” The narrator added: Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn held the view that most of what was attributed to ʿAlī was fabricated."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",128],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3707)."},{"num":9930,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بْنِ عُبَيْدَةَ، قَالَ: جَاءَ رَجُلٌ إِلَى ابْنِ عُمَرَ، فَسَأَلَهُ عَنْ عُثْمَانَ،، فَذَكَرَ عَنْ مَحَاسِنِ، عَمَلِهِ، قَالَ: لَعَلَّ ذَاكَ يَسُوؤُكَ. قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ فَأَرْغَمَ اللَّهُ بِأَنْفِكَ. ثُمَّ سَأَلَهُ عَنْ عَلِيٍّ، فَذَكَرَ مَحَاسِنَ عَمَلِهِ، قَالَ: هُوَ ذَاكَ، بَيْتُهُ أَوْسَطُ بُيُوتِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. ثُمَّ قَالَ: لَعَلَّ ذَاكَ يَسُوؤُكَ. قَالَ: أَجَلْ. قَالَ فَأَرْغَمَ اللَّهُ بِأَنْفِكَ، انْطَلِقْ فَاجْهَدْ عَلَىَّ جَهْدَكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3704) عن محمد بن رافع، ثنا حسين، عن زائدة، عن أبي حصين، عن سعد بن عبيدة قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار علي بن أبي طالب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3704).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah narrated: A man came to Ibn ʿUmar and asked him about ʿUthmān. Ibn ʿUmar mentioned the good qualities and virtuous deeds of ʿUthmān. He then asked the man: “Perhaps that displeases you?” The man replied: “Yes.” Ibn ʿUmar responded: “May Allah humble you.” The man then asked him about ʿAlī. Ibn ʿUmar mentioned the virtues and good qualities of ʿAlī and said: “There is his house, situated among the houses of the Prophet ﷺ.” He then asked: “Perhaps that displeases you?” The man replied: “Yes.” Ibn ʿUmar said: “May Allah humble you. Go and do your utmost against me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",129],"full":1,"rep":[9904],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3704)."},{"num":9931,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُبَيْدِ اللهِ بْنِ عِيَاضِ بْنِ عَمْرٍو الْقَارِيِّ قَالَ: جَاءَ عَبْدُ اللهِ بْنُ شَدَّادٍ، فَدَخَلَ عَلَى عَائِشَةَ، وَنَحْنُ عِنْدَهَا جُلُوسٌ، مَرْجِعَهُ مِنَ الْعِرَاقِ لَيَالِيَ قُتِلَ عَلِيٌّ، فَقَالَتْ لَهُ: يَا عَبْدَ اللهِ بْنَ شَدَّادٍ، هَلْ أَنْتَ صَادِقِي عَمَّا أَسْأَلُكَ عَنْهُ؟ تُحَدِّثُنِي عَنْ هَؤُلَاءِ الْقَوْمِ الَّذِينَ قَتَلَهُمْ عَلِيٌّ، قَالَ: وَمَا لِي لَا أَصْدُقُكِ؟ قَالَتْ: فَحَدِّثْنِي عَنْ قِصَّتِهِمْ.","قَالَ فَإِنَّ عَلِيًّا لَمَّا كَاتَبَ مُعَاوِيَةَ، وَحَكَّمَ الْحَكَمَيْنِ، خَرَجَ عَلَيْهِ ثَمَانِيَةُ آلافٍ مِنْ قُرَّاءِ النَّاسِ، فَنَزَلُوا بِأَرْضٍ يُقَالُ لَهَا: حَرُورَاءُ مِنْ جَانِبِ الْكُوفَةِ، وَإِنَّهُمْ عَتَبُوا عَلَيْهِ فَقَالُوا: انْسَلَخْتَ مِنْ قَمِيصٍ أَلْبَسَكَهُ اللهُ تَعَالَى، وَاسْمٍ سَمَّاكَ اللهُ تَعَالَى بِهِ، ثُمَّ انْطَلَقْتَ، فَحَكَّمْتَ فِي دِينِ اللهِ، فَلا حُكْمَ إِلا لِلهِ تَعَالَى.","فلما أن بلغ عليًّا ما عتبوا عليه، وفارقوه عليه، فأمر مؤذنا فأذّن: أن لا يدخل على أمير المؤمنين إلا رجل قد حمل القرآن، فلما أن امتلأت الدار من قُرَّاء الناس دعا بمصحف إمام عظيم، فوضعه بين يديه، فجعل يصكه بيده ويقول: أيها المصحف حدِّث الناسَ، فناداه الناس، فقالوا: يا أمير المؤمنين ما تسأل عنه إنما هو مداد في ورق، ونحن نتكلم بما رُوينا منه، فماذا تريد؟ قال: أصحابكم هؤلاء الذين خرجوا، بيني وبينهم كتاب الله يقول الله تعالى في كتابه في امرأة ورجل: ﴿وَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ شِقَاقَ بَيْنِهِمَا فَابْعَثُوا حَكَمًا مِنْ أَهْلِهِ وَحَكَمًا مِنْ أَهْلِهَا إِنْ يُرِيدَا إِصْلَاحًا يُوَفِّقِ اللَّهُ بَيْنَهُمَا﴾ [النساء: ٣٥] فأمة محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم أعظم دمًا وحرمةً من امرأة ورجل.","وَنَقَمُوا عَلَيَّ أَنْ كَاتَبْتُ مُعَاوِيَةَ: كَتَبَ عَلِيُّ بْنُ أَبِي طَالِبٍ، وَقَدْ جاءنا سُهَيْلُ بْنُ عَمْرٍو، وَنَحْنُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْحُدَيْبِيَةِ، حِينَ صَالَحَ قَوْمَهُ قُرَيْشًا، فَكَتَبَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيمِ فَقَالَ سُهَيْلٌ: لَا تَكْتُبْ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيمِ، فَقَالَ: كَيْفَ نَكْتُبُ؟ فَقَالَ: اكْتُبْ بِاسْمِكَ اللهُمَّ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فَاكْتُبْ مُحَمَّدٌ رَسُولُ اللهِ، فَقَالَ لَوْ أَعْلَمُ أَنَّكَ رَسُولُ اللهِ، لَمْ أُخَالِفْكَ، فَكَتَبَ: هَذَا مَا صَالَحَ مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ عبدالله قريشا.يقول اللهُ تَعَالَى فِي كِتَابِهِ: ﴿لَقَدْ كَانَ لَكُمْ فِي رَسُولِ اللهِ أُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ لِمَنْ كَانَ يَرْجُو اللهَ وَالْيَوْمَ الْآخِرَ﴾ [الأحزاب: ٢١]٢١]","فَبَعَثَ إِلَيْهِمْ عَلِيٌّ عَبْدَ اللهِ بْنَ عَبَّاسٍ فَخَرَجْتُ مَعَهُ، حَتَّى إِذَا تَوَسَّطْنَا عَسْكَرَهُمْ قَامَ ابْنُ الْكَوَّاءِ يَخْطُبُ النَّاسَ فَقَالَ: يَا حَمَلَةَ الْقُرْآنِ إِنَّ هَذَا عبدالله بْنُ عَبَّاسٍ، فَمَنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ يَعْرِفُهُ فَأَنَا أُعَرِّفُهُ مِنْ كِتَابِ اللهِ مَا يَعْرِفُهُ بِهِ هَذَا مِمَّنْ نَزَلَ فِيهِ وَفِي قَوْمِهِ قَوْمٌ خَصِمُونَ [الزخرف: ٥٨]","فردُّوه إلى صاحبه، ولا تواضعوه كتاب الله، فقام خطباؤهم فقالوا: والله لنواضعنه كتاب الله، فإن جاء بحق نعرفه لنتبعنّه، وإن جاء بباطل لنُبكتنَّه بباطله، فواضعوا عبد الله الكتاب ثلاثة أيام، فرجع منهم أربعة آلاف كلهم تائب، فيهم ابن الكوّاء، حتى أدخلهم على عليٍّ الكوفة، فبعث علي إلى بقيتهم، فقال: قد كان من أمرنا وأمر الناس ما قد رأيتم، فقفوا حيث شئتم، حتى تجتمع أمة محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم، بيننا وبينكم أن لا تسفكوا دمًا حرامًا، أو تقطعوا سبيلاً، أو تظلموا ذمةً، فإنكم إن فعلتم فقد نبذنا إليكم الحربَ على سواء، إن الله لا يحب الخائنين.","فَقَالَتْ لَهُ عَائِشَةُ: يَا ابْنَ شَدَّادٍ، فَقَدْ قَتَلَهُمْ! فَقَالَ: وَاللهِ مَا بَعَثَ إِلَيْهِمْ حَتَّى قَطَعُوا السَّبِيلَ، وَسَفَكُوا الدَّمَ، وَاسْتَحَلُّوا أَهْلَ الذِّمَّةِ، فَقَالَتْ: آَللَّهُ؟ قَالَ: آللَّهِ الَّذِي لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا هُوَ لَقَدْ كان.قالت: فَمَا شَيْءٌ بَلَغَنِي عَنْ أَهْلِ الْعِرَاقِ يَتَحَدَّثُونَهُ؟ يَقُولُونَ: ذُو الثُّدَيِّ، وَذُو الثدي.قال: قَدْ رَأَيْتُهُ، وَقُمْتُ مَعَ عَلِيٍّ عَلَيْهِ فِي الْقَتْلَى، فَدَعَا النَّاسَ فَقَالَ: أَتَعْرِفُونَ هَذَا؟ فَمَا أَكْثَرَ مَنْ جَاءَ يَقُولُ: قَدْ رَأَيْتُهُ فِي مَسْجِدِ بَنِي فُلَانٍ يُصَلِّي، وَرَأَيْتُهُ فِي مَسْجِدِ بَنِي فُلَانٍ يُصَلِّي، وَلَمْ يَأْتُوا فِيهِ بِثَبَتٍ يُعْرَفُ إِلَّا ذَلِكَ، قَالَتْ: فَمَا قَوْلُ عَلِيٍّ حِينَ قَامَ عَلَيْهِ كَمَا يَزْعُمُ أَهْلُ الْعِرَاقِ؟ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ: صَدَقَ اللهُ وَرَسُولُهُ، قَالَتْ: هَلْ سَمِعْتَ مِنْهُ أَنَّهُ قَالَ غَيْرَ ذَلِكَ؟ قَالَ: اللهُمَّ لا.قالت: أَجَلْ، صَدَقَ اللهُ وَرَسُولُهُ، يَرْحَمُ اللهُ عَلِيًّا إِنَّهُ كَانَ مِنْ كَلَامِهِ لَا يَرَى شَيْئًا يُعْجِبُهُ إِلَّا قَالَ: صَدَقَ اللهُ وَرَسُولُهُ، فَيَذْهَبُ أَهْلُ الْعِرَاقِ يَكْذِبُونَ عَلَيْهِ، وَيَزِيدُونَ عَلَيْهِ فِي الْحَدِيثِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (656)، وأبو يعلى (474) كلاهما من طريق يحيى بن سُليم، عن عبد الله بن عثمان بن خُثيم، عن عبيد الله بن عياض بن عمرو القاري قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار علي بن أبي طالب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (656) and Abū Yaʿlā (474).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿIyāḍ ibn ʿAmr al-Qārī narrated: ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād returned from Iraq a few nights after the killing of ʿAlī and visited ʿĀ’ishah while we were sitting with her. She asked him: “O ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād, will you answer me truthfully? Tell me about the people whom ʿAlī fought and killed.” He replied: “Why would I not tell you the truth?” She said: “Then tell me their story.” He explained that after ʿAlī and Muʿāwiyah agreed to arbitration, about eight thousand Qur’an reciters broke away from ʿAlī and settled at Ḥarūrāʾ near Kūfah. They objected to him, saying: “You have stripped off a garment that Allah Almighty clothed you with and a name by which Allah Almighty named you, then you went and appointed arbiters in the religion of Allah. Judgment belongs only to Allah Almighty.”","When ʿAlī learned of their objections, he gathered the scholars of the Qur’an before him and brought forth a large muṣḥaf. He placed it before them, struck it with his hand, and said: “O Muṣḥaf, speak to the people!” They replied that it was only ink upon paper and that people must speak according to what they had learned from it. ʿAlī then demonstrated from the Qur’an that arbitration is permitted, citing Allah’s command regarding marital disputes: “If you fear a breach between them, appoint an arbiter from his family and an arbiter from hers…” (Qur’an 4:35) He argued that if arbitration is permitted to reconcile a husband and wife, then reconciling the bloodshed of the Muslim community deserves it even more.","He also answered their objection to his writing to Muʿāwiyah under the name “ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib.” He recalled that Suhayl ibn ʿAmr came to them at al-Ḥudaybiyah while they were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he made peace with Quraysh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote: “In the Name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful.” Suhayl said: “Do not write ‘In the Name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful’; rather write: ‘In Your Name, O Allah.’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “Write: Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah.” Suhayl replied: “If I knew that you were the Messenger of Allah, I would not have opposed you.” So it was written: “This is what Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh has agreed upon in peace with Quraysh.” Allah Almighty says: “Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example.” (Qur’an 33:21).","ʿAlī then sent ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās to them, and he went out with him. When they reached the middle of their camp, Ibn al-Kawwāʾ stood to address the people and said: “O bearers of the Qur’an, this is ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās. Whoever does not know him, I know him from the Book of Allah. He is among those about whom, and about whose people, was revealed: ‘They are a contentious people.’ (Qur’an 43:58). Send him back to his companion and do not debate the Book of Allah with him.” Their speakers then stood and said: “By Allah, we will indeed debate the Book of Allah with him. If he brings the truth, we will recognize it and follow it; and if he brings falsehood, we will refute him with his falsehood.” He then debated them with the Qur’an for three days.","For three days Ibn ʿAbbās discussed the matter with them until four thousand repented and returned, including Ibn al-Kawwāʾ. ʿAlī then addressed those who remained, saying that they were free to stay apart provided they did not shed unlawful blood, terrorize travelers, or violate the rights of protected non-Muslims. If they committed those crimes, war would become unavoidable. ʿĀ’ishah asked: “So he eventually fought them?” He replied: “By Allah, he did not send forces against them until they began attacking travelers, shedding innocent blood, and violating the rights of protected people.”","She asked him to swear by Allah, and he confirmed it. She then asked about the reports circulating in Iraq concerning Dhu al-Thudayyah (the man with the deformed arm). He replied that he personally saw him among those killed and witnessed ʿAlī asking people whether they recognized him. Many testified that they had seen him praying in various mosques, but no further reliable information about him was established. She then asked: “What did ʿAlī say when he stood over him, as the people of Iraq claim?”","He answered: “I heard him say only: ‘Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.’” She asked: “Did you hear him say anything else?” He replied: “No, by Allah.” ʿĀ’ishah said: “Indeed, Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. May Allah have mercy upon ʿAlī. Whenever he witnessed something that amazed him, he would simply say: ‘Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.’ But the people of Iraq attributed false statements to him and added things to the narration.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",130],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (656)، وأبو يعلى (474)."},{"num":9932,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: اشْتَكَى عَلِيًّا النَّاسُ، قَالَ: فَقَامَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِينَا خَطِيبًا، فَسَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ: أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ لَا تَشْكُوا عَلِيًّا، فَوَاللهِ إِنَّهُ لَأُخَيْشِنٌ فِي ذَاتِ اللهِ، أَوْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (11817) –ومن طريقه الحاكم (4654)- عن يعقوب (هو ابن إبراهيم بن سعد بن إبراهيم الزهري)، حدثنا أبي، عن ابن إسحاق، قال: فحدثني عبدالله بن عبدالرحمن بن معمر بن حزم، عن سليمان بن محمد بن كعب بن عجرة، عن عمته زينب بنت كعب، وكانت عند أبي سعيد الخدري، عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار علي بن أبي طالب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (11817), and through his chain by al-Ḥākim (1/68).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Some people complained about ʿAlī. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then stood before us and delivered a sermon. I heard him say: “O people, do not complain about ʿAlī. By Allah, he is indeed uncompromising in the cause of Allah”—or he said—“in the path of Allah.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The Virtues of the Remaining Members of the Ten Who Were Given Glad Tidings of Paradise — They are:"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",131],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (11817)، ومن طريقه الحاكم (4654)."},{"num":9933,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: عَشَرَةٌ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ فِي الْجَنَّةِ: أَبُو بَكْرٍ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَعُمَرُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَعُثْمَانُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَعَلِيٌّ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَطَلْحَةُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَالزُّبَيْرُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَسَعْدٌ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَسَعِيدٌ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَعَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنُ عَوْفٍ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَأَبُوعُبَيْدَةَ بْنُ الْجَرَّاحِ فِي الْجَنَّةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (13823) وفي الأوسط (2222) وفي الصغير sh13068(62) من طرق عن حامد بن يحيى البلخي، عن سعير بن الخِمس، عن حبيب بن أبي ثابت، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار علي بن أبي طالب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (13823), al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (2222), and al-Muʿjam al-Ṣaghīr (62).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_no":49,"group_no":5,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ten men from Quraysh are in Paradise: Abū Bakr is in Paradise. ʿUmar is in Paradise. ʿUthmān is in Paradise. ʿAlī is in Paradise. Ṭalḥah is in Paradise. Al-Zubayr is in Paradise. Saʿd is in Paradise. Saʿīd is in Paradise. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf is in Paradise. Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ is in Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",132],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (13823)، وفي الأوسط (2222)، وفي الصغير sh13068(62)."},{"num":9934,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الزُّبَيْرِ بْنِ الْعَوَّامِ، قَالَ: كَانَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ دِرْعَانِ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، فَنَهَضَ إِلَى الصَّخْرَةِ، فَلَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ، فَأَقْعَدَ طَلْحَةَ تَحْتَهُ، فَصَعِدَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَيْهِ حَتَّى اسْتَوَى عَلَى الصَّخْرَةِ، فَقَالَ: سَمِعْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: أَوْجَبَ طَلْحَةُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1692، 3738)، وأحمد (1417)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (6979)، والحاكم (5602)، والبيهقي (6/370 و9/46) كلهم من طرق عن محمد بن إسحاق قال: حدثني يحيى بن عباد بن عبد الله بن الزبير، عن أبيه، عن جده عبد الله بن الزبير، عن الزبير بن العوام فذكره.وسقط ذكر \"أبيه\" من ابن حبان.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضل طلحة بن عبيد الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (1692, 3738), Aḥmad (1417), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6979).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب طلحة بن عبيد الله وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh","part_no":49,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām (may Allah be pleased with him) said: On the Day of Uḥud, the Prophet ﷺ was wearing two coats of armor. He attempted to climb onto a large rock but was unable to do so. Ṭalḥah sat beneath him, allowing the Prophet ﷺ to step upon him until he stood firmly upon the rock. I then heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Ṭalḥah has secured Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",133],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[7937,8813,9616],"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (1692، 3738)، وأحمد (1417)، وصححه ابن حبان (6979)."},{"num":9935,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عبد الله بن الزبير قال: سمعت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول: أوجب طلحة.حين صنع ما صنع برسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، وقد كان الناس انهزموا عن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم حتى انتهى بعضهم إلى المنقا دون الأعوص، وفرَّ عثمان بن عفان وعقبة بن عثمان، وسعد بن عثمان رجلان من الأنصار، ثم من بني زريق حتى بلغوا الجلعب – جبلا بناحية المدينة، فأقاموا به ثلاثا، ثم رجعوا إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، فقال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: لقد ذهبتم فيها عريضة."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه محمد بن إسحاق في سيرته (514) قال: حدثني يحيى بن عباد بن عبدالله بن الزبير، عن أبيه، عن عبد الله بن الزبير فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضل طلحة بن عبيد الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq in his Sīrah (514).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب طلحة بن عبيد الله وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh","part_no":49,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Ṭalḥah has secured Paradise.” This was because of what Ṭalḥah did in defense of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. During the Battle of Uḥud, the people fled from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Some retreated as far as al-Manqā before al-Aʿwaṣ. Among those who fled were ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, ʿUqbah ibn ʿUthmān, and Saʿd ibn ʿUthmān—two men from the Anṣār belonging to Banū Zurayq. They reached al-Jalʿab, a mountain near Madinah, where they remained for three days before returning to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: “You went very far indeed.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",134],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8827],"tks":"حسن: رواه محمد بن إسحاق في سيرته (514)."},{"num":9936,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، عَنْ أَبِي طَلْحَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: كُنْتُ فِيمَنْ تَغَشَّاهُ النُّعَاسُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، حَتَّى سَقَطَ سَيْفِي مِنْ يَدِي مِرَارًا، يَسْقُطُ وَآخُذُهُ، وَيَسْقُطُ فَآخُذُهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4068) عن خليفة، ثنا يزيد بن زريع، ثنا سعيد، عن قتادة، عن أنس، عن أبي طلحة قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب فضل طلحة بن عبيد الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4068).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب طلحة بن عبيد الله وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh","part_no":49,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated from Abū Ṭalḥah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I was among those overcome by drowsiness on the Day of Uḥud, to the extent that my sword repeatedly fell from my hand. It would fall, I would pick it up, then it would fall again, and I would pick it up once more."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",135],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4068)."},{"num":9937,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ طَلْحَةَ أَنَّ أَصْحَابَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالُوا لأَعْرَابِيٍّ جَاهِلٍ: سَلْه عَمَّنْ قَضَى نَحْبَهُ مَنْ هُوَ؟ وَكَانُوا لاَ يجترؤون عَلَى مَسْأَلَتِهِ، يُوَقِّرُونَهُ وَيَهَابُونَهُ، فَسَأَلَهُ الأَعْرَابِيُّ فَأَعْرَضَ عَنْهُ، ثُمَّ سَأَلَهُ فَأَعْرَضَ عَنْهُ، ثُمَّ سَأَلَهُ فَأَعْرَضَ عَنْهُ، ثُمَّ إِنِّي اطَّلَعْتُ مِنْ بَابِ الْمَسْجِدِ، وعليّ ثِيَابٌ خُضْرٌ، فَلَمَّا رَآنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: أَيْنَ السَّائِلُ عَمَّنْ قَضَى نَحْبَهُ.قَالَ الأَعْرَابِيُّ أَنَا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ.قَالَ: هَذَا مِمَّنْ قَضَى نَحْبَهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3203، 3742)، والبزار (943)، وأبو يعلى (663) كلهم من طريق يونس بن بكير، حدثنا طلحة بن يحيى، عن موسى وعيسى ابنى طلحة، عن أبيهما طلحة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضل طلحة بن عبيد الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3203, 3742), who graded it good, as well as al-Bazzār (943) and Abū Yaʿlā (663).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب طلحة بن عبيد الله وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh","part_no":49,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ṭalḥah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to an unlearned Bedouin: “Ask him who it is that has fulfilled his vow.” They themselves were too reverent and respectful to ask the Prophet ﷺ directly. The Bedouin asked him, but the Prophet ﷺ turned away. He asked again, and again the Prophet ﷺ turned away. He asked a third time, and the Prophet ﷺ again turned away. Then I entered through the door of the mosque wearing green garments. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me, he said: “Where is the one asking about the person who has fulfilled his vow?” The Bedouin replied: “I am, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “This is one of those who has fulfilled his vow.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",136],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13050],"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3203، 3742) وحسنه، والبزار (943)، وأبو يعلى (663)."},{"num":9938,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن السَّائِبِ بن يَزِيدَ قَالَ: صَحِبْتُ عَبْدَ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنَ عَوْفٍ، وَطَلْحَةَ بْنَ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ، وَالْمِقْدَادَ، وَسَعْدًا رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمْ فَمَا سَمِعْتُ أَحَدًا مِنْهُمْ يُحَدِّثُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، إِلاَّ أَنِّي سَمِعْتُ طَلْحَةَ يُحَدِّثُ عَنْ يَوْمِ أُحُدٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4062) عن عبد الله بن أبي الأسود، ثنا حاتم بن إسماعيل، عن محمد بن يوسف قال: سمعت السائب فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ثبات طلحة مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4062).","chapter_en":"Ṭalḥah’s Steadfastness with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uḥud","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب طلحة بن عبيد الله وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh","part_no":49,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Sā’ib ibn Yazīd said: I accompanied ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh, al-Miqdād, and Saʿd (may Allah be pleased with them all). I never heard any of them narrate from the Prophet ﷺ, except that I heard Ṭalḥah narrate about the Day of Uḥud."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",137],"full":1,"rep":[8861],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4062)."},{"num":9939,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ قَيْسٍ، قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ يَدَ طَلْحَةَ شَلاَّءَ، وَقَى بِهَا النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4063) عن عبد الله بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا وكيع، عن إسماعيل، عن قيس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ثبات طلحة مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4063).","chapter_en":"Ṭalḥah’s Steadfastness with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uḥud","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب طلحة بن عبيد الله وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh","part_no":49,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim said: I saw Ṭalḥah’s hand paralyzed. He had used it to shield the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uḥud."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",138],"full":1,"rep":[8862],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4063)."},{"num":9940,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ أُحُدٍ وَوَلَّى النَّاسُ، كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  فِي نَاحِيَةٍ فِي اثْنَىْ عَشَرَ رَجُلاً مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ، وَفِيهِمْ طَلْحَةُ بْنُ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ، فَأَدْرَكَهُمُ الْمُشْرِكُونَ فَالْتَفَتَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ،  وَقَالَ: مَنْ لِلْقَوْمِ. فَقَالَ طَلْحَةُ: أَنَا. قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  كَمَا أَنْتَ. فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ: أَنَا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. فَقَالَ: أَنْتَ. فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ، ثُمَّ الْتَفَتَ فَإِذَا الْمُشْرِكُونَ، فَقَالَ: مَنْ لِلْقَوْمِ. فَقَالَ طَلْحَةُ: أَنَا. قَالَ كَمَا أَنْتَ. فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ: أَنَا. فَقَالَ أَنْتَ. فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ، ثُمَّ لَمْ يَزَلْ يَقُولُ ذَلِكَ، وَيَخْرُجُ إِلَيْهِمْ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ فَيُقَاتِلُ قِتَالَ مَنْ قَبْلَهُ حَتَّى يُقْتَلَ، حَتَّى بَقِيَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  وَطَلْحَةُ بْنُ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  مَنْ لِلْقَوْمِ. فَقَالَ طَلْحَةُ: أَنَا. فَقَاتَلَ طَلْحَةُ قِتَالَ الأَحَدَ عَشَرَ، حَتَّى ضُرِبَتْ يَدُهُ، فَقُطِعَتْ أَصَابِعُهُ، فَقَالَ: حَسِّ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  لَوْ قُلْتَ: بِسْمِ اللَّهِ لَرَفَعَتْكَ الْمَلاَئِكَةُ وَالنَّاسُ يَنْظُرُونَ. ثُمَّ رَدَّ اللَّهُ الْمُشْرِكِينَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3149)، -وعنه ابن السني في عمل اليوم والليلة (670)- عن عمرو بن سوَّاد قال: أنبأنا ابن وهب، أخبرني يحيى بن أيوب، وذكر آخر قبله، عن عمارة بن غزية، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر بن عبدالله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ثبات طلحة مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī (3149), and through him by Ibn al-Sunnī in ʿAmal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah (670).","chapter_en":"Ṭalḥah’s Steadfastness with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uḥud","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب طلحة بن عبيد الله وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh","part_no":49,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him) said: On the Day of Uḥud, when the people had retreated, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one side of the battlefield with twelve men from the Anṣār, among whom was Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh. The polytheists caught up with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned and said: “Who will face these people?” Ṭalḥah replied: “I will.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Remain where you are.” One of the Anṣār then said: “I will, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “You.” The man fought until he was martyred. Again the Prophet ﷺ turned and saw the polytheists approaching and asked: “Who will face these people?” Ṭalḥah again said: “I will.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Remain where you are.” Another man from the Anṣār volunteered, and the Prophet ﷺ permitted him to fight. He fought until he was martyred. This continued, with each Anṣārī going forward one after another and fighting until he was killed, until only the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Ṭalḥah remained. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then asked: “Who will face these people?” Ṭalḥah replied: “I will.” Ṭalḥah then fought with the bravery of all eleven men combined until his hand was struck and his fingers were severed. He exclaimed: “Ḥas!” (an exclamation of pain) The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Had you said, ‘Bismillāh (In the Name of Allah),’ the angels would have raised you while the people watched.” Then Allah drove the polytheists back."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",139],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8864],"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3149)، وعنه ابن السني في عمل اليوم والليلة (670)."},{"num":9941,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي عُثْمَانَ، قَالَ: لَمْ يَبْقَ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي بَعْضِ تِلْكَ الأَيَّامِ الَّتِي قَاتَلَ فِيهِنَّ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ غَيْرُ طَلْحَةَ وَسَعْدٍ. عَنْ حَدِيثِهِمَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3722، 3723)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2414) كلاهما عن محمد بن أبي بكر المقدمي، ثنا معتمر، عن أبيه، عن أبي عثمان فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ثبات طلحة مع النبي ﷺ يوم أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3722, 3723) and Muslim (2414).","chapter_en":"Ṭalḥah’s Steadfastness with the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Uḥud","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب طلحة بن عبيد الله وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh","part_no":49,"group_no":6,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū ʿUthmān said: During one of the days on which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was fighting, no one remained with him except Ṭalḥah and Saʿd. This was narrated on the authority of both of them."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The phrase:","“on the authority of both of them”","means that both Ṭalḥah and Saʿd personally narrated this report."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",140],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3722، 3723)، ومسلم (2414)."},{"num":9942,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ الزُّبَيْرِ، قَالَ: كُنْتُ يَوْمَ الأَحْزَابِ جُعِلْتُ أَنَا وَعُمَرُ بْنُ أَبِي سَلَمَةَ، فِي النِّسَاءِ، فَنَظَرْتُ فَإِذَا أَنَا بِالزُّبَيْرِ، عَلَى فَرَسِهِ، يَخْتَلِفُ إِلَى بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ مَرَّتَيْنِ أَوْ ثَلاَثًا، فَلَمَّا رَجَعْتُ قُلْتُ: يَا أَبَتِ، رَأَيْتُكَ تَخْتَلِفُ. قَالَ أَوَهَلْ رَأَيْتَنِي يَا بُنَىَّ؟ قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَنْ يَأْتِ بَنِي قُرَيْظَةَ فَيَأْتِينِي بِخَبَرِهِمْ. فَانْطَلَقْتُ، فَلَمَّا رَجَعْتُ جَمَعَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَبَوَيْهِ، فَقَالَ: فِدَاكَ أَبِي وَأُمِّي."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3720)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2416) كلاهما من طريق هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عبد الله بن الزبير قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في شجاعة الزبير يوم الخندق وجمع النبي ﷺ له أبويه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3720) and Muslim (2416).","chapter_en":"The Courage of al-Zubayr on the Day of al-Khandaq and the Prophet’s ﷺ Statement, “May My Father and Mother Be Sacrificed for You”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب الزبير بن العوام وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_no":49,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr said: On the Day of al-Aḥzāb (the Battle of the Trench), I and ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah were placed with the women. I looked out and saw al-Zubayr riding repeatedly toward Banū Qurayẓah two or three times. When he returned, I said: “Father, I saw you going back and forth.” He asked: “Did you really see me, my son?” I replied: “Yes.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said: “Who will go to Banū Qurayẓah and bring me news of them?” So I went. When I returned, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ invoked both his father and mother for me, saying: “May my father and my mother be sacrificed for you.”"]},"intro_majmu":{"ar":["هو الزبير بن العوام، حواري رسول الله ﷺ، وابن عمته صفية بنت عبد المطلب، وأحد العشرة المشهود لهم بالجنة، وأحد الستة من أهل الشورى، وأول من سلَّ سيفه في سبيل الله. أسلم وهو حدث، وله سن عشر سنين.","وقد ورد أن الزبير كان رجلًا طويلًا، إذا ركب خطَّت رجلاه الأرض."],"en":["Al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām was the close disciple (ḥawārī) of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the son of the Prophet’s paternal aunt Ṣafiyyah bint ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, one of the ten who were given the glad tidings of Paradise, and one of the six members of the council (shūrā) appointed by ʿUmar.","He was also the first person to unsheathe his sword in the cause of Allah.","He embraced Islam while still very young, at approximately ten years of age.","It is also reported that al-Zubayr was a tall man; when he rode his mount, his feet would reach the ground."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",141],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3720)، ومسلم (2416)."},{"num":9943,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ يَأْتِينِي بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ يَوْمَ الأَحْزَابِ. قَالَ الزُّبَيْرُ: أَنَا. ثُمَّ قَالَ: مَنْ يَأْتِينِي بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ. قَالَ الزُّبَيْرُ: أَنَا. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ لِكُلِّ نَبِيٍّ حَوَارِيًّا، وَحَوَارِيَّ الزُّبَيْرُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الجهاد (2846) وفي المغازي bukhari(4113)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2415-48) كلاهما من طريق سفيان بن عيينة، عن محمد بن المنكدر، عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في شجاعة الزبير يوم الخندق وجمع النبي ﷺ له أبويه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2846, 4113) and Muslim (2415).","chapter_en":"The Courage of al-Zubayr on the Day of al-Khandaq and the Prophet’s ﷺ Statement, “May My Father and Mother Be Sacrificed for You”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب الزبير بن العوام وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_no":49,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Prophet ﷺ said: “Who will bring me news of the people on the Day of al-Aḥzāb?” Al-Zubayr replied: “I will.” The Prophet ﷺ asked again: “Who will bring me news of the people?” Al-Zubayr again replied: “I will.” The Prophet ﷺ then said: “Every prophet has a close disciple (ḥawārī), and my close disciple is al-Zubayr.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The Prophet’s ﷺ statement,","“Who will bring me news of the people?”","refers to obtaining information about Banū Qurayẓah after they had broken their treaty.","As for the incident involving Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān, that was a different mission to gather intelligence about Quraysh, and it occurred on an extremely cold night."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",142],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[7886],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2846، 4113)، ومسلم (2415)."},{"num":9944,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيِّ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ لِكُلِّ نَبِيٍّ حَوَارِيًّا، وَإِنَّ حَوَارِيَّ الزُّبَيْرُ بْنُ الْعَوَّامِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3744)، وأحمد (680) كلاهما من طريق عاصم (هو ابن أبي النجود)، عن زر، عن علي فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في شجاعة الزبير يوم الخندق وجمع النبي ﷺ له أبويه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3744) and Aḥmad (680).","chapter_en":"The Courage of al-Zubayr on the Day of al-Khandaq and the Prophet’s ﷺ Statement, “May My Father and Mother Be Sacrificed for You”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب الزبير بن العوام وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_no":49,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every prophet has a close disciple, and my close disciple is al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",143],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3744)، وأحمد (680)."},{"num":9945,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عُمَرَ أَنَّهُ سَمِعَ رَجُلًا يَقُولُ: يَا ابْنَ حَوَارِيِّ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنْ كُنْتُ مِنْ آلِ الزُّبَيْرِ وَإِلَّا فَلَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البزار في كشف الأستار (2594)، والطبراني في الكبير (1/78) كلاهما من طريق يزيد بن هارون، ثنا سعيد بن أبي عروبة، عن أيوب، عن نافع قال: سمع ابن عمر رجلا يقول: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في شجاعة الزبير يوم الخندق وجمع النبي ﷺ له أبويه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (2594) and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (1/78).","chapter_en":"The Courage of al-Zubayr on the Day of al-Khandaq and the Prophet’s ﷺ Statement, “May My Father and Mother Be Sacrificed for You”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب الزبير بن العوام وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_no":49,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) heard a man say: “O son of the close disciple of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!” He replied: “If you are addressing someone from the family of al-Zubayr, then yes; otherwise, no.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",144],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البزار في كشف الأستار (2594)، والطبراني في الكبير (1/78)."},{"num":9946,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِيهِ قَالَ:  قَالَتْ لِي عَائِشَةُ: أَبَوَاكَ وَاللهِ مِنَ الَّذِينَ اسْتَجَابُوا لِلهِ وَالرَّسُولِ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا أَصَابَهُمُ الْقَرْحُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2418-51) من طرق عن هشام، عن أبيه قال: قالت لي عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار الزبير بن العوام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2418, no. 51).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب الزبير بن العوام وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_no":49,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr said: ʿĀ’ishah said to me: “By Allah, your two fathers were among those who responded to Allah and the Messenger after they had been wounded.” Another wording adds: “She meant Abū Bakr and al-Zubayr.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",145],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2418/51)."},{"num":9947,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن مَرْوَانَ بن الْحَكَمِ قَالَ: أَصَابَ عُثْمَانَ بْنَ عَفَّانَ رُعَافٌ شَدِيدٌ سَنَةَ الرُّعَافِ، حَتَّى حَبَسَهُ عَنِ الْحَجِّ، وَأَوْصَى، فَدَخَلَ عَلَيْهِ رَجُلٌ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ، قَالَ: اسْتَخْلِفْ. قَالَ: وَقَالُوهُ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ وَمَنْ؟ فَسَكَتَ، فَدَخَلَ عَلَيْهِ رَجُلٌ آخَرُ، ـ أَحْسِبُهُ الْحَارِثَ ـ فَقَالَ: اسْتَخْلِفْ. فَقَالَ عُثْمَانُ: وَقَالُوا؟ فَقَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: وَمَنْ هُوَ؟ فَسَكَتَ، قَالَ: فَلَعَلَّهُمْ قَالُوا: الزُّبَيْرَ، قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ أَمَا وَالَّذِي نَفْسِي بِيَدِهِ إِنَّهُ لَخَيْرُهُمْ مَا عَلِمْتُ، وَإِنْ كَانَ لأَحَبَّهُمْ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3717) عن خالد بن مخلد، ثنا علي بن مسهر، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه: أخبرني مروان بن الحكم فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار الزبير بن العوام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3717).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب الزبير بن العوام وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_no":49,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam said: During the year known as “the Year of the Nosebleed,” ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān suffered a severe nosebleed that prevented him from performing Ḥajj. Thinking death might be near, he made his will. A man from Quraysh entered and said: “Appoint a successor.” ʿUthmān asked: “Have the people said this?” He replied: “Yes.” ʿUthmān asked: “Whom do they suggest?” The man remained silent. Later another man—Marwān thought it was al-Ḥārith—entered and also urged him to appoint a successor. ʿUthmān again asked: “Have the people said this?” He replied: “Yes.” ʿUthmān asked: “Whom?” The man remained silent. ʿUthmān then said: “Perhaps they have suggested al-Zubayr?” He replied: “Yes.” ʿUthmān said: “By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, as far as I know, he is the best of them, as far as I know, and he was certainly the most beloved of them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",146],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3717)."},{"num":9948,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ الزُّبَيْرِ قَالَ: لَمَّا وَقَفَ الزُّبَيْرُ يَوْمَ الْجَمَلِ دَعَانِي، فَقُمْتُ إِلَى جَنْبِهِ، فَقَالَ: يَا بُنَىِّ، إِنَّهُ لاَ يُقْتَلُ الْيَوْمَ إِلاَّ ظَالِمٌ أَوْ مَظْلُومٌ، وَإِنِّي لاَ أُرَانِي إِلاَّ سَأُقْتَلُ الْيَوْمَ مَظْلُومًا، وَإِنَّ مِنْ أَكْبَرِ هَمِّي لَدَيْنِي، أَفَتُرَى يُبْقِي دَيْنُنَا مِنْ مَالِنَا شَيْئًا؟ فَقَالَ: يَا بُنَىِّ بِعْ مَالَنَا، فَاقْضِ دَيْنِي. وَأَوْصَى بِالثُّلُثِ، وَثُلُثِهِ لِبَنِيهِ، يَعْنِي عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ الزُّبَيْرِ يَقُولُ: ثُلُثُ الثُّلُثِ، فَإِنْ فَضَلَ مِنْ مَالِنَا فَضْلٌ بَعْدَ قَضَاءِ الدَّيْنِ شَىْءٌ، فَثُلُثُهُ لِوَلَدِكَ. قَالَ هِشَامٌ: وَكَانَ بَعْضُ وَلَدِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَدْ وَازَى بَعْضَ بَنِي الزُّبَيْرِ خُبَيْبٌ وَعَبَّادٌ، وَلَهُ يَوْمَئِذٍ تِسْعَةُ بَنِينَ وَتِسْعُ بَنَاتٍ. قَالَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ: فَجَعَلَ يُوصِينِي بِدَيْنِهِ، وَيَقُولُ: يَا بُنَىِّ، إِنْ عَجَزْتَ عَنْهُ فِي شَىْءٍ فَاسْتَعِنْ عَلَيْهِ مَوْلاَىَ. قَالَ فَوَاللَّهِ مَا دَرَيْتُ مَا أَرَادَ حَتَّى قُلْتُ: يَا أَبَتِ مَنْ مَوْلاَكَ؟ قَالَ: اللَّهُ. قَالَ فَوَاللَّهِ مَا وَقَعْتُ فِي كُرْبَةٍ مِنْ دَيْنِهِ إِلاَّ قُلْتُ: يَا مَوْلَى الزُّبَيْرِ، اقْضِ عَنْهُ دَيْنَهُ. فَيَقْضِيهِ، فَقُتِلَ الزُّبَيْرُ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ، وَلَمْ يَدَعْ دِينَارًا وَلاَ دِرْهَمًا، إِلاَّ أَرَضِينَ مِنْهَا الْغَابَةُ، وَإِحْدَى عَشْرَةَ دَارًا بِالْمَدِينَةِ، وَدَارَيْنِ بِالْبَصْرَةِ، وَدَارًا بِالْكُوفَةِ، وَدَارًا بِمِصْرَ.","قال: إنما كان دينه الذي عليه أن الرجل كان يأتيه بالمال فيستودعه إياه، فيقول الزبير: لا ولكنه سلف فإني أخشى عليه الضيعة، وما ولي إمارة قط، ولا جباية خراج، ولا شيئا إلا أن يكون في غزوة مع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أو مع أبي بكر وعمر وعثمان رضي الله عنهم.","قَالَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ الزُّبَيْرِ: فَحَسَبْتُ مَا عَلَيْهِ مِنَ الدَّيْنِ، فَوَجَدْتُهُ أَلْفَىْ أَلْفٍ وَمِائَتَىْ ألف.قال: فَلَقِيَ حَكِيمُ بْنُ حِزَامٍ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ الزُّبَيْرِ، فَقَالَ: يَا ابْنَ أَخِي، كَمْ عَلَى أَخِي مِنَ الدَّيْنِ؟ فَكَتَمَهُ، فَقَالَ: مِائَةُ ألف.فقال حَكِيمٌ: وَاللَّهِ مَا أُرَى أَمْوَالَكُمْ تَسَعُ لهذه.فقال لَهُ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ: أَفَرَأَيْتَكَ إِنْ كَانَتْ أَلْفَىْ أَلْفٍ وَمِائَتَىْ أَلْفٍ؟ قَالَ: مَا أُرَاكُمْ تُطِيقُونَ هذا.فإن عَجَزْتُمْ عَنْ شَىْءٍ مِنْهُ فَاسْتَعِينُوا بِي.","قال: وكان الزبير اشترى الغابة بسبعين ومائة ألف، فباعها عبد الله بألف ألف وستمائة ألف، ثم قام، فقال: من كان له على الزبير حق فليوافنا بالغابة، فأتاه عبد الله بن جعفر وكان له على الزبير أربعمائة ألف، فقال لعبد الله: إن شئتم تركتها لكم.قال عبد الله: لا.قال: فإن شئتم جعلتموها فيما تؤخرون إن أخرتم.فقال عبد الله: لا.قال: قال: فاقطعوا لي قطعة.فقال عبد الله: لك من ها هنا إلى ها هنا.قال: فباع منها، فقضى دينه، فأوفاه، وبقي منها أربعة أسهم ونصف، فقدم على معاوية، وعنده عمرو بن عثمان، والمنذر بن الزبير، وابن زمعة.فقال له معاوية: كم قومت الغابة؟ قال: كل سهم مائة ألف.قال: كم بقي؟ قال: أربعة أسهم ونصف.قال المنذر بن الزبير: قد أخذت سهما بمائة ألف.قال عمرو بن عثمان: قد أخذت سهما بمائة ألف.وقال ابن زمعة: قد أخذت سهما بمائة ألف.فقال معاوية: كم بقي؟ فقال: سهم ونصف .قال أخذته بخمسين ومائة ألف.قال: وباع عبد الله بن جعفر نصيبه من معاوية بستمائة ألف.فلما فرغ ابن الزبير من قضاء دينه، قال بنو الزبير: اقسم بيننا ميراثنا.قال: لا، والله لا أقسم بينكم حتى أنادي بالموسم أربع سنين ألا من كان له على الزبير دين فليأتنا، فلنقضه، قال: فجعل كل سنة ينادي بالموسم، فلما مضى أربع سنين قسم بينهم.قال: فكان للزبير أربع نسوة، ورفع الثلث، فأصاب كل امرأة ألف ألف ومائتا ألف، فجميع ماله خمسون ألف ألف ومائتا ألف."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فرض الخمس (3129) عن إسحاق بن إبراهيم قال: قلت لأبي أسامة: أحدثكم هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عبد الله بن الزبير فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار الزبير بن العوام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3129).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب الزبير بن العوام وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_no":49,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr said: When al-Zubayr stood on the Day of the Battle of the Camel, he called me to him, and I stood beside him. He said: “My son, today no one will be killed except one who is either an oppressor or one who has been wronged. I believe that today I will be killed as one who has been wronged. One of my greatest concerns is my debt. Do you think anything of our wealth will remain after my debts are paid?” Then he said: “My son, sell our property and pay off my debts.” He also bequeathed one-third of his estate, and one-third of that one-third for the children of ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr. Hishām said: At that time, some of ʿAbdullāh’s children were already grown, including Khubayb and ʿAbbād. He then had nine sons and nine daughters. ʿAbdullāh continued: He kept reminding me about his debts, saying: “My son, if you are ever unable to pay any portion of it, seek help from my Mawlā.” I did not understand what he meant until I asked: “Father, who is your Mawlā?” He replied: “Allah.” By Allah, whenever I later faced difficulty in paying one of his debts, I would say: “O Mawlā of al-Zubayr, settle his debt.” And Allah would make it possible for it to be paid. Al-Zubayr was then killed, leaving behind neither gold nor silver coins. Rather, he left landed properties, including al-Ghābah, eleven houses in Madinah, two houses in Baṣrah, one in Kūfah, and one in Egypt. ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr continued: The reason my father had accumulated debt was that people would bring him money for safekeeping. Whenever someone entrusted him with wealth, al-Zubayr would say: “No, let it be considered a loan instead, for I fear it might be lost while in my possession.” He never held the office of governor, never collected land tax, and never occupied a position of public financial authority. His service was only in military expeditions alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with them all). I calculated the amount of his debt and found that it totaled 2,200,000. Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām met me and asked: “My nephew, how much debt did my brother leave?” I concealed the true amount and replied: “One hundred thousand.”","Ḥakīm said: “By Allah, I do not think your wealth will be sufficient even for that.” I then asked him: “What if it were 2,200,000?” He replied: “I do not think you can manage that. If you are unable to repay any part of it, seek my assistance.” Al-Zubayr had purchased al-Ghābah for 170,000, and I later sold it for 1,600,000. Then I stood and announced: “Whoever has a claim against al-Zubayr should come to us at al-Ghābah.” ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar came, for al-Zubayr owed him 400,000.","He said to me: “If you wish, I will forgo the debt.” I replied: “No.” He said: “Then, if you wish, defer it until later.” I replied: “No.” He then said: “Then allocate a portion of the land to me.” So I marked out a section of the property for him. I continued selling portions of the land until all of my father’s debts had been paid in full. Afterward, four and a half shares of the estate still remained. I then went to Muʿāwiyah, in whose company were ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān, al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr, and Ibn Zamʿah.","Muʿāwiyah asked: “At what value have you assessed al-Ghābah?” I replied: “Each share is worth one hundred thousand.” He asked: “How many shares remain?” I answered: “Four and a half.” Al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr said: “I have purchased one share for one hundred thousand.” ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān said: “I have also purchased one share for one hundred thousand.” Ibn Zamʿah likewise said: “I have purchased one share for one hundred thousand.” Muʿāwiyah then asked: “How much remains?” I replied: “One and a half shares.” He said: “I will purchase them for one hundred and fifty thousand.” Later, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar sold his share to Muʿāwiyah for 600,000. After I had completely settled my father’s debts, the children of al-Zubayr said: “Distribute our inheritance among us.” I replied: “No, by Allah. I will not divide it until I announce during the pilgrimage season for four consecutive years: ‘Whoever is owed anything by al-Zubayr should come to us so that we may repay it.’” He continued making this announcement every year during the pilgrimage season. When four years had passed, he distributed the estate. Al-Zubayr had four wives. After setting aside the one-third bequest, each wife received 1,200,000, and the total value of his estate amounted to 50,200,000."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",147],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3129)."},{"num":9949,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُرْوَةَ، قَالَ: كَانَ فِي الزُّبَيْرِ ثَلاَثُ ضَرَبَاتٍ بِالسَّيْفِ، إِحْدَاهُنَّ فِي عَاتِقِهِ، قَالَ: إِنْ كُنْتُ لأُدْخِلُ أَصَابِعِي فِيهَا. قَالَ ضُرِبَ ثِنْتَيْنِ يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ، وَوَاحِدَةً يَوْمَ الْيَرْمُوكِ. قَالَ عُرْوَةُ: وَقَالَ لِي عَبْدُ الْمَلِكِ بْنُ مَرْوَانَ حِينَ قُتِلَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ الزُّبَيْرِ: يَا عُرْوَةُ، هَلْ تَعْرِفُ سَيْفَ الزُّبَيْرِ؟ قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ فَمَا فِيهِ؟ قُلْتُ: فِيهِ فَلَّةٌ فُلَّهَا يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ. قَالَ صَدَقْتَ. بِهِنَّ فُلُولٌ مِنْ قِرَاعِ الْكَتَائِبِ ثُمَّ رَدَّهُ عَلَى عُرْوَةَ. قَالَ هِشَامٌ: فَأَقَمْنَاهُ بَيْنَنَا ثَلاَثَةَ آلاَفٍ، وَأَخَذَهُ بَعْضُنَا، وَلَوَدِدْتُ أَنِّي كُنْتُ أَخَذْتُهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (3973) عن إبراهيم بن موسى، ثنا هشام بن يوسف، عن معمر، عن هشام، عن عروة قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أخبار الزبير بن العوام في قتاله وشجاعته","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3973).","chapter_en":"Reports of al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām in Battle and His Bravery","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب الزبير بن العوام وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_no":49,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUrwah said: Al-Zubayr had three sword wounds. One of them was on his shoulder, and it was so deep that I used to put my fingers into it. Two of those wounds were inflicted on the Day of Badr, and one at the Battle of al-Yarmūk. ʿUrwah further said: After ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr was killed, ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān asked me: “Do you recognize al-Zubayr’s sword?” I replied: “Yes.” He asked: “What distinguishes it?” I said: “It has a notch that it received on the Day of Badr.” He replied: “You have spoken the truth.” Then he recited: “Its notches were made by the clash of battalions.” He then returned the sword to ʿUrwah. Hishām said: We valued it among ourselves at three thousand, and one of us eventually acquired it. I wish that I had been the one who obtained it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",148],"full":1,"rep":[8742],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3973)."},{"num":9950,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِيهِ، أَنَّ أَصْحَابَ، رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالُوا لِلزُّبَيْرِ يَوْمَ الْيَرْمُوكِ: أَلاَ تَشُدُّ فَنَشُدَّ مَعَكَ؟ فَقَالَ: إِنِّي إِنْ شَدَدْتُ كَذَبْتُمْ. فَقَالُوا لاَ نَفْعَلُ، فَحَمَلَ عَلَيْهِمْ حَتَّى شَقَّ صُفُوفَهُمْ، فَجَاوَزَهُمْ وَمَا مَعَهُ أَحَدٌ، ثُمَّ رَجَعَ مُقْبِلاً، فَأَخَذُوا بِلِجَامِهِ، فَضَرَبُوهُ ضَرْبَتَيْنِ عَلَى عَاتِقِهِ، بَيْنَهُمَا ضَرْبَةٌ ضُرِبَهَا يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ. قَالَ عُرْوَةُ: كُنْتُ أُدْخِلُ أَصَابِعِي فِي تِلْكَ الضَّرَبَاتِ أَلْعَبُ وَأَنَا صَغِيرٌ. قَالَ عُرْوَةُ: وَكَانَ مَعَهُ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ الزُّبَيْرِ يَوْمَئِذٍ وَهْوَ ابْنُ عَشْرِ سِنِينَ، فَحَمَلَهُ عَلَى فَرَسٍ وَكَّلَ بِهِ رَجُلاً."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (3975) عن أحمد بن محمد، ثنا عبد الله –هو ابن المبارك-، أنا هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أخبار الزبير بن العوام في قتاله وشجاعته","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3975).","chapter_en":"Reports of al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām in Battle and His Bravery","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب الزبير بن العوام وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_no":49,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to al-Zubayr on the Day of al-Yarmūk: “Will you charge the enemy so that we may charge with you?” Al-Zubayr replied: “If I charge, you will not keep up with me.” They said: “No, we will not fail you.” So he launched his attack and drove straight through the enemy ranks until he passed completely beyond them, with no one remaining alongside him. He then turned back toward his own army. As he returned, the enemy seized the reins of his horse and struck him twice on his shoulder, in addition to the wound he had previously received at the Battle of Badr. ʿUrwah said: When I was a small child, I used to put my fingers into those wounds while playing. He also said: On that day, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr was with him, and he was only ten years old. Al-Zubayr placed him upon a horse and entrusted him to the care of another man."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",149],"full":1,"rep":[8741],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3975)."},{"num":9951,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُرْوَةَ قَالَ: كَانَ سَيْفُ الزُّبَيْرِ مُحَلًّى بِفِضَّةٍ، قَالَ هِشَامٌ: وَكَانَ سَيْفُ عُرْوَةَ مُحَلًّى بِفِضَّةٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (3974) عن فروة، عن علي، عن هشام، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أخبار الزبير بن العوام في قتاله وشجاعته","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3974).","chapter_en":"Reports of al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām in Battle and His Bravery","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب الزبير بن العوام وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām","part_no":49,"group_no":7,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUrwah said: The sword of al-Zubayr was adorned with silver. Hishām added: The sword of ʿUrwah was likewise adorned with silver."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3974)."},{"num":9952,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: أَرِقَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ذَاتَ لَيْلَةٍ، فَقَالَ: لَيْتَ رَجُلاً صَالِحًا مِنْ أَصْحَابِي يَحْرُسُنِي اللَّيْلَةَ. إِذْ سَمِعْنَا صَوْتَ السِّلاَحِ قَالَ مَنْ هَذَا. قِيلَ سَعْدٌ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، جِئْتُ أَحْرُسُكَ. فَنَامَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى سَمِعْنَا غَطِيطَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التمني (7231)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2410-39) كلاهما من طريق سليمان بن بلال، ثني يحيى بن سعيد، سمعت عبدالله بن عامر بن ربيعة قال: قالت عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن سعد بن أبي وقاص رجل صالح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7231) and Muslim (2410, no. 39). The alternate wording is recorded by Muslim (2410, no. 40) through another chain.","chapter_en":"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ Was a Righteous Man","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: One night the Prophet ﷺ was unable to sleep. He said: “If only a righteous man from among my Companions would guard me tonight.” Then we heard the sound of weapons. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Who is this?” The man replied: “It is Saʿd, O Messenger of Allah. I have come to guard you.” After that, the Prophet ﷺ slept until we heard him snoring. Another narration states: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained awake one night shortly after arriving in Madinah. While they were in that state, they heard the clattering of weapons. He asked: “Who is this?” The reply came: “Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “What has brought you here?” Saʿd replied: “I became concerned for the safety of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I came to guard you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then supplicated for him before going to sleep."]},"intro_majmu":{"ar":["هو: سعد بن مالك بن وهيب بن عبد مناف، يجتمع مع النبي ﷺ في كلاب بن مُرَّة، وكنية أبيه “أبو وقاص”. وإن الله فتح العراق على يد سعد بن أبي وقاص، وكان مقدم الجيوش يوم وقعة القادسية، ونصر الله به دينه، ونزل سعد بالمدائن، ثم كان أمير الناس يوم جلولاء، فكان النصر على يده، واستأصل الله الأكاسرة. وأمه حمنة بنت سفيان بن أبي أمية، لم تُسلم، وسيأتي ذكرها في الباب الثالث."],"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ was Saʿd ibn Mālik ibn Wahayb ibn ʿAbd Manāf. His lineage meets that of the Prophet ﷺ at Kilāb ibn Murrah. His father’s kunyah was Abū Waqqāṣ.","Allah granted the conquest of Iraq through Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ. He commanded the Muslim armies at the Battle of al-Qādisiyyah, through whom Allah gave victory to His religion. He later settled in al-Madāʾin, and subsequently served as commander of the Muslims at the Battle of Jalūlāʾ, where victory again came through him. Through these victories, Allah brought about the downfall of the Persian emperors (the Kisrās).","His mother was Ḥamnah bint Sufyān ibn Abī Umayyah. She did not embrace Islam, and her account will be mentioned in the third chapter."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",151],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8923,14648],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7231)، ومسلم (2410/39)."},{"num":9953,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ علي يَقُولُ: مَا جَمَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَبَوَيْهِ لِأَحَدٍ غَيْرَِ سَعْدِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، فَإِنَّهُ جَعَلَ يَقُولُ لَهُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ: ارْمِ فِدَاكَ أَبِي وَأُمِّي."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الجهاد (2905) وفي المغازي bukhari(4059)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2411-41) كلاهما من طرق عن سعد بن إبراهيم، عن عبدالله بن شداد، سمعت عليا يقول: فذكره.واللفظ لمسلم، وساقه البخاري نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن النبي ﷺ جمع أبويه لسعد بن أبي وقاص","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2905, 4059) and Muslim (2411, no. 41).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Invoked Both His Father and Mother for Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never invoked both his father and mother as a ransom for anyone except Saʿd ibn Mālik. On the Day of Uḥud he repeatedly said to him: “Shoot, O Saʿd! May my father and my mother be sacrificed for you.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The name “Saʿd ibn Mālik” refers to Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",152],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2905، 4059)، ومسلم (2411/41)."},{"num":9954,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بْنِ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ قَالَ:  لَقَدْ جَمَعَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَبَوَيْهِ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3725)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2412) كلاهما من طريق يحيى بن سعيد، قال: سمعت سعيد بن المسيب قال: سمعت سعدا فذكره، واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن النبي ﷺ جمع أبويه لسعد بن أبي وقاص","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: The first wording is narrated by al-Bukhārī (3725) and Muslim (2412), with Muslim’s wording. The quiver wording is recorded by al-Bukhārī (4055). The next wording is recorded by al-Bukhārī (4057) and Muslim (2412, no. 42). Muslim (2412, no. 42) also records the final added wording.","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Invoked Both His Father and Mother for Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ invoked both his father and his mother as a ransom for me on the Day of Uḥud. Another narration states: The Prophet ﷺ handed me his quiver on the Day of Uḥud and said: “Shoot! May my father and my mother be sacrificed for you.” Another wording says: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ invoked both his father and mother for me on the Day of Uḥud when he said: “May my father and my mother be sacrificed for you,” while I was fighting. Another narration in Muslim adds: A man from among the polytheists was causing great harm to the Muslims. The Prophet ﷺ said to me: “Shoot! May my father and my mother be sacrificed for you.” So I shot an arrow without an iron head. It struck him in his side, causing him to fall. His private parts became exposed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until I could see his molar teeth."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",153],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3725)، ومسلم (2412)، واللفظ لمسلم."},{"num":9955,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن مصعب بن سَعْدٍ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ  أَنَّهُ نَزَلَتْ فِيهِ آيَاتٌ مِنَ الْقُرْآنِ، قَالَ: حَلَفَتْ أُمُّ سَعْدٍ أَنْ لَا تُكَلِّمَهُ أَبَدًا حَتَّى يَكْفُرَ بِدِينِهِ، وَلَا تَأْكُلَ، وَلَا تَشْرَبَ! قَالَتْ: زَعَمْتَ أَنَّ اللَّهَ وَصَّاكَ بِوَالِدَيْكَ، وَأَنَا أُمُّكَ، وَأَنَا آمُرُكَ بِهَذَا! قَالَ: مَكَثَتْ ثَلَاثًا حَتَّى غُشِيَ عَلَيْهَا مِنَ الْجَهْدِ، فَقَامَ ابْنٌ لَهَا يُقَالُ لَهُ: عُمَارَةُ فَسَقَاهَا، فَجَعَلَتْ تَدْعُو عَلَى سَعْدٍ، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ فِي الْقُرْآنِ هَذِهِ الْآيَةَ: ﴿وَوَصَّيْنَا الإِنْسَانَ بِوَالِدَيْهِ حُسْنًا﴾ ﴿وَإِنْ جَاهَدَاكَ عَلَى أَنْ تُشْرِكَ بِي﴾، وَفِيهَا: ﴿وَصَاحِبْهُمَا فِي الدُّنْيَا مَعْرُوفًا﴾. قَالَ:","قَالَ: وَأَصَابَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم غَنِيمَةً عَظِيمَةً، فَإِذَا فِيهَا سَيْفٌ، فَأَخَذْتُهُ فَأَتَيْتُ بِهِ الرَّسُولَ صلى الله عليه وسلم، فَقُلْتُ: نَفِّلْنِي هَذَا السَّيْفَ، فَأَنَا مَنْ قَدْ عَلِمْتَ حاله.فقال: رُدُّهُ مِنْ حَيْثُ أخذته.فانطلقت حَتَّى إِذَا أَرَدْتُ أَنْ أُلْقِيَهُ فِي الْقَبَضِ لَامَتْنِي نَفْسِي، فَرَجَعْتُ إِلَيْهِ، فَقُلْتُ: أعطنيه.قال: فَشَدَّ لِي صَوْتَهُ: رُدُّهُ مِنْ حَيْثُ أخذته.قال: فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عز وجل: يَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الأَنْفَالِ [الأنفال: ١].١].","قال: ومرضت فأرسلت إلى النبى صلى الله عليه وسلم، فأتاني، فقلت: دعني أقسم مالي حيث شئت.قال: فأبى.قلت: فالنصف.قال: فأبى.قلت: فالثلث.قال: فسكت، فكان بعد الثلث جائزا.","قَالَ: وَأَتَيْتُ عَلَى نَفَرٍ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ وَالْمُهَاجِرِينَ، فَقَالُوا: تَعَالَ نُطْعِمُكَ وَنَسْقِيكَ خمرا.وذلك قَبْلَ أَنْ تُحْرِمَ الْخَمْرُ، قَالَ: فَأَتَيْتُهُمْ فِي حَشٍّ -وَالْحَشِّ الْبُسْتَانِ- فَإِذَا رَأْسُ جَزُورٍ مَشْوِيٍّ عِنْدَهُمْ، وَزُقَّ مِنْ خَمْرٍ، قَالَ: فَأَكَلْتُ وَشَرِبْتُ معهم.قال: فَذَكَرْتُ الأَنْصَارَ والمهاجرون عندهم.فقلت: الْمُهَاجِرُونَ خَيْرٌ مِنَ الأنصار.قال: فَأَخَذَ رَجُلٌ أَحَدَ لَحْيَيِ الرَّأْسِ فَضَرَبَنِي بِهِ فَجَرَحَ بأنفى.فأتيت رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ فِي -يْعَنِي نَفْسَهُ- شَأْنَ الْخَمْرِ: ﴿إِنَّمَا الْخَمْرُ وَالْمَيْسِرُ وَالأَنْصَابُ وَالأَزْلَامُ رِجْسٌ مِنْ عَمَلِ الشَّيطَانِ﴾ [الْمَائِدَةُ:٩٠]."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (1748-43) من طرق عن الحسن بن موسى، ثنا زهير، ثنا سماك بن حرب، ثنا مصعب بن سعد، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن سعدًا نزلت فيه آيات من القرآن الكريم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1748, no. 43).","chapter_en":"Qur’anic Verses Revealed Concerning Saʿd","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd narrated from his father: Several verses of the Qur’an were revealed concerning me. My mother swore that she would never speak to me until I abandoned my religion. She also vowed that she would neither eat nor drink. She said: “You claim that Allah has commanded you to be dutiful to your parents. I am your mother, and I command you to do this.” I remained steadfast for three days until she collapsed from exhaustion. One of her sons, named ʿUmārah, gave her water to drink. Afterward she began supplicating against me. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “And We have enjoined upon man kindness to his parents…” (Qur’an 29:8) And: “But if they strive to make you associate with Me that of which you have no knowledge…” (Qur’an 31:15) Including His statement: ”…Yet accompany them in this world with kindness.” (Qur’an 31:15) The Messenger of Allah ﷺ acquired a large amount of war booty, among which was a sword. I took the sword and brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: “Grant this sword to me as an extra share, for you know my service and what I have done.”","He replied: “Return it to where you took it from.” So I went away. But when I was about to place it back with the collected spoils, I reproached myself and returned to him, saying: “Give it to me.” He raised his voice to me and said: “Return it to where you took it from.” Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “They ask you concerning the spoils of war…” (Qur’an 8:1) Later I became ill and sent for the Prophet ﷺ. He came to visit me. I said: “Allow me to distribute my wealth as I wish.”","He refused. I asked: “Then half of it?” He refused. I asked: “Then one-third?” He remained silent, and thereafter one-third became the permissible limit for making a bequest. I once passed by a group of the Anṣār and the Muhājirūn, and they said: “Come and eat with us, and drink some wine.” This was before wine had been prohibited. I joined them in a garden where there was a roasted camel’s head and a skin filled with wine. I ate and drank with them.","During the gathering, the Anṣār and the Muhājirūn were mentioned. I said: “The Muhājirūn are better than the Anṣār.” A man then took one of the jawbones of the roasted camel’s head and struck me with it, injuring my nose. I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of what had happened. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning me—that is, regarding the matter of wine— “Indeed, intoxicants, gambling, stone altars, and divining arrows are nothing but filth from the work of Satan…” (Qur’an 5:90)"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Another wording recorded by Muslim states:","“Four Qur’anic verses were revealed concerning me.”","He then mentioned the incident of the sword, adding that he repeated his request four times, and each time the Prophet ﷺ said:","“Put it back where you took it from.”","From the reports above, it is clear that four Qur’anic revelations were connected to Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ. However, in these narrations only three of those revelations have been mentioned. The fourth will be mentioned later, Allah willing."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1748/43)."},{"num":9956,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدٍ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ قَالَ: كُنَّا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي سِتَّةَ نَفَرٍ، فَقَالَ الْمُشْرِكُونَ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اطْرُدْ هَؤُلَاءِ لَا يَجْتَرِئُونَ عَلَيْنَا.قَالَ: وَكُنْتُ أَنَا وَابْنُ مَسْعُودٍ، وَرَجُلٌ مِنْ هُذَيْلٍ، وَبِلَالٌ، وَرَجُلَانِ لَسْتُ أُسَمِّيهِمَا.فَوَقَعَ فِي نَفْسِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَا شَاءَ اللَّهُ أَنْ يَقَعَ، فحدَّث نَفْسَهُ، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: ﴿وَلَا تَطْرُدِ الَّذِينَ يَدْعُونَ رَبَّهُمْ بِالْغَدَاةِ وَالْعَشِيِّ يُرِيدُونَ وَجْهَهُ مَا عَلَيْكَ مِنْ حِسَابِهِمْ مِنْ شَيْءٍ﴾ [الأنعام: ٥٢] ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2413-46) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة، ثنا محمد بن عبد الله الأسدي، عن إسرائيل، عن المقدام بن شريح، عن أبيه، عن سعد فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن سعدًا نزلت فيه آيات من القرآن الكريم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2413, no. 46).","chapter_en":"Qur’anic Verses Revealed Concerning Saʿd","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) said: There were six of us with the Prophet ﷺ when the polytheists said to him: “Drive these people away so that they will not presume equality with us.” Those present were myself, Ibn Masʿūd, a man from Hudhayl, Bilāl, and two others whose names I will not mention. A thought crossed the mind of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as Allah willed that it should. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His Face. You are not accountable for them in the least…” (Qur’an 6:52)"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2413/46)."},{"num":9957,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سَعْدِ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ يَقُولُ: مَا أَسْلَمَ أَحَدٌ إِلاَّ فِي الْيَوْمِ الَّذِي أَسْلَمْتُ فِيهِ، وَلَقَدْ مَكَثْتُ سَبْعَةَ أَيَّامٍ وَإِنِّي لَثُلُثُ الإِسْلاَمِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3727) عن إبراهيم بن موسى، أنا ابن أبي زائدة، ثنا هاشم بن هاشم بن عتبة بن أبي وقاص قال: سمعت سعيد بن المسيب يقول: سمعت سعد بن أبي وقاص يقول: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن سعدًا أسلم يوم أسلم وهو ثلث الإسلام","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3727).","chapter_en":"Saʿd Accepted Islam at a Time When He Was One-Third of the Muslim Community","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) said: No one embraced Islam before the day on which I embraced Islam. For seven days, I was one-third of the Muslim community."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “I was one-third of the Muslim community,” means that, according to his knowledge at that time, the Muslims consisted of Khadījah, Abū Bakr, and himself as the third. Others had accepted Islam before him, but they had concealed their faith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",156],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8570],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3727)."},{"num":9958,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ قَالَ: إِنِّي لأَوَّلُ الْعَرَبِ رَمَى بِسَهْمٍ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، وَرَأَيْتُنَا نَغْزُو وَمَا لَنَا طَعَامٌ إِلاَّ وَرَقُ الْحُبْلَةِ وَهَذَا السَّمُرُ، وَإِنَّ أَحَدَنَا لَيَضَعُ كَمَا تَضَعُ الشَّاةُ مَا لَهُ خِلْطٌ، ثُمَّ أَصْبَحَتْ بَنُو أَسَدٍ تُعَزِّرُنِي عَلَى الإِسْلاَمِ، خِبْتُ إذاً وضلَّ سَعْيِي."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الرقاق (6453)، ومسلم في الزهد (2966-12) كلاهما من طريق إسماعيل، ثنا قيس، سمعت سعدا يقول: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن سعد بن أبي وقاص أول العرب رمى في سبيل الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6453) and Muslim (2966, no. 12).","chapter_en":"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ Was the First Arab to Shoot an Arrow in the Cause of Allah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I was the first Arab to shoot an arrow in the cause of Allah. I remember that we used to go out on military expeditions while having no food except the leaves of the ḥablah plant and the samar tree. One of us would pass stool just as a sheep does, with nothing mixed into it because of the lack of proper food. And now Banū Asad are teaching me the laws of Islam! If that were so, then I would indeed have failed and all my efforts would have been in vain."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",157],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6453)، ومسلم (2966/12)."},{"num":9959,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَامِرِ بن سَعْدٍ قَالَ:  كَانَ سَعْدُ بْنُ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ فِي إِبِلِهِ، فَجَاءَهُ ابْنُهُ عُمَرُ، فَلَمَّا رَآهُ سَعْدٌ قَالَ: أَعُوذُ بِاللهِ مِنْ شَرِّ هَذَا الرَّاكِبِ، فَنَزَلَ، فَقَالَ لَهُ: أَنَزَلْتَ فِي إِبِلِكَ وَغَنَمِكَ وَتَرَكْتَ النَّاسَ يَتَنَازَعُونَ الْمُلْكَ بَيْنَهُمْ؟ فَضَرَبَ سَعْدٌ فِي صَدْرِهِ، فَقَالَ: اسْكُتْ، سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْعَبْدَ التَّقِيَّ الْغَنِيَّ الْخَفِيَّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الزهد (2965) من طرق عن أبي بكر الحنفي، ثنا بكير بن مسمار، ثني عامر بن سعد قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في انعزال سعد بن أبي وقاص عن الفتنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2965).","chapter_en":"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ’s Withdrawal from the Civil Strife (Fitnah)","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd said: Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ was tending his camels when his son ʿUmar came to him. When Saʿd saw him approaching, he said: “I seek refuge in Allah from the evil of this rider.” His son dismounted and said: “You remain here with your camels and sheep while the people are disputing among themselves over political authority?” Saʿd struck him on the chest and said: “Be quiet. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Indeed, Allah loves the servant who is God-fearing, self-sufficient, and unobtrusive.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Ḥajar said in al-Iṣābah (3208):","“When ʿUthmān was killed, Saʿd withdrew from the civil strife and remained in his home.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",158],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[15104],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2965)."},{"num":9960,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ دَخَلَ عَلَى سَعْدٍ يَعُودُهُ بِمَكَّةَ، فَبَكَى، قَالَ: مَا يُبْكِيكَ؟.فَقَالَ: قَدْ خَشِيتُ أَنْ أَمُوتَ بِالْأَرْضِ الَّتِي هَاجَرْتُ مِنْهَا، كَمَا مَاتَ سَعْدُ بْنُ خَوْلَةَ.فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اللَّهُمَّ اشْفِ سَعْدًا، اللَّهُمَّ اشْفِ سَعْدًا.ثَلَاثَ مِرَارٍ.قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ لِي مَالًا كَثِيرًا، وَإِنَّمَا يَرِثُنِي ابْنَتِي، أَفَأُوصِي بِمَالِي كُلِّهِ؟ قَالَ: لَا.قَالَ: فَبِالثُّلُثَيْنِ؟ قَالَ: لَا.قَالَ: فَالنِّصْفُ؟ قَالَ: لَا.قَالَ: فَالثُّلُثُ؟ قَالَ: الثُّلُثُ، وَالثُّلُثُ كَثِيرٌ، إِنَّ صَدَقَتَكَ مِنْ مَالِكَ صَدَقَةٌ، وَإِنَّ نَفَقَتَكَ عَلَى عِيَالِكَ صَدَقَةٌ، وَإِنَّ مَا تَأْكُلُ امْرَأَتُكَ مِنْ مَالِكَ صَدَقَةٌ، وَإِنَّكَ أَنْ تَدَعَ أَهْلَكَ بِخَيْرٍ - أَوْ قَالَ بِعَيْشٍ - خَيْرٌ مِنْ أَنْ تَدَعَهُمْ يَتَكَفَّفُونَ النَّاسَ.وَقَالَ: بِيَدِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الوصية (1628-8) عن محمد بن أبي عمر المكي، ثنا الثقفي، عن أيوب السختياني، عن عمرو بن سعيد، عن حميد بن عبد الرحمن، عن ثلاثة من ولد سعد، كلهم يحدثه عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ لسعد بالشفاء في مرضه عام حجة الوداع بمكة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1628, no. 8).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Supplication for Saʿd’s Recovery During His Illness in Makkah at the Farewell Pilgrimage","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet ﷺ visited him in Makkah while he was ill. Saʿd began to weep. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “What is making you weep?” He replied: “I fear that I may die in the land from which I emigrated, just as Saʿd ibn Khawlah died.” The Prophet ﷺ supplicated three times: “O Allah, cure Saʿd. O Allah, cure Saʿd. O Allah, cure Saʿd.” Saʿd then said: “O Messenger of Allah, I possess abundant wealth, and only my daughter will inherit from me. May I bequeath all of my wealth?” He replied: “No.” Saʿd asked: “Then two-thirds?” He replied: “No.” Saʿd asked: “Then half?” He replied: “No.” Saʿd asked: “Then one-third?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “One-third, and even one-third is much. Your charity from your wealth is charity, your spending on your family is charity, and whatever your wife eats from your wealth is charity. It is better for you to leave your family well provided—or he said: well off—than to leave them dependent upon people, begging from them.” He then gestured with his hand."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",159],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1628/8)."},{"num":9961,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ قَالَ: عَادَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حَجَّةِ الْوَدَاعِ مِنْ وَجَعٍ أَشْفَيْتُ مِنْهُ عَلَى الْمَوْتِ، فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ بَلَغَنِي مَا تَرَى مِنَ الْوَجَعِ، وَأَنَا ذُو مَالٍ، وَلَا يَرِثُنِي إِلَّا ابْنَةٌ لِي وَاحِدَةٌ، أَفَأَتَصَدَّقُ بِثُلُثَيْ مَالِي؟ قَالَ: لَا.قَالَ: قُلْتُ: أَفَأَتَصَدَّقُ بِشَطْرِهِ؟ قَالَ: لَا، الثُّلُثُ وَالثُّلُثُ كَثِيرٌ، إِنَّكَ أَنْ تَذَرَ وَرَثَتَكَ أَغْنِيَاءَ خَيْرٌ مِنْ أَنْ تَذَرَهُمْ عَالَةً يَتَكَفَّفُونَ النَّاسَ، وَلَسْتَ تُنْفِقُ نَفَقَةً تَبْتَغِي بِهَا وَجْهَ اللَّهِ، إِلَّا أُجِرْتَ بِهَا، حَتَّى اللُّقْمَةُ تَجْعَلُهَا فِي فِي امْرَأَتِكَ.قَالَ: قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أُخَلَّفُ بَعْدَ أَصْحَابِي؟.قَالَ: إِنَّكَ لَنْ تُخَلَّف فَتَعْمَلَ عَمَلًا تَبْتَغِي بِهِ وَجْهَ اللَّهِ إِلَّا ازْدَدْتَ بِهِ دَرَجَةً وَرِفْعَةً، وَلَعَلَّكَ تُخَلَّف حَتَّى يُنْفَع بِكَ أَقْوَامٌ، ويُضَرَّ بِكَ آخَرُونَ.اللَّهُمَّ أَمْضِ لِأَصْحَابِي هِجْرَتَهُمْ، وَلَا تَرُدَّهُمْ عَلَى أَعْقَابِهِمْ.لَكِنِ الْبَائِسُ سَعْدُ بْنُ خَوْلَةَ.","قَالَ: رَثَى لَهُ رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم مِنْ أَنْ تُوُفِّيَ بِمَكَّةَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3936)، ومسلم في الوصية (1628-5) كلاهما من طريق إبراهيم بن سعد، عن ابن شهاب، عن عامر بن سعد، عن أبيه سعد بن أبي وقاص فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب قوله ﷺ لسعد: يُنفع بك أقوام ويضر بك آخرون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3936) and Muslim (1628, no. 5).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Statement to Saʿd: “Through You Some People Will Benefit and Others Will Be Harmed”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited me during the Farewell Pilgrimage while I was suffering from an illness that had brought me close to death. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, you see the severity of my illness. I possess wealth, and only one daughter will inherit from me. May I give two-thirds of my wealth in charity?” He replied: “No.” I asked: “Then half?” He said: “No. One-third, and even one-third is much. It is better to leave your heirs wealthy than to leave them poor and dependent upon people. You will not spend anything seeking the Face of Allah except that you will be rewarded for it—even the morsel of food that you place into your wife’s mouth.” I then asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will I remain behind after my companions?” He replied: “You will not remain behind and perform any deed seeking the Face of Allah except that it will increase you in rank and honor. Perhaps you will live on so that through you some people will benefit and others will be harmed. O Allah, complete the migration of my Companions and do not cause them to turn back on their heels. But pitiable is Saʿd ibn Khawlah.” Saʿd explained: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ expressed sorrow because Saʿd ibn Khawlah had died in Makkah."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The Prophet’s ﷺ statement,","“Perhaps you will live on so that through you some people will benefit…”","meant that Saʿd would not die from this illness, but would live for many years thereafter. He later led the Muslim conquest of Iraq and other lands. Through him, the Muslims greatly benefited, while the disbelievers were defeated, most notably at the Battle of al-Qādisiyyah during the caliphate of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",160],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3936)، ومسلم (1628/5)."},{"num":9962,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى قَالَ: مَرِضَ سَعْدٌ بِمَكَّةَ، فَأَتَاهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَعُودُهُ، فَقَالَ لَهُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَلَيْسَ تَكْرَهُ أَنْ يَمُوتَ الرَّجُلُ فِي الأَرْضِ الَّتِي هَاجَرَ مِنْهَا؟ قَالَ: بَلَى، وَلَعَلَّ اللَّهَ تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالَى يَرْفَعُكَ فَيَضُرُّ بِكَ قَوْمًا، وَيَنْفَعُ آخَرِينَ بِكَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار (3139) عن محمد بن عمر بن هياج، أخبرنا الفضل بن دكين أبو نعيم، أخبرنا محمد بن قيس، عن أبي بردة، عن أبي موسى فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قوله ﷺ لسعد: يُنفع بك أقوام ويضر بك آخرون","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār (3139).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Statement to Saʿd: “Through You Some People Will Benefit and Others Will Be Harmed”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Saʿd became ill in Makkah, and the Prophet ﷺ came to visit him. Saʿd asked: “O Messenger of Allah, do you not dislike that a man should die in the land from which he emigrated?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Yes. But perhaps Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will raise your rank, and through you He will harm some people and benefit others.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",161],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار (3139)."},{"num":9963,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَامِرِ بْنِ سَعْدِ بْنِ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ  أَنَّ سَعْدَ بْنَ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ قَالَ: فِي مَرَضِهِ الَّذِي هَلَكَ فِيهِ: الْحَدُوا لِي لَحْدًا، وَانْصِبُوا عَلَيَّ اللَّبِنَ نَصْبًا، كَمَا صُنِعَ بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجنائز (966) عن يحيى بن يحيى، أنا عبد الله بن جعفر السوري، عن إسماعيل بن محمد بن سعد، عن عامر بن سعد بن أبي وقاص أن سعد بن أبي وقاص قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار سعد بن أبي وقاص","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (966).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated that Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ said during the illness from which he eventually died: “Dig a niche grave (laḥd) for me, and set the bricks over me upright, just as was done for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",162],"full":1,"rep":[3802,9377],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (966)."},{"num":9964,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ سَمُرَةَ، قَالَ: شَكَا أَهْلُ الْكُوفَةِ سَعْدًا إِلَى عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ، فَعَزَلَهُ وَاسْتَعْمَلَ عَلَيْهِمْ عَمَّارًا، فَشَكَوْا حَتَّى ذَكَرُوا أَنَّهُ لاَ يُحْسِنُ يُصَلِّي، فَأَرْسَلَ إِلَيْهِ، فَقَالَ: يَا أَبَا إِسْحَاقَ إِنَّ هَؤُلاَءِ يَزْعُمُونَ أَنَّكَ لاَ تُحْسِنُ تُصَلِّي؟ قَالَ أَبُو إِسْحَاقَ أَمَّا أَنَا وَاللَّهِ فَإِنِّي كُنْتُ أُصَلِّي بِهِمْ صَلاَةَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَا أَخْرِمُ عَنْهَا، أُصَلِّي صَلاَةَ الْعِشَاءِ فَأَرْكُدُ فِي الأُولَيَيْنِ وَأُخِفُّ فِي الأُخْرَيَيْنِ. قَالَ ذَاكَ الظَّنُّ بِكَ يَا أَبَا إِسْحَاقَ. فَأَرْسَلَ مَعَهُ رَجُلاً أَوْ رِجَالاً إِلَى الْكُوفَةِ، فَسَأَلَ عَنْهُ أَهْلَ الْكُوفَةِ، وَلَمْ يَدَعْ مَسْجِدًا إِلاَّ سَأَلَ عَنْهُ، وَيُثْنُونَ مَعْرُوفًا، حَتَّى دَخَلَ مَسْجِدًا لِبَنِي عَبْسٍ، فَقَامَ رَجُلٌ مِنْهُمْ، يُقَالُ لَهُ: أُسَامَةُ بْنُ قَتَادَةَ، يُكْنَى أَبَا سَعْدَةَ، قَالَ: أَمَّا إِذْ نَشَدْتَنَا، فَإِنَّ سَعْدًا كَانَ لاَ يَسِيرُ بِالسَّرِيَّةِ، وَلاَ يَقْسِمُ بِالسَّوِيَّةِ، وَلاَ يَعْدِلُ فِي الْقَضِيَّةِ. قَالَ سَعْدٌ: أَمَا وَاللَّهِ لأَدْعُوَنَّ بِثَلاَثٍ، اللَّهُمَّ إِنْ كَانَ عَبْدُكَ هَذَا كَاذِبًا، قَامَ رِيَاءً وَسُمْعَةً فَأَطِلْ عُمْرَهُ، وَأَطِلْ فَقْرَهُ، وَعَرِّضْهُ بِالْفِتَنِ، وَكَانَ بَعْدُ إِذَا سُئِلَ يَقُولُ: شَيْخٌ كَبِيرٌ مَفْتُونٌ، أَصَابَتْنِي دَعْوَةُ سَعْدٍ. قَالَ عَبْدُ الْمَلِكِ: فَأَنَا رَأَيْتُهُ بَعْدُ قَدْ سَقَطَ حَاجِبَاهُ عَلَى عَيْنَيْهِ مِنَ الْكِبَرِ، وَإِنَّهُ لَيَتَعَرَّضُ لِلْجَوَارِي فِي الطُّرُقِ يَغْمِزُهُنَّ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الأذان (755) عن موسى، ثنا أبو عوانة، ثنا عبد الملك بن عمير، عن جابر بن سمرة قال: فذكره.وهذا لفظه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن سعد بن أبي وقاص مجاب الدعاء","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (755) and Muslim (453).","chapter_en":"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ Was One Whose Supplications Were Answered","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The people of Kūfah complained about Saʿd to ʿUmar. As a result, ʿUmar removed him from office and appointed ʿAmmār as governor over them. They continued making complaints until they even claimed that Saʿd did not know how to lead the prayer properly. ʿUmar summoned him and said: “O Abū Isḥāq, these people claim that you do not perform the prayer correctly.” Abū Isḥāq (Saʿd) replied: “By Allah, I used to lead them exactly as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, without falling short in any way. I would prolong the first two rakʿahs of the ʿIshāʾ prayer and shorten the last two.” ʿUmar said: “That is exactly what I expected of you, O Abū Isḥāq.” He then sent one man—or several men—with Saʿd to Kūfah to investigate. They visited every mosque in the city, asking the people about him, and everywhere they went the people praised him. Finally they entered a mosque belonging to Banū ʿAbs. A man named Usāmah ibn Qatādah, whose kunyah was Abū Saʿdah, stood up and said: “Since you have placed us under oath, I will speak. Saʿd did not personally accompany military expeditions, he did not distribute wealth equally, and he was not just in his judgments.” Saʿd then said: “By Allah, I shall supplicate with three prayers: O Allah, if this servant of Yours is lying and has spoken only for showing off and seeking fame, then prolong his life, prolong his poverty, and expose him to trials.” Afterward, whenever that man was asked about his condition, he would say: “I am an old man afflicted by trials. The supplication of Saʿd has overtaken me.” ʿAbd al-Malik said: I later saw him myself. His eyebrows had drooped over his eyes from extreme old age, yet he still exposed himself to temptation by pursuing young women in the streets and winking at them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",163],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (755)، ومسلم (453)."},{"num":9965,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَامِرِ بْنِ سَعْدٍ  أَنَّ سَعْدًا رَكِبَ إِلَى قَصْرِهِ بِالْعَقِيقِ، فَوَجَدَ عَبْدًا يَقْطَعُ شَجَرًا أَوْ يَخْبِطُهُ، فَسَلَبَهُ، فَلَمَّا رَجَعَ سَعْدٌ جَاءَهُ أَهْلُ الْعَبْدِ، فَكَلَّمُوهُ أَنْ يَرُدَّ عَلَى غُلَامِهِمْ، أَوْ عَلَيْهِمْ مَا أَخَذَ مِنْ غُلَامِهِمْ، فَقَالَ: مَعَاذَ اللهِ أَنْ أَرُدَّ شَيْئًا نَفَّلَنِيهِ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَأَبَى أَنْ يَرُدَّ عَلَيْهِمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحج (1364) من طرق عن العقدي، أنا عبدالملك بن عمرو، ثنا عبدالله بن جعفر، عن إسماعيل بن محمد، عن عامر بن سعد، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب قصة سعد مع شخص قطع شجرًا في حدود الحرم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1364).","chapter_en":"Saʿd’s Incident with a Man Who Cut Trees Within the Sacred Precinct","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd narrated that Saʿd rode to his residence at al-ʿAqīq, where he found a slave cutting trees—or striking them to knock off their leaves. Saʿd confiscated what the slave had with him. When Saʿd returned, the slave’s family came to him and asked him to return to their servant—or to them—what he had taken. Saʿd replied: “Allah forbid that I should return something which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted to me as lawful spoils.” He refused to return it to them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",164],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1364)."},{"num":9966,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ، قَالَ: كُنَّا جُلُوسًا عِنْدَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَقْبَلَ سَعْدُ بْنُ أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: هَذَا خَالِي، فَلْيُرِنِي امْرُؤٌ خَالَهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3752) عن أبي كريب وأبي سعيد الأشج قالا: حدثنا أبو أسامة، عن مجالد (هو ا بن سعيد)، عن عامر الشعبي، عن جابر بن عبدالله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قول النبي ﷺ: هذا خالي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3752) and al-Ḥākim (6113).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Statement: “This Is My Maternal Uncle”","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب سعد بن أبي وقاص وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ","part_no":49,"group_no":8,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ approached. The Prophet ﷺ said: “This is my maternal uncle. Let each person show me his maternal uncle!”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Tirmidhī said:","“Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ belonged to Banū Zuhrah, and the Prophet’s ﷺ mother also belonged to Banū Zuhrah. For this reason the Prophet ﷺ said: ‘This is my maternal uncle.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",165],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3752)، والحاكم (6113)."},{"num":9967,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ عَوْفٍ، قَالَ: كَانَ اسْمِي عَبْدَ عَمْرٍو، فَسَمَّانِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَبْدَ الرَّحْمَنِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو نعيم في معرفة الصحابة (456)، وصحّحه الحاكم (5336) كلاهما من طرق عن إبراهيم بن سعد بن إبراهيم قال: حدثني أبي، عن أبيه، عن عبد الرحمن بن عوف فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في تغيير اسمه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Nuʿaym in Maʿrifat al-Ṣaḥābah (456), and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (5336).","chapter_en":"The Change of His Name","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل عبد الرحمن بن عوف وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf","part_no":49,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) said: My name was ʿAbd ʿAmr, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ renamed me ʿAbd al-Raḥmān."]},"intro_majmu":{"ar":["هو عبد الرحمن بن عوف القرشي الزهري، أحد العشرة المشهود لهم بالجنة، وأحد الستة أهل الشورى، وأحد السابقين البدريين، وأحد الثمانية الذين بادروا إلى الإسلام. وكان من أغنياء الصحابة، وبعثه النبي ﷺ إلى دومة الجندل، وأذن له أن يتزوج بنت ملكهم الأصبغ بن ثعلبة الكلبي، ففتح الله عليه فتزوجها، وهي تماضر أم ابنه أبي سلمة. الإصابة (٦/٥٤٤).","وذكر خليفة بسند له قوي عن ابن عمر قال: استخلف عمر عبد الرحمن بن عوف على الحج سنة ولي الخلافة، ثم حج عمر في بقية عمره. وقال ابن عبد البر: “كان مجدودًا في التجارة.” السير (١/٩٢). مات سنة إحدى وثلاثين، ودفن بالبقيع."],"en":["ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf al-Qurashī al-Zuhrī was one of the Ten Companions promised Paradise, one of the six members of the consultative council (shūrā), one of the early participants at Badr, and one of the first eight people to embrace Islam.","He was among the wealthiest of the Companions. The Prophet ﷺ sent him to Dūmat al-Jandal and permitted him to marry the daughter of their ruler, al-Aṣbagh ibn Thaʿlabah al-Kalbī. Allah granted success through him, and he married her. She was Tamāḍur, the mother of his son Abū Salamah. (Al-Iṣābah, 6/544).","Khalīfah ibn Khayyāṭ narrated with a strong chain from Ibn ʿUmar that when ʿUmar assumed the caliphate, he appointed ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf to lead the pilgrims during that year’s Ḥajj. Thereafter, ʿUmar himself performed Ḥajj in the remaining years of his caliphate.","Ibn ʿAbd al-Barr said:","“He was greatly blessed in trade.”","(Siyar, 1/92).","He died in 31 AH and was buried in al-Baqīʿ."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",166],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو نعيم في معرفة الصحابة (456)، وصححه الحاكم (5336)."},{"num":9968,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: قَدِمَ عَلَيْنَا عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنُ عَوْفٍ، وَآخَى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَ سَعْدِ بْنِ الرَّبِيعِ، وَكَانَ كَثِيرَ الْمَالِ، فَقَالَ سَعْدٌ: قَدْ عَلِمَتِ الأَنْصَارُ أَنِّي مِنْ أَكْثَرِهَا مَالاً، سَأَقْسِمُ مَالِي بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَكَ شَطْرَيْنِ، وَلِي امْرَأَتَانِ، فَانْظُرْ أَعْجَبَهُمَا إِلَيْكَ فَأُطَلِّقُهَا، حَتَّى إِذَا حَلَّتْ تَزَوَّجْتَهَا. فَقَالَ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ: بَارَكَ اللَّهُ لَكَ فِي أَهْلِكَ. فَلَمْ يَرْجِعْ يَوْمَئِذٍ حَتَّى أَفْضَلَ شَيْئًا مِنْ سَمْنٍ وَأَقِطٍ، فَلَمْ يَلْبَثْ إِلاَّ يَسِيرًا، حَتَّى جَاءَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَعَلَيْهِ وَضَرٌ مِنْ صُفْرَةٍ، فَقَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَهْيَمْ. قَالَ: تَزَوَّجْتُ امْرَأَةً مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ. فَقَالَ: مَا سُقْتَ فِيهَا. قَالَ: وَزْنَ نَوَاةٍ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ، أَوْ نَوَاةً مِنْ ذَهَبٍ، فَقَالَ: أَوْلِمْ وَلَوْ بِشَاةٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3781) عن قتيبة، حدثنا إسماعيل بن جعفر، عن حميد، عن أنس فذكره. ورواه مسلم في النكاح (81:1427) من طريق آخر عن قتادة وحميد، عن أنس به مختصرا.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في مؤاخاته","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3781) and Muslim (1427, no. 81).","chapter_en":"The Brotherhood Established Between Him and Saʿd ibn al-Rabīʿ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل عبد الرحمن بن عوف وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf","part_no":49,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf arrived in Madinah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established a bond of brotherhood between him and Saʿd ibn al-Rabīʿ. Saʿd was a man of great wealth and said: “The Anṣār know that I am among the wealthiest of them. I will divide my wealth equally between you and me. I also have two wives; look to see which one pleases you most, and I will divorce her so that, after her waiting period is complete, you may marry her.” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān replied: “May Allah bless your family and your wealth.” That very day, he went to the marketplace and returned having earned some clarified butter and dried yogurt. Not long afterward, he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with traces of yellow perfume upon him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “What is the matter?” He replied: “I have married a woman from the Anṣār.” The Prophet ﷺ asked: “What did you give her as her bridal gift (mahr)?” He replied: “The weight of a date-stone of gold.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Hold a wedding feast, even if only with one sheep.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",167],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3781)، ومسلم (81:1427)."},{"num":9969,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ الْمُغِيرَةِ بن شُعْبَةَ قَالَ فِي قِصَّةِ: فَانْتَهَيْنَا إِلَى الْقَوْمِ وَقَدْ قَامُوا فِي الصَّلَاةِ، يُصَلِّي بِهِمْ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنُ عَوْفٍ، وَقَدْ رَكَعَ بِهِمْ رَكْعَةً، فَلَمَّا أَحَسَّ بِالنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، ذَهَبَ يَتَأَخَّرُ، فَأَوْمَأَ إِلَيْهِ، فَلَمَّا سلَّم قَامَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَقُمْتُ فَرَكَعْنَا الرَّكْعَةَ الَّتِي سَبَقَتْنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الطهارة (274-81) عن محمد بن عبد الله بن بزيع، حدثنا يزيد (يعني ابن زريع)، حدثنا حميد الطويل، حدثنا بكر بن عبد الله المزني، عن عروة بن المغيرة بن شعبة، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن النبي ﷺ صلى خلف عبد الرحمن بن عوف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (274, no. 81).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Prayed Behind ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل عبد الرحمن بن عوف وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf","part_no":49,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We came to the people while they had already begun the prayer. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf was leading them, and they had already completed one rakʿah. When he realized that the Prophet ﷺ had arrived, he tried to step back, but the Prophet ﷺ motioned for him to remain where he was. After ʿAbd al-Raḥmān concluded the prayer with salām, the Prophet ﷺ and I stood and performed the rakʿah that we had missed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",168],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (274/81)."},{"num":9970,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ عَوْفٍ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ انْتَهَى إِلَيْهِ وَهُوَ يُصَلِّي بِالنَّاسِ، فَأَرَادَ أَنْ يَتَأَخَّرَ، فَأَوْمَأَ إِلَيْهِ، أَنْ مَكَانَكَ، فَصَلَّى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِصَلاةِ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ عَوْفٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الطيالسي (223)، والبزار (1014)، وأبو يعلى (853)، والشاشي في مسنده (246) كلهم من طريق إبراهيم بن سعد (هو إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن بن عوف)، عن أبيه (سعد)، عن جده (إبراهيم)، عن عبدالرحمن بن عوف فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن النبي ﷺ صلى خلف عبد الرحمن بن عوف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī (223), al-Bazzār (1014), Abū Yaʿlā (853), and al-Shāshī in his Musnad (246).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Prayed Behind ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل عبد الرحمن بن عوف وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf","part_no":49,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came while he was leading the people in prayer. He attempted to step back, but the Prophet ﷺ signaled to him: “Remain where you are.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ completed the prayer behind ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",169],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الطيالسي (223)، والبزار (1014)، وأبو يعلى (853)، والشاشي في مسنده (246)."},{"num":9971,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ سَلَمَةَ، قَالَتْ: دَخَلَ عَلَيْهَا عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنُ عَوْفٍ قَالَ: فَقَالَ: يَا أُمَّهْ، قَدْ خِفْتُ أَنْ يُهْلِكَنِي كَثْرَةُ مَالِي، أَنَا أَكْثَرُ قُرَيْشٍ مَالًا، قَالَتْ: يَا بُنَيَّ، فَأَنْفِقْ، فَإِنِّي سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: إِنَّ مِنْ أَصْحَابِي مَنْ لَا يَرَانِي بَعْدَ أَنْ أُفَارِقَهُ فَخَرَجَ فَلَقِيَ عُمَرَ فَأَخْبَرَهُ، فَجَاءَ عُمَرُ فَدَخَلَ عَلَيْهَا، فَقَالَ: لَهَا: بِاللهِ مِنْهُمْ أَنَا؟ فَقَالَتْ: لَا، وَلَنْ أُبْلِيَ أَحَدًا بَعْدَكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (26489)، والبزار في كشف الأستار (2496)، وأبو يعلى (7003) كلهم من طريق أبي معاوية محمد بن خازم، حدثنا الأعمش، عن شقيق، عن أم سلمة قالت: فذكرته.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في كثرة أمواله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (26489), al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (2496), and Abū Yaʿlā (7003).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Abundance of His Wealth","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل عبد الرحمن بن عوف وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf","part_no":49,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf came to her and said: “O my mother, I fear that the abundance of my wealth may destroy me. I am the wealthiest man among Quraysh.” She replied: “My son, spend generously, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Among my Companions are those who will not see me after I depart from them.’” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān then left and met ʿUmar, informing him of what Umm Salamah had said. ʿUmar came to her and asked: “By Allah, am I one of them?” She replied: “No, and I will not declare anyone else free from that after you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",170],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (26489)، والبزار في كشف الأستار (2496)، وأبو يعلى (7003)."},{"num":9972,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَلَمَةَ، عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ يَقُولُ: إِنَّ أَمْرَكُنَّ مِمَّا يُهِمُّنِي بَعْدِي، وَلَنْ يَصْبِرَ عَلَيْكُنَّ إِلاَّ الصَّابِرُونَ. قَالَ ثُمَّ تَقُولُ عَائِشَةُ: فَسَقَى اللَّهُ أَبَاكَ مِنْ سَلْسَبِيلِ الْجَنَّةِ. تُرِيدُ عَبْدَ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنَ عَوْفٍ، وَقَدْ كَانَ وَصَلَ أَزْوَاجَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِمَالٍ، يقالُ: بِيعَتْ بِأَرْبَعِينَ أَلْفًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3749)، وأحمد (24485)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (6995)، والحاكم (5360) كلهم من طريق بكر بن مضر، حدثنا صخر بن عبد الله بن حرملة، عن أبي سلمة بن عبد الرحمن، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب قصة إنفاقه على أزواج النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3749), Aḥmad (24485), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6995) and al-Ḥākim (5360).","chapter_en":"His Spending on the Wives of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل عبد الرحمن بن عوف وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf","part_no":49,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf narrated from ʿĀ’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to his wives: “Your welfare is one of the matters that concerns me after my death, and none will treat you with patience and care except those who are truly patient.” Thereafter, ʿĀ’ishah would say: “May Allah give your father to drink from the Salsabīl spring of Paradise,” referring to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, because he had provided financial support to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. It is said that the property he gave them was sold for forty thousand."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The Prophet’s ﷺ statement,","“Your welfare is one of the matters that concerns me after my death,”","refers to the affairs of his wives.","The Prophet ﷺ married eleven women. During his lifetime, Khadījah bint Khuwaylid and Zaynab bint Khuzaymah (Umm al-Masākīn) passed away, while he passed away leaving the remainder of his wives alive.","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf was among those who took special care of the Mothers of the Believers after the Prophet ﷺ. He bequeathed an orchard to them, which was later sold for forty thousand—or four hundred thousand, according to another narration recorded by al-Tirmidhī (3750)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",171],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3749)، وأحمد (24485)، وصححه ابن حبان (6995)، والحاكم (5360)."},{"num":9973,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنِ عَوْفٍ قَالَ: كَاتَبْتُ أُمَيَّةَ بْنَ خَلَفٍ كِتَابًا بِأَنْ يَحْفَظَنِي فِي صَاغِيَتِي بِمَكَّةَ، وَأَحْفَظَهُ فِي صَاغِيَتِهِ بِالمدِينَةِ، فَلَمَّا ذَكَرْتُ الرَّحْمَنَ قَالَ: لَا أَعْرِفُ الرَّحْمَنَ كَاتِبْنِي بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي كَانَ فِي الجاهِلِيَّةِ، فَكَاتَبْتُهُ عَبْدَ عَمْرٍو، فَلَمَّا كَانَ فِي يَوْمِ بَدْرٍ خَرَجْتُ إِلَى جَبَلٍ لِأُحْرِزَهُ حِينَ نَامَ النَّاسُ، فَأَبْصَرَهُ بِلَالٌ، فَخَرَجَ حَتَّى وَقَفَ عَلَى مَجْلِسٍ مِنْ الْأَنْصَارِ، فَقَالَ: أُمَيَّةُ بْنُ خَلَفٍ، لَا نَجَوْتُ إِنْ نَجَا أُمَيَّةُ، فَخَرَجَ مَعَهُ فَرِيقٌ مِنْ الْأَنْصَارِ فِي آثَارِنَا، فَلَمَّا خَشِيتُ أَنْ يَلْحَقُونَا خَلَّفْتُ لهُمْ ابْنَهُ لِأَشْغَلَهُمْ، فَقَتَلُوهُ، ثُمَّ أَبَوْا حَتَّى يَتْبَعُونَا - وَكَانَ رَجُلًا ثَقِيلًا - فَلَمَّا أَدْرَكُونَا قُلْتُ لَهُ: ابْرُكْ فَبَرَكَ، فَأَلْقَيْتُ عَلَيْهِ نَفْسِي لِأَمْنَعَهُ، فَتَخَلَّلُوهُ بِالسُّيُوفِ مِنْ تَحْتِي حَتَّى قَتَلُوهُ، وَأَصَابَ أَحَدُهُمْ رِجْلِي بِسَيْفِهِ، وَكَانَ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنُ عَوْفٍ يُرِينَا ذَلِكَ الْأَثَرَ فِي ظَهْرِ قَدَمِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الوكالة (2301) عن عبدالعزيز بن عبدالله قال: حدثني يوسف بن الماجشون، عن صالح بن إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن بن عوف، عن أبيه، عن جده عبد الرحمن بن عوف قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من أخبار عبد الرحمن بن عوف","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2301).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل عبد الرحمن بن عوف وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf","part_no":49,"group_no":9,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I entered into a written agreement with Umayyah ibn Khalaf: he would protect my property in Makkah, and I would protect his property in Madinah. When I wrote my name as ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, he said: “I do not recognize ‘al-Raḥmān.’ Write to me using the name you had during the pre-Islamic period.” So I wrote ʿAbd ʿAmr. On the Day of Badr, when the people had gone to sleep, I went with Umayyah toward a mountain to keep him safe. Bilāl saw him and cried out: “Umayyah ibn Khalaf! May I not survive if Umayyah survives!” He then called a group of the Anṣār, and they pursued us. When I feared they would catch us, I left Umayyah’s son behind for them in hopes of delaying them, but they killed him and continued after us. Umayyah was a heavy man. When they caught up to us, I said to him: “Kneel down.” He knelt, and I threw myself over him in an attempt to shield him. However, they thrust their swords beneath me until they killed him. One of their swords struck my foot, leaving a scar. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf used to show us that scar on the top of his foot."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",172],"full":1,"rep":[8767],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (2301)."},{"num":9974,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أنس قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إنَّ لكُلِّ أمةٍ أَمِينًا، وإنَّ أَمِينَنَا أَيَّتُهَا الأُمَّةُ: أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ بْنُ الْجَرَّاحِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4382) عن أبي الوليد، حدثنا شعبة، عن خالد الحذّاء، عن أبي قلابة، عن أنس فذكره.ورواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2419-53) من طريقين عن إسماعيل بن عُليّة، خالد الحذّاء به.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا عبيدة أمين هذه الأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3744) and Muslim (2419, no. 53).","chapter_en":"Abū ʿUbaydah Was the Trustworthy One of This Nation","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي عبيدة بن الجراح وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ","part_no":49,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every nation has a trustworthy guardian, and the trustworthy guardian of this nation is Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Another narration states:","The people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said:","“Send with us a man who will teach us the Sunnah and Islam.”","The Prophet ﷺ took Abū ʿUbaydah by the hand and said:","“This is the trustworthy guardian of this nation.”","Recorded by Muslim (2419, no. 54)."]},"intro_majmu":{"ar":["هو: عامر بن عبد الله بن الجراح، المشهور بكنيته، وبالنسبة إلى جده الجرَّاح، هاجر هجرتين، وشهد بدرًا وما بعدها، وهو الذي انتزع الحلقتين من وجه رسول الله ﷺ، فسقطت ثنيتاه."],"en":["He was ʿĀmir ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Jarrāḥ, widely known by his kunyah, Abū ʿUbaydah, and by attribution to his grandfather al-Jarrāḥ.","He made both migrations (to Abyssinia and to Madinah), participated in the Battle of Badr and every campaign thereafter, and was the Companion who removed the two rings of the Prophet’s ﷺ helmet that had become embedded in his blessed face, causing his own two front teeth to fall out."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",173],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4382)، ومسلم (2419/53)."},{"num":9975,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حديفة قَالَ: جَاءَ أهلُ نَجْرَانَ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالُوا: ابْعَثْ لَنَا رَجُلاً أَمِينًا، فَقَالَ: لأَبْعَثَنَّ إِلَيْكُمْ رَجُلاً أَمِينًا حَقَّ أَمِينٍ فَاسْتَشْرَفَ لَهُ النَّاسُ، فَبَعَثَ أَبَا عُبَيْدَةَ بْنَ الْجَرَّاحِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4381)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2420-55) كلاهما عن محمد بن بشار، ثنا محمد بن جعفر، ثنا شعبة، قال: سمعت أبا إسحاق عن صلة بن زفر، عن حذيفة فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا عبيدة أمين هذه الأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4381) and Muslim (2420, no. 55).","chapter_en":"Abū ʿUbaydah Was the Trustworthy One of This Nation","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي عبيدة بن الجراح وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ","part_no":49,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The people of Najrān came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Send us a trustworthy man.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “I will certainly send you a man who is truly trustworthy.” The people eagerly looked on to see whom he would choose. He then sent Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Additional Wording","Another narration recorded by al-Bukhārī states:","The al-ʿĀqib and al-Sayyid, the two leaders of Najrān, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intending to invoke mutual imprecation (mubāhalah).","One of them said to the other:","“Do not do it. By Allah, if he is truly a prophet and we invoke mutual imprecation against him, neither we nor our descendants after us will ever prosper.”","They then said:","“We will give you what you have asked of us. Send with us a trustworthy man, and send only one who is trustworthy.”","The Prophet ﷺ said:","“I will certainly send with you a man who is truly trustworthy.”","The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eagerly hoped to be chosen.","Then he said:","“Stand up, O Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ.”","When he stood, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ declared:","“This is the trustworthy guardian of this nation.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",174],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4381)، ومسلم (2420/55)."},{"num":9976,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن مَسْعُودٍ قَالَ: جَاءَ الْعَاقِبُ وَالسَّيِّدُ صَاحِبَا نَجْرَانَ، قَالَ: وَأَرَادَا أَنْ يُلَاعِنَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ أَحَدُهُمَا لِصَاحِبِهِ: لَا تُلَاعِنْهُ، فَوَاللهِ لَئِنْ كَانَ نَبِيًّا فَلَعَنَّا، -قَالَ خَلَفٌ: فلاعَنَّا- لَا نُفْلِحُ نَحْنُ وَلَا عَقِبُنَا أَبَدًا، قَالَ: فَأَتَيَاهُ، فَقَالَا: لَا نُلَاعِنُكَ، وَلَكِنَّا نُعْطِيكَ مَا سَأَلْتَ، فَابْعَثْ مَعَنَا رَجُلًا أَمِينًا، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَأَبْعَثَنَّ رَجُلًا أَمِينًا حَقَّ أَمِينٍ، حَقَّ أَمِينٍ قَالَ: فَاسْتَشْرَفَ لَهَا أَصْحَابُ مُحَمَّدٍ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ: قُمْ يَا أَبَا عُبَيْدَةَ بْنَ الْجَرَّاحِ قَالَ: فَلَمَّا قفّى، قَالَ: هَذَا أَمِينُ هَذِهِ الْأُمَّةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (136)، والنسائي في فضائل الصحابة (93)، وأحمد (3930)، وصحّحه الحاكم (5162) كلهم من طريق إسرائيل، عن أبي إسحاق، عن صلة (هو ابن زفر العبسي)، عن ابن مسعود فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا عبيدة أمين هذه الأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (136), al-Nasā’ī in Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (93), and Aḥmad (3930).","chapter_en":"Abū ʿUbaydah Was the Trustworthy One of This Nation","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي عبيدة بن الجراح وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ","part_no":49,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The al-ʿĀqib and al-Sayyid, the two leaders of Najrān, came intending to invoke mutual imprecation with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One of them said to the other: “Do not invoke mutual imprecation with him. By Allah, if he is truly a prophet and we do so, neither we nor our descendants will ever succeed.” So they came to him and said: “We will not invoke mutual imprecation with you. Rather, we will give you what you requested. Send with us a trustworthy man.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “I will surely send with you a man who is truly trustworthy—truly trustworthy.” The Companions eagerly anticipated being chosen. The Prophet ﷺ then said: “Stand up, O Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ.” When he stood, the Prophet ﷺ said: “This is the trustworthy guardian of this nation.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",175],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (136)، والنسائي في فضائل الصحابة (93)، وأحمد (3930)."},{"num":9977,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن خَالِدِ بن الْوَلِيدِ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: لِكُلِّ أُمَّةٍ أَمِينٌ، وَأَمِينُ هَذِهِ الْأُمَّةِ أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ بْنُ الْجَرَّاحِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (3825) عن محمد بن عبد الله الحضرمي، حدثنا مقدم بن محمد بن يحيى، ثنا عمي القاسم بن يحيى، عن عبد الله بن عثمان بن خيثم، عن أبي الزبير (محمد بن مسلم)، عن جابر، عن خالد بن الوليد فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن أبا عبيدة أمين هذه الأمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (3825).","chapter_en":"Abū ʿUbaydah Was the Trustworthy One of This Nation","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي عبيدة بن الجراح وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ","part_no":49,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Khālid ibn al-Walīd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Every nation has a trustworthy guardian, and the trustworthy guardian of this nation is Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",176],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (3825)."},{"num":9978,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن شَقِيقٍ قَالَ: قُلْتُ لِعَائِشَةَ: أي أَصْحَابِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ أَحَبَّ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَتْ: أَبُو بَكْرٍ، قُلْتُ: ثُمَّ مَنْ؟ قَالَتْ: عُمَرُ، قُلْتُ: ثُمَّ مَنْ؟ قَالَتْ: ثُمَّ أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ بْنُ الْجَرَّاحِ، قُلْتُ ثُمَّ مَنْ؟ قَالَ: فَسَكَتَتْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3657)، وابن ماجه (102)، وأبو يعلى (4732) كلهم من طرق عن الجريري-هو سعيد بن إياس-، عن عبدالله بن شقيق فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب كان أبو عبيدة أحب الناس إلى رسول الله ﷺ بعد أبي بكر وعمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3657), Ibn Mājah (102), and Abū Yaʿlā (4732).","chapter_en":"Abū ʿUbaydah Was Among the Most Beloved People to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ After Abū Bakr and ʿUmar","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع مناقب أبي عبيدة بن الجراح وأخباره","group_en":"The Collected Virtues and Reports Concerning Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ","part_no":49,"group_no":10,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaqīq said: I asked ʿĀ’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): “Which of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was most beloved to him?” She replied: “Abū Bakr.” I asked: “Then who?” She said: “ʿUmar.” I asked: “Then who?” She replied: “Then Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ.” I asked: “Then who?” He said: She remained silent."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Among the notable reports concerning Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ is that, at the gathering of Saqīfah Banī Sāʿidah following the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq said:","“I am pleased for you to choose either of these two men: ʿUmar or Abū ʿUbaydah.”","Abū Bakr also appointed Abū ʿUbaydah to oversee the Bayt al-Māl (the treasury of the Muslims).","Among his achievements was that Abū Bakr appointed him commander of the Muslim forces in Greater Syria (al-Shām). Through his leadership, most of Syria was conquered.","He passed away during the Plague of ʿAmwās in Syria in the year 18 AH, at the age of fifty-eight."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10019],"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3657)، وابن ماجه (102)، وأبو يعلى (4732)."},{"num":9979,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ إِسْمَاعِيلَ، عَنْ قَيْسٍ، قَالَ سَمِعْتُ سَعِيدَ بْنَ زَيْدِ بْنِ عَمْرِو بْنِ نُفَيْلٍ، فِي مَسْجِدِ الْكُوفَةِ: يَقُولُ وَاللَّهِ لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنِي وَإِنَّ عُمَرَ لَمُوثِقِي عَلَى الإِسْلاَمِ قَبْلَ أَنْ يُسْلِمَ عُمَرُ، وَلَوْ أَنَّ أُحُدًا ارْفَضَّ لِلَّذِي صَنَعْتُمْ بِعُثْمَانَ لَكَانَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3862) عن قتيبة بن سعيد، حدثنا سفيان، عن إسماعيل، عن قيس قال: سمعت سعيد بن زيد بن عمرو بن نفيل في مسجد الكوفة يقول: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إسلام سعيد بن زيد بن عمرو بن نفيل بن عبد العزى العدوي (زوج أخت عمر بن الخطاب)","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3862).","chapter_en":"The Acceptance of Islam by Saʿīd ibn Zayd ibn ʿAmr ibn Nufayl al-ʿAdawī (the Husband of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s Sister)","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع أخبار سعيد بن زيد بن عمرو العدوي","group_en":"The Collected Reports Concerning Saʿīd ibn Zayd ibn ʿAmr al-ʿAdawī","part_no":49,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿīd ibn Zayd ibn ʿAmr ibn Nufayl (may Allah be pleased with him) said in the mosque of Kūfah: “By Allah, I remember when ʿUmar had me bound because of my Islam before he himself embraced Islam. If Mount Uḥud had collapsed because of what you did to ʿUthmān, it would have been justified.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Another wording states:","“You should have seen me when ʿUmar had me and his sister bound because of Islam before he himself embraced Islam. If Mount Uḥud had collapsed because of what you did to ʿUthmān, it would indeed have been justified in collapsing.”","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (3867)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",177],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3862)."},{"num":9980,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عُمَر بن مُحَمَّدٍ، أَنَّ أَبَاهُ حَدَّثَهُ، عَنْ سَعِيدِ بْنِ زَيْدِ بْنِ عَمْرِو بْنِ نُفَيْلٍ أَنَّ أَرْوَى خَاصَمَتْهُ فِى بَعْضِ دَارِهِ، فَقَالَ: دَعُوهَا وَإِيَّاهَا، فَإِنِّي سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: مَنْ أَخَذَ شِبْرًا مِنَ الأَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ حَقِّهِ طُوِّقَهُ فِى سَبْعِ أَرَضِينَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ.","اللَّهُمَّ إِنْ كَانَتْ كَاذِبَةً فَأَعْمِ بَصَرَهَا، وَاجْعَلْ قَبْرَهَا فِى دَارِهَا.","قَالَ: فَرَأَيْتُهَا عَمْيَاءَ تَلْتَمِسُ الْجُدُرَ، تَقُولُ: أَصَابَتْنِى دَعْوَةُ سَعِيدِ بْنِ زَيْدٍ، فَبَيْنَمَا هِي تَمْشِي فِى الدَّارِ، مَرَّتْ عَلَى بِئْرٍ فِى الدَّارِ، فَوَقَعَتْ فِيهَا، فَكَانَتْ قَبْرَهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في المساقاة (1610: 138) عن حرملة بن يحيى، أخبرنا عبدالله بن وهب حدثني عمر بن محمد فال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب كان سعيد بن زيد مستجاب الدعوة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1610, no. 138).","chapter_en":"Saʿīd ibn Zayd Was One Whose Supplications Were Answered","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع أخبار سعيد بن زيد بن عمرو العدوي","group_en":"The Collected Reports Concerning Saʿīd ibn Zayd ibn ʿAmr al-ʿAdawī","part_no":49,"group_no":11,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad narrated that his father narrated from Saʿīd ibn Zayd ibn ʿAmr ibn Nufayl (may Allah be pleased with him): A woman named Arwā disputed with him over a portion of his property. Saʿīd said: “Leave her and her claim, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever wrongfully takes even a handspan of land will be burdened with it from the depths of seven earths on the Day of Resurrection.’” Then Saʿīd supplicated: “O Allah, if she is lying, then take away her eyesight and make her grave within her own house.” The narrator said: Later I saw her blind, feeling her way along the walls, saying: “The supplication of Saʿīd ibn Zayd has struck me.” Then, while she was walking within her property, she passed by a well in the courtyard, fell into it, and it became her grave."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Among the reports concerning Saʿīd ibn Zayd is that he was one of the earliest people to embrace Islam. He accepted Islam before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Dār al-Arqam.","ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb embraced Islam in Saʿīd’s house, because Saʿīd was married to ʿUmar’s sister, Fāṭimah.","Arwā mentioned in the narration was Arwā bint Uways.","Saʿīd ibn Jubayr said:","“Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, ʿUthmān, ʿAlī, Saʿd, Saʿīd, Ṭalḥah, al-Zubayr, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf all occupied the same position with the Prophet ﷺ: they stood before him in battle and behind him in prayer.”","This was mentioned by Ibn Ḥajar in al-Iṣābah.","Al-Wāqidī said:","Saʿīd died at al-ʿAqīq and was then carried to Madinah for burial. This occurred in 50 AH, though it has also been said 51 AH or 52 AH. He lived to be over seventy years of age."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",178],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1610: 138)."},{"num":9981,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["أَخْبَرَنِي أَبُو حُمَيْدٍ السَّاعِدِيُّ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّهُمْ قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ كَيْفَ نُصَلِّي عَلَيْكَ؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: قُولُوا: اللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَأَزْوَاجِهِ وَذُرِّيَّتِهِ، كَمَا صَلَّيْتَ عَلَى آلِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ، وَبَارِكْ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَأَزْوَاجِهِ وَذُرِّيَّتِهِ، كَمَا بَارَكْتَ عَلَى آلِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ، إِنَّكَ حَمِيدٌ مَجِيدٌ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في أحاديث الأنبياء (3369)، ومسلم في الصلاة (407-69) كلاهما من طريق مالك بن أنس، عن عبدالله بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن عمرو بن حزم ، عن أبيه، عن عمرو بن سليم الزرقي، أخبرني أبو حميد الساعدي قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أهل البيت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3369) and Muslim (407, no. 69).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the Household of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī narrated that the Companions asked: “O Messenger of Allah, how should we invoke Allah’s blessings upon you?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Say: O Allah, bestow Your blessings upon Muḥammad, his wives, and his descendants, just as You bestowed Your blessings upon the family of Ibrāhīm. And bless Muḥammad, his wives, and his descendants, just as You blessed the family of Ibrāhīm. Indeed, You are the Praiseworthy, the Glorious.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The author said:","The wording recorded by al-Bukhārī, Muslim, and others—as previously mentioned in the chapter on prayer—is:","“And upon the family of Muḥammad,”","in place of:","“His wives and descendants.”","This demonstrates that the term “family” includes his wives and descendants."]},"intro":{"ar":["قال الله تعالى:","﴿يَا نِسَاءَ النَّبِيِّ لَسْتُنَّ كَأَحَدٍ مِنَ النِّسَاءِ إِنِ اتَّقَيْتُنَّ فَلَا تَخْضَعْنَ بِالْقَوْلِ فَيَطْمَعَ الَّذِي فِي قَلْبِهِ مَرَضٌ وَقُلْنَ قَوْلًا مَعْرُوفًا ۝ وَقَرْنَ فِي بُيُوتِكُنَّ وَلَا تَبَرَّجْنَ تَبَرُّجَ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ الْأُولَى وَأَقِمْنَ الصَّلَاةَ وَآتِينَ الزَّكَاةَ وَأَطِعْنَ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ لِيُذْهِبَ عَنْكُمُ الرِّجْسَ أَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ وَيُطَهِّرَكُمْ تَطْهِيرًا ۝ وَاذْكُرْنَ مَا يُتْلَى فِي بُيُوتِكُنَّ مِنْ آيَاتِ اللَّهِ وَالْحِكْمَةِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كَانَ لَطِيفًا خَبِيرًا﴾ [الأحزاب: ٣٢-٣٤].","قال أبو بكر الصديق: ارقبوا محمدًا ﷺ في أهل بيته. رواه البخاري (٣٧١٣).","قوله: “ارقبوا” أي احفظوه."],"en":["Allah Most High said:","“O wives of the Prophet, you are not like any other women, provided that you remain mindful of Allah. So do not be overly soft in speech, lest one in whose heart is a disease should be moved with desire; rather, speak in an appropriate manner. Remain in your homes, and do not display yourselves as women did in the former days of ignorance. Establish prayer, give zakāh, and obey Allah and His Messenger. Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O People of the Household, and to purify you completely. And remember what is recited in your homes of Allah’s revelations and wisdom. Indeed, Allah is Most Subtle, All-Aware.”","Al-Aḥzāb 33:32–34.","Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq said:","“Honor and safeguard Muḥammad ﷺ by honoring and safeguarding the members of his household.”","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (3713).","The word “ارقبوا” means: preserve his rights and show due care regarding him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",179],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3369)، ومسلم (407-69)."},{"num":9982,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن زَيْدِ بن أَرْقَمَ قَالَ: قَامَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمًا فِينَا خَطِيبًا بِمَاءٍ يُدْعَى خُمًّا بَيْنَ مَكَّةَ وَالْمَدِينَةِ، فَحَمِدَ اللَّهَ وَأَثْنَى عَلَيْهِ، وَوَعَظَ وَذَكَّرَ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَمَّا بَعْدُ، أَلَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ! فَإِنَّمَا أَنَا بَشَرٌ يُوشِكُ أَنْ يَأْتِيَ رَسُولُ رَبِّي فَأُجِيبَ، وَأَنَا تَارِكٌ فِيكُمْ ثَقَلَيْنِ: أَوَّلُهُمَا كِتَابُ اللَّهِ فِيهِ الْهُدَى وَالنُّورُ، فَخُذُوا بِكِتَابِ اللَّهِ، وَاسْتَمْسِكُوا بِهِ - فَحَثَّ عَلَى كِتَابِ اللَّهِ وَرَغَّبَ فِيهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: وَأَهْلُ بَيْتِي، أُذَكِّرُكُمُ اللهَ فِي أَهْلِ بَيْتِي، أُذَكِّرُكُمُ اللهَ فِي أَهْلِ بَيْتِي، أُذَكِّرُكُمُ اللهَ فِي أَهْلِ بَيْتِي. فَقَالَ لَهُ حُصَيْنٌ: وَمَنْ أَهْلُ بَيْتِهِ يَا زَيْدُ؟ أَلَيْسَ نِسَاؤُهُ مِنْ أَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ؟ قَالَ: نِسَاؤُهُ مِنْ أَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ، وَلَكِنْ أَهْلُ بَيْتِهِ مَنْ حُرِمَ الصَّدَقَةَ بَعْدَهُ. قَالَ: وَمَنْ هُمْ؟ قَالَ: هُمْ آلُ عَلِيٍّ، وَآلُ عَقِيلٍ، وَآلُ جَعْفَرٍ، وَآلُ عَبَّاسٍ. قَالَ: كُلُّ هَؤُلَاءِ حُرِمَ الصَّدَقَةَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2408) من طرق عن إسماعيل بن إبراهيم، حدثني ابو حيان، حدثني يزيد بن حيان قال: انطلقت أنا وحصين بن سبرة وعمر بن مسلم إلى زيد بن أرقم، فلما جلسنا إليه قال له حصين: لقد لقيت يازيد خيراً كثيراً، رأيت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، وسمعت حديثه، وغزوت معه، وصليت خلفه، لقد لقيت يازيد خيراً كثيراً، حدثنا يازيد ما سمعت من رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، قال: يا ابن أخي، والله لقد كبرت سني، وقدم عهدي، ونسيت بعض الذي كنت أعي من رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، فما حدثتكم فاقبلوا، ومالا فلا تكلِّفونيه، ثم قال: قام رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يوماً فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أهل البيت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2408).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the Household of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zayd ibn Arqam narrated: One day, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us to deliver a sermon at a watering place called Khumm, situated between Makkah and Madinah. He praised and extolled Allah, admonished us, and reminded us. He then said: “To proceed: O people, I am only a human being. The messenger of my Lord may soon come to me, and I will answer his call. I am leaving among you two weighty things. The first of them is the Book of Allah, in which there is guidance and light. So hold firmly to the Book of Allah and adhere to it.” He strongly encouraged them to adhere to the Book of Allah and urged them toward it. Then he said: “And the members of my household. I remind you of Allah regarding the members of my household. I remind you of Allah regarding the members of my household. I remind you of Allah regarding the members of my household.” Ḥuṣayn asked Zayd: “Who are the members of his household, O Zayd? Are his wives not among the members of his household?” He replied: “His wives are among the members of his household. However, the members of his household referred to here are those for whom charity remained forbidden after him.” Ḥuṣayn asked: “Who are they?” He replied: “They are the family of ʿAlī, the family of ʿAqīl, the family of Jaʿfar, and the family of al-ʿAbbās.” He asked: “Was charity forbidden to all of them?” Zayd replied: “Yes.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["This hadith does not contain a command to adhere to the guidance of the Prophet’s household. Rather, it establishes the obligation of caring for them, loving them, and avoiding whatever would cause them harm, provided that they adhere to the Qur’an and Sunnah.","This is how the Companions understood it.","Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq said:","“By the One in whose hand is my soul, maintaining ties with the relatives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is more beloved to me than maintaining ties with my own relatives.”","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (3712).","As for the claim that their statements and actions must be adhered to alongside the Book of Allah, nothing authentic has been established concerning that."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",180],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2408)."},{"num":9983,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: وَالَّذِي نَفْسِي بِيَدِهِ، لَا يُبْغِضُنَا أَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ رَجُلٌ إِلَاّ أَدْخَلَهُ اللَّهُ النَّارَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (6978) عن الحسين بن عبدالله بن يزيد القطان بالرقة قال: حدثنا هشام بن عمار قال: حدثنا أسد بن موسى قال: حدثنا سليم بن حيان، عن أبي المتوكل الناجي، عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أهل البيت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6978).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the Household of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, no man hates us, the People of the Household, except that Allah will admit him into the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",181],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن حبان (6978)."},{"num":9984,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيِّ بْنِ رَبِيعَةَ الأسَدِيِّ الْوَالِبِيِّ قَالَ: لَقِيتُ زَيْدَ بْنَ أرْقَمَ – وَهُوَ يُرِيدُ الدُّخُولَ عَلَى الْمُخْتَارِ- فَقُلْتُ لَهُ: بَلَغَنِي عَنْكَ حديث.قال: مَا هُوَ؟ قُلْتُ: أسَمَعْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: إِنِّي تَارِكٌ فِيكُمُ الثَّقَلَيْنِ: كِتَابُ اللَّهِ عُزَوْجَلٌ، وعترتي.قال: نَعَمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه يعقوب الفسوي في المعرفة والتاريخ (1/537) عن عبيد الله بن موسى، والطحاوي في شرح المشكل (3463)، والطبراني في الكبير (5/210) من طرق عن أبي غسان مالك بن إسماعيل النهدي – كلاهما عن إسرائيل بن يونس، عن عثمان بن المغيرة، عن علي بن ربيعة قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أهل البيت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Yaʿqūb al-Fasawī in al-Maʿrifah wa-al-Tārīkh (1/537) and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (5/210).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the Household of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAlī ibn Rabīʿah al-Asadī al-Wālibī narrated: I met Zayd ibn Arqam while he was intending to enter upon al-Mukhtār. I said to him: “A hadith has reached me from you.” He asked: “What is it?” I said: “Did you hear the Prophet ﷺ say: ‘I am leaving among you two weighty things: the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and my close family’?” He replied: “Yes.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement “my close family” means: the members of my household."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",182],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه يعقوب الفسوي في المعرفة والتاريخ (1/537)، والطبراني في الكبير (5/210)."},{"num":9985,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ يَزِيدَ بْنِ حَيَّانَ، عَنْ زَيْدِ بْنِ أَرْقَمَ قَالَ:  دَخَلْنَا عَلَيْهِ فَقُلْنَا لَهُ: لَقَدْ رَأَيْتَ خَيْرًا، لَقَدْ صَاحَبْتَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَصَلَّيْتَ خَلْفَهُ، - وَسَاقَ الْحَدِيثَ بِنَحْوِ حَدِيثِ أَبِي حَيَّانَ، غَيْرَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: أَلَا وَإِنِّي تَارِكٌ فِيكُمْ ثَقَلَيْنِ؛ أَحَدُهُمَا كِتَابُ اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ، هُوَ حَبْلُ اللهِ، مَنِ اتَّبَعَهُ كَانَ عَلَى الْهُدَى، وَمَنْ تَرَكَهُ كَانَ عَلَى ضَلَالَةٍ وَفِيهِ. فَقُلْنَا: مَنْ أَهْلُ بَيْتِهِ؟ نِسَاؤُهُ؟ قَالَ: لَا، وَايْمُ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ الْمَرْأَةَ تَكُونُ مَعَ الرَّجُلِ الْعَصْرَ مِنَ الدَّهْرِ ثُمَّ يُطَلِّقُهَا فَتَرْجِعُ إِلَى أَبِيهَا وَقَوْمِهَا، أَهْلُ بَيْتِهِ أَصْلُهُ وَعَصَبَتُهُ الَّذِينَ حُرِمُوا الصَّدَقَةَ بَعْدَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2408): حدثنا محمد بن بكار بن الريان، حدثنا حسان (يعني بن إبراهيم) ، عن سعيد (وهو بن مسروق)، عن يزيد بن حيان، عن زيد بن أرقم فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أهل البيت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2407).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the Household of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yazīd ibn Ḥayyān narrated from Zayd ibn Arqam: We entered upon him and said: “You have witnessed much good. You accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and prayed behind him.” He then related the hadith with wording similar to that of Abū Ḥayyān, except that he said that the Prophet ﷺ stated: “Indeed, I am leaving among you two weighty things. One of them is the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. It is the rope of Allah. Whoever follows it will remain upon guidance, and whoever abandons it will be upon misguidance.” The narration also states: We asked: “Who are the members of his household? Are they his wives?” Zayd replied: “No, by Allah. A woman may remain with a man for a long period of time, and then he may divorce her, whereupon she returns to her father and her people. The members of his household are his blood relatives and paternal kin, for whom charity was forbidden after him.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement:","“It is the rope of Allah,”","means that it is the means that leads to His pleasure and mercy.","It has also been said that it refers to His light by which He guides, and it has been said that it refers to His covenant."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",183],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2408)."},{"num":9986,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عُمَرَ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: أُرِيتُ فِي الْمَنَامِ أَنِّي أَنْزِعُ بِدَلْوِ بَكْرَةٍ عَلَى قَلِيبٍ، فَجَاءَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ فَنَزَعَ ذَنُوبًا أَوْ ذَنُوبَيْنِ نَزْعًا ضَعِيفًا، وَاللَّهُ يَغْفِرُ لَهُ، ثُمَّ جَاءَ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ فَاسْتَحَالَتْ غَرْبًا، فَلَمْ أَرَ عَبْقَرِيًّا يَفْرِي فَرِيَّهُ، حَتَّى رَوِيَ النَّاسُ وَضَرَبُوا بِعَطَنٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3682)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2393) كلاهما عن محمد بن عبدالله بن نمير، حدثنا محمد بن بشر، حدثنا عبيدالله بن عمر قال: حدثني أبو بكر بن سالم، عن سالم بن عبدالله، عن عبدالله بن عمر، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أبي بكر وعمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3682) and Muslim (2393).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Abū Bakr and ʿUmar","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I was shown in a dream that I was drawing water from a well with a bucket attached to a pulley. Abū Bakr came and drew one or two buckets, and there was some weakness in his drawing—may Allah forgive him. Then ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb came, and the bucket transformed into a large one. I have never seen a remarkably strong man perform as he did, until the people had drunk their fill and brought their camels to their resting places.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Another wording recorded by al-Bukhārī states:","“I saw the people gathered upon an open plain…”","It also states:","“There was some weakness in his drawing.”","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (3633)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",184],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11713],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3682)، ومسلم (2393)."},{"num":9987,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: بَيْنَا أَنَا نَائِمٌ، رَأَيْتُنِي عَلَى قَلِيبٍ عَلَيْهَا دَلْوٌ، فَنَزَعْتُ مِنْهَا مَا شَاءَ اللَّهُ، ثُمَّ أَخَذَهَا ابْنُ أَبِي قُحَافَةَ، فَنَزَعَ بِهَا ذَنُوبًا أَوْ ذَنُوبَيْنِ، وَفِي نَزْعِهِ ضَعْفٌ وَاللَّهُ يَغْفِرُ لَهُ ضَعْفَهُ،ثُمَّ اسْتَحَالَتْ غَرْبًا فَأَخَذَهَا ابْنُ الْخَطَّابِ، فَلَمْ أَرَ عَبْقَرِيًّا مِنَ النَّاسِ يَنْزِعُ نَزْعَ عُمَرَ، حَتَّى ضَرَبَ النَّاسُ بِعَطَنٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3664)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2392-17) كلاهما من طريق عبدالله بن وهب عن يونس، عن الزهري قال:أخبرني ابن المسيب سمع أبا هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أبي بكر وعمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3664) and Muslim (2392, no. 17).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Abū Bakr and ʿUmar","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “While I was sleeping, I saw myself beside a well with a bucket upon it. I drew from it for as long as Allah willed. Then the son of Abū Quḥāfah took it and drew one or two buckets, and there was some weakness in his drawing—may Allah forgive his weakness. Then it transformed into a large bucket, and Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb took it. I have never seen any remarkably strong man draw water as ʿUmar did, until the people brought their camels to their resting places.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",185],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3664)، ومسلم (2392-17)."},{"num":9988,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: قَالَ:  بَيْنَا أَنَا نَائِمٌ، أُرِيتُ أَنِّي أَنْزِعُ عَلَى حَوْضِي أَسْقِي النَّاسَ، فَجَاءَنِي أَبُو بَكْرٍ فَأَخَذَ الدَّلْوَ مِنْ يَدِي لِيُرَوِّحَنِي، فَنَزَعَ دَلْوَيْنِ وَفِي نَزْعِهِ ضَُعْفٌ، وَاللهُ يَغْفِرُ لَهُ، فَجَاءَ ابْنُ الْخَطَّابِ فَأَخَذَ مِنْهُ، فَلَمْ أَرَ نَزْعَ رَجُلٍ قَطُّ أَقْوَى مِنْهُ، حَتَّى تَوَلَّى النَّاسُ وَالْحَوْضُ مَلْآنُ يَتَفَجَّرُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2392-18) عن أحمد بن عبدالرحمن بن وهب، حدثنا عمي عبدالله بن وهب، أخبرني عمرو بن الحارث أن أبا يونس مولى أبي هريره حدثه عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أبي بكر وعمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2392, no. 18).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Abū Bakr and ʿUmar","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “While I was sleeping, I was shown that I was drawing water at my basin and giving the people drink. Abū Bakr came and took the bucket from my hand to relieve me. He drew two buckets, and there was some weakness in his drawing—may Allah forgive him. Then Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb came and took it from him. I have never seen any man draw more powerfully than he did, until the people departed while the basin was full and overflowing.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-ʿaṭan is the resting place to which camels return after they have drunk and withdrawn from the water."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",186],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2392-18)."},{"num":9989,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ يَقُولُ:  وُضِعَ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ عَلَى سَرِيرِهِ، فَتَكَنَّفَهُ النَّاسُ يَدْعُونَ وَيُثْنُونَ، وَيُصَلُّونَ عَلَيْهِ قَبْلَ أَنْ يُرْفَعَ، وَأَنَا فِيهِمْ. قَالَ: فَلَمْ يَرُعْنِي إِلَّا بِرَجُلٍ قَدْ أَخَذَ بِمَنْكِبِي مِنْ وَرَائِي، فَالْتَفَتُّ إِلَيْهِ فَإِذَا هُوَ عَلِيٌّ، فَتَرَحَّمَ عَلَى عُمَرَ وَقَالَ: مَا خَلَّفْتَ أَحَدًا أَحَبَّ إِلَيَّ، أَنْ أَلْقَى اللهَ بِمِثْلِ عَمَلِهِ مِنْكَ، وَايْمُ اللَّهِ إِنْ كُنْتُ لَأَظُنُّ أَنْ يَجْعَلَكَ اللهُ مَعَ صَاحِبَيْكَ، وَذَاكَ أَنِّي كُنْتُ أُكَثِّرُ أَسْمَعُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: جِئْتُ أَنَا وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ، وَدَخَلْتُ أَنَا وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ، وَخَرَجْتُ أَنَا وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ، فَإِنْ كُنْتُ لَأَرْجُو، أَوْ لَأَظُنُّ أَنْ يَجْعَلَكَ اللهُ مَعَهُمَا."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3685)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2389) كلاهما من طرق عن عبدالله ابن المبارك، حدثنا عمر بن سعيد، عن ابن أبي مليكة قال: سمعت ابن عباس يقول: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أبي بكر وعمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3685) and Muslim (2389).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Abū Bakr and ʿUmar","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb was placed upon his bier, and the people gathered around him, supplicating for him, praising him, and invoking blessings upon him before he was carried away. I was among them. Suddenly, a man placed his hand upon my shoulder from behind. I turned and saw that it was ʿAlī. He prayed for mercy upon ʿUmar and said: “You have left behind no one whose deeds I would more dearly wish to meet Allah with than yours. By Allah, I have always believed that Allah would join you with your two companions, for I frequently heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘I came with Abū Bakr and ʿUmar; I entered with Abū Bakr and ʿUmar; and I went out with Abū Bakr and ʿUmar.’ Therefore, I used to hope—or believe—that Allah would join you with them.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Another wording recorded by al-Bukhārī states:","“Suddenly, a man behind me placed his forearm upon my shoulder and said: ‘May Allah have mercy upon you.’”","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (3677)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",187],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3685)، ومسلم (2389)."},{"num":9990,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["سَمِعَا أَبَا هُرَيْرَةَ يَقُولُ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  بَيْنَمَا رَجُلٌ يَسُوقُ بَقَرَةً لَهُ، قَدْ حَمَلَ عَلَيْهَا، الْتَفَتَتْ إِلَيْهِ الْبَقَرَةُ فَقَالَتْ: إِنِّي لَمْ أُخْلَقْ لِهَذَا، وَلَكِنِّي إِنَّمَا خُلِقْتُ لِلْحَرْثِ! فَقَالَ النَّاسُ: سُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ - تَعَجُّبًا وَفَزَعًا، - أَبَقَرَةٌ تَكَلَّمُ؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فَإِنِّي أُومِنُ بِهِ وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ.","قال أبو هريرة: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم : بينا راع في غنمه، عدا عليه الذئب فأخذ منها شاة، فطلبه الراعي حتى استنقذها منه، فالتفت إليه الذئب فقال له: من لها يوم السبع، يوم ليس لها راعٍ غيري؟.فقال الناس: سبحان الله، فقال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: فإني أومن بذلك، أنا وأبو بكر وعمر."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3663)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2388-13) كلاهما من طريق الزهري، أخبرني أبو سلمة بن عبدالرحمن، عن أبي هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أبي بكر وعمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3663) and Muslim (2388, no. 13).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Abū Bakr and ʿUmar","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “While a man was driving a cow upon which he had placed a load, the cow turned toward him and said: ‘I was not created for this. I was created only for plowing.’” The people exclaimed: “Glory be to Allah!” They were amazed and alarmed, saying: “A cow speaks?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I believe it, and so do Abū Bakr and ʿUmar.” Abū Hurayrah also narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “While a shepherd was tending his sheep, a wolf attacked and seized one of them. The shepherd pursued it until he rescued the sheep from it. The wolf then turned toward him and said: ‘Who will care for it on the Day of the Beast, when it will have no shepherd other than me?’”","The people exclaimed: “Glory be to Allah!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I believe that, and so do Abū Bakr and ʿUmar.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",188],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8314,15957],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3663)، ومسلم (2388-13)."},{"num":9991,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ ابْنِ الْحَنَفِيَّةِ، قَالَ: قُلْتُ لأَبِي: أَىُّ النَّاسِ خَيْرٌ بَعْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ قَالَ: أَبُو بَكْرٍ. قُلْتُ: ثُمَّ مَنْ؟ قَالَ: ثُمَّ عُمَرُ. وَخَشِيتُ أَنْ يَقُولَ: عُثْمَانُ، قُلْتُ: ثُمَّ أَنْتَ؟ قَالَ: مَا أَنَا إِلاَّ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3671) عن محمد بن كثير أنا سفيان، حدثنا جامع بن أبي راشد، ثنا أبو يعلى، عن محمد بن الحنفية قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أبي بكر وعمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3671).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Abū Bakr and ʿUmar","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah narrated: I asked my father, ʿAlī: “Who is the best of people after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He replied: “Abū Bakr.” I asked: “Then who?” He replied: “Then ʿUmar.” I feared that he would next say ʿUthmān, so I asked: “Then you?” He replied: “I am only one man among the Muslims.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",189],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3671)."},{"num":9992,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حُذَيْفَةَ قَالَ: كُنَّا جُلُوسًا عِنْدَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: إِنِّي لَا أَدْرِي مَا قَدْرُ بَقَائِي فِيكُمْ، فَاقْتَدُوا بالذين بَعْدِي - وَأَشَارَ إِلَى أَبِي بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرَ- واهتدوا بهدي عَمَّارٍ، وَمَا حَدَّثَكُمْ ابْنُ مَسْعُودٍ فَصَدِّقُوهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3799)، وابن ماجه (97)، وأحمد (23276،23419) كلهم من طريق وكيع، عن سفيان (هو الثوري)، عن عبد الملك بن عمير، عن مولى لربعي، عن ربعي بن حراش، عن حذيفة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أبي بكر وعمر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3799), Ibn Mājah (97), and Aḥmad (23276, 23419).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Abū Bakr and ʿUmar","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥudhayfah narrated: We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when he said: “I do not know how much longer I will remain among you. Therefore, follow the two who will come after me,” and he pointed toward Abū Bakr and ʿUmar. He continued: “Follow the guidance of ʿAmmār, and believe whatever Ibn Masʿūd narrates to you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",190],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3799)، وابن ماجه (97)، وأحمد (23276، 23419)."},{"num":9993,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أَبِي جُحَيْفَةَ عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ سَيِّدَا كُهُولِ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ مِنَ الأَوَّلِينَ وَالآخِرِينَ إِلاَّ النَّبِيِّينَ وَالْمُرْسَلِينَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (100)، عن أبي شعيب صالح بن الهيثم الواسطي قال: حدثنا عبد القدوس بن بكر بن خنيس قال: حدثنا مالك بن مغول، عن عون بن أبي جحيفة، عن أبيه قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن أبا بكر وعمر سيدا كهول أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (100).","chapter_en":"Abū Bakr and ʿUmar Are the Leaders of the Mature Men of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Juḥayfah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Abū Bakr and ʿUmar are the leaders of the mature men of Paradise, from the earlier and later generations, except for the prophets and messengers.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",191],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (100)."},{"num":9994,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي هريرة قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم لأبي بكر وعمر: هذان سيدان كهول أهل الجنة."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه عبدالله بن أحمد في زوائد الفضائل (200) عن محمد بن بشار بندار، قال: ثنا سلم بن قتيبة، قال: ثنا يونس بن أبي إسحاق، عن الشعبي، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن أبا بكر وعمر سيدا كهول أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad in Zawāʾid Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (200).","chapter_en":"Abū Bakr and ʿUmar Are the Leaders of the Mature Men of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding Abū Bakr and ʿUmar: “These two are the leaders of the mature men of Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",192],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه عبد الله بن أحمد في زوائد الفضائل (200)."},{"num":9995,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيِّ بْنِ أبِي طَالِبٍ قَالَ: إِنِّي لَجَالِسٌ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَيْسَ مَعَنَا أحَدْ مِنَ الْبَشَرِ، إِذِ أقَبَلَ أبُو بَكْرٌ وَعُمَرُ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا يَمْشِيَانِ كُلَّ وَاحِدٍ مِنْهُمَا آخُذَا بِيَدِ صَاحِبِهِ قُفَالٌ لِي: هَذَانِ سَيّدًا كَهَوْلٍ أهَلْ الْجَنَّةَ مِنْ الَأولَيْنِ وَالِآخَرِينِ إِلَّا النَّبِيِّينَ وَالْمُرْسَلِينَ، لَا تُخْبِرْهُمَا يَا علي.فما أخَبَرْتُهُمَا وَلَوْ كَانَا حَيِيَّيْنِ مَا حَدَّثَتْ بِهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الدولابي في الكنى (2/99) عن أبي هاشم زياد بن أيوب، قال حدثنا علي بن محمد الطنافسي – ابن أخت يعلى بن عبيد - قال: حدثنا عبدالله أبو محمد مولى بني هاشم – وكان ثقه - قال: حدثنا زهير بن معاوية، عن عاصم، عن زر (هو ابن حبيش)، عن علي قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن أبا بكر وعمر سيدا كهول أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Dūlābī in al-Kunā (2/99).","chapter_en":"Abū Bakr and ʿUmar Are the Leaders of the Mature Men of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and no one else was with us, when Abū Bakr and ʿUmar approached, each holding the other’s hand. The Prophet ﷺ said: “These two are the leaders of the mature men of Paradise, from the earlier and later generations, except for the prophets and messengers. Do not tell them, O ʿAlī.” So I did not tell them. Had they still been alive, I would not have narrated it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",193],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الدولابي في الكنى (2/99)."},{"num":9996,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُمَرَ بن الْخَطَّابِ قَالَ: أَمَرَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمًا أَنْ نَتَصَدَّقَ، فَوَافَقَ ذالك مَالاً عِنْدِي، فَقُلْتُ: الْيَوْمَ أَسْبِقُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ إِنْ سَبَقْتُهُ يَوْمًا فَجِئْتُ بِنِصْفِ مَالِي، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ : مَا أَبْقَيْتَ لأَهْلِكَ؟.فَقُلْتُ: مِثْلَهُ.قَالَ: وَأَتَى أَبُو بَكْرٍ بِكُلِّ مَا عِنْدَهُ، فَقَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا أَبْقَيْتَ لأَهْلِكَ؟.قَالَ: أَبْقَيْتُ لَهُمُ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ، قُلْتُ لاَ أُسَابِقُكَ إِلَى شيء أَبَدًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1678)، والترمذي (3675)، وصحّحه الحاكم (1510) كلهم من طريق أبي نعيم الفضل بن دكين، حدثنا هشام بن سعد، عن زيد بن أسلم، عن أبيه قال: سمعت عمر بن الخطاب يقول: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن أبا بكر وعمر سيدا كهول أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1678) and al-Tirmidhī (3675). Al-Tirmidhī said: “good authentic hadith.”","chapter_en":"Abū Bakr and ʿUmar Are the Leaders of the Mature Men of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated: One day, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to give charity. At that time, I happened to possess some wealth, so I said to myself: “Today I will surpass Abū Bakr, if I am ever able to surpass him.” I brought half of my wealth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “What have you left for your family?” I replied: “An equal amount.” Then Abū Bakr came with everything he possessed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him: “What have you left for your family?” He replied: “I have left Allah and His Messenger for them.” I then said: “I will never compete with you in anything again.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",194],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1678)، والترمذي (3675)، وقال الترمذي: “حسن صحيح”."},{"num":9997,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنَّ الرَّجُلَ مِنْ أَهْلِ عِلِّيِّينَ يُشْرِفُ عَلَى أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ كَأَنَّهُ كَوْكَبٌ دُرِّيٌّ، وَإِنَّ أَبَا بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرَ مِنْهُمْ، وَأَنْعَمَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد في فضائل الصحابة (706)، والبزار في مسنده (9619)، والطبراني في الأوسط (مجمع البحرين3643) –واللفظ له- كلهم من طريق سلم بن قتيبة أبي قتيبة، عن يونس بن أبي إسحاق، عن الشعبي، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن أبا بكر وعمر سيدا كهول أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad in Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (706) and al-Bazzār in his Musnad (9619).","chapter_en":"Abū Bakr and ʿUmar Are the Leaders of the Mature Men of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A man from the inhabitants of ʿIlliyyīn will look down upon the people of Paradise like a brilliant star, and Abū Bakr and ʿUmar are among them—and what excellent men they are.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",195],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد في فضائل الصحابة (706)، والبزار في مسنده (9619)."},{"num":9998,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ أَهْلَ عِلِّيِّينَ ليراهم مَنْ هُوَ أَسْفَلَ مِنْهُمْ كَمَا يُرَى الْكَوْكَبُ الدُّرِّيَّ فِي أفق السَّمَاءِ، وَإِنَّ أَبَا بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرَ لمِنْهُم، وَأَنْعَمَا ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (3987)، والترمذي (3658)، وابن ماجه (96)، و أحمد (11882،11467) كلهم من طرق عن عطية بن سعد العوفي، عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن أبا بكر وعمر سيدا كهول أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Good through supporting narrations: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (3987), al-Tirmidhī (3658), Ibn Mājah (96), and Aḥmad (11882, 11467).","chapter_en":"Abū Bakr and ʿUmar Are the Leaders of the Mature Men of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The inhabitants of ʿIlliyyīn will be seen by those below them just as a brilliant star is seen upon the horizon of the sky. Abū Bakr and ʿUmar are indeed among them—and what excellent men they are.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The first part of the hadith is authentically established with the following wording:","“The people of Paradise will see the inhabitants of the lofty chambers above them just as you see a brilliant star disappearing on the eastern or western horizon, because of the difference in rank between them.”","They asked:","“O Messenger of Allah, are those the dwellings of the prophets, which no one else can attain?”","He replied:","“No. By the One in whose hand is my soul, they are men who believed in Allah and affirmed the messengers.”","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (3256) and Muslim (2831)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",196],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (3987)، والترمذي (3658)، وابن ماجه (96)، وأحمد (11882، 11467)."},{"num":9999,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: كُنَّا نُخَيِّرُ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ فِي زَمَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَنُخَيِّرُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ، ثُمَّ عُمَرَ بْنَ الْخَطَّابِ، ثُمَّ عُثْمَانَ بْنَ عَفَّانَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3655) عن عبد العزيز بن عبدالله، ثنا سليمان، عن يحيى بن سعيد، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3655).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar narrated: During the lifetime of the Prophet ﷺ, we used to rank the people in virtue. We gave precedence to Abū Bakr, then ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, and then ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with them all."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",197],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3655)."}]);